window.HARVEY_READING_BOOKS = [{"id":"jane","zh":"简爱","en":"Jane Eyre","chapters":[{"en":"The Red Room","zh":"红房间","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["There was no question of going outside that afternoon.","那天下午根本出不了门。"],[" Rain beat against the windows of Gateshead, and the bare branches bent in the wind.","雨点敲打着盖茨黑德府的窗户，光秃秃的树枝在风中弯折。"],[" My cousins sat beside their mother, Mrs Reed.","表兄妹坐在他们的母亲里德太太身边。"],[" I had been told to stay away until I could behave more pleasantly.","她叫我离远点，等我能表现得讨人喜欢些再过去。"],[" I was ten years old, and I suspected that no amount of pleasant behaviour would make my aunt glad to see me.","我那年十岁，心里明白，无论我表现得多好，舅妈大概都不会乐意见到我。"]],"translation":"那天下午根本出不了门。雨点敲打着盖茨黑德府的窗户，光秃秃的树枝在风中弯折。表兄妹坐在他们的母亲里德太太身边。她叫我离远点，等我能表现得讨人喜欢些再过去。我那年十岁，心里明白，无论我表现得多好，舅妈大概都不会乐意见到我。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["I slipped into the breakfast room, took a book of birds from the shelf, and hid behind the curtain by the window.","我溜进早餐室，从架上取下一本画着鸟的书，躲到窗帘后面。"],[" The pictures carried me to empty beaches and icy seas.","图画把我带到空无一人的海滩和冰冷的海上。"],[" I had almost forgotten where I was when my cousin John came looking for me.","我几乎忘了自己在哪里，表哥约翰却找来了。"],[" He was older and stronger, and he knew that nobody would stop him.","他比我大，力气也比我大，知道没人会拦着他。"],[" He seized my book and threw it.","他抢过书朝我扔来。"],[" I fell against the door and felt blood at my temple.","我撞在门上，感觉到太阳穴流了血。"]],"translation":"我溜进早餐室，从架上取下一本画着鸟的书，躲到窗帘后面。图画把我带到空无一人的海滩和冰冷的海上。我几乎忘了自己在哪里，表哥约翰却找来了。他比我大，力气也比我大，知道没人会拦着他。他抢过书朝我扔来。我撞在门上，感觉到太阳穴流了血。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["For once I fought back.","这一次我还了手。"],[" When the servants came running, they pulled me away from John.","佣人跑进来，把我从约翰身边拉开。"],[" My aunt ordered them to lock me in the red room, where my uncle had died.","舅妈叫他们把我关进舅舅去世的红房间。"],[" The curtains, the carpet and the heavy bed all seemed to hold the same cold, dark colour.","窗帘、地毯和沉重的床架，仿佛都浸在同一种冷暗的红色里。"],[" Uncle Reed had taken me in when my parents died.","父母死后，是里德舅舅收留了我。"],[" Before his death, he had asked his wife to raise me as one of her own children.","他临终前请妻子像抚养亲生孩子一样养大我。"],[" I wondered what he would think if he could see me now.","我想，要是他能看见现在的我，会怎么想呢？"]],"translation":"这一次我还了手。佣人跑进来，把我从约翰身边拉开。舅妈叫他们把我关进舅舅去世的红房间。窗帘、地毯和沉重的床架，仿佛都浸在同一种冷暗的红色里。父母死后，是里德舅舅收留了我。他临终前请妻子像抚养亲生孩子一样养大我。我想，要是他能看见现在的我，会怎么想呢？"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["A light moved across the wall.","一道光掠过墙面。"],[" It might have been a lantern passing outside, but I thought of the dead and screamed.","也许只是有人提着灯从屋外经过，我却想起死去的人，尖叫起来。"],[" My aunt came to the door. I begged her to let me out. She shut it again, and I remember nothing more until I woke in my own bed.","舅妈来到门口，我求她放我出去。她又把门关上了。此后我什么也不记得，直到在自己的床上醒来。"]],"translation":"一道光掠过墙面。也许只是有人提着灯从屋外经过，我却想起死去的人，尖叫起来。舅妈来到门口，我求她放我出去。她又把门关上了。此后我什么也不记得，直到在自己的床上醒来。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Mr Lloyd, who had come to see how I was, asked whether I would like to go to school.","来看我的劳埃德先生问我愿不愿意去上学。"],[" Until then, I had scarcely known that my life could change.","直到这时，我才隐约知道，日子还有可能改变。"],[" I said yes.","我说愿意。"]],"translation":"来看我的劳埃德先生问我愿不愿意去上学。直到这时，我才隐约知道，日子还有可能改变。我说愿意。"}],"terms":[{"term":"no question of","meaning":"完全没有……的可能","usage":"There is no question of + 名词或动名词，排除一种可能；no question that 后常接确定的事实。","example":"With the roads flooded, there was no question of leaving before noon.","exampleZh":"道路被淹了，中午前根本没法出发。","meaningEn":"no possibility of doing something in the circumstances","usageEn":"Use “there is no question of” with a noun or an -ing form. “There is no question that” instead introduces something certain."},{"term":"slip into","forms":["slipped into"],"meaning":"悄悄溜进","usage":"强调动作轻、不引人注意；slip into a coat 则指迅速穿上外套。","example":"She slipped into the kitchen before anyone noticed her.","exampleZh":"趁谁也没发现，她溜进了厨房。","meaningEn":"to enter quietly and without attracting attention","usageEn":"Use it with a room or other place. “Slip into a coat” uses the same verb for putting something on quickly."},{"term":"seize","forms":["seized"],"meaning":"猛地抓住、夺过","usage":"比 take 突然且有力；抽象搭配 seize an opportunity 指果断把握机会。","example":"He seized the rope before it fell into the river.","exampleZh":"绳子还没掉进河里，他一把抓住了。","meaningEn":"to grab something suddenly and forcefully","usageEn":"Choose “seize” over “take” when the speed or force matters. Figuratively, “seize an opportunity” means to act on it decisively."},{"term":"scarcely","meaning":"几乎不、刚刚才","usage":"本身有否定意味，通常不再叠加 not；放句首时可用 Scarcely had ... when ...。","example":"I had scarcely sat down when the doorbell rang.","exampleZh":"我刚坐下，门铃就响了。","meaningEn":"hardly, or only just","usageEn":"The word already has a negative sense. For events that happen almost together, use “had scarcely … when …” or the more formal “Scarcely had … when …”."}],"glossary":[["bare branches","光秃的树枝"],["slip into","悄悄溜进"],["seize","猛地夺过"],["temple","太阳穴"],["fight back","还手"],["take someone in","收留某人"],["scarcely","几乎不"]]},{"en":"A Morning with Bessie","zh":"贝茜陪伴的早晨","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["For a while after the red room, I was allowed to stay upstairs.","红房间那场惊吓过后，我获准在楼上待了一阵。"],[" Bessie brought me a little cake on a painted plate I had often admired.","贝茜端来一块小蛋糕，盛在我常常羡慕的一只彩绘盘子里。"],[" It was the first time I could remember being allowed to touch the plate.","我记得，这还是头一回有人准我碰那盘子。"],[" To my surprise, neither the cake nor the bright flowers round its edge gave me any pleasure.","奇怪的是，蛋糕也好，盘沿的鲜艳花朵也好，都没能让我高兴。"],[" I asked for a book about a traveller among tiny people and giants.","我想读一本书，讲一个旅行者走进小人国和巨人国的故事。"],[" I had always thought the book delightful. That morning I found it frightening.","以前我总爱看，那天早上却越看越怕。"]],"translation":"红房间那场惊吓过后，我获准在楼上待了一阵。贝茜端来一块小蛋糕，盛在我常常羡慕的一只彩绘盘子里。我记得，这还是头一回有人准我碰那盘子。奇怪的是，蛋糕也好，盘沿的鲜艳花朵也好，都没能让我高兴。我想读一本书，讲一个旅行者走进小人国和巨人国的故事。以前我总爱看，那天早上却越看越怕。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Bessie sat at her work and sang.","贝茜坐着做针线，一边唱歌。"],[" The songs she knew were not all cheerful. In one of them, a child had to find a road through a country where no one knew her name.","她会唱的歌并不都快活，有一首唱的是一个孩子要在举目无亲的地方寻找出路。"],[" I wished Bessie would stay near me when she finished, although on ordinary days I would have been afraid to ask her.","我希望她唱完还能留在我身边，平日里我却多半不敢开口留她。"],[" She could speak sharply when she was in a hurry, but she had sat beside my bed when I was frightened.","她忙起来说话很冲，可当我害怕时，她曾坐在床边陪我。"]],"translation":"贝茜坐着做针线，一边唱歌。她会唱的歌并不都快活，有一首唱的是一个孩子要在举目无亲的地方寻找出路。我希望她唱完还能留在我身边，平日里我却多半不敢开口留她。她忙起来说话很冲，可当我害怕时，她曾坐在床边陪我。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Mr Lloyd asked whether I might prefer to live with poor relations.","劳埃德先生问我，会不会更愿意和贫穷的亲戚一起过。"],[" I thought of the children I sometimes saw outside the cottages and said I would rather go to school.","我想起偶尔在农舍外见到的孩子，说还是想去上学。"],[" I had a great deal to learn about poverty.","那时我对贫穷所知甚少。"],[" At ten, I could imagine being cold and hungry more easily than I could imagine being poor and dearly loved.","十岁的我很容易想象又冷又饿的日子，却几乎想不出，一个人可以很穷，同时也很受疼爱。"]],"translation":"劳埃德先生问我，会不会更愿意和贫穷的亲戚一起过。我想起偶尔在农舍外见到的孩子，说还是想去上学。那时我对贫穷所知甚少。十岁的我很容易想象又冷又饿的日子，却几乎想不出，一个人可以很穷，同时也很受疼爱。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Around that time I learned something of my parents.","大约那阵子，我也听说了一点父母的事。"],[" My mother’s family had been angry when she married a clergyman with little money.","母亲嫁给一位没什么钱的牧师，家里人为此动怒。"],[" She had chosen him all the same.","她还是选了他。"],[" They both died while I was very small.","我很小的时候，他们就都去世了。"],[" Until then, my parents had been little more than names to me.","此前，父母对我而言几乎只是两个名字。"],[" I began to wonder whether I had taken after my mother in ways my aunt would never tell me.","我开始想，我会不会在哪些地方像母亲，只是舅妈从来不肯告诉我。"]],"translation":"大约那阵子，我也听说了一点父母的事。母亲嫁给一位没什么钱的牧师，家里人为此动怒。她还是选了他。我很小的时候，他们就都去世了。此前，父母对我而言几乎只是两个名字。我开始想，我会不会在哪些地方像母亲，只是舅妈从来不肯告诉我。"}],"terms":[{"term":"in a hurry","meaning":"赶时间、匆匆忙忙","usage":"be in a hurry 描述状态；in no hurry to do 表示并不急着做。","example":"I was in such a hurry that I left my keys on the table.","exampleZh":"我太匆忙，把钥匙落在桌上了。","meaningEn":"moving or acting quickly because time is short","usageEn":"“Be in a hurry” describes the person's state. “Be in no hurry to do something” means they see no need to rush."},{"term":"dearly loved","meaning":"深受疼爱的","usage":"dearly 可表示感情深厚；pay dearly for 中却指付出巨大代价。","example":"He was dearly loved by everyone in the house.","exampleZh":"家里每个人都很疼爱他。","meaningEn":"loved deeply and affectionately","usageEn":"“Dearly” intensifies affection here. With “pay dearly for,” it describes a high cost or a painful consequence."},{"term":"all the same","meaning":"即便如此、还是","usage":"承认前面有不利条件，再补充结果；It’s all the same to me 则表示哪样都可以。","example":"The road was long, but we walked it all the same.","exampleZh":"路很长，但我们还是走完了。","meaningEn":"despite what has just been said","usageEn":"Often comes at the end of the clause and can be replaced by “even so.” “It’s all the same to me” is a different expression for having no preference."},{"term":"take after","forms":["taken after"],"meaning":"在外貌或性格上像家人","usage":"take after somebody 常用于家族相似；look after somebody 意为照顾。","example":"Nora takes after her father in the way she tells stories.","exampleZh":"诺拉讲故事的方式很像她父亲。","meaningEn":"to resemble a family member in looks or character","usageEn":"Use a person directly after “take after,” and add “in” to name the similarity. “Look after someone” means to take care of them."}],"glossary":[["painted plate","彩绘盘子"],["admire","欣赏；羡慕"],["in a hurry","匆忙"],["poor relations","贫穷的亲戚"],["dearly loved","深受疼爱"],["all the same","即便如此"],["take after","长得像或性格像某位家人"]]},{"en":"Lowood in Winter","zh":"洛伍德的冬天","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Before I left Gateshead, a tall man named Mr Brocklehurst came to inspect me.","离开盖茨黑德府前，一个名叫布罗克尔赫斯特的高个子男人来看我。"],[" My aunt told him that I often lied.","舅妈告诉他，我常撒谎。"],[" After he had gone, I told her exactly what I thought.","他走后，我把心里话一股脑说了出来。"],[" I did not love her, and I would tell anyone who asked me how she had treated me.","我不爱她，谁问起她是怎么待我的，我都会照实说。"],[" The words frightened me even as I spoke them, but afterwards I could breathe more freely.","说这些话时，连我自己也害怕。可说完后，连呼吸都轻松些了。"]],"translation":"离开盖茨黑德府前，一个名叫布罗克尔赫斯特的高个子男人来看我。舅妈告诉他，我常撒谎。他走后，我把心里话一股脑说了出来。我不爱她，谁问起她是怎么待我的，我都会照实说。说这些话时，连我自己也害怕。可说完后，连呼吸都轻松些了。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["At Lowood School we rose before daylight.","在洛伍德学校，天没亮我们就得起床。"],[" In winter the water in our basins froze, and our breakfast was sometimes so badly cooked that we could not eat it.","冬天，脸盆里的水结了冰，早饭有时做得难以下咽。"],[" Miss Temple, the superintendent, did what she could to help us.","主管坦普尔小姐尽力照顾我们。"],[" Mr Brocklehurst, who controlled the school, preached against comfort and fine clothes.","掌管学校的布罗克尔赫斯特先生教训大家不可贪图安逸，也不要穿讲究的衣服。"],[" When he brought his own family on a visit, I noticed the warm silk and fur they wore.","可他带家人来参观时，我注意到，她们穿着暖和的绸衣和皮毛。"]],"translation":"在洛伍德学校，天没亮我们就得起床。冬天，脸盆里的水结了冰，早饭有时做得难以下咽。主管坦普尔小姐尽力照顾我们。掌管学校的布罗克尔赫斯特先生教训大家不可贪图安逸，也不要穿讲究的衣服。可他带家人来参观时，我注意到，她们穿着暖和的绸衣和皮毛。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["My closest friend was Helen Burns.","我最要好的朋友是海伦·彭斯。"],[" A teacher often found fault with her, yet Helen never seemed to wish her any harm.","有位老师常挑她的毛病，海伦却似乎从不记恨。"],[" I could not understand how she bore such treatment.","我不明白她怎么受得了。"],[" She told me that she tried to remember what mattered beyond the anger of the moment.","她说，她努力提醒自己，除了眼前的愤怒，还有更值得在意的事。"],[" I did not always agree with her, but I liked sitting beside her and listening.","我不总同意她，却喜欢坐在她身旁听她说话。"]],"translation":"我最要好的朋友是海伦·彭斯。有位老师常挑她的毛病，海伦却似乎从不记恨。我不明白她怎么受得了。她说，她努力提醒自己，除了眼前的愤怒，还有更值得在意的事。我不总同意她，却喜欢坐在她身旁听她说话。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["One day Mr Brocklehurst made me stand on a stool in front of the school and warned the girls that I was a liar.","有一天，布罗克尔赫斯特先生让我站在凳子上，当着全校的面警告大家我是个撒谎的人。"],[" Helen passed close by and smiled at me.","海伦从我身边走过，朝我微笑。"],[" Later, Miss Temple heard my account of Gateshead and wrote to Mr Lloyd to check it.","后来，坦普尔小姐听我讲了在盖茨黑德府的遭遇，写信向劳埃德先生核实。"],[" When his letter came, she told the school that the charge against me was false.","收到回信后，她告诉全校，那项指责并不属实。"]],"translation":"有一天，布罗克尔赫斯特先生让我站在凳子上，当着全校的面警告大家我是个撒谎的人。海伦从我身边走过，朝我微笑。后来，坦普尔小姐听我讲了在盖茨黑德府的遭遇，写信向劳埃德先生核实。收到回信后，她告诉全校，那项指责并不属实。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["In spring, typhus spread through Lowood.","春天，斑疹伤寒在洛伍德蔓延。"],[" Helen, who was ill with consumption, was taken to another room.","海伦得的是肺结核，被安置在另一间房里。"],[" I found her one night and slipped into her bed.","一天夜里，我找到她，悄悄钻进她的被窝。"],[" We spoke quietly until I fell asleep with my arm around her.","我们轻声说话，直到我搂着她睡着。"],[" In the morning I was carried away.","第二天一早，有人把我抱走。"],[" Helen had died in the night.","海伦已在夜间去世。"]],"translation":"春天，斑疹伤寒在洛伍德蔓延。海伦得的是肺结核，被安置在另一间房里。一天夜里，我找到她，悄悄钻进她的被窝。我们轻声说话，直到我搂着她睡着。第二天一早，有人把我抱走。海伦已在夜间去世。"}],"terms":[{"term":"find fault with","forms":["found fault with"],"meaning":"挑……的毛病","usage":"多指反复指责；fault 单数放进这个固定搭配，不需冠词。","example":"The teacher found fault with every line of his drawing.","exampleZh":"老师对他画的每一根线都挑毛病。","meaningEn":"to pick out flaws and criticise someone or something","usageEn":"Often suggests persistent criticism. In this expression, “fault” is singular and has no article."},{"term":"preach against","forms":["preached against"],"meaning":"公开训诫人们反对……","usage":"against 后接议题或行为；preach about 可以只表示就某个主题布道。","example":"He preached against luxury while living in a large house.","exampleZh":"他住在大宅里，却总训诫人们不要追求奢华。","meaningEn":"to speak strongly in public against a practice or belief","usageEn":"Follow “against” with what the speaker opposes. “Preach about” introduces a topic without specifying a stance."},{"term":"bear","forms":["bore"],"meaning":"忍受","usage":"bear the pain 或 bear to look 都可用；此义过去式 bore 与名词 bore（令人厌烦的人）同形。","example":"She could not bear to hear the child cry.","exampleZh":"她受不了听见那孩子哭。","meaningEn":"to endure something difficult or painful","usageEn":"It can take a noun or an infinitive, as in “bear the pain” or “bear to look.” In this sense, the past tense is “bore.”"},{"term":"consumption","meaning":"肺结核（旧称）","usage":"历史小说中还会见到 die of consumption；现代通用病名称 tuberculosis。","example":"Two characters in the novel die of consumption.","exampleZh":"小说里有两个人物死于肺结核。","meaningEn":"a historical name for tuberculosis, especially when it affects the lungs","usageEn":"In older fiction you may read “suffer from consumption” or “die of consumption.” Use “tuberculosis” for the disease in current English."}],"glossary":[["inspect","察看；审视"],["basin","脸盆"],["superintendent","学校主管"],["preach against","训诫人们不要……"],["find fault with","挑……的毛病"],["bear","忍受"],["typhus","斑疹伤寒"],["consumption","肺结核的旧称"]]},{"en":"A Change at Lowood","zh":"洛伍德的变化","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["I had never liked the walls of Lowood as much as I did that spring.","我从没有像那个春天那样喜欢洛伍德的围墙。"],[" Wild flowers came up near them, and the hills around us were as green as any place I had imagined in winter.","墙边长出了野花，四周的小山青翠，胜过我在冬天想象的任何地方。"],[" One could follow the stream and find a spot where the water could be heard above everything else.","沿溪走一段，就能找到一个所在，耳朵里只剩水声。"],[" It seemed strange that a place should grow so beautiful while so many girls inside it were ill.","一个地方可以变得这么美，里面却有这么多女孩病倒，实在让人想不通。"]],"translation":"我从没有像那个春天那样喜欢洛伍德的围墙。墙边长出了野花，四周的小山青翠，胜过我在冬天想象的任何地方。沿溪走一段，就能找到一个所在，耳朵里只剩水声。一个地方可以变得这么美，里面却有这么多女孩病倒，实在让人想不通。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["When the sickness was over, people began to ask how we had lived before it came. They wanted to know what we ate and whether our rooms were fit for children.","疫病过后，有人开始打听我们先前是怎么生活的，问我们吃些什么，房间适不适合孩子住。"],[" Until then, most of us had supposed there was nobody outside the school who would take an interest.","在那之前，我们大多以为，学校外面根本没人关心。"],[" Once the facts were known, people raised money and took a greater part in the running of the place.","实情为人所知后，有人筹钱，也更认真地参与学校的管理。"],[" Mr Brocklehurst could no longer decide so much for us on his own.","布罗克尔赫斯特先生再也不能独自替我们决定那么多事了。"]],"translation":"疫病过后，有人开始打听我们先前是怎么生活的，问我们吃些什么，房间适不适合孩子住。在那之前，我们大多以为，学校外面根本没人关心。实情为人所知后，有人筹钱，也更认真地参与学校的管理。布罗克尔赫斯特先生再也不能独自替我们决定那么多事了。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["At first I found it difficult to trust any improvement.","起先，我很难相信日子真的会变好。"],[" When there was enough breakfast for everyone, I ate quickly, as if there might be a mistake and someone would take it away.","早餐够每个人吃时，我反而吃得飞快，仿佛有人弄错了，随时会把它收走。"],[" In time I became used to sitting at a table without counting how much each girl had received.","过了一阵，我才习惯坐在桌前，不必去数每个女孩分到了多少。"],[" There were changes to the rooms and grounds as well, but being able to eat without anxiety was the change I noticed first.","房间和校园也有变化，但我最先留意到的，是吃东西终于不用提心吊胆。"]],"translation":"起先，我很难相信日子真的会变好。早餐够每个人吃时，我反而吃得飞快，仿佛有人弄错了，随时会把它收走。过了一阵，我才习惯坐在桌前，不必去数每个女孩分到了多少。房间和校园也有变化，但我最先留意到的，是吃东西终于不用提心吊胆。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["I went on with my lessons.","我继续上课。"],[" I liked drawing because I could make a place on paper and look at it for as long as I pleased.","绘画让我喜欢，因为我可以在纸上画出一个地方，想看多久就看多久。"],[" I liked French partly because each new word led to another.","我喜欢法语，一部分是因为每学会一个新词，又会牵出另一个。"],[" Miss Temple paid attention when I began to do well.","成绩好起来时，坦普尔小姐留意到了。"],[" Although she could not give me back what I had lost, she helped me see that there was something ahead.","她无法把我失去的东西还给我，却让我看见，前面还有事情值得期待。"],[" For several years, that was enough to make me content to stay.","有好几年，单是这一点就足以让我安心留下。"]],"translation":"我继续上课。绘画让我喜欢，因为我可以在纸上画出一个地方，想看多久就看多久。我喜欢法语，一部分是因为每学会一个新词，又会牵出另一个。成绩好起来时，坦普尔小姐留意到了。她无法把我失去的东西还给我，却让我看见，前面还有事情值得期待。有好几年，单是这一点就足以让我安心留下。"}],"terms":[{"term":"fit for","meaning":"适合……使用","usage":"fit for 后接名词；fit to do 接动词，也可表示身体或状态足以做某事。","example":"The room was too damp to be fit for children.","exampleZh":"那个房间太潮，不适合孩子待。","meaningEn":"suitable or safe enough for a particular purpose or person","usageEn":"Use “fit for” before a noun, such as “fit for children.” Use “fit to” before a verb, as in “fit to travel.”"},{"term":"take an interest","meaning":"表示关注、产生兴趣","usage":"take an interest in + 人或事，有主动关注的意味；lose interest in 表示失去兴趣。","example":"A neighbour took an interest in our school garden.","exampleZh":"一位邻居开始关心我们学校的花园。","meaningEn":"to start paying attention to something or showing that you care about it","usageEn":"Use “take an interest in” to name the person or topic. “Have an interest in” can describe an interest you already have."},{"term":"on one’s own","forms":["on his own"],"meaning":"独自、靠自己","usage":"随主语变化为 on my/her/their own；常强调没有帮助或陪伴。","example":"She finished the repairs on her own.","exampleZh":"她独自把东西修好了。","meaningEn":"without help or company","usageEn":"Change the possessive to match the person, such as “on my own” or “on their own.” Context tells you whether the emphasis is on independence or being alone."},{"term":"content to","meaning":"乐意、满足于……","usage":"此处 content 重音在后一音节；content with 后用名词或动名词。","example":"For now, he is content to stay in his small flat.","exampleZh":"眼下他乐意继续住在自己的小公寓里。","meaningEn":"satisfied and willing to do or accept something","usageEn":"In this sense, “content” is stressed on the second syllable. Use “content to” with a verb and “content with” with a noun or an -ing form."}],"glossary":[["come up","（植物）长出来"],["fit for","适合……"],["take an interest","表示关心"],["raise money","筹钱"],["on one’s own","独自地"],["become used to","渐渐习惯"],["content to","愿意；满足于"]]},{"en":"A New Road","zh":"新的去处","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["The illness at Lowood brought visitors who wanted to know why so many girls had become sick.","洛伍德的疫情引来访客，他们想知道为什么有那么多女孩病倒。"],[" Better food and warmer rooms followed.","后来，饭食和房间都改善了。"],[" I stayed six years as a pupil and two more as a teacher.","我在那里做了六年学生，又教了两年书。"],[" I might have stayed longer if Miss Temple had not married and left.","要不是坦普尔小姐结婚离开，我或许还会待下去。"],[" After she went, I began to notice how little of the world I knew.","她走后，我渐渐意识到，自己了解的世界实在太小。"],[" I put an advertisement in a newspaper and received an offer to teach a young girl at a house called Thornfield.","我在报纸上登了一则求职广告，收到一份邀请，要我到桑菲尔德庄园教一个小女孩。"]],"translation":"洛伍德的疫情引来访客，他们想知道为什么有那么多女孩病倒。后来，饭食和房间都改善了。我在那里做了六年学生，又教了两年书。要不是坦普尔小姐结婚离开，我或许还会待下去。她走后，我渐渐意识到，自己了解的世界实在太小。我在报纸上登了一则求职广告，收到一份邀请，要我到桑菲尔德庄园教一个小女孩。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Mrs Fairfax welcomed me by the fire.","费尔法克斯太太在炉火边迎接我。"],[" I took her for the owner until she explained that she kept house for Mr Rochester, who was often away.","我起先以为她是女主人，后来才知道，她是管家，替经常外出的罗切斯特先生打理庄园。"],[" My pupil, Adèle, spoke French when she was excited and liked to sing the songs her mother had taught her.","我的学生阿黛勒一兴奋就说法语，爱唱母亲教她的歌曲。"],[" I enjoyed teaching her. In the evenings, however, I sometimes walked on the roof and looked towards the road. I wanted a life with more people in it and more to do than I could see from there.","我喜欢教她，只是有些傍晚，我会走上屋顶，朝远处的道路眺望。我想见到更多的人，也想多做些事。站在那里，我还看不出这愿望该怎么实现。"]],"translation":"费尔法克斯太太在炉火边迎接我。我起先以为她是女主人，后来才知道，她是管家，替经常外出的罗切斯特先生打理庄园。我的学生阿黛勒一兴奋就说法语，爱唱母亲教她的歌曲。我喜欢教她，只是有些傍晚，我会走上屋顶，朝远处的道路眺望。我想见到更多的人，也想多做些事。站在那里，我还看不出这愿望该怎么实现。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["One winter afternoon I set out to post a letter.","一个冬日的下午，我出门寄信。"],[" As the light was failing, a horse came down the lane. It slipped on the ice, and the rider fell.","天色渐暗，一匹马沿小路走来，在冰上一滑，骑马的人摔了下来。"],[" He was a dark, broad-shouldered man, and he was annoyed at needing help.","他头发乌黑，肩膀很宽，对自己需要别人帮忙有些恼火。"],[" When he found that I lived at Thornfield, he asked me to stand still while he used my shoulder to raise himself.","得知我住在桑菲尔德，他让我站稳，扶着我的肩膀站起来。"],[" I thought I would never see him again.","我以为再也不会见到他。"],[" By the time I got back, his dog was lying by the fire.","回到庄园时，他的狗却卧在炉火边。"],[" The stranger was Mr Rochester himself.","那个陌生人就是罗切斯特先生。"]],"translation":"一个冬日的下午，我出门寄信。天色渐暗，一匹马沿小路走来，在冰上一滑，骑马的人摔了下来。他头发乌黑，肩膀很宽，对自己需要别人帮忙有些恼火。得知我住在桑菲尔德，他让我站稳，扶着我的肩膀站起来。我以为再也不会见到他。回到庄园时，他的狗却卧在炉火边。那个陌生人就是罗切斯特先生。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["He sent for Adèle and me the next evening.","第二天晚上，他叫我和阿黛勒过去。"],[" He looked through my drawings and asked blunt questions about my life at Lowood.","他翻看我的画，直截了当地问起我在洛伍德的生活。"],[" He did not put me at ease, exactly. Yet he listened to my answers as if an opinion from the governess might be worth hearing.","他的态度并不让人特别放松，却认真听完我的话，仿佛家庭女教师的看法也值得一听。"],[" I had not expected that.","这是我没有料到的。"]],"translation":"第二天晚上，他叫我和阿黛勒过去。他翻看我的画，直截了当地问起我在洛伍德的生活。他的态度并不让人特别放松，却认真听完我的话，仿佛家庭女教师的看法也值得一听。这是我没有料到的。"}],"terms":[{"term":"keep house","forms":["kept house"],"meaning":"料理家务、主持家政","usage":"不带冠词，可接 for somebody 指为谁料理家务；keep the house clean 有具体的宾补 clean。","example":"She kept house for an elderly uncle for many years.","exampleZh":"她给年迈的叔叔料理了多年家务。","meaningEn":"to manage the everyday work of a household","usageEn":"The expression has no article. “Keep house for someone” names the person whose household you run."},{"term":"set out","meaning":"动身、出发","usage":"set out to do 可指动身去做，也可指着手实现目标；set out for 后接目的地。","example":"They set out for the village just after dawn.","exampleZh":"他们天刚亮就动身去村里。","meaningEn":"to start a journey or set off to do something","usageEn":"Use “set out for” before a destination. “Set out to do something” can describe a journey’s purpose or the start of a deliberate attempt."},{"term":"blunt","meaning":"直截了当甚至有些不客气的","usage":"a blunt question 语气比 a direct question 更不客气；形容刀时指不锋利。","example":"Her blunt reply made the room go quiet.","exampleZh":"她直言不讳地回答，房间一下子安静了。","meaningEn":"direct in a way that may sound rude or insensitive","usageEn":"A “blunt question” leaves little room for tact. When applied to a knife, “blunt” means the edge is not sharp."},{"term":"put someone at ease","forms":["put me at ease"],"meaning":"让某人放松、自在","usage":"固定结构 put + 人 + at ease；feel at ease 是当事人自己觉得自在。","example":"A warm welcome put the new student at ease.","exampleZh":"热情的欢迎让新同学放松下来。","meaningEn":"to make someone feel relaxed or comfortable","usageEn":"Put the person between “put” and “at ease.” The person themselves can “feel at ease” once their discomfort has passed."}],"glossary":[["pupil","学生"],["advertisement","广告；启事"],["keep house","打理家务"],["set out","出发"],["lane","乡间小路"],["blunt","直截了当的"],["put someone at ease","让某人放松"],["governess","家庭女教师"]]},{"en":"Of Dresses and Songs","zh":"裙子与歌声","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["One evening Mr Rochester asked me to bring Adèle into the drawing room.","一天晚上，罗切斯特先生让我把阿黛勒带到客厅。"],[" He had a box for her, and it was no use pretending she could wait to see what was inside.","他有个盒子要送给她。看她的样子，也知道根本等不及要打开。"],[" Out came a dress.","盒子里是一条裙子。"],[" She ran upstairs to put it on and returned to dance before us.","她跑上楼换好，回来在我们面前跳舞。"],[" I had never seen her so pleased with anything she had been given.","我没见过她为哪份礼物这么高兴。"],[" Mr Rochester watched a little while, then looked away.","罗切斯特先生看了一会儿，就移开了目光。"]],"translation":"一天晚上，罗切斯特先生让我把阿黛勒带到客厅。他有个盒子要送给她。看她的样子，也知道根本等不及要打开。盒子里是一条裙子。她跑上楼换好，回来在我们面前跳舞。我没见过她为哪份礼物这么高兴。罗切斯特先生看了一会儿，就移开了目光。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Later he told me about her mother, Céline Varens, who had danced in Paris. Years before, he had paid for her rooms and given her presents. He had thought she loved him.","后来，他给我讲起阿黛勒的母亲塞莉娜·瓦朗。她以前在巴黎跳舞。多年前，他替她付房钱，也常送礼物，以为她爱他。"],[" One night, while he was waiting for her, he saw her arrive with another man.","有一晚，他等着她，却看见她和另一个男人一同回来。"],[" Listening without their knowing he was there, he heard them laugh at him.","他没让两人察觉，在一旁听见他们取笑自己。"],[" I could see that the memory still troubled him, though he told the story as if the young man in it had been a stranger.","他讲来仿佛故事里的年轻人是个陌生人，可我看得出，那段记忆还在折磨他。"]],"translation":"后来，他给我讲起阿黛勒的母亲塞莉娜·瓦朗。她以前在巴黎跳舞。多年前，他替她付房钱，也常送礼物，以为她爱他。有一晚，他等着她，却看见她和另一个男人一同回来。他没让两人察觉，在一旁听见他们取笑自己。他讲来仿佛故事里的年轻人是个陌生人，可我看得出，那段记忆还在折磨他。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Céline later left Adèle behind.","塞莉娜后来丢下了阿黛勒。"],[" Mr Rochester did not believe that he was her father, but he brought her to England and had her cared for.","罗切斯特先生不相信自己是她的父亲，却把她接到英格兰，安排人照顾。"],[" He was afraid, he said, that she would take after her mother.","他说，他担心她像母亲。"],[" When he spoke of her in that way, I thought of how readily grown people had judged me by what they had been told about my family.","听到这话，我想起大人们过去多么轻易就凭别人口中的家世来评判我。"],[" Adèle’s delight in the dress seemed perfectly ordinary to me.","阿黛勒为一条裙子高兴，我觉得再平常不过。"],[" She could be impatient, but she could also take pains over a lesson when she understood what she was being asked to do.","她有时是没耐心，但只要明白要做什么，也肯在功课上下功夫。"]],"translation":"塞莉娜后来丢下了阿黛勒。罗切斯特先生不相信自己是她的父亲，却把她接到英格兰，安排人照顾。他说，他担心她像母亲。听到这话，我想起大人们过去多么轻易就凭别人口中的家世来评判我。阿黛勒为一条裙子高兴，我觉得再平常不过。她有时是没耐心，但只要明白要做什么，也肯在功课上下功夫。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["I said I would go on teaching her just as before.","我说，我还是会照旧教她。"],[" Whatever had happened in Paris, she had not arranged any of it.","巴黎发生的事，无一件是她安排的。"],[" The following morning she came in trying to hide a yawn.","第二天早上，她进门时努力忍住哈欠。"],[" We sat down with a map of England, and the two of us began again with the places she knew.","我们摊开一张英格兰的地图，从她认得的地方重新学起。"]],"translation":"我说，我还是会照旧教她。巴黎发生的事，无一件是她安排的。第二天早上，她进门时努力忍住哈欠。我们摊开一张英格兰的地图，从她认得的地方重新学起。"}],"terms":[{"term":"no use pretending","meaning":"假装也没有用","usage":"it is no use + 动名词；pretend 后可接 that 从句或 to do。","example":"It is no use pretending we have plenty of time.","exampleZh":"假装时间充足也无济于事。","meaningEn":"pretending will not help or change the situation","usageEn":"Use “it’s no use” with an -ing form. “Pretend” can then take a “that” clause or a “to” infinitive."},{"term":"leave someone behind","forms":["left Adèle behind"],"meaning":"把某人撇下、留在原地","usage":"宾语若为代词，置于 leave 与 behind 之间；也可用来比喻未跟上时代。","example":"The hikers slowed down so they would not leave anyone behind.","exampleZh":"徒步的人放慢了脚步，免得有人掉队。","meaningEn":"to go away while someone else remains","usageEn":"Place a pronoun before “behind,” as in “leave her behind.” It can also describe failing to include someone in progress or change."},{"term":"take pains over","meaning":"认真在……上花功夫","usage":"over 后常接任务或作品；take pains to do 也常用。pains 保持复数。","example":"The carpenter took pains over every joint.","exampleZh":"木匠在每个接头上都下了功夫。","meaningEn":"to give something a great deal of care and effort","usageEn":"Use “over” with a task or work. “Take pains to do something” names the action you carry out with particular care."},{"term":"just as before","meaning":"仍和以前一样、照旧","usage":"just 强调完全一样；as before 也可以单独作状语。","example":"After the repairs, the old clock chimed just as before.","exampleZh":"修好后，老钟照旧报时。","meaningEn":"in exactly the same way as earlier","usageEn":"“Just” emphasises that nothing about the pattern changed. “As before” also works on its own."}],"glossary":[["pretend","假装"],["out came","从里面拿了出来"],["trouble","使不安；困扰"],["leave someone behind","丢下某人"],["take pains over","在……上下功夫"],["just as before","照旧"],["hide a yawn","忍住哈欠"]]},{"en":"Fire at Thornfield","zh":"桑菲尔德的火光","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["One night a low laugh woke me.","有天夜里，一阵低低的笑声把我惊醒。"],[" The sound was close to my door.","那声音离房门很近。"],[" I called out, and for a moment I heard nothing. Then came the noise of footsteps along the passage and towards the stairs.","我喊了一声，一时间什么也听不见，接着便有脚步沿着走廊朝楼梯远去。"],[" When I got up and looked out, a candle was burning on the floor.","我起身探头看，见地上燃着一支蜡烛。"],[" I could smell smoke.","空气里有烟味。"]],"translation":"有天夜里，一阵低低的笑声把我惊醒。那声音离房门很近。我喊了一声，一时间什么也听不见，接着便有脚步沿着走廊朝楼梯远去。我起身探头看，见地上燃着一支蜡烛。空气里有烟味。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["The door of Mr Rochester’s room was open.","罗切斯特先生的房门开着。"],[" His bed curtains were on fire, and he was still asleep.","床帘着了火，他还在睡。"],[" I tried to wake him.","我想把他叫醒。"],[" When he did not move, I seized the water jug and threw its contents over him.","他一动不动，我便抓起水壶，把里面的水泼到他身上。"],[" I went looking for more water, and between the two of us the fire went out.","我又去找水，两个人总算把火弄熄了。"],[" The room was dark, wet and full of smoke.","屋里漆黑、潮湿，全是烟。"],[" He wanted to know why I had come into it. I told him about the laugh.","他想知道我怎么会来，我就讲了那阵笑声。"]],"translation":"罗切斯特先生的房门开着。床帘着了火，他还在睡。我想把他叫醒。他一动不动，我便抓起水壶，把里面的水泼到他身上。我又去找水，两个人总算把火弄熄了。屋里漆黑、潮湿，全是烟。他想知道我怎么会来，我就讲了那阵笑声。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["He took the candle and went upstairs alone.","他拿起蜡烛，独自上楼。"],[" I sat where he had left me, wrapped in a shawl, thinking of the locked doors above.","我裹着披肩留在原处，想着楼上那些锁起来的门。"],[" When he came back, he said that I must tell nobody.","他回来后，嘱咐我不要告诉任何人。"],[" I thought the laugh belonged to Grace Poole, who worked in the upper rooms. He let me keep that idea.","我以为那阵笑声来自在楼上做事的格雷斯·普尔，他由着我这么想。"],[" Before I left, he took my hand.","临走时，他握住我的手。"],[" He had no light to see my face by.","当时没有灯照见我的脸。"],[" I was glad of it.","我庆幸是这样。"]],"translation":"他拿起蜡烛，独自上楼。我裹着披肩留在原处，想着楼上那些锁起来的门。他回来后，嘱咐我不要告诉任何人。我以为那阵笑声来自在楼上做事的格雷斯·普尔，他由着我这么想。临走时，他握住我的手。当时没有灯照见我的脸。我庆幸是这样。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["In the morning I found that the servants believed he had fallen asleep with a candle burning.","第二天早晨，佣人们相信，他是点着蜡烛睡着的。"],[" Grace was sewing in the room where the fire had been.","格雷斯正在烧过火的那间屋里做针线。"],[" I asked whether she had heard anything during the night.","我问她，夜间可曾听见什么。"],[" She asked, in return, whether I usually locked my door.","她反过来问我平常锁不锁房门。"],[" There was nothing in her face to tell me what she meant.","我从她的脸上看不出问这话的用意。"],[" That evening I made sure to lock it.","当天晚上，我特意锁好了门。"]],"translation":"第二天早晨，佣人们相信，他是点着蜡烛睡着的。格雷斯正在烧过火的那间屋里做针线。我问她，夜间可曾听见什么。她反过来问我平常锁不锁房门。我从她的脸上看不出问这话的用意。当天晚上，我特意锁好了门。"}],"terms":[{"term":"call out","forms":["called out"],"meaning":"出声喊","usage":"可独用或接人名；call out for help 即呼救。call out a mistake 另有当众指出之义。","example":"I called out, but the corridor was empty.","exampleZh":"我喊了一声，走廊里却没有人。","meaningEn":"to speak or shout loudly enough for someone to hear","usageEn":"It can stand alone or be followed by a name. “Call out for help” names the purpose of the shout."},{"term":"passage","meaning":"走廊、通道","usage":"in the passage 在建筑物内部通道；a passage from a book 中 passage 指一段文字。","example":"A narrow passage led to the back door.","exampleZh":"一条窄走廊通向后门。","meaningEn":"a corridor or narrow way through a building","usageEn":"“Along the passage” refers to movement through a building. “A passage from a book” is a section of writing."},{"term":"go out","forms":["went out"],"meaning":"火或光熄灭","usage":"the fire goes out 是不及物，put out the fire 才是把火扑灭。","example":"The candle went out when the window opened.","exampleZh":"窗户一开，蜡烛就灭了。","meaningEn":"to stop burning or giving light","usageEn":"The flame or light is the subject of “go out.” Use “put out” when someone or something extinguishes it."},{"term":"in return","meaning":"作为回应或回报","usage":"in return for + 对方先做的事；单独用时，可指用问题回敬一个问题。","example":"He lent me a coat, and I offered him my umbrella in return.","exampleZh":"他借我一件外套，我便把伞借给了他。","meaningEn":"as a response to something received or done","usageEn":"Use “in return for” to name what came first. On its own, the phrase can describe returning a favour or responding with a question."}],"glossary":[["call out","出声喊"],["passage","走廊"],["water jug","装水的壶"],["contents","里面装的东西"],["go out","（火）熄灭"],["wrap in","用……裹住"],["in return","作为回应；反过来"]]},{"en":"Two Portraits","zh":"两幅肖像","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Mr Rochester left Thornfield to visit friends.","罗切斯特先生离开桑菲尔德去访友。"],[" Mrs Fairfax mentioned that Blanche Ingram was likely to be among them.","费尔法克斯太太提起，布兰奇·英格拉姆也可能在那里。"],[" She had seen Miss Ingram before and remembered her dark hair, her fine figure, and her confidence in company.","她从前见过英格拉姆小姐，记得她乌黑的头发、优美的身姿，以及待人接物时的自信。"],[" I listened rather too closely.","我听得有点太认真了。"],[" Afterwards I went upstairs and looked at myself in the mirror.","事后，我上楼到镜前看自己。"]],"translation":"罗切斯特先生离开桑菲尔德去访友。费尔法克斯太太提起，布兰奇·英格拉姆也可能在那里。她从前见过英格拉姆小姐，记得她乌黑的头发、优美的身姿，以及待人接物时的自信。我听得有点太认真了。事后，我上楼到镜前看自己。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["I drew two pictures.","我画了两幅画。"],[" The first was mine, made with little more than chalk. I drew what I could actually see.","第一幅是我，只用了些粉笔，老老实实地画自己看见的样子。"],[" The second was of Blanche, whom I had never met. For her I used colour and made the best picture I could from Mrs Fairfax’s description.","第二幅画布兰奇，我还没见过她，就照着费尔法克斯太太的描述用上颜色，尽量画得好看。"],[" The pictures were to remind me where I stood whenever I began to imagine Mr Rochester was in love with me.","每当我开始想象罗切斯特先生爱我时，这两幅画可以提醒我，自己究竟处在怎样的位置。"],[" I had to go on living in his house, and I wanted to be able to do my work without waiting for him to come home.","我还得在他家里过日子，希望做好手头的工作，不用老盼着他回来。"]],"translation":"我画了两幅画。第一幅是我，只用了些粉笔，老老实实地画自己看见的样子。第二幅画布兰奇，我还没见过她，就照着费尔法克斯太太的描述用上颜色，尽量画得好看。每当我开始想象罗切斯特先生爱我时，这两幅画可以提醒我，自己究竟处在怎样的位置。我还得在他家里过日子，希望做好手头的工作，不用老盼着他回来。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["He came back with guests.","他带了一群客人回来。"],[" On the first evening he told me that Adèle and I must join them in the drawing room.","第一天晚上，他叫阿黛勒和我也到客厅去。"],[" She put on her prettiest dress and went in eagerly.","她穿上最好看的裙子，迫不及待地进了门。"],[" I chose a seat by the window.","我找了个靠窗的位置。"],[" Blanche Ingram was taller than I had expected. She could sing well, and she knew how to hold the attention of a room.","布兰奇·英格拉姆比我想象的高，歌唱得好，也知道如何让满屋子的人都注意她。"],[" She spoke of governesses as though none of the people she was describing could possibly hear her.","她谈起家庭女教师，仿佛被她说到的人根本听不到这些话。"]],"translation":"他带了一群客人回来。第一天晚上，他叫阿黛勒和我也到客厅去。她穿上最好看的裙子，迫不及待地进了门。我找了个靠窗的位置。布兰奇·英格拉姆比我想象的高，歌唱得好，也知道如何让满屋子的人都注意她。她谈起家庭女教师，仿佛被她说到的人根本听不到这些话。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["When I tried to leave, Mr Rochester met me in the hall.","我想离开，却在门厅遇见了罗切斯特先生。"],[" He asked whether I was tired and examined my face more closely than I liked.","他问我是不是累了，比我愿意的更仔细地看了看我的脸。"],[" Then he told me I might go, but that he expected me to come down again the following evening.","接着他同意我走，但说明晚还要我下楼。"],[" I went upstairs angry with him for noticing my feelings, and more angry with myself for being glad he had noticed.","我上了楼，既生气他看出了我的心情，又更生自己的气，因为他留意了，我竟有一点高兴。"]],"translation":"我想离开，却在门厅遇见了罗切斯特先生。他问我是不是累了，比我愿意的更仔细地看了看我的脸。接着他同意我走，但说明晚还要我下楼。我上了楼，既生气他看出了我的心情，又更生自己的气，因为他留意了，我竟有一点高兴。"}],"terms":[{"term":"in company","meaning":"在众人面前、与人相处时","usage":"此处 company 指有人作伴的场合；in the company of 后接同行者。","example":"He was talkative at home but shy in company.","exampleZh":"他在家健谈，在别人面前却很腼腆。","meaningEn":"when other people are present","usageEn":"“In company” describes social situations generally. “In the company of” is followed by the person or people present."},{"term":"little more than","meaning":"不过是、仅比……多一点","usage":"常用来压低评价或数量；much more than 则表示远不止。","example":"The shelter was little more than a roof on four posts.","exampleZh":"那个棚子不过是四根柱子撑着个屋顶。","meaningEn":"only slightly more than something basic or unimpressive","usageEn":"Often downplays what you are describing. “Much more than” puts the emphasis in the opposite direction."},{"term":"where one stands","forms":["where I stood"],"meaning":"自己在某事中的地位或处境","usage":"know where you stand 可表示清楚别人对你的态度，也可接 on 表示对议题的立场。","example":"I wanted to know where I stood with the rest of the team.","exampleZh":"我想知道队里其他人是怎么看待我的。","meaningEn":"how one is regarded, or what one’s position in a situation is","usageEn":"Use “where you stand with someone” for your relationship and “where you stand on an issue” for your position or opinion."},{"term":"hold the attention","meaning":"抓住、维持注意力","usage":"hold the attention of... 强调持续吸引；catch someone's attention 强调先让人注意到。","example":"The speaker held the attention of the whole room.","exampleZh":"演讲者始终吸引着全场的注意力。","meaningEn":"to keep people interested and listening or watching","usageEn":"“Hold” stresses that the interest continues. “Catch someone’s attention” stresses getting them to notice in the first place."}],"glossary":[["in company","与人相处时"],["chalk","粉笔"],["where one stands","某人的处境或地位"],["eagerly","迫不及待地"],["hold someone’s attention","吸引某人的注意"],["examine","仔细看；查看"]]},{"en":"The Visitor in Disguise","zh":"乔装的来客","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["The guests grew used to playing games after dinner.","客人们习惯了晚饭后做游戏。"],[" One evening Mr Rochester and Blanche acted together in a game of charades.","有一晚，罗切斯特先生和布兰奇一起玩表演猜词。"],[" She seemed pleased whenever people took them for a pair.","别人把他们当作一对，她似乎很高兴。"],[" Watching them, I thought she wanted to marry him.","我看着两人，觉得她是想嫁给他。"],[" Whether she was interested in what he was like when nobody was watching, I could not tell.","至于没有旁人看着时他是什么样，她是否也有兴趣，我就不知道了。"],[" By then, I knew what silence beside him could be like.","到那时，我已懂得同他安静地坐一会儿是什么感觉。"],[" I could not imagine replacing it with an afternoon of games.","我难以想象用一下午的游戏来换那份安静。"]],"translation":"客人们习惯了晚饭后做游戏。有一晚，罗切斯特先生和布兰奇一起玩表演猜词。别人把他们当作一对，她似乎很高兴。我看着两人，觉得她是想嫁给他。至于没有旁人看着时他是什么样，她是否也有兴趣，我就不知道了。到那时，我已懂得同他安静地坐一会儿是什么感觉。我难以想象用一下午的游戏来换那份安静。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["A stranger arrived from the West Indies. His name was Richard Mason.","一个陌生人从西印度群岛来到庄园，名叫理查德·梅森。"],[" He said he had known Mr Rochester abroad and sat down to wait for him.","他说，他在国外就认识罗切斯特先生，于是坐下来等他。"],[" That evening an old woman arrived at the house and offered to tell fortunes.","当晚又来了一位老妇人，说可以给大家算命。"],[" Blanche went first and came back looking offended.","布兰奇第一个去，回来时脸色难看。"],[" I was not going to go in, but the others urged me until I gave way.","我本不想进去，可大家一再劝我，我终于答应了。"]],"translation":"一个陌生人从西印度群岛来到庄园，名叫理查德·梅森。他说，他在国外就认识罗切斯特先生，于是坐下来等他。当晚又来了一位老妇人，说可以给大家算命。布兰奇第一个去，回来时脸色难看。我本不想进去，可大家一再劝我，我终于答应了。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["The woman sat near the fire in the library.","老妇人坐在图书室的炉火旁。"],[" She asked what I expected from the future.","她问我对未来有什么期望。"],[" I said that I had a place to work and that I could find another if I needed one.","我说现在有地方工作，必要时可以再找。"],[" She was more interested in how I felt when I sat by the window and watched the company.","她更想知道，我坐在窗边看那一屋子人时，心里是什么滋味。"],[" She also seemed to know why Blanche had gone away angry. Blanche, she said, had been told that Mr Rochester might not have so much money after all.","她似乎也知道布兰奇为何生气，说布兰奇听到了这样一个消息：罗切斯特先生也许并没有那么多钱。"]],"translation":"老妇人坐在图书室的炉火旁。她问我对未来有什么期望。我说现在有地方工作，必要时可以再找。她更想知道，我坐在窗边看那一屋子人时，心里是什么滋味。她似乎也知道布兰奇为何生气，说布兰奇听到了这样一个消息：罗切斯特先生也许并没有那么多钱。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["As the woman spoke her voice changed.","老妇人说着说着，声音变了。"],[" I looked more closely and recognised a hand I had seen many times.","我仔细一看，认出一只见过许多次的手。"],[" The fortune-teller was Mr Rochester.","算命人就是罗切斯特先生。"],[" I told him it was unfair to make me answer questions in such a way.","我说，他用这种办法让我回答问题，不公平。"],[" He put aside his disguise and began to laugh.","他脱下伪装，笑了起来。"],[" Then I told him about Mason.","接着我告诉他梅森来了。"],[" He stopped laughing and reached for the back of a chair.","他立刻不笑了，伸手扶住椅背。"],[" I had never known a name to change his face so quickly.","我从未见过一个名字能这么快改变他的脸色。"]],"translation":"老妇人说着说着，声音变了。我仔细一看，认出一只见过许多次的手。算命人就是罗切斯特先生。我说，他用这种办法让我回答问题，不公平。他脱下伪装，笑了起来。接着我告诉他梅森来了。他立刻不笑了，伸手扶住椅背。我从未见过一个名字能这么快改变他的脸色。"}],"terms":[{"term":"in disguise","meaning":"乔装打扮、身份被掩饰","usage":"in disguise 作状语或补语；disguise oneself as 后面接扮作的人。","example":"The prince travelled in disguise to avoid being recognised.","exampleZh":"王子乔装出行，以免被认出来。","meaningEn":"wearing something or acting in a way that conceals one’s identity","usageEn":"Use “in disguise” after verbs like “travel” or “be.” “Disguise yourself as” names the role or identity you take on."},{"term":"take someone for","forms":["took them for"],"meaning":"把某人当成……","usage":"take A for B 指根据表象误认 A；be taken for 是相应被动。","example":"I took the visitor for a new teacher.","exampleZh":"我误把来访者当成了新老师。","meaningEn":"to suppose, often mistakenly, that someone is a particular person or type","usageEn":"The structure is “take A for B.” In the passive, “A was taken for B” conveys the same mistaken impression."},{"term":"tell fortunes","meaning":"算命、预言运势","usage":"fortune 在此义常用复数；tell someone's fortune 也成立，与 make a fortune（发财）含义不同。","example":"A woman at the fair offered to tell fortunes.","exampleZh":"集市上有一位女子给人算命。","meaningEn":"to predict people’s futures as a practice","usageEn":"Use the plural to name the activity. “Tell someone’s fortune” is for one person, and “make a fortune” means to become wealthy."},{"term":"give way","forms":["gave way"],"meaning":"让步、屈从","usage":"give way to pressure 指屈服；桥梁等作主语时，give way 可指承重不住而坍塌。","example":"After several requests, he finally gave way and agreed to help.","exampleZh":"对方请求了好几次，他终于让步，答应帮忙。","meaningEn":"to yield or stop resisting","usageEn":"“Give way to pressure” names the force that makes you yield. A bridge or floor can also “give way” when it collapses under weight."}],"glossary":[["charades","用动作表演、让别人猜词的游戏"],["take someone for","把某人当成……"],["tell fortunes","算命"],["offended","被冒犯而生气的"],["give way","让步"],["after all","原来；终究"],["disguise","伪装"]]},{"en":"A Night with Mason","zh":"梅森受伤的夜晚","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["A cry rang through the upper floor that night.","那天夜里，楼上传来一声尖叫。"],[" People came out of their rooms carrying candles.","人们拿着蜡烛走出各自的房间。"],[" Mr Rochester assured them that someone had had a bad dream and told them to go back to bed.","罗切斯特先生说，有人做了噩梦，让大家放心回去睡觉。"],[" When the house was quiet again, he tapped at my door. He asked whether I could bear the sight of blood.","等屋里重新安静下来，他来敲我的门，问我受不受得了看见血。"],[" I said I thought I could, and followed him upstairs.","我说我想可以，就跟他上楼了。"]],"translation":"那天夜里，楼上传来一声尖叫。人们拿着蜡烛走出各自的房间。罗切斯特先生说，有人做了噩梦，让大家放心回去睡觉。等屋里重新安静下来，他来敲我的门，问我受不受得了看见血。我说我想可以，就跟他上楼了。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Richard Mason sat against a pillow, his shirt wet with blood.","理查德·梅森靠在枕头上坐着，血把衬衫浸湿了。"],[" Mr Rochester told me to hold a sponge to the wound and keep it from bleeding. He said he would fetch a surgeon.","罗切斯特先生让我用海绵按住伤口止血，他去请外科医生。"],[" Neither Mason nor I was to speak while he was gone.","在他回来前，梅森和我都不许说话。"],[" There was another door in the room. It remained shut, but from time to time I heard a movement beyond it.","房间里还有一扇门，一直关着，可我时不时听见门后有动静。"],[" The candle burned down, and I could not tell whether the steps I hoped to hear would come from the passage or from behind the door.","蜡烛一点点烧短，我盼着有脚步声，却想不出它会从走廊传来，还是从那扇门后传来。"]],"translation":"理查德·梅森靠在枕头上坐着，血把衬衫浸湿了。罗切斯特先生让我用海绵按住伤口止血，他去请外科医生。在他回来前，梅森和我都不许说话。房间里还有一扇门，一直关着，可我时不时听见门后有动静。蜡烛一点点烧短，我盼着有脚步声，却想不出它会从走廊传来，还是从那扇门后传来。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["At last Mr Rochester returned with the surgeon.","罗切斯特先生终于带着医生回来了。"],[" The wound had to be dressed quickly, before the other guests were awake.","得趁其他客人没醒，赶紧包扎好。"],[" Mason was weak, but with help he made it down to a carriage.","梅森很虚弱，在众人扶持下坐上了马车。"],[" Before he left, he asked Mr Rochester to look after the person who had hurt him.","临走前，他请罗切斯特先生照顾那个伤了自己的人。"],[" I wondered why a man who was so anxious to get away should worry about leaving that person behind.","我不明白，一个这么急着离开的人，为什么还要为留下的人操心。"]],"translation":"罗切斯特先生终于带着医生回来了。得趁其他客人没醒，赶紧包扎好。梅森很虚弱，在众人扶持下坐上了马车。临走前，他请罗切斯特先生照顾那个伤了自己的人。我不明白，一个这么急着离开的人，为什么还要为留下的人操心。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Outside, the morning had begun to brighten.","外面的天色渐亮。"],[" Mr Rochester asked me to walk a little way with him. He began to talk of a young man who had made a serious mistake abroad and had spent years trying to forget it.","罗切斯特先生请我陪他走一小段路，开始讲一个年轻男人的事。他在国外犯过一个大错，许多年都想忘掉。"],[" Would I blame such a man, he asked, for wanting a better life?","这样的人想过上更好的生活，我会怪他吗？"],[" I could see he wanted an answer that would quiet some fear of his own.","我看得出，他想听到一个能让自己心里踏实的答案。"],[" I did not yet know enough to give it.","那时，我还不懂得怎样回答。"]],"translation":"外面的天色渐亮。罗切斯特先生请我陪他走一小段路，开始讲一个年轻男人的事。他在国外犯过一个大错，许多年都想忘掉。这样的人想过上更好的生活，我会怪他吗？我看得出，他想听到一个能让自己心里踏实的答案。那时，我还不懂得怎样回答。"}],"terms":[{"term":"ring through","forms":["rang through"],"meaning":"声响传遍、响彻","usage":"主语常为声音；ring out 强调声音突然响起，ring through 强调传播的空间。","example":"A bell rang through the empty building.","exampleZh":"铃声响彻空楼。","meaningEn":"to sound clearly throughout a place","usageEn":"A cry, voice or bell can “ring through” a building. “Ring out” calls attention to the start or clarity of the sound rather than where it travels."},{"term":"assure","forms":["assured"],"meaning":"向某人保证、使某人放心","usage":"assure somebody that... 需有人作宾语；ensure that... 则表示确保某事。","example":"She assured me that the documents were safe.","exampleZh":"她向我保证文件是安全的。","meaningEn":"to tell someone firmly that something is true or will happen","usageEn":"Use “assure someone that …” with a person as object. “Ensure that” means to make certain of a result."},{"term":"bear the sight of","meaning":"受得了看见……","usage":"多出现于 can/could 或否定式；the sight of 指看到的场面。","example":"He could not bear the sight of an injured animal.","exampleZh":"他实在看不得动物受伤。","meaningEn":"to be able to tolerate seeing something upsetting","usageEn":"Usually follows “can” or “could,” often in a question or negative. “The sight of” introduces the upsetting thing or scene."},{"term":"dress a wound","forms":["wound had to be dressed","be dressed"],"meaning":"给伤口敷药并包扎","usage":"医疗语境的 dress 可接 wound 或 cut；a dressing 是覆盖伤口的敷料。","example":"The nurse cleaned and dressed the wound.","exampleZh":"护士清理并包扎了伤口。","meaningEn":"to treat and cover an injury, typically with a bandage or similar material","usageEn":"“Dress” in this medical sense takes “wound” or “cut.” A “dressing” is the material that covers the injury."}],"glossary":[["ring through","响彻"],["assure","向……保证"],["bear the sight of","受得了看见……"],["sponge","海绵"],["wound","伤口"],["dress a wound","包扎伤口"],["surgeon","外科医生"]]},{"en":"The Letter from Madeira","zh":"来自马德拉的信","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["A messenger came from Gateshead.","盖茨黑德府派人来报信。"],[" My cousin John was dead, and Mrs Reed had been taken seriously ill. She wanted to speak to me.","表哥约翰死了，里德太太病重，有话要和我说。"],[" I had once promised never to come back. Nevertheless, I asked Mr Rochester for leave.","我曾发誓再也不回去，还是向罗切斯特先生请了假。"],[" He agreed, though he could not understand why I felt bound to go so far to see a woman who had been so unkind.","他答应了，却想不通我为什么觉得应该走这么远，去看一个从前对我那么不好的人。"]],"translation":"盖茨黑德府派人来报信。表哥约翰死了，里德太太病重，有话要和我说。我曾发誓再也不回去，还是向罗切斯特先生请了假。他答应了，却想不通我为什么觉得应该走这么远，去看一个从前对我那么不好的人。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Bessie met me at Gateshead. She had children of her own now.","贝茜在盖茨黑德府迎接我，如今她也有自己的孩子了。"],[" My cousins Eliza and Georgiana were still in the house, but each lived as if she had no sister.","表姐妹伊丽莎和乔治安娜还在府里，可两人都像没有姐妹一样各过各的。"],[" Georgiana spoke of parties in London and dreaded being left alone.","乔治安娜念着伦敦的聚会，害怕独处。"],[" Eliza divided her time so strictly that she could tell what she should be doing at almost any hour.","伊丽莎把时间安排得很严格，几乎任何时刻都知道该做什么。"],[" Looking at the two of them, I remembered how much I had once wanted to be allowed to sit with them.","看着她们，我想起自己小时候多么盼着能获准同她们坐在一起。"]],"translation":"贝茜在盖茨黑德府迎接我，如今她也有自己的孩子了。表姐妹伊丽莎和乔治安娜还在府里，可两人都像没有姐妹一样各过各的。乔治安娜念着伦敦的聚会，害怕独处。伊丽莎把时间安排得很严格，几乎任何时刻都知道该做什么。看着她们，我想起自己小时候多么盼着能获准同她们坐在一起。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["My aunt knew me, although she did not welcome me.","舅妈认得我，却没有欢迎我。"],[" After a while she told me to look in a drawer for a letter.","过了一阵，她让我去抽屉里找一封信。"],[" It had come from my father’s brother, John Eyre, three years before.","信是三年前我父亲的兄弟约翰·爱寄来的。"],[" He lived in Madeira, had money, and wished to make me his daughter and his heir.","他住在马德拉，有一笔钱，希望收我做女儿，让我继承财产。"],[" Mrs Reed had written back that I had died at Lowood.","里德太太回信说，我已经死在洛伍德。"],[" Until that moment I had not known that anyone had looked for me.","直到这时，我才知道曾经有人找过我。"]],"translation":"舅妈认得我，却没有欢迎我。过了一阵，她让我去抽屉里找一封信。信是三年前我父亲的兄弟约翰·爱寄来的。他住在马德拉，有一笔钱，希望收我做女儿，让我继承财产。里德太太回信说，我已经死在洛伍德。直到这时，我才知道曾经有人找过我。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["I asked her to let the matter rest between us.","我求她就此放下那件事。"],[" She turned her face away, and we never came to an understanding.","她把脸转开，我们终究没能和解。"],[" She died at midnight.","午夜，她去世了。"],[" I stayed for some time to help my cousins before I went back to Thornfield.","我留下来帮了表姐妹一阵，才回桑菲尔德。"],[" During those weeks I had many chances to walk through the house where I had grown up.","那几个星期里，我有许多机会走过自己长大的那座宅子。"],[" The rooms were just as large as I remembered, but I no longer had to ask permission to leave them.","那些房间还像记忆里那么大，可要离开它们，我已经不用再求人准许了。"]],"translation":"我求她就此放下那件事。她把脸转开，我们终究没能和解。午夜，她去世了。我留下来帮了表姐妹一阵，才回桑菲尔德。那几个星期里，我有许多机会走过自己长大的那座宅子。那些房间还像记忆里那么大，可要离开它们，我已经不用再求人准许了。"}],"terms":[{"term":"ask for leave","forms":["asked Mr Rochester for leave"],"meaning":"请假、请求离开许可","usage":"leave 作休假时不可数；take leave of somebody 为较正式的告别。","example":"She asked her manager for leave to visit her family.","exampleZh":"她向经理请假去探望家人。","meaningEn":"to request formal permission to be absent or go away","usageEn":"“Leave” is uncountable here. “Ask someone for leave” names the person who can grant permission. “Take leave of someone” means to say goodbye."},{"term":"feel bound to","forms":["felt bound to"],"meaning":"觉得自己有义务……","usage":"feel bound to do 侧重责任感；be bound to happen 可指某事一定发生。","example":"I felt bound to tell her what I had seen.","exampleZh":"我觉得自己有义务把见到的事告诉她。","meaningEn":"to feel a duty or moral obligation to do something","usageEn":"Follow it with the base form of a verb. “Be bound to happen” is a different use and means that something is certain or very likely."},{"term":"dread","forms":["dreaded"],"meaning":"很怕、预想时就感到不安","usage":"常接名词或动名词；dread doing 指对未来情景怀有持续的畏惧。","example":"He dreaded returning to the empty house.","exampleZh":"他很害怕回到空荡荡的房子。","meaningEn":"to feel great fear or anxiety about something that is coming","usageEn":"Use it with a noun or an -ing form, as in “dread the visit” or “dread being left alone.”"},{"term":"heir","meaning":"继承人","usage":"heir to + 财产、头衔或王位；h 不发音，因此说 an heir。","example":"Her youngest child became heir to the estate.","exampleZh":"她最小的孩子成了庄园的继承人。","meaningEn":"a person entitled to inherit property, a title or a position","usageEn":"Use “heir to” before what may be inherited. The “h” is silent, so use “an heir.”"}],"glossary":[["messenger","送信的人"],["ask for leave","请假"],["feel bound to","觉得有义务……"],["dread","害怕；担心"],["heir","继承人"],["let the matter rest","不再追究此事"],["come to an understanding","取得谅解"]]},{"en":"Under the Chestnut Tree","zh":"栗树下","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["I had expected Thornfield to feel strange after my visit to Gateshead.","我原以为从盖茨黑德府回来后，桑菲尔德会显得陌生。"],[" Instead, as I came up the road and saw Mr Rochester waiting near the gate, I felt that I had come home.","可沿路走近，看见罗切斯特先生等在门旁时，我只觉得自己回了家。"],[" The feeling pleased me until I remembered that a marriage might soon send me away.","这感觉让我高兴，直到我想起，一场婚事可能很快就会让我离开这里。"]],"translation":"我原以为从盖茨黑德府回来后，桑菲尔德会显得陌生。可沿路走近，看见罗切斯特先生等在门旁时，我只觉得自己回了家。这感觉让我高兴，直到我想起，一场婚事可能很快就会让我离开这里。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["On a warm evening we walked in the orchard.","一个温暖的傍晚，我们在果园里散步。"],[" He told me that he had found me a new place in Ireland.","他说给我在爱尔兰找了个新职位。"],[" I tried to thank him for his care, but the thought of the sea between us made me cry.","我努力向他道谢，一想到从此隔着一片海，却忍不住落泪。"],[" He asked whether I was sorry to leave.","他问我是不是舍不得走。"],[" I told him I was.","我说是的。"],[" I had worked hard to keep my feelings to myself. Now I wanted him to understand that leaving would hurt me as deeply as it could hurt anyone.","我曾很努力地把感情藏起来，这一刻却想让他明白，离开同样会让我心痛。"],[" My money and my position had nothing to do with my right to feel.","我有没有钱、是什么身份，都与我有没有资格感受这份痛无关。"]],"translation":"一个温暖的傍晚，我们在果园里散步。他说给我在爱尔兰找了个新职位。我努力向他道谢，一想到从此隔着一片海，却忍不住落泪。他问我是不是舍不得走。我说是的。我曾很努力地把感情藏起来，这一刻却想让他明白，离开同样会让我心痛。我有没有钱、是什么身份，都与我有没有资格感受这份痛无关。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Then he asked me to marry him.","他接着向我求婚。"],[" At first I thought he was making fun of me.","起初我以为他在取笑我。"],[" What about Blanche?","布兰奇呢？"],[" He told me that he had never meant to marry her.","他说，他从没打算娶她。"],[" I looked at him for a long time before I believed him.","我望了他很久，才相信他的话。"],[" We stayed under the chestnut tree until the night broke into a storm.","我们一直待在栗树下，直到夜里下起暴雨。"],[" The next morning I learned that lightning had split the tree.","第二天一早，我得知闪电把树劈开了。"]],"translation":"他接着向我求婚。起初我以为他在取笑我。布兰奇呢？他说，他从没打算娶她。我望了他很久，才相信他的话。我们一直待在栗树下，直到夜里下起暴雨。第二天一早，我得知闪电把树劈开了。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["During the weeks that followed, he wanted to buy me silk dresses and jewels.","接下来的几周，他想给我买丝绸裙子和珠宝。"],[" I preferred my ordinary clothes and asked to go on teaching Adèle until the wedding.","我更愿意穿着平日的衣服，请他让我继续教阿黛勒，直到婚礼那天。"],[" I also wrote to my uncle in Madeira.","我也给马德拉的叔叔写了信。"],[" If he still meant to help me, I thought I might one day bring something of my own to the marriage.","我想，如果他仍愿意帮我，有一天我也能带着属于自己的东西走进这段婚姻。"]],"translation":"接下来的几周，他想给我买丝绸裙子和珠宝。我更愿意穿着平日的衣服，请他让我继续教阿黛勒，直到婚礼那天。我也给马德拉的叔叔写了信。我想，如果他仍愿意帮我，有一天我也能带着属于自己的东西走进这段婚姻。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Two nights before the wedding I woke and saw a woman I did not recognise standing over my new veil.","婚礼前两晚，我醒来看见一个不认识的女人站在我新买的面纱旁。"],[" She put it on, looked in the mirror, and tore it in two.","她戴上面纱，照了照镜子，把它撕成两半。"],[" Mr Rochester blamed Grace Poole and tried to persuade me that I had dreamed the rest.","罗切斯特先生说那是格雷斯·普尔，试图让我相信其余的情形只是一场梦。"],[" In the morning, however, the torn veil lay on the floor.","可到了早晨，撕破的面纱还在地上。"]],"translation":"婚礼前两晚，我醒来看见一个不认识的女人站在我新买的面纱旁。她戴上面纱，照了照镜子，把它撕成两半。罗切斯特先生说那是格雷斯·普尔，试图让我相信其余的情形只是一场梦。可到了早晨，撕破的面纱还在地上。"}],"terms":[{"term":"orchard","meaning":"果园","usage":"专指种果树、坚果树的园地；an apple orchard 指苹果园。","example":"They walked through the orchard after lunch.","exampleZh":"午饭后，他们穿过了果园。","meaningEn":"an area of land where fruit or nut trees are grown","usageEn":"Use the name of the fruit before the word to be specific, as in “an apple orchard.”"},{"term":"keep something to oneself","meaning":"把某事藏在心里、秘而不宣","usage":"keep news to yourself 有保密之意；keep to yourself 没有宾语时可指不爱交际。","example":"She kept the good news to herself until Friday.","exampleZh":"她把这个好消息一直保密到星期五。","forms":["keep my feelings to myself"],"meaningEn":"to avoid telling other people about a thought, feeling or piece of news","usageEn":"Include what is being kept private, as in “keep the news to yourself.” Without an object, “keep to yourself” can mean avoiding company."},{"term":"have nothing to do with","meaning":"与……无关","usage":"It has nothing to do with me 用于否认关联或责任；have something to do with 表示可能有关。","example":"The noise had nothing to do with the storm.","exampleZh":"那声响与暴风雨没有关系。","forms":["had nothing to do with"],"meaningEn":"to have no connection or involvement with something","usageEn":"It can deny a connection, a responsibility or an influence. “Have something to do with” suggests there may be a connection."},{"term":"make fun of","meaning":"取笑","usage":"of 后接被取笑的人或事；have fun with 指一起玩得开心。","example":"Please don’t make fun of the way he speaks.","exampleZh":"请别笑话他说话的方式。","forms":["making fun of"],"meaningEn":"to tease or mock someone or something","usageEn":"The target goes after “of.” “Have fun with someone” is an unrelated expression for enjoying their company."}],"glossary":[["orchard","果园"],["keep something to oneself","把某事藏在心里"],["have nothing to do with","与……无关"],["make fun of","取笑"],["chestnut tree","栗树"],["veil","面纱"],["persuade","说服"]]},{"en":"The Night Before the Wedding","zh":"婚礼前夜","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["On the last evening before the wedding, Mr Rochester was away on business. I went into the orchard to wait.","婚礼前最后一个晚上，罗切斯特先生外出办事，我到果园去等他。"],[" A cold wind was blowing, though the day had been warm.","白天还暖和，这时却吹着冷风。"],[" By the path stood the chestnut tree, still split from the storm. Its two sides had not fallen apart.","小路旁是那棵被雷劈开的栗树，两半还没有分离。"],[" I could see where they held together near the ground.","我看见它们在靠近地面的地方仍连在一起。"]],"translation":"婚礼前最后一个晚上，罗切斯特先生外出办事，我到果园去等他。白天还暖和，这时却吹着冷风。小路旁是那棵被雷劈开的栗树，两半还没有分离。我看见它们在靠近地面的地方仍连在一起。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["There was a wedding dress upstairs, but I was thinking more about the journey that was to follow.","楼上摆着婚纱，我心里想得更多的，却是婚礼后的旅程。"],[" My trunk was ready. A label with the name I was to take after the wedding lay nearby. I had not fixed it to the trunk.","行李箱已经备好，旁边有张写着婚后姓名的标签，我还没有把它贴上。"],[" It seemed too early to put the name on anything of mine.","把那个名字写在自己的东西上，似乎还太早。"],[" I had said yes to a man I loved, and I had told myself the rest would feel natural in time.","我已经答应嫁给自己爱的人，也告诉自己，其余的事迟早会变得自然。"]],"translation":"楼上摆着婚纱，我心里想得更多的，却是婚礼后的旅程。行李箱已经备好，旁边有张写着婚后姓名的标签，我还没有把它贴上。把那个名字写在自己的东西上，似乎还太早。我已经答应嫁给自己爱的人，也告诉自己，其余的事迟早会变得自然。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["When Mr Rochester returned, I told him about the woman who had torn the veil.","罗切斯特先生回来时，我把撕面纱的女人告诉了他。"],[" He asked me to sleep in Adèle’s room. He said that one day he would tell me why Grace Poole was still in the house after all the trouble she had caused.","他让我去阿黛勒的房间睡，说总有一天会告诉我，为什么格雷斯·普尔闯了这么多祸，仍能留在宅子里。"],[" He did not want to say any more that night.","那天夜里，他不肯再说下去。"],[" I could hear how tired he was, but what troubled me was that he seemed to have decided how much truth I could bear.","我听得出他疲惫，可最让我不安的是，他似乎已经替我决定了我能承受多少实情。"]],"translation":"罗切斯特先生回来时，我把撕面纱的女人告诉了他。他让我去阿黛勒的房间睡，说总有一天会告诉我，为什么格雷斯·普尔闯了这么多祸，仍能留在宅子里。那天夜里，他不肯再说下去。我听得出他疲惫，可最让我不安的是，他似乎已经替我决定了我能承受多少实情。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Adèle was asleep when I went upstairs.","我上楼时，阿黛勒已经睡着。"],[" I stood by the bed until I could see the small movement of her shoulders as she breathed.","我站在床边，看见她的肩膀随着呼吸微微起伏。"],[" I did not want to wake her to say goodbye.","我不想叫醒她来道别。"],[" We had spent a great many ordinary days together, and it was hard to believe there would be no lesson the next morning.","我们一起过了那么多平常日子，我很难相信，明天早晨就不用再上课了。"],[" I set my candle down and lay beside her until the house went still.","我放下蜡烛，在她身旁躺下，直到整座房子安静下来。"]],"translation":"我上楼时，阿黛勒已经睡着。我站在床边，看见她的肩膀随着呼吸微微起伏。我不想叫醒她来道别。我们一起过了那么多平常日子，我很难相信，明天早晨就不用再上课了。我放下蜡烛，在她身旁躺下，直到整座房子安静下来。"}],"terms":[{"term":"on business","meaning":"因公、为办事","usage":"travel on business 指出差；in business 指经营，out of business 指停业。","example":"She is in Leeds on business this week.","exampleZh":"她这周在利兹出差。","meaningEn":"for work or to deal with professional matters","usageEn":"Use “travel on business” for a work trip. “In business” describes operating a business, and “out of business” means it has shut down."},{"term":"fall apart","forms":["fallen apart"],"meaning":"裂开、散掉","usage":"实物可散架，计划或关系也可 fall apart；动词为不及物。","example":"The old suitcase fell apart on the platform.","exampleZh":"旧行李箱在站台上散了架。","meaningEn":"to break into pieces or stop holding together","usageEn":"It takes no direct object: a suitcase can fall apart. In figurative use, a plan, arrangement or relationship can also fall apart."},{"term":"trunk","meaning":"大行李箱","usage":"此处为早期旅行常用的硬质大箱；tree trunk 是树干，美语也是汽车后备厢。","example":"They put the heavy trunk at the foot of the bed.","exampleZh":"他们把沉重的大衣箱放在床尾。","meaningEn":"a large, rigid travelling chest","usageEn":"In older travel scenes, a trunk is a large container for luggage. The word also names the main stem of a tree or, in American English, the boot of a car."},{"term":"go still","forms":["went still"],"meaning":"忽然静下来、纹丝不动","usage":"go + 形容词表示状态变化，如 go quiet；still 可指身体不动，也可指环境无声。","example":"The room went still as she opened the letter.","exampleZh":"她打开信时，房间一下子静了下来。","meaningEn":"to suddenly stop moving or making noise","usageEn":"“Go” plus an adjective describes a change of state. Whether “still” refers to motion or sound depends on the subject and scene."}],"glossary":[["on business","因公办事"],["fall apart","裂开；散开"],["trunk","大行李箱"],["fix something to","把某物贴上或固定在……上"],["veil","面纱"],["bear","承受"],["go still","变得安静"]]},{"en":"The Wedding That Stopped","zh":"中断的婚礼","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["We reached the church early.","我们很早就到了教堂。"],[" As the clergyman began the service, a man stepped forward and said there was a legal reason why the wedding could not go ahead.","牧师刚开始主持仪式，一个男人走上前，说有法律上的理由，婚礼不能继续。"],[" He was a lawyer, Mr Briggs.","他是布里格斯律师。"],[" Mr Rochester already had a wife who was still alive.","罗切斯特先生已有一位仍然在世的妻子。"],[" Richard Mason, standing beside the lawyer, said that she was his sister. Her name was Bertha Mason.","站在律师身旁的理查德·梅森说，那是他的姐姐，名叫伯莎·梅森。"]],"translation":"我们很早就到了教堂。牧师刚开始主持仪式，一个男人走上前，说有法律上的理由，婚礼不能继续。他是布里格斯律师。罗切斯特先生已有一位仍然在世的妻子。站在律师身旁的理查德·梅森说，那是他的姐姐，名叫伯莎·梅森。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Mr Rochester did not deny it.","罗切斯特先生没有否认。"],[" He led us back to Thornfield and up to the rooms I had never been allowed to enter.","他带我们回桑菲尔德，上楼走进那些我从未获准进入的房间。"],[" Grace Poole was there. So was Bertha, the woman who had torn my veil.","格雷斯·普尔在那里，伯莎也在那里。她就是撕破我面纱的女人。"],[" I understood at last who had set the fire and injured Mason.","我终于明白，是谁放了火，又是谁伤了梅森。"],[" For years, Bertha had been kept in those rooms under Grace’s care.","多年来，伯莎一直被安置在这些房间里，由格雷斯看护。"],[" Now I had seen for myself that the marriage in the church could never have been lawful.","如今我亲眼看见，教堂里的那场婚礼绝不可能合法。"]],"translation":"罗切斯特先生没有否认。他带我们回桑菲尔德，上楼走进那些我从未获准进入的房间。格雷斯·普尔在那里，伯莎也在那里。她就是撕破我面纱的女人。我终于明白，是谁放了火，又是谁伤了梅森。多年来，伯莎一直被安置在这些房间里，由格雷斯看护。如今我亲眼看见，教堂里的那场婚礼绝不可能合法。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Later Mr Rochester told me how the marriage had been arranged when he was young and living in Jamaica.","后来，罗切斯特告诉我，他年轻时在牙买加，这门婚事是别人安排的。"],[" He said he had not known what their life together would be like.","他说，当时他并不知道婚后会过怎样的生活。"],[" He wanted me to go abroad with him and live as his wife.","他想带我去国外，让我像他的妻子一样与他同住。"],[" He begged me to think of the home we could have.","他求我想想我们本来可以有的家。"],[" I could picture it so clearly that, for a while, my desire to stay frightened me more than the thought of leaving.","我几乎能清楚地看见那个家。有一阵子，我想留下的念头，比离开的念头更让我害怕。"]],"translation":"后来，罗切斯特告诉我，他年轻时在牙买加，这门婚事是别人安排的。他说，当时他并不知道婚后会过怎样的生活。他想带我去国外，让我像他的妻子一样与他同住。他求我想想我们本来可以有的家。我几乎能清楚地看见那个家。有一阵子，我想留下的念头，比离开的念头更让我害怕。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["I forgave him in my heart, but I knew I could not go with him.","我在心里原谅了他，却知道不能跟他走。"],[" He had let me make a promise without telling me what it meant.","他让我许下承诺，却没有告诉我那个承诺意味着什么。"],[" If I stayed, I would soon be asking him to decide for both of us again.","如果留下，我恐怕很快又会让他替我们两人作决定。"],[" I wanted to be able to look back on my choice without shame, even if nobody else ever knew what I had chosen.","我希望将来回想起自己的选择时，能无愧于心，即使永远没有旁人知道我选了什么。"]],"translation":"我在心里原谅了他，却知道不能跟他走。他让我许下承诺，却没有告诉我那个承诺意味着什么。如果留下，我恐怕很快又会让他替我们两人作决定。我希望将来回想起自己的选择时，能无愧于心，即使永远没有旁人知道我选了什么。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Before dawn, while the house was quiet, I put a few things in a bundle and went out.","天亮以前，屋里一片寂静。我把几件东西包起来，走了出去。"],[" On the steps I listened for a voice behind me.","在台阶上，我停下来听身后是否有人叫我。"],[" There was none.","没有。"],[" Then I walked to the road.","于是我朝大路走去。"]],"translation":"天亮以前，屋里一片寂静。我把几件东西包起来，走了出去。在台阶上，我停下来听身后是否有人叫我。没有。于是我朝大路走去。"}],"terms":[{"term":"clergyman","meaning":"教会牧师","usage":"历史语境中 clergyman 指男性教士；member of the clergy 不规定性别。","example":"A clergyman was waiting inside the church.","exampleZh":"教堂里有位牧师在等候。","meaningEn":"a male member of the Christian clergy","usageEn":"The word is common in older fiction. “Member of the clergy” can refer to a person of any gender."},{"term":"step forward","forms":["stepped forward"],"meaning":"走上前、主动站出来","usage":"字面上可以迈前一步，也可说 step forward to help，表示主动帮忙。","example":"A witness stepped forward to speak.","exampleZh":"一名目击者主动站出来发言。","meaningEn":"to move in front of others or volunteer to act","usageEn":"The movement can be literal. “Step forward to help” or “a witness stepped forward” usually emphasises willingness to get involved."},{"term":"go ahead","meaning":"继续进行、照原计划做","usage":"go ahead with + 计划；口语单用 Go ahead 表示请便或许可。","example":"The meeting went ahead despite the snow.","exampleZh":"尽管下了雪，会议仍照常进行。","meaningEn":"to proceed with what was planned","usageEn":"Use “go ahead with” before a plan or activity. “Go ahead” on its own can also give someone permission to do something."},{"term":"lawful","meaning":"法律上有效、符合法律的","usage":"常用于 lawful marriage、lawful authority；lawful 强调有法律依据。","example":"The court had to decide who the lawful owner was.","exampleZh":"法院必须判定谁是合法所有人。","meaningEn":"permitted or recognised as valid under the law","usageEn":"Often used in legal expressions such as “lawful marriage,” “lawful owner” or “lawful authority.”"}],"glossary":[["clergyman","牧师"],["step forward","走上前"],["go ahead","继续进行"],["deny","否认"],["lawful","合法的"],["go abroad","出国"],["dawn","黎明"],["bundle","包裹"]]},{"en":"A Door in the Dark","zh":"黑暗中的一扇门","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["I took a coach as far as my money would carry me.","我搭上一辆马车，把剩下的钱全付了车费。"],[" When it drove away, I discovered that my bundle had gone with it.","车驶走后，我才发现包裹也落在了车上。"],[" I stood where several roads met, with no idea which one to take.","我站在几条路的交会处，不知道该往哪儿走。"],[" For two days I walked from one place to another, asking for work and sometimes for food.","两天里，我从一个地方走到另一个地方，求人给我一份工作，有时也讨一点吃的。"],[" People did not know me.","没人认识我。"],[" A woman at a shop refused to let me stay, and I spent a night out on the moor.","一个店里的女人不肯让我留下，我只好在荒野上过了一夜。"]],"translation":"我搭上一辆马车，把剩下的钱全付了车费。车驶走后，我才发现包裹也落在了车上。我站在几条路的交会处，不知道该往哪儿走。两天里，我从一个地方走到另一个地方，求人给我一份工作，有时也讨一点吃的。没人认识我。一个店里的女人不肯让我留下，我只好在荒野上过了一夜。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["On the third evening I saw a light in a house among the trees.","第三天傍晚，我看见树林里一户人家亮着灯。"],[" Through the window I watched two young women reading at a table.","隔着玻璃，我看见两个年轻女子坐在桌边读书。"],[" The housekeeper came to the door but would not let me in.","女管家来到门口，却不肯让我进去。"],[" I had almost stopped asking by then.","到那时，我几乎连请求的力气都没有了。"],[" I sank down outside and thought I might die there.","我倒在门外，以为自己可能就要死在那里。"],[" The women’s brother, St John Rivers, found me and carried me inside.","她们的哥哥圣约翰·里弗斯发现了我，把我抱进屋。"],[" When they asked my name, I called myself Jane Elliott.","她们问我叫什么，我说我叫简·埃利奥特。"],[" I was afraid Mr Rochester might find me.","我怕罗切斯特先生找到我。"]],"translation":"第三天傍晚，我看见树林里一户人家亮着灯。隔着玻璃，我看见两个年轻女子坐在桌边读书。女管家来到门口，却不肯让我进去。到那时，我几乎连请求的力气都没有了。我倒在门外，以为自己可能就要死在那里。她们的哥哥圣约翰·里弗斯发现了我，把我抱进屋。她们问我叫什么，我说我叫简·埃利奥特。我怕罗切斯特先生找到我。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["The sisters, Diana and Mary, talked to me as if I were already their friend.","黛安娜和玛丽把我当作老朋友一样说话。"],[" While I recovered, they lent me books and let me help with small things about the house.","养身体时，她们借书给我，也让我帮着做点家务。"],[" Their brother spoke less and had plans of his own.","她们的哥哥话少，有自己的打算。"],[" He meant to go to India as a missionary.","他想去印度传教。"],[" When he heard I needed work, he offered me a place teaching in a village school for girls at Morton.","听说我需要工作，他给我在莫顿乡村女校安排了一个教书的职位。"]],"translation":"黛安娜和玛丽把我当作老朋友一样说话。养身体时，她们借书给我，也让我帮着做点家务。她们的哥哥话少，有自己的打算。他想去印度传教。听说我需要工作，他给我在莫顿乡村女校安排了一个教书的职位。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["My new home was a little cottage beside the school.","我的新家是学校旁的一间小屋。"],[" Some of the girls knew their letters and some had never held a pencil.","有的女孩认得字母，有的连铅笔也没握过。"],[" It took me time to understand how much they were being asked to learn all at once.","我过了一阵才明白，她们一下子要学的东西有多少。"],[" On the first evening, after I shut the door and made my supper, the room seemed very quiet.","第一天晚上，我关上门做好晚饭，觉得屋里异常安静。"],[" I missed Thornfield so badly that I could scarcely eat.","我太想念桑菲尔德，几乎吃不下饭。"],[" The next morning there were girls waiting outside for me.","第二天早上，有女孩在外面等我。"],[" I opened the school.","我打开了校门。"]],"translation":"我的新家是学校旁的一间小屋。有的女孩认得字母，有的连铅笔也没握过。我过了一阵才明白，她们一下子要学的东西有多少。第一天晚上，我关上门做好晚饭，觉得屋里异常安静。我太想念桑菲尔德，几乎吃不下饭。第二天早上，有女孩在外面等我。我打开了校门。"}],"terms":[{"term":"coach","meaning":"长途马车","usage":"小说时代通常指马拉客车；现代英式英语可指长途客车，美语常指教练。","example":"A coach carried them across the county.","exampleZh":"一辆长途马车载着他们穿过全郡。","meaningEn":"a horse-drawn passenger carriage for long journeys","usageEn":"In the novel’s setting this is a form of transport. Modern British English can use “coach” for a long-distance bus, while a different sense is a sports trainer."},{"term":"moor","meaning":"荒原、旷野","usage":"unfenced moor 常指开阔、树少的高地；动词 moor a boat 则是把船系住。","example":"Mist settled over the moor in the evening.","exampleZh":"傍晚，薄雾笼罩了荒原。","meaningEn":"an open stretch of uncultivated upland with few trees","usageEn":"“Across the moor” describes a route through that landscape. As a verb, “moor a boat” means to secure the boat in place."},{"term":"sink down","forms":["sank down"],"meaning":"无力地坐下、倒下","usage":"sink/sank/sunk；sink down onto the floor 强调身体向下沉落的动作。","example":"Tired from walking, he sank down onto the bench.","exampleZh":"他走得累了，一屁股坐到长椅上。","meaningEn":"to lower oneself heavily or weakly into a seat or onto the ground","usageEn":"The past tense is “sank down.” Add “onto” to name the surface reached, as in “sank down onto the bench.”"},{"term":"know one’s letters","forms":["knew their letters"],"meaning":"认识字母","usage":"letters 在这类旧式教育语境指字母；learn one's letters 是开始识字。","example":"At five she already knew her letters.","exampleZh":"她五岁就认得字母了。","meaningEn":"to be able to recognise the letters of the alphabet","usageEn":"In this older educational expression, “letters” are alphabet characters. “Learn one’s letters” describes starting to acquire that skill."}],"glossary":[["coach","长途马车"],["moor","荒野；荒原"],["housekeeper","女管家"],["sink down","无力地倒下或坐下"],["recover","恢复健康"],["missionary","传教士"],["cottage","小屋"],["know one’s letters","认得字母"]]},{"en":"Bread at Moor House","zh":"荒原屋里的面包","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Before I began teaching at Morton, I had spent some days recovering at Moor House.","去莫顿教书前，我在荒原屋养了几天身体。"],[" The first morning I felt strong enough to go downstairs, there was a smell of bread in the passage.","第一天早晨，我觉得有力气下楼了，走廊里飘来面包香。"],[" Hannah, the woman who had turned me away, was at the table with flour on her hands.","那晚把我拒之门外的汉娜正在桌边忙，手上沾着面粉。"],[" She said I ought to be in bed.","她说我该在床上躺着。"],[" I sat down and told her I could not forget what it had been like to stand outside her door.","我坐下来，告诉她，我忘不了站在她门外的感觉。"]],"translation":"去莫顿教书前，我在荒原屋养了几天身体。第一天早晨，我觉得有力气下楼了，走廊里飘来面包香。那晚把我拒之门外的汉娜正在桌边忙，手上沾着面粉。她说我该在床上躺着。我坐下来，告诉她，我忘不了站在她门外的感觉。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["She had thought I was a beggar.","她当时以为我是乞丐。"],[" I asked her why that would have made it right to leave me out in the weather.","我问她，就算我是，难道就该把我留在外面挨冻吗？"],[" She was quiet for a moment and then said she had been wrong.","她沉默片刻，承认自己错了。"],[" I could think of people who would sooner have called me ungrateful than admitted so much.","我认识有些人，宁愿骂我忘恩负义，也不肯承认这么多。"],[" After that, we found it easier to talk.","从那以后，我们说话容易多了。"],[" She told me that the sisters had come home after their father died.","她告诉我，姐妹俩是父亲去世后才回来的。"],[" Their family had once been better off, but he had lost much of his money in business.","这个家过去宽裕得多，可她们父亲做生意亏掉了大部分钱。"],[" Diana and Mary had earned a living by teaching in other people’s houses, as I had.","黛安娜和玛丽都曾到别人家教书谋生，和我一样。"]],"translation":"她当时以为我是乞丐。我问她，就算我是，难道就该把我留在外面挨冻吗？她沉默片刻，承认自己错了。我认识有些人，宁愿骂我忘恩负义，也不肯承认这么多。从那以后，我们说话容易多了。她告诉我，姐妹俩是父亲去世后才回来的。这个家过去宽裕得多，可她们父亲做生意亏掉了大部分钱。黛安娜和玛丽都曾到别人家教书谋生，和我一样。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["It was good to talk to women who understood the kind of work I had done.","能同明白我做过什么工作的人说话，很好。"],[" Mary and I liked to read the same books.","我和玛丽喜欢同样的书。"],[" Diana could put a question so clearly that I always wanted to answer it.","黛安娜把问题问得很清楚，总让我想回答。"],[" They did not insist that I tell them where I had come from.","她们没有执意追问我从哪里来。"],[" I began to tell them what I could, which was more than I could have said at first.","我渐渐肯讲一些能讲的事，比刚来时能说的多。"]],"translation":"能同明白我做过什么工作的人说话，很好。我和玛丽喜欢同样的书。黛安娜把问题问得很清楚，总让我想回答。她们没有执意追问我从哪里来。我渐渐肯讲一些能讲的事，比刚来时能说的多。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Their own money would not last forever.","她们的钱也不会永远够用。"],[" They were preparing to go back to their employers, and I had no wish to live on their kindness.","两人正准备回各自的雇主家，我也不愿一直靠她们的好意生活。"],[" When St John could offer me work at Morton, I was grateful for the smallness of what he asked me to do.","圣约翰在莫顿给我找来工作时，我很感激那是一件小事。"],[" I could begin with something I knew.","我可以从自己懂的事情做起。"]],"translation":"她们的钱也不会永远够用。两人正准备回各自的雇主家，我也不愿一直靠她们的好意生活。圣约翰在莫顿给我找来工作时，我很感激那是一件小事。我可以从自己懂的事情做起。"}],"terms":[{"term":"turn someone away","forms":["turned me away"],"meaning":"拒绝让某人进来、不予接待","usage":"turn somebody away 的对象是来访者、求助者等；turn away 也可只指转脸。","example":"The shelter never turned a hungry traveller away.","exampleZh":"那间收容所从未把挨饿的旅人拒之门外。","meaningEn":"to refuse someone entry or refuse to help them when they arrive","usageEn":"Separate “turn” and “away” with the person. With no object, “turn away” can simply describe turning your face or body elsewhere."},{"term":"better off","meaning":"境况较好、手头较宽裕","usage":"通常接 be；better off doing... 则表示做某事对自己更有利。","example":"The family was better off after she found steady work.","exampleZh":"她找到稳定工作后，家里的境况好些了。","meaningEn":"in a better situation, often with more money or security","usageEn":"“Be better off” describes a relative improvement. “Be better off doing something” recommends an option as more beneficial."},{"term":"earn a living","meaning":"谋生","usage":"earn a living as + 职业，by + 动名词说明谋生方式。","example":"He earned a living by repairing shoes.","exampleZh":"他靠修鞋谋生。","forms":["earned a living"],"meaningEn":"to make enough money to support oneself","usageEn":"Add “as” for an occupation or “by” plus an -ing form for the method of making money."},{"term":"live on","meaning":"靠……生活","usage":"live on a small income 指以收入维生；live on bread and tea 指饮食仅靠这些。","example":"They lived on what they could grow in the garden.","exampleZh":"他们靠菜园里种出来的东西生活。","meaningEn":"to survive or support oneself on a given income or food","usageEn":"Use it with income such as “a small pension,” or with a limited diet such as “bread and tea.”"}],"glossary":[["turn someone away","把某人拒之门外"],["beggar","乞丐"],["ungrateful","不知感激的"],["better off","经济状况更好的"],["earn a living","谋生"],["insist","坚持要求"],["live on","靠……生活"]]},{"en":"Rosamond’s Portrait","zh":"罗莎蒙德的肖像","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Not all the girls at Morton found school easy, but I soon learned that the quietest child could sometimes make the best use of a lesson.","莫顿的女孩并非个个都觉得读书容易，不过我很快发现，最安静的孩子，有时反而最能从一堂课里学到东西。"],[" One girl who had hardly spoken in the first week stayed behind to show me the letters she had copied.","有个女孩第一周几乎没说几句话，放学后却留下来让我看她抄的字母。"],[" She had written the same word at home, on a piece of wood, to make sure she could do it without my help.","她回家还在一块木头上写了同一个词，要确认不用我帮忙也能写出来。"],[" I thought of her that evening when I sat down to draw.","那晚我坐下画画时想起了她。"],[" There was satisfaction in being able to do one thing well.","能把一件事做好，本身就让人满足。"]],"translation":"莫顿的女孩并非个个都觉得读书容易，不过我很快发现，最安静的孩子，有时反而最能从一堂课里学到东西。有个女孩第一周几乎没说几句话，放学后却留下来让我看她抄的字母。她回家还在一块木头上写了同一个词，要确认不用我帮忙也能写出来。那晚我坐下画画时想起了她。能把一件事做好，本身就让人满足。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Rosamond Oliver often came to the school.","罗莎蒙德·奥利弗常到学校来。"],[" Her father was wealthy and had helped to provide my cottage.","她父亲有钱，帮忙为我安排了那间小屋。"],[" She would arrive on her pony with something to say that made the girls laugh.","她骑着小马来到学校，总有些话能逗女孩们笑。"],[" When St John happened to be there, she spoke most readily to him.","圣约翰偶尔在场时，她最乐意同他说话。"],[" He answered with care, as if a warmer word might give something away.","他回答得很谨慎，仿佛语气再亲切一点，就会泄露心事。"]],"translation":"罗莎蒙德·奥利弗常到学校来。她父亲有钱，帮忙为我安排了那间小屋。她骑着小马来到学校，总有些话能逗女孩们笑。圣约翰偶尔在场时，她最乐意同他说话。他回答得很谨慎，仿佛语气再亲切一点，就会泄露心事。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["One day she asked me to paint her portrait.","一天，她请我为她画肖像。"],[" St John came in while I was finishing it.","快画完时，圣约翰来了。"],[" He took the picture in his hands and looked at it for a long time.","他把画拿在手里看了很久。"],[" I offered to make him another. Then I went a step further and asked why he did not marry her, since she seemed to care for him.","我提出可以再画一幅给他，又多问了一步：既然她似乎在意他，为什么不娶她呢？"],[" He said that he loved her. He also said she would not want the life he meant to lead.","他说，他爱她，也说她不会喜欢他打算过的生活。"],[" He was going to India, and there were things he would not give up to be happy at home.","他要去印度。有些事，他不会为了留在家中过得幸福而放弃。"]],"translation":"一天，她请我为她画肖像。快画完时，圣约翰来了。他把画拿在手里看了很久。我提出可以再画一幅给他，又多问了一步：既然她似乎在意他，为什么不娶她呢？他说，他爱她，也说她不会喜欢他打算过的生活。他要去印度。有些事，他不会为了留在家中过得幸福而放弃。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["When he put the drawing down, he noticed a scrap of paper beneath it. He tore off a corner and took it away.","放下画时，他留意到下面有片纸，撕下一角带走了。"],[" I supposed he had found something useful to him. I had no idea what I had written there.","我猜他找到了什么对自己有用的东西，却一点也想不起自己在上面写过什么。"]],"translation":"放下画时，他留意到下面有片纸，撕下一角带走了。我猜他找到了什么对自己有用的东西，却一点也想不起自己在上面写过什么。"}],"terms":[{"term":"stay behind","forms":["stayed behind"],"meaning":"别人离开后留下","usage":"可接 after 或 to do，说明留下的时间和目的；leave behind 则指撇下人或忘带东西。","example":"Two students stayed behind to stack the chairs.","exampleZh":"两个学生留下来把椅子叠好。","meaningEn":"to remain after other people have left","usageEn":"Add “to” and a verb to explain the purpose. “Leave someone behind” presents the event from the point of view of the person who goes."},{"term":"happen to","forms":["happened to"],"meaning":"碰巧……","usage":"happen to do 引出偶然行为；happen to somebody 则表示发生在某人身上。","example":"I happened to see her at the station.","exampleZh":"我碰巧在车站看见她。","meaningEn":"to do something by chance","usageEn":"“Happen to” plus a verb describes an accidental event. In “what happened to her,” the person after “to” is instead affected by what took place."},{"term":"readily","meaning":"爽快地、毫不犹豫地","usage":"readily agree 表示欣然同意；readily available 指随时容易取得。","example":"The shopkeeper readily agreed to keep my bag.","exampleZh":"店主爽快地答应替我保管包。","meaningEn":"willingly and without hesitation","usageEn":"“Readily agree” highlights willingness. “Readily available” uses another sense and means easy to obtain."},{"term":"go a step further","forms":["went a step further"],"meaning":"更进一步","usage":"可用于进一步推论、追问或采取行动；take things a step further 也常见。","example":"She went a step further and tested the idea herself.","exampleZh":"她又进一步，亲自验证了这个想法。","meaningEn":"to extend an action, question or argument beyond what came before","usageEn":"Useful when introducing an additional action or stronger conclusion. “Take things a step further” is another common form."}],"glossary":[["stay behind","在别人走后留下"],["satisfaction","满足感"],["happen to","碰巧……"],["readily","乐意地；自然地"],["give something away","无意中泄露某事"],["go a step further","再进一步"],["beneath","在……下面"]]},{"en":"An Unexpected Family","zh":"意外找到的家人","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Life at Morton took on a pleasant order.","莫顿的日子渐渐有了让我喜欢的节奏。"],[" I knew the girls better now, and their parents stopped me in the lane to talk.","我更了解孩子们了，她们的父母也会在小路上停下来和我说话。"],[" At night I drew or read by the fire.","晚上，我在炉火边画画或读书。"],[" One evening St John came in through a snowstorm.","一天夜里，圣约翰冒着风雪来找我。"],[" Instead of speaking about the school, he began to tell a story about a governess named Jane Eyre, who had disappeared from Thornfield.","他没说学校的事，却讲起一个叫简·爱的家庭女教师，说她从桑菲尔德失踪了。"],[" I set down the book I was holding.","我放下手里的书。"]],"translation":"莫顿的日子渐渐有了让我喜欢的节奏。我更了解孩子们了，她们的父母也会在小路上停下来和我说话。晚上，我在炉火边画画或读书。一天夜里，圣约翰冒着风雪来找我。他没说学校的事，却讲起一个叫简·爱的家庭女教师，说她从桑菲尔德失踪了。我放下手里的书。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["He had seen my real name on a scrap of paper I had used for a drawing.","他在我画画时用过的一张纸片上看到了我的真名。"],[" A lawyer was looking for me, he said.","他说，有律师正在找我。"],[" My uncle in Madeira had died and left me twenty thousand pounds.","我在马德拉的叔叔去世了，给我留下两万英镑。"],[" When I asked why the lawyer had thought to write to him, St John told me something I had never expected to hear.","我问律师为什么会想到写信给他，他告诉我一件从没料到的事。"],[" John Eyre had been his uncle too.","约翰·爱也是他的舅舅。"],[" Diana, Mary, and St John were my cousins.","黛安娜、玛丽和圣约翰是我的表亲。"]],"translation":"他在我画画时用过的一张纸片上看到了我的真名。他说，有律师正在找我。我在马德拉的叔叔去世了，给我留下两万英镑。我问律师为什么会想到写信给他，他告诉我一件从没料到的事。约翰·爱也是他的舅舅。黛安娜、玛丽和圣约翰是我的表亲。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["St John thought I would need time to get used to being rich.","圣约翰以为我需要时间适应自己成了有钱人。"],[" I was busy thinking how I could divide the money.","我却正忙着想怎么分这笔钱。"],[" I did not need twenty thousand pounds, but I did need people I could count as my family.","我不需要两万英镑，但我需要能视为家人的人。"],[" Five thousand pounds each would give us all a choice about how to live.","四个人每人五千英镑，都能多一点选择自己生活的余地。"],[" St John argued that my uncle had intended the whole sum for me.","圣约翰说，叔叔原本打算把整笔钱留给我。"],[" I told him the choice was mine now.","我告诉他，如今我可以决定怎么用。"],[" In the end, he agreed.","最后他同意了。"]],"translation":"圣约翰以为我需要时间适应自己成了有钱人。我却正忙着想怎么分这笔钱。我不需要两万英镑，但我需要能视为家人的人。四个人每人五千英镑，都能多一点选择自己生活的余地。圣约翰说，叔叔原本打算把整笔钱留给我。我告诉他，如今我可以决定怎么用。最后他同意了。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["When the school closed for Christmas, I got Moor House ready for Diana and Mary to return.","学校放圣诞假后，我把荒原屋收拾妥当，等黛安娜和玛丽回来。"],[" I had chosen my work before, but this was the first home I had ever had a hand in making for myself.","以前我也选过自己的工作，但这是我头一次有机会亲手为自己安置一个家。"],[" I could hear my cousins’ voices in the rooms and knew that nobody had the right to send me away.","我听得见表亲们在各个房间里说话，也知道谁都没有权利赶我走。"]],"translation":"学校放圣诞假后，我把荒原屋收拾妥当，等黛安娜和玛丽回来。以前我也选过自己的工作，但这是我头一次有机会亲手为自己安置一个家。我听得见表亲们在各个房间里说话，也知道谁都没有权利赶我走。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["St John was glad that we were together, though he spent little time resting with us.","圣约翰为我们团聚而高兴，但很少留在家里与我们一起休息。"],[" India was still on his mind.","他心里始终想着印度。"],[" Before long he asked me to help him with his plans.","不久，他问我愿不愿意参与他的计划。"]],"translation":"圣约翰为我们团聚而高兴，但很少留在家里与我们一起休息。他心里始终想着印度。不久，他问我愿不愿意参与他的计划。"}],"terms":[{"term":"take on","forms":["took on"],"meaning":"呈现出、开始具有","usage":"take on a new meaning 即开始有新的含义；take on new work 则指承担新工作。","example":"His words took on a different meaning after the news.","exampleZh":"消息传来后，他的话有了另一层意思。","meaningEn":"to begin to have a new quality, appearance or meaning","usageEn":"“Take on a different meaning” signals a change in how something is understood. With a task or responsibility, “take on” means to agree to do it."},{"term":"scrap of paper","meaning":"一小片纸、纸条","usage":"scrap of 强调零碎小片，也可比喻 a scrap of evidence（一点证据）。","example":"He wrote the address on a scrap of paper.","exampleZh":"他在一小片纸上写了地址。","meaningEn":"a small irregular piece of paper","usageEn":"“Scrap of” often names a small leftover piece. It can also describe tiny amounts of something abstract, as in “a scrap of evidence.”"},{"term":"count as","meaning":"算作、视为","usage":"可用 something counts as...，也可用 count something as... 表示判定。","example":"A late arrival may count as an absence.","exampleZh":"迟到可能按缺席计算。","meaningEn":"to be regarded or treated as a particular thing","usageEn":"Use “A counts as B” for the judgment. “Count A as B” gives the same judgment with a person or rule doing the classifying."},{"term":"have a hand in","forms":["had a hand in"],"meaning":"参与、出一份力","usage":"in 后接名词或动名词；有时委婉暗示与某个问题有牵连。","example":"Several neighbours had a hand in building the bridge.","exampleZh":"好几位邻居参与了搭桥。","meaningEn":"to take part in or help bring about something","usageEn":"Use “in” with a noun or an -ing form. Depending on the context, the expression can imply responsibility for a difficulty as well as credit for success."}],"glossary":[["take on","呈现；形成"],["scrap of paper","一小片纸"],["divide","分配"],["count as","视为"],["intend something for","打算把某物给某人"],["have a hand in","参与；出一份力"]]},{"en":"Christmas at Moor House","zh":"荒原屋的圣诞节","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Hannah and I had work to do before Diana and Mary came home.","黛安娜和玛丽回来前，汉娜和我有不少事要忙。"],[" We moved furniture, put down carpets and hung curtains in the spare rooms.","我们挪家具、铺地毯，给空房间挂上窗帘。"],[" In the middle of it all, I kept finding things that had belonged to people I was only now beginning to think of as my relations.","我一边收拾，一边不断找到一些东西，原来的主人是我直到现在才开始当作亲人看待的人。"],[" I put what I could back where it belonged.","能放回原处的，我尽量放回去。"],[" It felt good to be preparing a home that other people would be glad to come back to.","为别人收拾好一个他们愿意回来的家，感觉很好。"]],"translation":"黛安娜和玛丽回来前，汉娜和我有不少事要忙。我们挪家具、铺地毯，给空房间挂上窗帘。我一边收拾，一边不断找到一些东西，原来的主人是我直到现在才开始当作亲人看待的人。能放回原处的，我尽量放回去。为别人收拾好一个他们愿意回来的家，感觉很好。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["When the sisters arrived, it was cold outside.","姐妹俩到家时，外面很冷。"],[" They had scarcely got through the door before Hannah was talking and the dog was trying to reach both of them at once.","两人还没完全进门，汉娜已经说起话来，狗也想同时凑到两个人身边。"],[" I had spent many years in places where a child or an employee was expected to know when to keep out of the way.","许多年来，我住过的地方总要求小孩或雇员识趣，知道什么时候该避开。"],[" Here there was no reason to go upstairs until I was tired, and no reason to be quiet when I was pleased.","这里，累了才用上楼，高兴时也不必硬把声音压低。"]],"translation":"姐妹俩到家时，外面很冷。两人还没完全进门，汉娜已经说起话来，狗也想同时凑到两个人身边。许多年来，我住过的地方总要求小孩或雇员识趣，知道什么时候该避开。这里，累了才用上楼，高兴时也不必硬把声音压低。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["A boy came later that evening.","那天晚些时候来了个男孩。"],[" His mother was ill and had asked for St John.","他的母亲病了，想请圣约翰过去。"],[" The way to their house lay over several miles of bad ground.","去他们家的路有好几英里，而且不好走。"],[" Hannah warned him about the weather, but he went without waiting to finish his meal.","汉娜劝他留意天气，他却连饭也没吃完就走了。"],[" When he came back, he was wet and hungry, and looked more at peace than he had looked when we were all sitting together.","回来时，他又湿又饿，神情却比我们围坐在一起时更安宁。"]],"translation":"那天晚些时候来了个男孩。他的母亲病了，想请圣约翰过去。去他们家的路有好几英里，而且不好走。汉娜劝他留意天气，他却连饭也没吃完就走了。回来时，他又湿又饿，神情却比我们围坐在一起时更安宁。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["I thought of this during the rest of the holiday.","假期剩下的日子里，我一直想着这件事。"],[" My cousins and I were happy reading, talking and walking on the moor.","我和表亲们读书、聊天，到荒原上散步，过得很愉快。"],[" Our happiness gave St John little pleasure, yet when someone needed help he could go where few others would go. I admired him for that. I also began to see why it would be hard to ask him to share the kind of life I wanted.","这些事给不了圣约翰多少快乐。可一旦有人需要帮助，他就能去别人往往不肯去的地方。我敬佩他这一点，也渐渐看明白，为什么很难请他与我过同一种生活。"]],"translation":"假期剩下的日子里，我一直想着这件事。我和表亲们读书、聊天，到荒原上散步，过得很愉快。这些事给不了圣约翰多少快乐。可一旦有人需要帮助，他就能去别人往往不肯去的地方。我敬佩他这一点，也渐渐看明白，为什么很难请他与我过同一种生活。"}],"terms":[{"term":"spare room","meaning":"空房、客房","usage":"spare 指目前没有固定用途、可以腾出来；room to spare 则表示还绰绰有余。","example":"My aunt offered me her spare room for the night.","exampleZh":"姑妈让我在她的空房里过一夜。","forms":["spare rooms"],"meaningEn":"an extra room available for occasional use, often for guests","usageEn":"“Spare” means the room is not otherwise needed. “Room to spare” means there is more space than necessary."},{"term":"at once","meaning":"立刻；同时","usage":"时间命令 Come at once 用立刻义；all at once 可指突然，也可表示一齐。","example":"Three people began talking at once.","exampleZh":"三个人同时开口说话。","meaningEn":"immediately, or at the same time","usageEn":"An instruction such as “come at once” means immediately. With several people or actions, “at once” can mean simultaneously."},{"term":"keep out of the way","meaning":"避开、不碍事","usage":"keep out of someone's way 可因礼貌或怕惹麻烦而回避；get out of the way 强调让开这一动作。","example":"We kept out of the way while they moved the piano.","exampleZh":"他们搬钢琴时，我们躲到一边没挡路。","meaningEn":"to stay where you will not obstruct or disturb someone","usageEn":"“Keep out of someone’s way” can also mean avoid contact. “Get out of the way” focuses on the moment you move aside."},{"term":"at peace","meaning":"安宁、内心平静","usage":"be at peace with oneself 指心安；两国 at peace 指没有交战。","example":"For the first time in months she felt at peace.","exampleZh":"几个月来，她第一次感到内心平静。","meaningEn":"calm and free from inner conflict or distress","usageEn":"“At peace with oneself” describes acceptance or calm. Countries can also be “at peace” when they are not fighting."}],"glossary":[["spare room","空余的房间；客房"],["put down a carpet","铺地毯"],["at once","同时；立刻"],["keep out of the way","避开；不挡路"],["lie over","（道路）穿过"],["warn someone about","提醒某人当心……"],["at peace","安宁的；平静的"]]},{"en":"Letters without Answers","zh":"没有回音的信","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Money made it possible for me to send a letter without wondering whether I could afford the postage.","有了钱，我寄信时再也不用盘算付不付得起邮资。"],[" It did not make anyone answer it.","但钱没法让人回信。"],[" I wrote to Mrs Fairfax to ask about Thornfield.","我写信给费尔法克斯太太，打听桑菲尔德的情况。"],[" I waited for news and then wrote again.","等了一阵消息，又写了一封。"],[" On the evenings when Diana and Mary were busy with their own work, I could still find myself listening for someone at the door, although it was too late for the post.","有些晚上，黛安娜和玛丽各忙各的，我还会忍不住留神有没有人敲门，虽然送信的人早就不会来了。"]],"translation":"有了钱，我寄信时再也不用盘算付不付得起邮资。但钱没法让人回信。我写信给费尔法克斯太太，打听桑菲尔德的情况。等了一阵消息，又写了一封。有些晚上，黛安娜和玛丽各忙各的，我还会忍不住留神有没有人敲门，虽然送信的人早就不会来了。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["St John noticed how long I could sit at a task.","圣约翰注意到，我在一件事上能坐很久。"],[" He asked me to leave my German for a while and study the language he would need in India. Teaching me would help him remember what he had learnt, he said.","他请我暂时放下德语，学他到印度要用的语言，说教我也能帮他温习已经学过的东西。"],[" It seemed a reasonable favour to do him. I began with the letters and sounds, and before long there were hours in the day that belonged to our lessons as surely as they once had belonged to Adèle’s.","这忙帮得不算过分，我就从字母和发音学起。不久，每天便有固定的几个小时用来上课，就像从前固定有几个小时属于阿黛勒。"]],"translation":"圣约翰注意到，我在一件事上能坐很久。他请我暂时放下德语，学他到印度要用的语言，说教我也能帮他温习已经学过的东西。这忙帮得不算过分，我就从字母和发音学起。不久，每天便有固定的几个小时用来上课，就像从前固定有几个小时属于阿黛勒。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["He was a patient teacher when I made mistakes.","我出错时，他很有耐心。"],[" What I found harder to deal with was his approval.","我更难应付的是他的赞许。"],[" It mattered more to me than I wanted it to, and when he was pleased with my work I took on a little more.","我比自己愿意承认的更在意它。每当他对我的功课满意，我就愿意再多做一点。"],[" I caught myself putting a book down because I thought he would think it a waste of time.","有一次，我发觉自己放下了正看的一本书，只因为我觉得，他会认为那是在浪费时间。"],[" My cousins had invited me to make a home with them.","表亲们邀我一起安家。"],[" I did not want to find myself waiting for permission to enjoy it.","我不希望到了这里，还要等人许可我享受自己的生活。"]],"translation":"我出错时，他很有耐心。我更难应付的是他的赞许。我比自己愿意承认的更在意它。每当他对我的功课满意，我就愿意再多做一点。有一次，我发觉自己放下了正看的一本书，只因为我觉得，他会认为那是在浪费时间。表亲们邀我一起安家。我不希望到了这里，还要等人许可我享受自己的生活。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["We heard that Rosamond was going to marry another man.","后来我们听说，罗莎蒙德要嫁给别人。"],[" St John reported it quietly and went back to his books.","圣约翰平静地告诉大家，然后回去读他的书。"],[" I did not know how much it cost him to speak in that way.","我不知道那样说话对他有多难。"],[" I knew only that the things he gave up for India were things he had chosen to give up.","我只知道，他为了印度放弃的每一样东西，都是他自己选的。"],[" It was a choice I could not ask him to make for me.","我不能让他替我作同样的选择。"]],"translation":"后来我们听说，罗莎蒙德要嫁给别人。圣约翰平静地告诉大家，然后回去读他的书。我不知道那样说话对他有多难。我只知道，他为了印度放弃的每一样东西，都是他自己选的。我不能让他替我作同样的选择。"}],"terms":[{"term":"afford","meaning":"负担得起","usage":"通常与 can/could 连用；可接名词或 to do，后者也能指承受某个后果。","example":"We couldn’t afford to miss the last train.","exampleZh":"我们不能冒错过末班车的风险。","meaningEn":"to have enough money, time or freedom to bear the cost of something","usageEn":"Usually used with “can” or “could.” A noun names the thing you can pay for, while “afford to do” can also describe whether you can risk the consequences."},{"term":"postage","meaning":"邮费、邮资","usage":"常不可数；pay the postage 是付邮费，邮票本身则称 stamp。","example":"The listed price includes postage.","exampleZh":"标出的价格含邮费。","meaningEn":"the charge for sending letters or parcels by mail","usageEn":"It is normally uncountable, as in “pay the postage.” A “stamp” is the item that shows the charge has been paid."},{"term":"favour","meaning":"帮忙、人情","usage":"ask someone a favour 或 ask someone for a favour 都可；in favour of 表示支持。","example":"May I ask you a favour?","exampleZh":"可以请你帮个忙吗？","meaningEn":"an act of help someone does for another person","usageEn":"British “favour” corresponds to American “favor.” Ask “someone for a favour” or “ask someone a favour.” “In favour of” means in support of."},{"term":"deal with","meaning":"应付、处理","usage":"deal/dealt/dealt；deal with a problem 是处理，a book deals with a subject 则指内容涉及该主题。","example":"She dealt with the complaint calmly.","exampleZh":"她冷静地处理了投诉。","meaningEn":"to handle or respond to a matter or problem","usageEn":"The past tense is “dealt with.” When a book or talk deals with a topic, that topic is what it discusses."}],"glossary":[["afford","负担得起"],["postage","邮资"],["for a while","一阵子"],["favour","帮忙；人情"],["deal with","应付；处理"],["approval","认可；赞许"],["catch oneself doing","忽然发现自己正在做……"]]},{"en":"The Voice Across the Moor","zh":"越过荒原的呼唤","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["St John taught me the language he was studying for India, and he noticed that I worked hard even when the lessons tired me.","圣约翰教我他为赴印度而学的语言。他注意到，即使上课让我疲惫，我还是学得很用功。"],[" To him, this was a reason for me to join his mission.","在他看来，这正是我该加入传教工作的理由。"],[" He said I would make a useful missionary’s wife.","他说，我会是一个能帮上忙的传教士妻子。"],[" When he asked me to marry him, he spoke with the same care he used in planning a journey.","求婚时，他的语气像在仔细筹划一次远行。"]],"translation":"圣约翰教我他为赴印度而学的语言。他注意到，即使上课让我疲惫，我还是学得很用功。在他看来，这正是我该加入传教工作的理由。他说，我会是一个能帮上忙的传教士妻子。求婚时，他的语气像在仔细筹划一次远行。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["I told him I could go with him as his sister, but he would take me only as his wife.","我告诉他，我可以以妹妹的身份同行，但他只愿带自己的妻子去。"],[" He believed that a shared duty was reason enough to marry.","他相信，共同承担一项职责就足够成为结婚的理由。"],[" I respected him and knew he would be brave in work that frightened other people.","我尊重他，也知道在别人畏惧的工作面前，他会很勇敢。"],[" Yet I could imagine how it would feel to spend every day beside him, obeying a man who had never wanted to know my heart.","可我想象得出，若天天与他相伴，服从一个从没想了解我内心的人，会是什么滋味。"],[" He told me I should give the matter more thought.","他让我再想想。"]],"translation":"我告诉他，我可以以妹妹的身份同行，但他只愿带自己的妻子去。他相信，共同承担一项职责就足够成为结婚的理由。我尊重他，也知道在别人畏惧的工作面前，他会很勇敢。可我想象得出，若天天与他相伴，服从一个从没想了解我内心的人，会是什么滋味。他让我再想想。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["One evening, as he pressed me for an answer, I almost agreed.","一个傍晚，他催我答复，我几乎就同意了。"],[" I was tired of resisting him.","我已经没有太多力气再抵抗。"],[" I stood by the window and asked, aloud, what I ought to do.","我站在窗边，出声问自己该怎么办。"],[" Then I heard my name called three times.","就在这时，我听见有人叫了我三声。"],[" The voice seemed to be Mr Rochester’s.","那声音像是罗切斯特先生的。"],[" There was no one in the garden, and there was nothing to see on the moor.","花园里空无一人，荒原上也看不见任何身影。"],[" I could not explain what I had heard, but I knew what I wanted to find out.","我说不清听见的究竟是什么，却知道自己想去弄清什么。"],[" By morning I was making arrangements to return to Thornfield.","第二天早晨，我已开始安排返回桑菲尔德。"]],"translation":"一个傍晚，他催我答复，我几乎就同意了。我已经没有太多力气再抵抗。我站在窗边，出声问自己该怎么办。就在这时，我听见有人叫了我三声。那声音像是罗切斯特先生的。花园里空无一人，荒原上也看不见任何身影。我说不清听见的究竟是什么，却知道自己想去弄清什么。第二天早晨，我已开始安排返回桑菲尔德。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["When the coach set me down near the house, I hurried along the road, expecting to see the familiar windows. Instead there were broken walls and a gap where the roof had been.","马车在宅子附近放下我。我匆匆沿路走去，本以为会看见熟悉的窗户，眼前只剩断墙，屋顶所在的地方空了。"],[" At the inn I learned what had happened. Bertha had set the house on fire.","在旅店里，我得知伯莎放火烧了房子。"],[" Mr Rochester had helped the servants escape and tried to save her, but she had jumped from the roof.","罗切斯特先生先帮佣人逃出去，又试图救她，可她从屋顶跳了下去。"],[" He had lost a hand and his sight. He was living at Ferndean, a house deep in the woods.","他失去了一只手，也失去了视力，如今住在树林深处一座叫芬丁的房子里。"],[" I asked the innkeeper how to get there.","我问旅店老板该怎么去。"]],"translation":"马车在宅子附近放下我。我匆匆沿路走去，本以为会看见熟悉的窗户，眼前只剩断墙，屋顶所在的地方空了。在旅店里，我得知伯莎放火烧了房子。罗切斯特先生先帮佣人逃出去，又试图救她，可她从屋顶跳了下去。他失去了一只手，也失去了视力，如今住在树林深处一座叫芬丁的房子里。我问旅店老板该怎么去。"}],"terms":[{"term":"mission","meaning":"使命、传教工作","usage":"go on a mission 可指赴某地执行任务；历史语境常带宗教传教含义。","example":"He returned from a mission overseas.","exampleZh":"他完成海外传教工作后回来了。","meaningEn":"a purposeful task, here Christian missionary work","usageEn":"In historical contexts it can involve travelling to spread a religion. In other settings, “mission” describes an organised task or long-term purpose."},{"term":"press someone for an answer","forms":["pressed me for an answer"],"meaning":"催某人给出答复","usage":"press + 人 + for + 所求；press somebody to do 则强调催促对方采取行动。","example":"They pressed her for an answer before she was ready.","exampleZh":"她还没准备好，他们就催着她答复。","meaningEn":"to urge someone repeatedly or insistently to reply","usageEn":"“Press someone for” names what you want to get. “Press someone to do something” names the action you want them to take."},{"term":"resist","meaning":"抗拒、不屈从","usage":"可接名词或动名词；resist the urge to do 意为克制想做某事的冲动。","example":"I resisted the urge to answer at once.","exampleZh":"我忍住了立刻回答的冲动。","forms":["resisting"],"meaningEn":"to refuse to give in to a person, pressure or impulse","usageEn":"Use it with a noun or an -ing form. “Resist the urge to do something” means to hold back an impulse."},{"term":"aloud","meaning":"出声地","usage":"read aloud 强调让声音听得见；loudly 强调音量大，低声也可以是 aloud。","example":"She read the letter aloud so everyone could hear.","exampleZh":"她把信念出声，好让大家都听见。","meaningEn":"in a voice that can be heard","usageEn":"“Read aloud” distinguishes speaking the words from reading silently. “Loudly” instead describes the volume, which can be high or low when reading aloud."}],"glossary":[["mission","传教工作；使命"],["shared duty","共同的责任"],["press someone for an answer","催某人答复"],["resist","抵抗；不屈从"],["aloud","出声地"],["set someone down","让某人下车"],["innkeeper","旅店老板"]]},{"en":"At the Rochester Arms","zh":"在罗切斯特旅店","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["For a little while I remained at the inn, asking the man to tell me what he remembered of the fire.","我在旅店里多留了一会儿，请那人说说他还记得哪些火灾里的情形。"],[" I had seen Thornfield empty and broken, but the rooms he spoke of were still complete in my mind.","我亲眼见过空荡荡的残垣，可他说到的那些房间，在我脑海里还完好无损。"],[" I knew the stairs the servants must have come down and the passage they would have crossed on their way out.","我认得佣人们一定跑下来的楼梯，也认得他们出门前会穿过的走廊。"],[" It was hard to keep the building I saw in my mind separate from the one I had just walked past.","我很难把脑海里那所房子，同刚刚走过的废墟分开。"]],"translation":"我在旅店里多留了一会儿，请那人说说他还记得哪些火灾里的情形。我亲眼见过空荡荡的残垣，可他说到的那些房间，在我脑海里还完好无损。我认得佣人们一定跑下来的楼梯，也认得他们出门前会穿过的走廊。我很难把脑海里那所房子，同刚刚走过的废墟分开。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["The innkeeper told me that Mr Rochester had gone back into the burning house.","旅店老板说，罗切斯特先生折回了着火的房子。"],[" The people outside could see Bertha on the roof.","外面的人能看见伯莎站在屋顶上。"],[" He called to her and tried to reach her. She jumped before he could get to her.","他叫她，试着够到她，她却在他赶到前跳了下去。"],[" He was still in the building when part of it fell.","屋子有一部分坍塌时，他还在里面。"],[" Afterwards, when they got him out, he could no longer see.","众人把他救出来，他已经看不见了。"],[" One hand was so badly injured that it had to be taken off.","一只手伤得太重，只能截掉。"],[" I had wanted news for many months.","好几个月里我都想知道消息。"],[" Now I found myself wishing, again and again, that he could have sent me one line.","如今听到了，我却一遍遍地想，要是他能给我写上一行字该多好。"]],"translation":"旅店老板说，罗切斯特先生折回了着火的房子。外面的人能看见伯莎站在屋顶上。他叫她，试着够到她，她却在他赶到前跳了下去。屋子有一部分坍塌时，他还在里面。众人把他救出来，他已经看不见了。一只手伤得太重，只能截掉。好几个月里我都想知道消息。如今听到了，我却一遍遍地想，要是他能给我写上一行字该多好。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["The innkeeper said there was little reason for anyone to go to Ferndean.","老板说，很少有人会去芬丁。"],[" It stood far back from the road, and the woods kept the ground damp.","那小屋离大路远，树林让附近的地面一直潮湿。"],[" Mr Rochester lived there with John and Mary, two servants.","罗切斯特先生住在那里，和两个佣人约翰、玛丽在一起。"],[" I asked whether I could get a carriage.","我问能不能找辆马车。"],[" The man looked at me with some surprise, but he agreed to find one.","男人有些惊讶地看着我，还是答应帮我找。"]],"translation":"老板说，很少有人会去芬丁。那小屋离大路远，树林让附近的地面一直潮湿。罗切斯特先生住在那里，和两个佣人约翰、玛丽在一起。我问能不能找辆马车。男人有些惊讶地看着我，还是答应帮我找。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["As I waited, I thought of the first time I had come into that part of the country.","等待时，我想起头一回来这地方。"],[" I had been looking for a place where I could earn a living.","我那时是来找个能谋生的去处的。"],[" This time there was a house to go to if I turned back, and work I could do almost anywhere.","这一回，要是我转身，已有一处可以回去的家，也有到哪里大概都能做的工作。"],[" I hurried because I wanted to get to Ferndean before night, and because I wanted to know what he would say when he heard my voice.","我急着赶路，是想天黑前到芬丁，也是想知道，他听见我的声音会说什么。"]],"translation":"等待时，我想起头一回来这地方。我那时是来找个能谋生的去处的。这一回，要是我转身，已有一处可以回去的家，也有到哪里大概都能做的工作。我急着赶路，是想天黑前到芬丁，也是想知道，他听见我的声音会说什么。"}],"terms":[{"term":"remain","forms":["remained"],"meaning":"继续逗留、保留某种状态","usage":"remain at the inn 表示仍在某地，remain silent 后接形容词表示状态不变。","example":"The guest remained at the inn until morning.","exampleZh":"那位客人在旅店一直待到早晨。","meaningEn":"to continue staying somewhere or to continue in a state","usageEn":"It can take a location, as in “remain at the inn,” or an adjective, as in “remain silent.”"},{"term":"get someone out","meaning":"把某人救出、带离","usage":"get somebody out of... 指让人脱离某地或困境，常含设法成功的意味。","example":"A neighbour got the children out before help arrived.","exampleZh":"救援人员到达之前，一位邻居就把孩子们救了出来。","forms":["got him out"],"meaningEn":"to help someone escape or leave a dangerous or difficult place","usageEn":"Add “of” followed by the place if it is not clear. The expression often implies that someone succeeded in helping the person leave."},{"term":"take off","forms":["taken off"],"meaning":"截掉、切除","usage":"take + 身体部位 + off 在本文伤情中指切除，通常写成被动；take off 另可指飞机起飞。","example":"The surgeon explained why the damaged toe had to be taken off.","exampleZh":"外科医生解释了为什么受伤的脚趾必须切除。","meaningEn":"to remove something, here a body part by surgery","usageEn":"In this context the object names what is removed and often becomes the subject in the passive, as in “the hand was taken off.” “Take off” has other senses, such as a plane leaving the ground."},{"term":"turn back","forms":["turned back"],"meaning":"折返","usage":"可不接宾语；turn somebody back 则表示拦住对方、令其回去。","example":"We turned back when the path disappeared under snow.","exampleZh":"小路被雪盖住后，我们就折返了。","meaningEn":"to reverse direction and return the way you came","usageEn":"Use it on its own when travellers change direction. “Turn someone back” means to stop them from continuing and make them return."}],"glossary":[["remain","逗留"],["separate from","把……与……分开"],["get someone out","把某人救出来"],["take off","截去；切除（本页语境）"],["far back from","离……较远而隐蔽"],["damp","潮湿的"],["turn back","折返"]]},{"en":"Finding Home","zh":"找到归处","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["The path to Ferndean was so dark that I nearly missed the house.","通往芬丁小屋的路太暗了，我差点没看见那座房子。"],[" Mr Rochester came to the door while I watched from between the trees.","我从树间望出去时，罗切斯特先生走到了门口。"],[" He put out a hand to test the weather and stood listening to the rain.","他伸出手探了探天气，站着听雨。"],[" He could not see me.","他看不见我。"],[" After a moment he went back inside.","过了一会儿，他转身回屋。"],[" I followed and asked the servant to let me take him a glass of water.","我跟进去，请佣人让我给他端一杯水。"]],"translation":"通往芬丁小屋的路太暗了，我差点没看见那座房子。我从树间望出去时，罗切斯特先生走到了门口。他伸出手探了探天气，站着听雨。他看不见我。过了一会儿，他转身回屋。我跟进去，请佣人让我给他端一杯水。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Pilot knew me before his master did.","帕洛特比主人先认出了我。"],[" The dog came close, and Mr Rochester asked who was there.","狗凑过来，罗切斯特先生问是谁。"],[" I answered.","我应了一声。"],[" He put down the glass and reached for me with his good hand.","他放下杯子，用那只完好的手伸向我。"],[" Even when he had found my hand, he asked whether I could really be there.","握到我的手后，他还问我是不是真的来了。"],[" I told him that I had money of my own, and that I had come because I wished to see him.","我告诉他，我现在有自己的钱，我来，是因为我想见他。"],[" All he had to do was ask, and I would stay.","只要他开口，我就愿意留下。"]],"translation":"帕洛特比主人先认出了我。狗凑过来，罗切斯特先生问是谁。我应了一声。他放下杯子，用那只完好的手伸向我。握到我的手后，他还问我是不是真的来了。我告诉他，我现在有自己的钱，我来，是因为我想见他。只要他开口，我就愿意留下。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["The next day, as we walked a little way from the house, he told me that he had once called out my name in his loneliness. He thought he had heard me answer.","第二天，我们沿屋外的小路走了一段。他说，有一次他孤独难耐，大声叫了我的名字，仿佛还听见了我的回答。"],[" We discovered that he had called on the evening when I had heard him at Moor House.","我们发现，他喊出我名字的那晚，正是我在荒原屋听见他的那晚。"],[" I kept my part of the story to myself.","我把自己听见的事藏在心里。"],[" It was enough to be there with him, and to know that we had both been free to choose.","能坐在他身边，又知道彼此都能自由作选择，对我来说已经足够。"]],"translation":"第二天，我们沿屋外的小路走了一段。他说，有一次他孤独难耐，大声叫了我的名字，仿佛还听见了我的回答。我们发现，他喊出我名字的那晚，正是我在荒原屋听见他的那晚。我把自己听见的事藏在心里。能坐在他身边，又知道彼此都能自由作选择，对我来说已经足够。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["We were married quietly in the village church.","我们在村里的教堂安静地结了婚。"],[" I visited Adèle at her school and found her unhappy there, so I moved her to a kinder one.","我去学校看阿黛勒，发现她在那里过得不开心，就替她转到一所待学生更好的学校。"],[" Diana and Mary married and remained part of my life.","黛安娜和玛丽也成了家，依然是我生活的一部分。"],[" After two years, my husband recovered enough sight in one eye to see the face of our first child.","两年后，我丈夫的一只眼睛恢复了部分视力，能看见我们第一个孩子的脸。"],[" We read together when his eyes tired, and when we went out, I described what lay ahead on the path.","眼睛累时，我们就一起读书。出门散步时，我会告诉他小路前面有什么。"],[" This time, when I spoke of home, I meant a place I had chosen.","这一回，我说起家，说的是自己选定的归处。"]],"translation":"我们在村里的教堂安静地结了婚。我去学校看阿黛勒，发现她在那里过得不开心，就替她转到一所待学生更好的学校。黛安娜和玛丽也成了家，依然是我生活的一部分。两年后，我丈夫的一只眼睛恢复了部分视力，能看见我们第一个孩子的脸。眼睛累时，我们就一起读书。出门散步时，我会告诉他小路前面有什么。这一回，我说起家，说的是自己选定的归处。"}],"terms":[{"term":"put out a hand","meaning":"伸出手","usage":"put out a hand 可表示试探、求助或者示意握手；put out a fire 是同形的另一义。","example":"She put out a hand to steady herself against the wall.","exampleZh":"她伸手扶墙，好站稳身子。","meaningEn":"to extend a hand toward something or someone","usageEn":"It may be to feel for an obstacle, get support or greet someone. “Put out a fire” uses the same verb with a different meaning."},{"term":"reach for","forms":["reached for"],"meaning":"伸手去够","usage":"for 后接想要取得的东西，未必够到；reach something 可指已经触及。","example":"He reached for his glasses beside the lamp.","exampleZh":"他伸手去够灯旁的眼镜。","meaningEn":"to stretch toward something you want to get or touch","usageEn":"“Reach for” describes the attempt without saying whether you get hold of it. “Reach the object” says you were able to get to it."},{"term":"recover one’s sight","meaning":"恢复视力","usage":"sight 在此表示视觉能力；recover from an illness 则是病后康复。","example":"The patient slowly recovered her sight after treatment.","exampleZh":"经过治疗，病人的视力逐渐恢复了。","forms":["recovered enough sight"],"meaningEn":"to regain the ability to see","usageEn":"“Sight” means the physical ability to see. “Recover” takes “sight” directly, but use “recover from” before the name of an illness."},{"term":"lie ahead","forms":["lay ahead"],"meaning":"在前方、今后等待着","usage":"用在时间上表示未来将遇到；lie 的过去式 lay，和 lay something 的放置义不同。","example":"Neither of them knew what lay ahead.","exampleZh":"两个人都不知道接下来将遇到什么。","meaningEn":"to be in front of someone, or to await them in the future","usageEn":"The past tense of “lie” here is “lay,” as in “what lay ahead.” There is no direct object in this use."}],"glossary":[["put out a hand","伸出手"],["good hand","未受伤的那只手"],["reach for","伸手去够"],["call out","大声喊"],["keep something to oneself","把某事留在心里"],["recover one’s sight","恢复视力"],["lie ahead","在前方；即将遇到"]]},{"en":"Ten Years Later","zh":"十年以后","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["It is ten years since we went to the church.","从我们并肩走进教堂到现在，已经十年。"],[" When I think of the years in which I had no place of my own, I am still surprised by small things.","想到曾有那么多年，我没有自己的立足之地，生活里的小事至今还会让我惊讶。"],[" I can sit down to breakfast and expect to finish it.","坐下来吃早饭，我可以安安心心吃完。"],[" I can tell my husband when I disagree with him.","不同意丈夫的话，我可以告诉他。"],[" If we wish to spend an evening quietly, there is no company we are obliged to entertain.","想安静地度过一个晚上，也没有非得应酬的客人。"],[" Sometimes I read to him.","有时我读书给他听。"],[" Sometimes he sets me right about something I have misunderstood, and sometimes I set him right.","有时我弄错了什么，他会帮我纠正，有时也轮到我纠正他。"]],"translation":"从我们并肩走进教堂到现在，已经十年。想到曾有那么多年，我没有自己的立足之地，生活里的小事至今还会让我惊讶。坐下来吃早饭，我可以安安心心吃完。不同意丈夫的话，我可以告诉他。想安静地度过一个晚上，也没有非得应酬的客人。有时我读书给他听。有时我弄错了什么，他会帮我纠正，有时也轮到我纠正他。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Adèle worked well once she was at a school where she was treated kindly.","到了待她和善的学校，阿黛勒学得很好。"],[" In time she became a young woman I liked to have near me.","后来她成了一个我愿意常留在身边的年轻人。"],[" When we spoke of her childhood, I was glad that she could remember things besides lessons and partings.","我们说起她的童年，我很高兴她还能记起功课和离别以外的事情。"],[" Diana and Mary have homes of their own and are near enough for us to see one another.","黛安娜和玛丽有了自己的家，住得也不远，我们还能相见。"],[" It still gives me pleasure to hear one of them come into the house without knocking.","我听见她们中有谁不用敲门就进屋，仍会感到高兴。"]],"translation":"到了待她和善的学校，阿黛勒学得很好。后来她成了一个我愿意常留在身边的年轻人。我们说起她的童年，我很高兴她还能记起功课和离别以外的事情。黛安娜和玛丽有了自己的家，住得也不远，我们还能相见。我听见她们中有谁不用敲门就进屋，仍会感到高兴。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["St John never married. He went to India, as he had intended, and the letters I receive from him tell of hard journeys and work that continues when he is tired.","圣约翰没有结婚，按他的打算去了印度。我收到的信里，写着艰难的旅程，也写着即使疲倦仍得继续做的工作。"],[" He did not write to congratulate me on my marriage. I never expected that he would.","他没有写信祝贺我结婚，我也没指望他会这么做。"],[" His latest letter makes me think that I may not hear from him again.","最近一封信让我觉得，也许我不会再有他的消息。"],[" He believes he has nearly finished the work he was sent to do.","他相信自己受托去做的事已快完成。"],[" I hope he finds the rest he has so seldom allowed himself.","我希望他能得到那份他很少准许自己享有的休息。"]],"translation":"圣约翰没有结婚，按他的打算去了印度。我收到的信里，写着艰难的旅程，也写着即使疲倦仍得继续做的工作。他没有写信祝贺我结婚，我也没指望他会这么做。最近一封信让我觉得，也许我不会再有他的消息。他相信自己受托去做的事已快完成。我希望他能得到那份他很少准许自己享有的休息。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["I have not forgotten the girl who looked for a place behind a curtain at Gateshead.","我没忘记那个在盖茨黑德府要躲到窗帘后面的女孩。"],[" When I look up from my book and hear footsteps outside the room, I no longer ask myself whether I ought to move out of the way.","如今，我从书上抬起眼睛，听见房门外响起脚步，已经不会再想，是不是该让开了。"],[" Often it is someone I have been waiting for.","来的人往往是我正在等的人。"],[" I put the book down and make room.","我放下书，腾出一个位置。"]],"translation":"我没忘记那个在盖茨黑德府要躲到窗帘后面的女孩。如今，我从书上抬起眼睛，听见房门外响起脚步，已经不会再想，是不是该让开了。来的人往往是我正在等的人。我放下书，腾出一个位置。"}],"terms":[{"term":"obliged to","meaning":"有义务、不得不……","usage":"be obliged to do 可来自规则或情势；I’m much obliged 是偏旧式的致谢。","example":"We were obliged to wait until the bridge reopened.","exampleZh":"我们只得等桥重新开放。","meaningEn":"required by a rule, sense of duty or set of circumstances","usageEn":"“Be obliged to” is followed by a verb. “I’m much obliged” is a separate, rather old-fashioned expression of thanks."},{"term":"entertain company","meaning":"招待客人","usage":"company 在待客语境为来访的客人，可说 have company；entertain 这里强调做东。","example":"They rarely entertained company during the winter.","exampleZh":"他们冬天很少招待客人。","forms":["company we are obliged to entertain"],"meaningEn":"to receive and look after social guests","usageEn":"“Company” is uncountable in this sense. “Have company” means guests are visiting, while “entertain company” puts the emphasis on hosting them."},{"term":"parting","meaning":"离别、分别的时刻","usage":"a parting glance 是临别一瞥；at parting 偏书面，表示分别时。","example":"Their parting was brief, but both remembered it.","exampleZh":"他们分别得很匆忙，但两人一直记得那一刻。","forms":["partings"],"meaningEn":"a separation or the moment people say goodbye","usageEn":"It can also describe something done at that moment, as in “a parting glance.” “At parting” is a more literary way to say “when they separated.”"},{"term":"make room","meaning":"让出空间、容纳","usage":"make room for 可指腾出实际空间，也可说 make room for other ideas。","example":"Please move the basket to make room for another chair.","exampleZh":"请把篮子挪一下，腾出地方再放把椅子。","meaningEn":"to create enough space for someone or something","usageEn":"Use “make room for” before what you want to accommodate. It can also mean allowing for a different opinion, activity or priority."}],"glossary":[["obliged to","有义务；不得不"],["entertain company","招待客人"],["set someone right","纠正某人的错误"],["parting","离别"],["near enough","离得够近"],["congratulate someone on","就某事向某人道贺"],["make room","让出地方；腾出空间"]]}]},{"id":"wind","zh":"追风少年","en":"The Boy Who Harnessed the Wind","chapters":[{"en":"A Light in Wimbe","zh":"温贝村的一盏灯","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["In a village in central Malawi, a light came on in a house that had no connection to the electricity grid.","在马拉维中部的一个村子里，一户没有接入电网的人家亮起了灯。"],[" Outside stood a tower made from wood. At the top, blades turned in the wind.","屋外立着一座木塔，塔顶的叶片在风中转动。"],[" A line ran down from the machine to the house.","一根线从机器接进屋里。"],[" The tower, the moving blades, and the light inside belonged to the same system.","木塔、转动的叶片和屋里的灯，都是同一个系统的一部分。"],[" The person who had brought them together was a teenager named William Kamkwamba.","把它们组装起来的人，是一个名叫威廉·卡姆宽巴的少年。"]],"translation":"在马拉维中部的一个村子里，一户没有接入电网的人家亮起了灯。屋外立着一座木塔，塔顶的叶片在风中转动。一根线从机器接进屋里。木塔、转动的叶片和屋里的灯，都是同一个系统的一部分。把它们组装起来的人，是一个名叫威廉·卡姆宽巴的少年。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["There is an easy way to tell this story.","这个故事可以讲得很简单。"],[" A boy has a clever idea, finds some old parts, and builds a machine.","一个男孩想到了一个好主意，找来一些旧零件，造出一台机器。"],[" The light comes on and the story is over.","灯一亮，故事就结束了。"],[" Look a little closer, though, and the light raises a number of questions.","可再仔细看看，那盏灯会引出许多问题。"],[" How did he learn that a turning wheel could make electricity?","他是怎么知道转动的轮子可以发电的？"],[" Where could he find a generator?","上哪儿找发电机？"],[" Who would help him?","谁愿意帮他？"],[" And what would count as success for a family trying to make it through a severe food crisis?","对一个正努力熬过严重粮食危机的家庭来说，什么才算成功？"]],"translation":"这个故事可以讲得很简单。一个男孩想到了一个好主意，找来一些旧零件，造出一台机器。灯一亮，故事就结束了。可再仔细看看，那盏灯会引出许多问题。他是怎么知道转动的轮子可以发电的？上哪儿找发电机？谁愿意帮他？对一个正努力熬过严重粮食危机的家庭来说，什么才算成功？"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["To answer those questions, we will follow two stories that meet in the village of Wimbe.","要回答这些问题，我们要沿着两条线索走，它们在温贝村交汇。"],[" One is about a student whose family ran out of money for school and who tried to keep learning.","一条线索关乎一名学生。家里交不起学费，他却想继续学习。"],[" The other is about an object that slowly changed shape as he found books and materials.","另一条线索关乎一件慢慢成形的东西。威廉找到的书和材料越多，它的样子就越清楚。"],[" A bicycle belonged on the road, a piece of pipe belonged in a water system, and a picture of a windmill belonged in a textbook.","自行车原本在路上跑，塑料管原本用来输水，风车的图片原本印在课本里。"],[" William found ways to bring them into the same project.","威廉找到了把它们带进同一个项目的办法。"]],"translation":"要回答这些问题，我们要沿着两条线索走，它们在温贝村交汇。一条线索关乎一名学生。家里交不起学费，他却想继续学习。另一条线索关乎一件慢慢成形的东西。威廉找到的书和材料越多，它的样子就越清楚。自行车原本在路上跑，塑料管原本用来输水，风车的图片原本印在课本里。威廉找到了把它们带进同一个项目的办法。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["The story continues past the first light.","故事还会讲到第一盏灯亮起之后。"],[" William had to live with the machine, discover what it could do, and decide what to change.","威廉得继续使用这台机器，看看它能做什么，再决定哪些地方需要改。"],[" He also had to explain his work to people far from home.","他还要向远方的人解释自己的工作。"],[" As we read, we will pause where the story benefits from a closer look at farming, electricity, or how people learn.","读到与农业、电力或学习有关的地方，我们会停下来仔细看看。"],[" Those explanations help us see why a little light in Wimbe was such a difficult thing to make.","了解这些背景，就能明白为什么在温贝村点亮一盏小灯，是一件那么难的事。"]],"translation":"故事还会讲到第一盏灯亮起之后。威廉得继续使用这台机器，看看它能做什么，再决定哪些地方需要改。他还要向远方的人解释自己的工作。读到与农业、电力或学习有关的地方，我们会停下来仔细看看。了解这些背景，就能明白为什么在温贝村点亮一盏小灯，是一件那么难的事。"}],"terms":[{"term":"electricity grid","meaning":"电网","usage":"be connected to the grid 指接入供电网络；off-grid 指独立供电或未接入公共电网。","example":"The clinic had solar panels but no connection to the electricity grid.","exampleZh":"诊所有太阳能板，却没有接入电网。","meaningEn":"The network that supplies electric power to homes and other buildings.","usageEn":"A house can be connected to the grid. Off-grid homes use a source outside the public supply network."},{"term":"generator","meaning":"发电机","usage":"generator 将机械能等转成电能；motor 通常反过来，把电能变成机械运动。","example":"The generator powered a lamp and a small radio.","exampleZh":"发电机给一盏灯和一台小收音机供电。","meaningEn":"A device that produces electricity from motion or another form of energy.","usageEn":"The windmill's generator turns motion into electricity. A motor typically does the reverse."},{"term":"food crisis","meaning":"粮食危机","usage":"food 在这里作定语，常见搭配 face a food crisis 或 respond to a food crisis。","example":"A poor harvest left the district facing a food crisis.","exampleZh":"歉收使这个地区面临粮食危机。","meaningEn":"A period when many people cannot get enough food.","usageEn":"Food modifies crisis. A community can face a food crisis, and relief agencies can respond to one."},{"term":"make it through","meaning":"熬过去、挺过难关","usage":"it 是固定搭配的一部分；through 后可接困难时期、考试等持续过程。","example":"We had just enough grain to make it through the winter.","exampleZh":"我们的粮食刚够撑过冬天。","meaningEn":"To get to the end of a difficult period or experience.","usageEn":"Keep it in the fixed phrase. Through can introduce a stretch of time, as in make it through the winter."}],"glossary":[["electricity grid","电网"],["blade","叶片"],["generator","发电机"],["food crisis","粮食危机"],["make it through","熬过，挺过"],["benefit from","从……中受益"]]},{"en":"The Road to Kasungu","zh":"去卡松古的路","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Find the long lake on the eastern side of Malawi on a map. Now look west of the lake, toward the interior.","在地图上找到马拉维东边那个狭长的湖，再从湖向西看，望向内陆。"],[" Kasungu, a town in central Malawi, is one of the places that helps you locate William's home.","马拉维中部有座城镇叫卡松古。找到它，就比较容易确定威廉家的位置了。"],[" Wimbe lies in the surrounding district, in an area where fields, houses, and roads are part of the same working landscape.","温贝村位于附近的卡松古区。在这里，田地、房屋和道路连成了一片供人生活和劳作的土地。"],[" A journey by bicycle can connect a home with a trading centre or a field with a buyer.","骑上自行车，人就可以从家到集市，也可以把田里的收成送到买家手上。"]],"translation":"在地图上找到马拉维东边那个狭长的湖，再从湖向西看，望向内陆。马拉维中部有座城镇叫卡松古。找到它，就比较容易确定威廉家的位置了。温贝村位于附近的卡松古区。在这里，田地、房屋和道路连成了一片供人生活和劳作的土地。骑上自行车，人就可以从家到集市，也可以把田里的收成送到买家手上。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["A bicycle can carry a sack of grain as well as a person.","自行车既能载人，也能驮一袋粮食。"],[" Its value begins to make more sense if you imagine walking the same road with a heavy load.","想象一下自己背着沉重的东西步行走同一条路，就会明白车有多宝贵。"],[" The bicycle also needs attention.","它也得有人保养。"],[" Its chain can come off. A tyre can lose air.","链条可能脱落，车胎可能漏气。"],[" The wheel has to turn freely without rubbing against its frame.","车轮必须转得顺畅，不能蹭到车架。"],[" Someone who knows how to repair those simple faults gives the machine a longer working life.","有人懂得修理这些小毛病，自行车就能多用好几年。"]],"translation":"自行车既能载人，也能驮一袋粮食。想象一下自己背着沉重的东西步行走同一条路，就会明白车有多宝贵。它也得有人保养。链条可能脱落，车胎可能漏气。车轮必须转得顺畅，不能蹭到车架。有人懂得修理这些小毛病，自行车就能多用好几年。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["The same habit of repair applies to other things.","修理东西的习惯也体现在别处。"],[" A radio may have a loose wire.","收音机里可能只是一根电线松了。"],[" A handle can break while the tool it belongs to is still useful.","工具的把手断掉，工具本身却还有用。"],[" When replacing an object costs money or means making a long trip, there is a reason to open it, take a closer look, and keep the parts that are in good condition.","换个新的要花钱，有时还得跑很远的路。于是，人们有理由拆开东西仔细看看，把状态好的零件留下来。"],[" Some of those parts will find a use years after their original job has ended.","有些零件在原来的用处消失多年后，还能派上新的用场。"]],"translation":"修理东西的习惯也体现在别处。收音机里可能只是一根电线松了。工具的把手断掉，工具本身却还有用。换个新的要花钱，有时还得跑很远的路。于是，人们有理由拆开东西仔细看看，把状态好的零件留下来。有些零件在原来的用处消失多年后，还能派上新的用场。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["William grew up in a farming family in this setting.","威廉就在这样的环境里长大，家里靠种地生活。"],[" The project that later made him famous depended on pieces that already belonged to daily life.","让他后来出名的发明，靠的是日常生活中本已有的物件。"],[" His knowledge of a bicycle did not start with a lesson on wind power. It started in a place where bicycles mattered every day.","他最早了解自行车，源于一个天天都用得上自行车的地方。"],[" To understand the windmill, keep that road to town in mind.","读到风车时，可以想想通往镇上的那条路。"],[" It helps explain both where the parts came from and why each one was worth keeping.","那条路能帮我们理解零件是从哪里来的，也能让我们明白，为什么每个零件都值得留着。"]],"translation":"威廉就在这样的环境里长大，家里靠种地生活。让他后来出名的发明，靠的是日常生活中本已有的物件。他最早了解自行车，源于一个天天都用得上自行车的地方。读到风车时，可以想想通往镇上的那条路。那条路能帮我们理解零件是从哪里来的，也能让我们明白，为什么每个零件都值得留着。"}],"terms":[{"term":"interior","meaning":"内陆、内部地区","usage":"此处为地理名词，the interior 指远离海岸或边缘的区域；interior design 中它是形容词。","example":"The road runs from the coast into the interior.","exampleZh":"这条路从海岸延伸到内陆。","meaningEn":"An inland part of a country or region.","usageEn":"In geography, the interior is away from the coast or border. In interior design, the word describes the inside of a building."},{"term":"trading centre","meaning":"集市、交易中心","usage":"centre 是英式拼写，对应美式 center；它可指有买卖活动的地方，不限于商场建筑。","example":"Farmers brought their crops to the nearest trading centre.","exampleZh":"农民把作物运到最近的集市。","meaningEn":"A place where people buy and sell goods.","usageEn":"Centre is the British spelling of center. The phrase can describe a market town or district as well as a building."},{"term":"rub against","meaning":"与……摩擦、蹭到……","usage":"against 点出摩擦的表面；rub oil into wood 则强调把油擦进木材里。","example":"The wheel rubs against the frame when the load is too heavy.","exampleZh":"负载太重时，轮子会蹭到车架。","forms":["rubbing against"],"meaningEn":"To move in contact with another surface.","usageEn":"Against identifies the surface being touched. In rub oil into wood, into instead shows where the oil is worked."},{"term":"loose wire","meaning":"松脱、接触不牢的电线","usage":"loose 描述连接不紧，和 lose（丢失）拼写相近；a loose connection 指接触不良。","example":"A loose wire made the light go on and off.","exampleZh":"一根松脱的电线让灯忽明忽暗。","meaningEn":"A wire that is no longer connected firmly.","usageEn":"A loose wire can produce a loose connection that works only intermittently. Loose is an adjective, while lose is a verb."}],"glossary":[["interior","内陆；内部"],["trading centre","集市，贸易点"],["rub against","摩擦，蹭到"],["fault","故障"],["loose wire","松动的电线"],["replace","更换"]]},{"en":"The Year in the Fields","zh":"田里的一年","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["For a family that grows much of its food, the year has two important calendars.","对于一家主要靠自己种粮食的人来说，一年里有两套重要的日历。"],[" One gives the names of the months. The other records work and waiting.","一套标着月份，另一套记着农活和等待。"],[" There is a time to prepare the ground, a time to put seeds into it, and a time to see whether rain will come when the young plants need it.","有整地的时候，有播种的时候，也有等着看幼苗需要水时会不会下雨的时候。"],[" Families in Malawi who rely on maize have to think well beyond the day of harvest.","马拉维以玉米为生的家庭，要考虑的日子远远超过收获的那一天。"]],"translation":"对于一家主要靠自己种粮食的人来说，一年里有两套重要的日历。一套标着月份，另一套记着农活和等待。有整地的时候，有播种的时候，也有等着看幼苗需要水时会不会下雨的时候。马拉维以玉米为生的家庭，要考虑的日子远远超过收获的那一天。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Maize can be ground into flour.","玉米可以磨成粉。"],[" With water and heat, the flour becomes a thick food called nsima. It can be eaten with vegetables, beans, or other relishes when they are available.","玉米粉加水煮熟，会变成一种叫恩西玛的稠食，有蔬菜、豆子或其他配菜时，就搭着一起吃。"],[" In an ordinary month, making this meal is simply part of the day.","在平常的月份，做这顿饭只是日常生活的一部分。"],[" In a bad year, even preparing the same bowl every evening may depend on how carefully the family measures what remains in its grain store.","在收成不好的年头，每晚能不能做出同样一碗饭，可能就取决于家里把剩下的存粮算得有多仔细。"]],"translation":"玉米可以磨成粉。玉米粉加水煮熟，会变成一种叫恩西玛的稠食，有蔬菜、豆子或其他配菜时，就搭着一起吃。在平常的月份，做这顿饭只是日常生活的一部分。在收成不好的年头，每晚能不能做出同样一碗饭，可能就取决于家里把剩下的存粮算得有多仔细。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Rain decides a great deal, but the amount of rain is only part of the question.","雨水能决定很多事情，但降雨量只是其中一项。"],[" Heavy rain can flood a field.","雨太大，会把田淹了。"],[" A dry spell can arrive at a stage when plants are especially sensitive to a lack of water.","干旱也可能赶上作物最缺不得水的阶段。"],[" Two farms can receive a similar total for the season and bring in different harvests.","两户农家一个雨季下的总雨量差不多，最后的收成却可能很不一样。"],[" Soil, timing, seeds, and access to other resources all affect what a household can take home.","土壤、时机、种子和手头能用的其他资源，都会影响一家人能从地里带回多少粮食。"]],"translation":"雨水能决定很多事情，但降雨量只是其中一项。雨太大，会把田淹了。干旱也可能赶上作物最缺不得水的阶段。两户农家一个雨季下的总雨量差不多，最后的收成却可能很不一样。土壤、时机、种子和手头能用的其他资源，都会影响一家人能从地里带回多少粮食。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["William's later interest in moving water grew in this world.","威廉后来对抽水产生兴趣，正是因为生活在这样的地方。"],[" Light solved a problem that a family could feel as soon as the sun went down.","电灯解决的是一个太阳落山后全家立刻能感受到的问题。"],[" Water had a different reach.","水能起到的作用有所不同。"],[" If a household could bring water to the right place at the right time, it could lower one of the risks that followed every planting.","如果一家人能在合适的时间把水送到需要的地方，播种后要面对的风险就少了一项。"],[" That possibility explains why a boy who had first learned to make a small electrical light would eventually talk about pumping water for crops.","这也解释了为什么一个最先学会点亮小电灯的男孩，后来会谈到给作物抽水。"]],"translation":"威廉后来对抽水产生兴趣，正是因为生活在这样的地方。电灯解决的是一个太阳落山后全家立刻能感受到的问题。水能起到的作用有所不同。如果一家人能在合适的时间把水送到需要的地方，播种后要面对的风险就少了一项。这也解释了为什么一个最先学会点亮小电灯的男孩，后来会谈到给作物抽水。"}],"terms":[{"term":"maize","meaning":"玉米","usage":"英式或农业语境常用 maize；美语通常说 corn。作物名称本身常作不可数名词。","example":"The family dried the maize before storing it.","exampleZh":"一家人把玉米晒干后才入仓。","meaningEn":"The grain crop often called corn in American English.","usageEn":"Maize is common in British English and agricultural writing. It is usually uncountable when it names the crop."},{"term":"relish","meaning":"和主食搭配的配菜","usage":"在马拉维饮食语境可泛指搭配恩西玛的菜；relish 作动词则是享受、乐在其中。","example":"She served the maize porridge with a relish made from greens.","exampleZh":"她给玉米糊配了一道绿叶菜。","forms":["relishes"],"meaningEn":"A dish eaten alongside a staple food such as nsima.","usageEn":"In this Malawian context, relish includes sides such as vegetables or beans. The verb relish means greatly enjoy."},{"term":"grain store","meaning":"储粮处、粮仓","usage":"store 此处是储存设施，不是出售粮食的店；a store of grain 可指一批储备粮。","example":"The grain store was nearly empty before the next harvest.","exampleZh":"下一次收获之前，粮仓几乎空了。","meaningEn":"A place used to keep grain for later use.","usageEn":"Store refers to a storage facility here. A store of grain emphasizes the reserve itself."},{"term":"dry spell","meaning":"一段少雨期","usage":"spell 有一段时间之义；比 drought 更不限定持续时间或严重程度。","example":"The seedlings struggled through a two-week dry spell.","exampleZh":"幼苗艰难地熬过了两周少雨天气。","meaningEn":"A period with little or no rain.","usageEn":"Spell can mean a period of a certain condition. Dry spell leaves the length and severity more open than drought."}],"glossary":[["maize","玉米"],["nsima","恩西玛，玉米糊类主食"],["relish","配菜"],["grain store","粮仓，存粮处"],["dry spell","一段少雨天气"],["household","家庭，住户"]]},{"en":"The Things a Radio Teaches","zh":"收音机教会的事","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Before he built a windmill, William was curious about radios.","造风车之前，威廉就对收音机好奇。"],[" A radio can put a voice into a room even though the speaker is many kilometres away.","说话的人明明在许多公里以外，收音机却能把那个人的声音送进房间。"],[" For a child who wants to know how things work, the box invites attention.","对一个爱琢磨东西怎么运作的孩子来说，这个盒子处处值得留意。"],[" Someone turns a dial and the voice changes.","有人转一下旋钮，传来的声音就换了。"],[" Some radios grow quiet as their batteries get old.","电池快没电时，有些收音机的声音会变弱。"],[" A fault inside may be hard to see, yet it can silence the whole set.","机器里面有个难以看见的小毛病，整台收音机就可能没了声音。"]],"translation":"造风车之前，威廉就对收音机好奇。说话的人明明在许多公里以外，收音机却能把那个人的声音送进房间。对一个爱琢磨东西怎么运作的孩子来说，这个盒子处处值得留意。有人转一下旋钮，传来的声音就换了。电池快没电时，有些收音机的声音会变弱。机器里面有个难以看见的小毛病，整台收音机就可能没了声音。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Working on radios with his cousin Geoffrey gave William practice with small parts and practical questions.","威廉和表亲杰弗里一起修收音机，逐渐熟悉了小零件，也练习了怎样解决实际问题。"],[" The first reasonable question when a set falls silent is simply whether it has power.","一台收音机突然没声，首先可以查查它有没有电。"],[" If a battery works in another radio, there is a reason to look elsewhere.","一节电池放到另一台收音机里能用，就有理由去查别处。"],[" A damaged contact can stop electricity from reaching a part that is still in good condition.","一个接点损坏了，可能让一块完好的零件接不到电。"],[" Finding out where the trouble lies is usually more work than naming the object that has failed.","找到毛病出在哪儿，往往比说出哪台机器坏了要费劲得多。"]],"translation":"威廉和表亲杰弗里一起修收音机，逐渐熟悉了小零件，也练习了怎样解决实际问题。一台收音机突然没声，首先可以查查它有没有电。一节电池放到另一台收音机里能用，就有理由去查别处。一个接点损坏了，可能让一块完好的零件接不到电。找到毛病出在哪儿，往往比说出哪台机器坏了要费劲得多。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["One skill you can learn here is to change one thing at a time.","这里可以学到一个本领，就是每次只改动一样东西。"],[" Imagine moving two wires and replacing the batteries before testing a radio again. If the voice returns, you will have several possible explanations.","想想看，要是把两根线挪了位置，还换了电池，然后才重新测试，收音机恢复声音也有好几种可能的原因。"],[" If you test a fresh battery first and the radio stays quiet, you have better information about what to check next.","要是先只换一节新电池，发现收音机依然没声，就更能判断下一步该查什么。"],[" The set teaches you if you give it a clear question to answer.","把问题问清楚，这台机器就能给你一点有用的信息。"]],"translation":"这里可以学到一个本领，就是每次只改动一样东西。想想看，要是把两根线挪了位置，还换了电池，然后才重新测试，收音机恢复声音也有好几种可能的原因。要是先只换一节新电池，发现收音机依然没声，就更能判断下一步该查什么。把问题问清楚，这台机器就能给你一点有用的信息。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["William's first windmill also had to answer questions one at a time.","威廉的第一台风车也要一个一个地回答问题。"],[" A blade could turn while the generator stayed still.","叶片或许在转，发电机却没动。"],[" A generator could turn while the lamp remained dark.","发电机转了，电灯也可能还是暗的。"],[" The habits that make it possible to track down a fault in a radio can help with all of these problems.","排查收音机故障的习惯，同样可以用来解决这些问题。"],[" A person who learns to ask where a small current stops is already doing part of the work required to build a much larger machine.","一个人开始追查微弱的电流在哪里断掉，就已经在做建造更大机器时需要做的一部分工作了。"]],"translation":"威廉的第一台风车也要一个一个地回答问题。叶片或许在转，发电机却没动。发电机转了，电灯也可能还是暗的。排查收音机故障的习惯，同样可以用来解决这些问题。一个人开始追查微弱的电流在哪里断掉，就已经在做建造更大机器时需要做的一部分工作了。"}],"terms":[{"term":"dial","meaning":"调节旋钮、刻度盘","usage":"turn the dial 调节旋钮，read the dial 看刻度；dial a number 中它作动词，意为拨号。","example":"She turned the dial until the music came through clearly.","exampleZh":"她转动旋钮，直到音乐清晰了。","meaningEn":"A control you turn, often with markings that show the setting.","usageEn":"Turn the dial means adjust it. Dial a number uses the word as a verb."},{"term":"set","meaning":"一台设备，本文指收音机","usage":"a radio set 可缩称为 a set；set 在 a set of tools 中则指一组事物。","example":"The old set worked again after the battery was replaced.","exampleZh":"换了电池后，那台旧收音机又能用了。","meaningEn":"A piece of equipment, here a radio receiver.","usageEn":"A radio set can be shortened to a set when the context is clear. A set of tools is a group of items."},{"term":"track down","meaning":"循线追查并找到","usage":"通常含经过一番努力；宾语为代词时说 track it down。","example":"It took an hour to track down the damaged wire.","exampleZh":"花了一个小时才找到那根损坏的线。","meaningEn":"To locate something after following clues or making an effort.","usageEn":"A full noun can follow down, as in track down a fault. Put a pronoun in the middle, as in track it down."},{"term":"current","meaning":"电流","usage":"current flows through a wire 是常见说法；electrical current 是电荷流动，voltage 是电势差。","example":"No current flowed until she closed the switch.","exampleZh":"她合上开关后，电流才开始流动。","meaningEn":"The flow of electric charge.","usageEn":"Current flows through a wire. Voltage is the difference in electric potential that can drive the flow."}],"glossary":[["dial","旋钮，刻度盘"],["set","一台设备，此处指收音机"],["contact","电接点"],["lie","位于，存在于"],["track down","追查，找到"],["current","电流"]]},{"en":"A Place at School","zh":"中学里的一席之地","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["For William, starting secondary school meant access to lessons that he wanted to keep following.","对威廉来说，上中学意味着能接着听那些他想学下去的课。"],[" A timetable gives a student a place to be and a sequence of things to learn.","一张课表告诉学生每天该去哪里，该按什么顺序学。"],[" Someone explains a new idea, sets an exercise, and returns to see how the class has done.","老师讲解一个新概念，布置一道练习，再回来看看班里做得怎么样。"],[" Behind that routine is a piece of security that can be easy to miss.","这种规律的生活里，有一种容易忽略的安稳。"],[" The student expects to come back tomorrow.","学生知道，自己明天还可以回来上课。"]],"translation":"对威廉来说，上中学意味着能接着听那些他想学下去的课。一张课表告诉学生每天该去哪里，该按什么顺序学。老师讲解一个新概念，布置一道练习，再回来看看班里做得怎么样。这种规律的生活里，有一种容易忽略的安稳。学生知道，自己明天还可以回来上课。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["At the time, that expectation depended on payments William's family struggled to make.","在当时，这份安稳取决于威廉家能不能交出一笔越来越吃力的费用。"],[" A school fee is a figure on a list, but for a farming family it also belongs to the budget for food, transport, tools, and seed.","学费是单子上的一个数字，对种地的家庭来说，它又要和吃饭、交通、农具、种子一起算进家里的账。"],[" When a harvest falls short, many of those costs stay where they were.","收成不够时，许多开销一分也不会少。"],[" Money that might have paid for a term at school has to be used before the end of the week to buy something to eat.","本来能交一学期学费的钱，可能在这个星期还没过完的时候，就得拿去买吃的。"]],"translation":"在当时，这份安稳取决于威廉家能不能交出一笔越来越吃力的费用。学费是单子上的一个数字，对种地的家庭来说，它又要和吃饭、交通、农具、种子一起算进家里的账。收成不够时，许多开销一分也不会少。本来能交一学期学费的钱，可能在这个星期还没过完的时候，就得拿去买吃的。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Missing school has an effect beyond losing a seat in the classroom.","离开学校，损失的不只是教室里的一个座位。"],[" Lessons continue while the student is away.","学生不在，课照样往下上。"],[" Friends move on to the next set of exercises.","朋友们已经做上了下一套练习。"],[" A person who returns after a long gap may have to learn new things while catching up on older work.","隔了很久再回到学校的人，可能一边要学新的内容，一边得补旧课。"],[" Even a student who reads every day misses the chance to check an answer with someone who can explain the mistake.","就算坚持每天看书，也少了一个可以帮忙核对答案、讲清错在哪里的人。"]],"translation":"离开学校，损失的不只是教室里的一个座位。学生不在，课照样往下上。朋友们已经做上了下一套练习。隔了很久再回到学校的人，可能一边要学新的内容，一边得补旧课。就算坚持每天看书，也少了一个可以帮忙核对答案、讲清错在哪里的人。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["William had been pleased to reach secondary school.","威廉原本很高兴能上中学。"],[" He wanted to continue when he could no longer attend as before.","无法像从前一样去学校时，他仍想继续学习。"],[" There were books he could try to read on his own.","他还能试着自己读一些书。"],[" That choice gave him some control over what to study, and it made him responsible for finding his own way through difficult material.","这样做，他可以决定要学什么，也得自己想办法读懂难的内容。"],[" He was still a student in the ordinary sense of someone learning a subject.","只要还在学习一门东西，他就依然是个学生。"],[" The room, timetable, and next day's lesson now had to be found in a different way.","只是上课的房间、课表和明天要学的内容，都得另想办法找。"],[" It would take time for this unexpected form of study to lead him to a windmill.","这种原先没想到的学习方式，还要过一段时间才会把他带到风车面前。"]],"translation":"威廉原本很高兴能上中学。无法像从前一样去学校时，他仍想继续学习。他还能试着自己读一些书。这样做，他可以决定要学什么，也得自己想办法读懂难的内容。只要还在学习一门东西，他就依然是个学生。只是上课的房间、课表和明天要学的内容，都得另想办法找。这种原先没想到的学习方式，还要过一段时间才会把他带到风车面前。"}],"terms":[{"term":"school fee","meaning":"学费","usage":"fee 是为特定服务付的钱，常用复数 school fees；fare 指乘车或乘船等的费用。","example":"The harvest did not bring in enough to pay the school fees.","exampleZh":"收成带来的收入不够支付学费。","meaningEn":"Money charged for attending a school.","usageEn":"School fees is common in the plural. A fare is the charge for a journey rather than a service such as schooling."},{"term":"fall short","meaning":"不足、未达到目标","usage":"fall short of + 目标或预期；fall behind 则表示进度落在后面。","example":"The money raised fell short of what the repairs would cost.","exampleZh":"筹到的钱不够支付维修费用。","forms":["falls short"],"meaningEn":"To be insufficient or fail to reach a target.","usageEn":"Fall short of introduces the target. Fall behind usually means failing to keep pace with a schedule or another person."},{"term":"catch up on","meaning":"补上落下的事情","usage":"catch up on homework 强调补做；catch up with a person 指赶上对方或聊聊近况。","example":"He used the weekend to catch up on his reading.","exampleZh":"他利用周末补上没读完的内容。","forms":["catching up on"],"meaningEn":"To do work you previously missed or left unfinished.","usageEn":"Catch up on homework means complete accumulated work. Catch up with someone can mean reach them or exchange news."},{"term":"attend","meaning":"上学、出席","usage":"attend school 或 attend a class 直接接宾语；attend to somebody 则指照顾或处理。","example":"She could no longer attend school every day.","exampleZh":"她没法再每天去上学了。","meaningEn":"To go to school, a lesson, or an event.","usageEn":"Attend school takes a direct object. Attend to means deal with a task or look after a person."}],"glossary":[["secondary school","中学"],["timetable","课表"],["school fee","学费"],["fall short","低于预期，不足"],["catch up on","补上，赶上"],["attend","上学，出席"]]},{"en":"When Grain Became Scarce","zh":"粮食紧缺的时候","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["A bad harvest can be seen in a field.","收成不好，在田里就能看出来。"],[" A food crisis is also visible in places where no plants are growing.","粮食危机还会出现在没有庄稼生长的地方。"],[" It appears in the price of a bag of maize and in the distance people travel to buy it.","它体现在一袋玉米的价钱里，也体现在人们得走多远才能买到粮食。"],[" A household can have money and still have trouble finding grain.","一家手里有钱，却可能买不到玉米。"],[" Another household can live near a market and be unable to pay what the sellers are asking.","另一家就住在市场旁，却可能付不起卖家要的价。"],[" The crisis William's family faced in 2001 and 2002 involved both the amount of food available and people's access to it.","2001 到 2002 年，威廉家遭遇的危机，既和粮食总量有关，也和人们能不能买到粮食有关。"]],"translation":"收成不好，在田里就能看出来。粮食危机还会出现在没有庄稼生长的地方。它体现在一袋玉米的价钱里，也体现在人们得走多远才能买到粮食。一家手里有钱，却可能买不到玉米。另一家就住在市场旁，却可能付不起卖家要的价。2001 到 2002 年，威廉家遭遇的危机，既和粮食总量有关，也和人们能不能买到粮食有关。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["A joint assessment by the United Nations food and agriculture agencies in 2002 described several pressures on Malawi.","2002 年，联合国的粮农机构做了一次联合调查，指出马拉维同时面临几方面的压力。"],[" The previous harvest had been poor. Maize stocks were low.","上一次收成很差，玉米库存很低。"],[" Rains arrived late in many areas, floods affected some districts, and a dry period followed in early 2002.","许多地方雨季来得迟，一些地区发生了洪水，2002 年初又有一段干旱期。"],[" Rising prices made every problem harder for families that needed to buy part of their food.","需要买一部分口粮的家庭遇上价格上涨，所有问题都变得更难应付了。"],[" Even when some fields began producing again, many people still needed help.","有些田地开始恢复生产后，依然有许多人需要援助。"]],"translation":"2002 年，联合国的粮农机构做了一次联合调查，指出马拉维同时面临几方面的压力。上一次收成很差，玉米库存很低。许多地方雨季来得迟，一些地区发生了洪水，2002 年初又有一段干旱期。需要买一部分口粮的家庭遇上价格上涨，所有问题都变得更难应付了。有些田地开始恢复生产后，依然有许多人需要援助。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["A farming family has to decide when to eat what it has and when to save it.","农家得决定，手里的粮食什么时候该吃，什么时候得留。"],[" Eating maize before it is fully mature can make a difference today.","玉米还没完全成熟就摘下来吃，可以暂时解一天的急。"],[" It also leaves less to harvest and keep for later.","留到收获时可以储藏的粮食也就少了。"],[" Selling a useful object might pay for food for a short time. The object disappears from a household that may need it to make a living after the emergency has passed.","卖掉一件有用的东西，可能换几天吃的，但危机过去之后，一家人或许原本还要靠那件东西谋生。"]],"translation":"农家得决定，手里的粮食什么时候该吃，什么时候得留。玉米还没完全成熟就摘下来吃，可以暂时解一天的急。留到收获时可以储藏的粮食也就少了。卖掉一件有用的东西，可能换几天吃的，但危机过去之后，一家人或许原本还要靠那件东西谋生。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["William's windmill is sometimes introduced as a response to drought.","人们介绍威廉的风车时，有时会说它是为应对干旱而造的。"],[" That description points to the importance of water in his life.","这句话说明了水在他生活里的重要性。"],[" The food emergency itself had several causes.","粮食危机本身有好几种成因。"],[" A machine capable of pumping water could address one piece of a large problem.","会抽水的机器，只能解决这个大问题里的一部分。"],[" The early machine that William actually built had a smaller, clear job. It made electricity for light.","威廉最早真正造出来的机器，任务小一些，也很明确，就是发电照明。"],[" Keeping those two stages in view gives the family, the emergency, and the invention their proper places in the story.","把这两个阶段都记在心里，才能看清一家人的处境、粮食紧缺和发明之间的关系。"]],"translation":"人们介绍威廉的风车时，有时会说它是为应对干旱而造的。这句话说明了水在他生活里的重要性。粮食危机本身有好几种成因。会抽水的机器，只能解决这个大问题里的一部分。威廉最早真正造出来的机器，任务小一些，也很明确，就是发电照明。把这两个阶段都记在心里，才能看清一家人的处境、粮食紧缺和发明之间的关系。"}],"terms":[{"term":"scarce","meaning":"稀缺、难以取得","usage":"become scarce 指供应变紧；scarce 不一定表示完全没有。副词 scarcely 意为几乎不。","example":"Clean water became scarce late in the dry season.","exampleZh":"旱季后期，干净的水变得稀缺。","meaningEn":"In short supply and hard to obtain.","usageEn":"A resource can become scarce while some of it remains available. The adverb scarcely means hardly or almost not."},{"term":"stocks","meaning":"库存、储备","usage":"food stocks 或 grain stocks 常用复数；stock prices 中 stocks 则指股票。","example":"Local food stocks fell faster than expected.","exampleZh":"当地的粮食储备下降得比预期快。","meaningEn":"Quantities of supplies kept for future use.","usageEn":"Food stocks and grain stocks commonly use the plural. In finance, stocks can mean company shares."},{"term":"mature","meaning":"作物成熟、长成","usage":"作动词可不接宾语；对水果来说 ripe 更强调成熟到可以食用。","example":"The maize would take another month to mature.","exampleZh":"玉米还要一个月才能成熟。","meaningEn":"To reach the stage of full development.","usageEn":"The verb can stand without an object, as in the maize matured. Ripe describes fruit ready to eat more specifically."},{"term":"make a living","meaning":"谋生","usage":"make a living by doing... 说明途径，make a living as... 说明职业。","example":"Many families made a living by growing and selling vegetables.","exampleZh":"许多家庭种菜卖菜谋生。","meaningEn":"To earn enough to support yourself.","usageEn":"Make a living by doing something names the method. Make a living as a farmer names the occupation."}],"glossary":[["scarce","稀缺的"],["assessment","评估，调查"],["stocks","储备，库存"],["mature","成熟的"],["make a living","谋生"],["emergency","紧急情况，危机"]]},{"en":"A Library Nearby","zh":"附近的一间图书馆","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["William found lessons in a local library after he stopped attending school.","不再去学校上课之后，威廉在当地的图书馆里找到了可以学的东西。"],[" Imagine the practical difference between finding no books at all and finding even a few that you can return to.","想想看，手头一本书都没有，和有几本书可以反复读，两者的实际差别有多大。"],[" A book can wait while a difficult paragraph is read again.","难懂的一段，可以从头再读，书会等你。"],[" The same drawing is there the next time you open it.","下次翻开，插图还在原处。"],[" You can study a subject on a day when you have no teacher and come back to a question a week later.","就算当天没有老师，也可以学一门新东西。一周以后，还可以回来看看当初没想通的题。"]],"translation":"不再去学校上课之后，威廉在当地的图书馆里找到了可以学的东西。想想看，手头一本书都没有，和有几本书可以反复读，两者的实际差别有多大。难懂的一段，可以从头再读，书会等你。下次翻开，插图还在原处。就算当天没有老师，也可以学一门新东西。一周以后，还可以回来看看当初没想通的题。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["The library and the school offered different kinds of help.","图书馆和学校能给人的帮助不一样。"],[" A school usually tells students where to start and when they have learned enough to move on.","学校一般会告诉学生从哪里开始、学到什么程度就能往下走。"],[" A library leaves many of those choices to the reader.","图书馆把许多选择留给读者。"],[" A book written for older students may assume knowledge that a younger reader has yet to gain.","写给高年级的书，可能默认读者懂得一些低年级学生还没学过的内容。"],[" Another book may explain the same idea in a picture that is easier to follow.","另一本书或许用了一张更容易读懂的图来讲同一个概念。"],[" Moving between books can become part of learning.","在不同的书之间来回查找，也就成了学习的一部分。"]],"translation":"图书馆和学校能给人的帮助不一样。学校一般会告诉学生从哪里开始、学到什么程度就能往下走。图书馆把许多选择留给读者。写给高年级的书，可能默认读者懂得一些低年级学生还没学过的内容。另一本书或许用了一张更容易读懂的图来讲同一个概念。在不同的书之间来回查找，也就成了学习的一部分。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["There was also a question of language.","还有语言上的困难。"],[" William was studying from science books in English at a time when reading every line comfortably was difficult.","当时，威廉看的是英文科学书，要轻松读懂每一行并不容易。"],[" A reader in that situation can spend so much effort on individual words that the main idea slips away.","读者在这种情况下，可能在一个个单词上花了太多力气，反倒顾不上理解全段的意思。"],[" Pictures, labels, repeated examples, and knowledge of familiar objects can make the path through the text shorter.","插图、图注、反复出现的例子，以及对熟悉物件的了解，都会让阅读省力一些。"],[" It becomes possible to understand an important part and leave a harder sentence for the next visit.","这样，人就可以先弄懂重要的一部分，把更难的句子留到下次再看。"]],"translation":"还有语言上的困难。当时，威廉看的是英文科学书，要轻松读懂每一行并不容易。读者在这种情况下，可能在一个个单词上花了太多力气，反倒顾不上理解全段的意思。插图、图注、反复出现的例子，以及对熟悉物件的了解，都会让阅读省力一些。这样，人就可以先弄懂重要的一部分，把更难的句子留到下次再看。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["The library did more than give William a room in which to read. It made a new kind of question possible.","图书馆让威廉有地方看书，也让他能提出以前想不到的问题。"],[" If a book described a machine, he could try to learn what job each part did and whether something similar was possible at home.","如果书里介绍了一台机器，他可以试着弄明白每个零件负责什么，以及在家乡能不能做个类似的东西。"],[" The more he knew about the things near him, the more useful a book from far away could become.","他越了解身边的物件，来自远方的一本书就可能越有用。"],[" The meeting of those two kinds of knowledge was the beginning of his project.","这两种知识碰到一起，他的项目也就有了开端。"]],"translation":"图书馆让威廉有地方看书，也让他能提出以前想不到的问题。如果书里介绍了一台机器，他可以试着弄明白每个零件负责什么，以及在家乡能不能做个类似的东西。他越了解身边的物件，来自远方的一本书就可能越有用。这两种知识碰到一起，他的项目也就有了开端。"}],"terms":[{"term":"assume","meaning":"默认、在未证实情况下假定","usage":"assume + that 从句可指出当时未经证实的想法；presume 通常暗示根据某种理由推定。","example":"I assumed the library was closed because the door was shut.","exampleZh":"门关着，我以为图书馆闭馆了。","meaningEn":"To take something to be true without checking it first.","usageEn":"Assume that introduces the unverified belief. Presume may suggest that there are some grounds for the belief."},{"term":"slip away","meaning":"悄然离开、在不知不觉中消失","usage":"人可悄悄离开，机会或时间也可 slip away；后者强调没留意便错过。","example":"If we waited any longer, the opportunity might slip away.","exampleZh":"再等下去，机会可能就悄悄溜走了。","forms":["slips away"],"meaningEn":"To leave quietly or disappear before anyone notices.","usageEn":"A person can slip away from a room. Time or an opportunity can slip away while your attention is elsewhere."},{"term":"label","forms":["labels"],"meaning":"图注、标签","usage":"图中紧挨零件的文字可叫 label；caption 通常是整幅图下面的说明。","example":"Each part in the diagram had a short label.","exampleZh":"图中每个零件旁都有简短标注。","meaningEn":"A short piece of text identifying an item or part of a diagram.","usageEn":"A label points to an individual part. A caption usually describes the illustration as a whole."},{"term":"leave something for later","meaning":"把某件事留待以后处理","usage":"leave 此处表示暂不处理；for later 指日后需要时再做。","example":"She read the instructions first and left the difficult questions for later.","exampleZh":"她先读说明，把难题留到以后再处理。","forms":["leave a harder sentence for the next visit"],"meaningEn":"To postpone dealing with something until another time.","usageEn":"Leave means let the task or question remain unfinished. For later identifies when you intend to return to it."}],"glossary":[["assume","假定，默认"],["slip away","溜走，此处指没抓住"],["label","标签，图注"],["individual","单个的"],["comfortably","轻松地"],["leave something for later","把某事留待以后"]]},{"en":"What the Picture Showed","zh":"那张图画着什么","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["One book William found was called Using Energy.","威廉找到的一本书叫《利用能源》。"],[" A picture of a windmill gave him something concrete to study.","里面的一幅风车图给了他一个可以仔细研究的对象。"],[" He could see that the blades were set above the ground and fixed to a structure.","他看得出来，叶片被架在高处，固定在某种结构上。"],[" He could also see a connection between a form of motion he knew well, the movement of air, and a form of power that many homes around him did not have.","他还看到，自己熟悉的空气流动，和周围许多人家用不上的电力之间，原来可以建立联系。"],[" The picture gave him a place to begin thinking.","那幅图给了他一个可以着手思考的地方。"]],"translation":"威廉找到的一本书叫《利用能源》。里面的一幅风车图给了他一个可以仔细研究的对象。他看得出来，叶片被架在高处，固定在某种结构上。他还看到，自己熟悉的空气流动，和周围许多人家用不上的电力之间，原来可以建立联系。那幅图给了他一个可以着手思考的地方。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["A useful way to read a machine drawing is to start at its edges.","读机器示意图，有个有用的办法，就是从两头看起。"],[" Something enters from outside. Something else becomes available at the end.","有什么东西从外面进来，最后又有什么东西可供使用。"],[" Inside are pieces that carry the change from one step to the next.","中间的零件把变化从一步传到下一步。"],[" In a simple wind generator, air moves past blades.","在一台简单的风力发电机里，空气从叶片旁流过。"],[" The blades turn a shaft or drive another moving part.","叶片带动轴转动，或者带动另一件活动的零件。"],[" That movement reaches a generator. An electrical device connected to the generator can use some of the energy that began in the wind.","这股转动传到发电机，接在发电机上的电器，就可以用到一部分原来存在于风里的能量。"]],"translation":"读机器示意图，有个有用的办法，就是从两头看起。有什么东西从外面进来，最后又有什么东西可供使用。中间的零件把变化从一步传到下一步。在一台简单的风力发电机里，空气从叶片旁流过。叶片带动轴转动，或者带动另一件活动的零件。这股转动传到发电机，接在发电机上的电器，就可以用到一部分原来存在于风里的能量。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["The drawing also leaves things out.","图上也会省去一些东西。"],[" It may show a straight line where a real builder has to find a strong piece of material and fasten it against movement.","图里一根直线，实际造的时候，可能需要找一块结实的材料，再牢牢固定住。"],[" It may use a symbol for a generator without giving the reader a place to obtain one.","图里可能用一个符号代表发电机，却不会告诉读者去哪里找来这么一台。"],[" It rarely explains what happens when the wind is weak for a long time or rises suddenly.","图画也很少解释，风弱很久，或者突然变大时，机器会怎样。"],[" Those questions become important as soon as the idea is carried outdoors.","等到真想把这个主意搬到室外，这些问题立刻就变重要了。"]],"translation":"图上也会省去一些东西。图里一根直线，实际造的时候，可能需要找一块结实的材料，再牢牢固定住。图里可能用一个符号代表发电机，却不会告诉读者去哪里找来这么一台。图画也很少解释，风弱很久，或者突然变大时，机器会怎样。等到真想把这个主意搬到室外，这些问题立刻就变重要了。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["William could use the illustration to work out what kinds of parts he would need.","威廉可以用插图来判断自己需要哪几类零件。"],[" The parts in the book and the parts he could actually obtain had different histories and shapes.","书里的零件和实际找得到的东西，来历不同，形状也不同。"],[" Reading the diagram well meant understanding its connections.","读懂示意图，关键是弄懂各部分怎么连在一起。"],[" Once he saw that a blade had to turn something and a generator had to be turned, he could begin looking for pieces that performed those jobs.","他明白叶片得带动一样东西转，发电机也必须被带着转，于是就可以去找能完成这些任务的零件。"],[" That was a question the village could sometimes answer better than the book.","这个问题，有时村里给出的答案比书里的还好。"]],"translation":"威廉可以用插图来判断自己需要哪几类零件。书里的零件和实际找得到的东西，来历不同，形状也不同。读懂示意图，关键是弄懂各部分怎么连在一起。他明白叶片得带动一样东西转，发电机也必须被带着转，于是就可以去找能完成这些任务的零件。这个问题，有时村里给出的答案比书里的还好。"}],"terms":[{"term":"concrete","meaning":"具体、可以观察到的","usage":"a concrete example 指具体例子；作不可数名词时 concrete 才是混凝土。","example":"The drawing gave him a concrete idea of how the pieces fitted.","exampleZh":"这幅图让他具体明白了各零件如何配合。","meaningEn":"Specific enough to observe, describe, or illustrate clearly.","usageEn":"A concrete example shows an idea in a particular situation. The noun concrete also names a building material."},{"term":"shaft","meaning":"轴、转轴","usage":"a rotating shaft 传递旋转；axle 更特指安装或承托车轮的轴。","example":"The blades turned a shaft inside the housing.","exampleZh":"叶片带动外壳中的一根转轴。","meaningEn":"A rod or spindle that transmits rotating motion.","usageEn":"Rotating shaft is common in machinery. An axle is more specifically a shaft or support on which wheels are mounted."},{"term":"fasten against movement","forms":["fasten it against movement"],"meaning":"固定住，以免移动","usage":"fasten A to B 表示把 A 固定到 B；against movement 此处补充要防止的情况。","example":"Fasten the strip to the frame so it cannot shift.","exampleZh":"把条带固定在框架上，让它无法移动。","meaningEn":"To secure a part so it cannot shift.","usageEn":"Fasten A to B identifies what the part is attached to. Against movement tells you what the fastening prevents."},{"term":"obtain","meaning":"取得、弄到","usage":"比 get 正式，常见 obtain permission 或 obtain a replacement；可用 from 说明来源。","example":"She obtained a spare wheel from a local repair shop.","exampleZh":"她从当地修理店弄到一个备用车轮。","meaningEn":"To acquire or secure something.","usageEn":"Obtain is more formal than get and often goes with permission or supplies. From introduces where something came from."}],"glossary":[["concrete","具体的，可看见摸得着的"],["shaft","转轴"],["fasten","固定，系牢"],["illustration","插图"],["obtain","获得，找到"],["perform","执行，完成"]]},{"en":"Power without a Socket","zh":"没有插座的电","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["A person who usually meets electricity at a wall socket can switch on a lamp without seeing how its electricity is made.","平时在墙上插座取电的人，可以随手开灯，完全不用看电是怎么发出来的。"],[" Generators, wires, and the people who keep them working lie at some distance from the room.","发电机、电线和维护它们的人，都离那间屋子有一段距离。"],[" For William's family, a connection to the grid was absent.","威廉家没有接入电网。"],[" If they wanted electric light at home, one possible approach was to bring a much smaller source of power close to the place where it would be used.","如果他们想在家用上电灯，一个可能的办法，是在用电的地方附近找一个小得多的电源。"]],"translation":"平时在墙上插座取电的人，可以随手开灯，完全不用看电是怎么发出来的。发电机、电线和维护它们的人，都离那间屋子有一段距离。威廉家没有接入电网。如果他们想在家用上电灯，一个可能的办法，是在用电的地方附近找一个小得多的电源。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Consider a bicycle lamp that works while the wheel turns.","想想一种随着车轮转动才会发亮的自行车灯。"],[" The rider supplies energy by pushing the pedals. A small generator, often called a dynamo in this setting, receives some of the motion and sends electricity to the lamp.","骑车人踩踏板提供能量，一台小发电装置接收一部分转动，再把电送给灯。用在这里的小发电机通常叫自行车发电机。"],[" The light tends to change as the rider changes speed.","骑车速度一变，灯光亮度也往往会变。"],[" When the cycle stands still, a simple system of this kind supplies no new energy.","车停住了，这种简单的系统就不会再提供新的能量。"],[" The lamp has shown something important about where its electricity comes from.","那盏灯就这样展示了一件重要的事，让人看见它的电从哪里来。"]],"translation":"想想一种随着车轮转动才会发亮的自行车灯。骑车人踩踏板提供能量，一台小发电装置接收一部分转动，再把电送给灯。用在这里的小发电机通常叫自行车发电机。骑车速度一变，灯光亮度也往往会变。车停住了，这种简单的系统就不会再提供新的能量。那盏灯就这样展示了一件重要的事，让人看见它的电从哪里来。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["William could ask whether the rider's effort had to come from a human being.","威廉可以进一步问一个问题，一定得由人来踩吗？"],[" The bicycle was already evidence that turning a small generator could light a bulb.","自行车已经证明，转动一台小发电机，就能点亮灯泡。"],[" Now he needed another way to make it turn.","现在他需要的是另一种让它转起来的办法。"],[" Wind, which arrives without a rider, could push on a set of blades.","风不需要骑车人就会吹来，它可以推着一组叶片动。"],[" In theory those blades could drive the dynamo.","按道理说，这些叶片可以带动小发电机。"],[" The question was how to connect the two so that the wind turned the dynamo fast enough.","问题在于该怎么把两者连起来，让风带着发电机转得足够快。"]],"translation":"威廉可以进一步问一个问题，一定得由人来踩吗？自行车已经证明，转动一台小发电机，就能点亮灯泡。现在他需要的是另一种让它转起来的办法。风不需要骑车人就会吹来，它可以推着一组叶片动。按道理说，这些叶片可以带动小发电机。问题在于该怎么把两者连起来，让风带着发电机转得足够快。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["A generator and a bulb also have to suit each other.","发电机和灯泡还得互相匹配。"],[" A light designed for a large source of electricity might do very little when connected to a small dynamo.","一个为大电源设计的灯，接在小发电机上可能几乎没有反应。"],[" A modest lamp gives a model a sensible first task.","功率不高的小灯，很适合作为模型的第一个任务。"],[" Once a machine has met that task, a builder can think about whether it can supply more.","完成了这一步，再来考虑机器能不能多供些电。"],[" So a little device made for a bicycle gave William both a real part and a useful limit.","因此，一件为自行车做的小装置，既给了威廉一个真正能用的零件，也帮他找到了一个实际的范围。"],[" It helped him define a project that could actually be started with the materials around him.","有了这个范围，他就可以用身边的材料把项目开起来。"]],"translation":"发电机和灯泡还得互相匹配。一个为大电源设计的灯，接在小发电机上可能几乎没有反应。功率不高的小灯，很适合作为模型的第一个任务。完成了这一步，再来考虑机器能不能多供些电。因此，一件为自行车做的小装置，既给了威廉一个真正能用的零件，也帮他找到了一个实际的范围。有了这个范围，他就可以用身边的材料把项目开起来。"}],"terms":[{"term":"socket","meaning":"插座","usage":"plug 指插头，socket 或美语 outlet 指插座；lamp socket 也可以指灯座。","example":"There was only one working socket in the room.","exampleZh":"这个房间只有一个可用的插座。","meaningEn":"A fitting that accepts a plug or another electrical component.","usageEn":"A plug fits into a wall socket, called an outlet in American English. A lamp socket holds a bulb."},{"term":"at some distance","meaning":"相隔一段距离","usage":"可接 from，说明与什么分隔；in the distance 则指在远处的视野或听觉范围内。","example":"The switch was mounted at some distance from the lamp.","exampleZh":"开关装在离灯有一段距离的地方。","meaningEn":"Some way away from a place or object.","usageEn":"From introduces the reference point. In the distance describes something you can see or hear far away."},{"term":"dynamo","meaning":"小型发电机","usage":"bicycle dynamo 是自行车用来给车灯供电的装置；严格分类时 dynamo 原指产生直流的发电机。","example":"The bicycle dynamo powered the front light as the wheel turned.","exampleZh":"车轮转动时，自行车的小发电机给前灯供电。","meaningEn":"A small device that generates electricity from motion.","usageEn":"A bicycle dynamo powers a lamp as the wheel turns. Strictly speaking, a dynamo is a generator that produces direct current."},{"term":"stand still","meaning":"保持静止、不转动","usage":"still 作形容词表示不动；standstill 是名词，如 come to a standstill（完全停止）。","example":"The wheel stood still after the belt slipped off.","exampleZh":"皮带滑脱后，轮子就停住不动了。","forms":["stands still"],"meaningEn":"To stop moving or remain motionless.","usageEn":"Still is an adjective here. Standstill is a noun, as in come to a standstill."}],"glossary":[["socket","插座"],["at some distance","相隔一段距离"],["dynamo","小型发电机"],["pedal","踏板；踩踏板"],["stand still","静止不动"],["modest","适度的，不大的"]]},{"en":"Three Jobs for One Machine","zh":"一台机器的三个任务","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Before a project like William's can be a success, it helps to know what the parts have to achieve.","像威廉这样的项目，想做成功，最好先知道各处的零件要完成哪些任务。"],[" The first job is to catch enough of the moving air. The second is to pass that movement on. The third is to turn some of the movement into electricity and get it to the point of use.","第一项是借到足够的风力，第二项是把转动传下去，第三项是把一部分转动的能量变成电，再送到要用电的地方。"],[" A fault at any one stage can make it look as though the entire machine has failed.","其中任何一环出了毛病，都可能让整台机器看起来像是坏了。"]],"translation":"像威廉这样的项目，想做成功，最好先知道各处的零件要完成哪些任务。第一项是借到足够的风力，第二项是把转动传下去，第三项是把一部分转动的能量变成电，再送到要用电的地方。其中任何一环出了毛病，都可能让整台机器看起来像是坏了。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Catching air might sound like putting a flat board in the wind.","借风听着像是在风里竖起一块平板。"],[" A blade has a more specific task.","叶片要做的事更具体。"],[" The force of the air on it has to help it turn around the centre of the machine.","风作用在叶片上的力，得帮助它绕着机器的中心转动。"],[" Part of that force has to act in the direction of rotation.","其中一部分力得顺着叶片转动的方向起作用。"],[" If it is hard for the blades to get moving at all, the next part of the machine never gets the chance to do its work.","叶片若压根难以启动，下一部分就没有机会发挥作用。"]],"translation":"借风听着像是在风里竖起一块平板。叶片要做的事更具体。风作用在叶片上的力，得帮助它绕着机器的中心转动。其中一部分力得顺着叶片转动的方向起作用。叶片若压根难以启动，下一部分就没有机会发挥作用。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Passing on movement brings its own choices.","把转动传下去，也有好几种选择。"],[" The blades may turn at a different speed from the speed that suits a particular generator.","叶片的转速，可能和某台发电机最合适的转速不同。"],[" A wheel, belt, or direct contact can carry the motion across.","可以用轮子、皮带或彼此接触的零件传递转动。"],[" Some energy is lost along the way.","一部分能量会在途中损失。"],[" A belt may slip, a moving wheel may rub where it should run freely, and loose supports may allow the parts to shift apart.","皮带可能打滑，转轮可能蹭到本来不该碰到的地方，松动的支架也可能让接合的部件偏离原位。"],[" Watching the machine from a safe position tells a builder where to look next.","从安全的位置观察机器，可以帮建造者判断接下来该查哪里。"]],"translation":"把转动传下去，也有好几种选择。叶片的转速，可能和某台发电机最合适的转速不同。可以用轮子、皮带或彼此接触的零件传递转动。一部分能量会在途中损失。皮带可能打滑，转轮可能蹭到本来不该碰到的地方，松动的支架也可能让接合的部件偏离原位。从安全的位置观察机器，可以帮建造者判断接下来该查哪里。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["The last job belongs to the electrical circuit.","最后一项任务交给了电路。"],[" A useful current needs a path through the lamp and back to the source.","要形成可用的电流，需要一条穿过灯并回到电源的通路。"],[" One poor connection in that path can leave the lamp dark.","这条路上只要有一个地方接触不良，灯可能就是暗的。"],[" It helps to imagine William looking at these jobs separately.","可以想象把这些任务分别摆在威廉面前。"],[" Turning blades are definite progress.","叶片转动了，是确实的进展。"],[" A working generator is another step.","发电机开始工作，又往前走了一步。"],[" A light that stays bright enough for people to use is a different achievement again.","灯足够亮、亮得足够久，人们可以拿来用，那又是另一项成果。"],[" A series of small questions gives a person something to work on even before the full machine is ready.","只要有这些小问题可以一个个做，一个人在整台机器造好之前，就总能找到手头能推进的工作。"]],"translation":"最后一项任务交给了电路。要形成可用的电流，需要一条穿过灯并回到电源的通路。这条路上只要有一个地方接触不良，灯可能就是暗的。可以想象把这些任务分别摆在威廉面前。叶片转动了，是确实的进展。发电机开始工作，又往前走了一步。灯足够亮、亮得足够久，人们可以拿来用，那又是另一项成果。只要有这些小问题可以一个个做，一个人在整台机器造好之前，就总能找到手头能推进的工作。"}],"terms":[{"term":"rotation","meaning":"旋转、转动","usage":"名词，常用 the rotation of the shaft；rotate 作动词，可作及物或不及物动词。","example":"The rotation of the wheel drove the small generator.","exampleZh":"车轮的转动带动了小发电机。","meaningEn":"Movement around a fixed centre or axis.","usageEn":"The rotation of the shaft names the movement. Rotate can describe a part turning or somebody turning it."},{"term":"direct contact","meaning":"直接接触","usage":"be in direct contact with 强调两物相触；make contact with 也可用于取得联系等其他语境。","example":"The two metal strips worked only when they were in direct contact.","exampleZh":"两条金属片只有直接接触时才起作用。","meaningEn":"Immediate physical contact between two objects.","usageEn":"Be in direct contact with emphasizes that the surfaces touch. Make contact with can also mean communicate with someone."},{"term":"slip","meaning":"打滑、失去摩擦","usage":"皮带或轮子 slip 表示无法维持抓力；slip off 进一步说明脱离原位。","example":"The belt slipped whenever the wheel turned too slowly.","exampleZh":"轮子转得太慢，皮带就打滑。","meaningEn":"To lose grip and move where it should hold.","usageEn":"A belt slips when it loses its grip on the wheel. Slip off specifies that it comes away from its position."},{"term":"electrical circuit","meaning":"电路","usage":"closed circuit 可通电，open circuit 有断点；complete a circuit 指接通电路。","example":"The switch completes the electrical circuit when you press it.","exampleZh":"按下开关就会接通电路。","meaningEn":"A path through which electric current can flow.","usageEn":"A closed circuit provides a complete path. An open circuit has a break in it."}],"glossary":[["force","力，作用力"],["rotation","转动"],["direct contact","直接接触"],["slip","打滑"],["electrical circuit","电路"],["shift apart","移位并分开"]]},{"en":"A Different Kind of Shop","zh":"另一种零件商店","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["In a shop that sells new parts, a builder can ask for an item by name.","在卖新零件的店里，造东西的人可以直接报出配件的名字。"],[" In a pile of scrap, the builder starts with whatever happens to be there.","在一堆废料里，只能从碰巧在那里的一切看起。"],[" A broken bicycle might have a frame strong enough for another job.","一辆坏自行车的车架可能还够结实，可以拿去干另一件事。"],[" A piece of plastic pipe might keep a useful curve even after it can no longer carry water.","一截塑料管即使不能再输水，也可能保留了一段有用的弧度。"],[" The shopper has to be able to describe the job before deciding whether a piece will do.","得先说清需要完成什么任务，才知道捡到的东西能不能用。"]],"translation":"在卖新零件的店里，造东西的人可以直接报出配件的名字。在一堆废料里，只能从碰巧在那里的一切看起。一辆坏自行车的车架可能还够结实，可以拿去干另一件事。一截塑料管即使不能再输水，也可能保留了一段有用的弧度。得先说清需要完成什么任务，才知道捡到的东西能不能用。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["William looked for things he could recover from old machinery and other discarded objects.","威廉在旧机器和其他被丢弃的物件里寻找可回收的材料。"],[" The record of his windmills includes bicycle parts, plastic pipe, wires, wood, and a fan from a tractor.","他的几台风车用过自行车零件、塑料管、电线、木料和拖拉机的风扇。"],[" These objects are easier to understand if you sort them by what they can contribute.","按它们能做的事来想，就容易理解了。"],[" The wood can support a load.","木头可以承重。"],[" The bicycle pieces can allow motion or take it from one point to another.","自行车零件可以让东西转起来，也可以把转动从一处传到另一处。"],[" The plastic can present a shaped surface to the wind.","塑料能用一定的形状迎风。"],[" Each piece has to fit both the job and its neighbours.","每个零件既要胜任自己的工作，也要接得上旁边的零件。"]],"translation":"威廉在旧机器和其他被丢弃的物件里寻找可回收的材料。他的几台风车用过自行车零件、塑料管、电线、木料和拖拉机的风扇。按它们能做的事来想，就容易理解了。木头可以承重。自行车零件可以让东西转起来，也可以把转动从一处传到另一处。塑料能用一定的形状迎风。每个零件既要胜任自己的工作，也要接得上旁边的零件。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Reusing material takes time.","旧料再利用需要花时间。"],[" A part that looks strong from one side may be cracked on the other.","一块材料从正面看很结实，背面也许有裂纹。"],[" Two very good pieces may have sizes that make them difficult to join.","两样各自很好用的东西，也可能因为尺寸不合而难以相接。"],[" A person may have to change a plan because a suitable item is already doing something more important in somebody else's home.","有人原本打算用一样东西，后来发现它在别人家还担着更重要的活儿，计划就得改。"],[" The value of an object depends on who still needs it and what it would cost to replace.","一个物件有多值钱，要看还有谁用得上它，还要看换一个得花多大代价。"]],"translation":"旧料再利用需要花时间。一块材料从正面看很结实，背面也许有裂纹。两样各自很好用的东西，也可能因为尺寸不合而难以相接。有人原本打算用一样东西，后来发现它在别人家还担着更重要的活儿，计划就得改。一个物件有多值钱，要看还有谁用得上它，还要看换一个得花多大代价。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["This way of working explains why the finished machine could not look just like the one in the book.","这样做，也说明了成品为什么不会和书上的样子一模一样。"],[" The picture made the purpose clear. The pile of available parts helped decide the shape.","图片让人看清机器的用途，手里能找到的零件决定了它大概会长成什么样。"],[" William's design developed as he asked what each thing could do and how it might be connected.","威廉一边问每样东西能做什么、该怎么接上去，一边改进设计。"],[" Answers that came easily in a drawing became small problems of judgment.","在图上很容易回答的事，到现实里都成了小小的判断题。"],[" Getting those judgments right was as much a part of the invention as the idea of using the wind.","答好这些题，和先想到可以借风发电一样，都是发明的一部分。"]],"translation":"这样做，也说明了成品为什么不会和书上的样子一模一样。图片让人看清机器的用途，手里能找到的零件决定了它大概会长成什么样。威廉一边问每样东西能做什么、该怎么接上去，一边改进设计。在图上很容易回答的事，到现实里都成了小小的判断题。答好这些题，和先想到可以借风发电一样，都是发明的一部分。"}],"terms":[{"term":"scrap","meaning":"报废的材料、可回收的旧料","usage":"scrap metal 指废金属；a scrap of paper 则指小纸片，语义来自零碎小块。","example":"They built a bracket from scrap metal.","exampleZh":"他们用废金属做了一个支架。","meaningEn":"Discarded material that may still be useful for its parts.","usageEn":"Scrap metal refers to unwanted metal that can be recovered. A scrap of paper is a small piece of paper."},{"term":"discarded","meaning":"已经被丢弃的","usage":"discarded 属于过去分词作定语；比 old 更明确说明原来的使用者已经扔掉它。","example":"A discarded bicycle provided most of the parts.","exampleZh":"一辆废弃自行车提供了大部分零件。","meaningEn":"Thrown away or no longer wanted by its former user.","usageEn":"Discarded is a past participle that can modify a noun. An old part might still be used, while a discarded part has been thrown away."},{"term":"load","meaning":"负载、机器承受的重量或需求","usage":"under load 指承载或工作时；a load of 可口语化地表示许多。","example":"The frame bent slightly under the load.","exampleZh":"承重后，框架略微弯曲。","meaningEn":"The weight, force, or demand that a structure or machine bears.","usageEn":"Under load describes a machine while it is carrying or driving something. A load of can also mean a large quantity in conversation."},{"term":"sort by","forms":["sort them by"],"meaning":"按某种标准归类","usage":"sort A by B 可按用途、大小或来源分类；sort A into B 之后接分出的类别。","example":"Try sorting the parts by the jobs they can do.","exampleZh":"试着按各零件能发挥的作用把它们归类。","meaningEn":"To arrange things according to a feature or criterion.","usageEn":"Sort parts by size names the criterion. Sort the parts into three groups names the resulting categories."}],"glossary":[["scrap","废料；可回收的旧材料"],["recover","找回，回收"],["discarded","被丢弃的"],["contribute","提供，作出贡献"],["load","负荷，重量"],["judgment","判断"]]},{"en":"The Piece Gilbert Brought","zh":"吉尔伯特帮忙买的零件","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["A project can depend on the price of a single object.","一个项目有时会卡在一件东西的价格上。"],[" William could find many useful things among the materials people no longer needed.","别人已经不用的物件里，威廉能找到不少有用的材料。"],[" The dynamo was different.","小发电机不同。"],[" It was a working electrical part, and obtaining one required money he did not have.","它是一件还能工作的电气零件，要弄到手就得花钱，而威廉拿不出这笔钱。"],[" Its size gave a misleading impression of its importance.","它的尺寸容易让人低估它的重要性。"],[" A machine made of large pieces could still depend on something that fitted into a hand.","好些大零件搭起来的机器，仍可能离不开一个手掌就能托住的小东西。"]],"translation":"一个项目有时会卡在一件东西的价格上。别人已经不用的物件里，威廉能找到不少有用的材料。小发电机不同。它是一件还能工作的电气零件，要弄到手就得花钱，而威廉拿不出这笔钱。它的尺寸容易让人低估它的重要性。好些大零件搭起来的机器，仍可能离不开一个手掌就能托住的小东西。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Gilbert, William's friend, helped him get the dynamo.","威廉的朋友吉尔伯特帮他买到了小发电机。"],[" The story of this help is sometimes easy to pass over because the tower and blades make a more striking picture.","人们讲起这个故事，很容易一带而过，因为塔和叶片在照片里更显眼。"],[" Think of it from William's side.","可以站在威廉这边想一想。"],[" He has a way of turning the blades and a reason to expect light from a generator.","他已经有了让叶片转动的办法，也有理由相信发电机能让灯亮起来。"],[" Yet hoping for light leaves him in exactly the same place until he can get the part that produces electricity.","可在他拿到真正发电的零件之前，再多期待也无法推动事情往前走。"],[" Gilbert's help changes which experiment William can actually carry out.","吉尔伯特的帮助，让原本只能设想的实验可以真的做起来了。"]],"translation":"威廉的朋友吉尔伯特帮他买到了小发电机。人们讲起这个故事，很容易一带而过，因为塔和叶片在照片里更显眼。可以站在威廉这边想一想。他已经有了让叶片转动的办法，也有理由相信发电机能让灯亮起来。可在他拿到真正发电的零件之前，再多期待也无法推动事情往前走。吉尔伯特的帮助，让原本只能设想的实验可以真的做起来了。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["A friend can support a project before anyone sees a finished result.","朋友可以在成果出来之前就支持一个项目。"],[" At that stage the evidence may consist of a drawing, an explanation, and a few objects on the ground.","到了那个阶段，看得见的证据可能只有一张图、几句说明和地上的几个零件。"],[" Someone who helps has to accept that the machine might never work.","愿意帮忙的人，得接受机器最后也许用不了。"],[" The risk is modest compared with investments made by large companies, but the value of a purchase depends on the money available to the people making it.","和大公司的投资相比，这承担的风险不算大。但一笔花销有多重，要看出钱的人手头有多少钱。"],[" It mattered to both boys.","对两个男孩来说，这件事都有分量。"]],"translation":"朋友可以在成果出来之前就支持一个项目。到了那个阶段，看得见的证据可能只有一张图、几句说明和地上的几个零件。愿意帮忙的人，得接受机器最后也许用不了。和大公司的投资相比，这承担的风险不算大。但一笔花销有多重，要看出钱的人手头有多少钱。对两个男孩来说，这件事都有分量。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["It is possible to give the machine a single inventor and still tell the story of the people behind it.","即使一台机器有一位明确的发明者，也可以把身后那些帮过他的人讲清楚。"],[" William put the pieces together and made the technical decisions that turned an idea into a working device.","威廉组装了零件，也作出了把想法变成机器的技术决定。"],[" Gilbert helped close a gap the builder could not close alone.","吉尔伯特补上了威廉一个人补不了的缺口。"],[" The school, the library, and the people around them had roles of their own.","学校、图书馆和他们身边的人也各有作用。"],[" At the top of the tower, all of that help became difficult to see.","后来，风车立在塔顶，这些帮助就不容易看见了。"],[" At the moment William needed a dynamo, it was easy to see what it was worth.","然而在威廉缺一台小发电机的时候，它的价值再清楚不过。"]],"translation":"即使一台机器有一位明确的发明者，也可以把身后那些帮过他的人讲清楚。威廉组装了零件，也作出了把想法变成机器的技术决定。吉尔伯特补上了威廉一个人补不了的缺口。学校、图书馆和他们身边的人也各有作用。后来，风车立在塔顶，这些帮助就不容易看见了。然而在威廉缺一台小发电机的时候，它的价值再清楚不过。"}],"terms":[{"term":"depend on","forms":["depends on"],"meaning":"依靠、取决于","usage":"人作主语时常指依赖；结果作主语时常指由某条件决定。","example":"The brightness of the bulb depends on how fast the wheel turns.","exampleZh":"灯泡亮度取决于轮子的转速。","meaningEn":"To rely on somebody or something, or to be determined by a condition.","usageEn":"A person can depend on a friend for help. A result can depend on whether suitable parts are available."},{"term":"carry out","meaning":"实施、执行到底","usage":"常搭配 test、plan、repair；宾语为代词时说 carry it out。","example":"The students carried out a test before rebuilding the model.","exampleZh":"学生在重做模型前先做了一次测试。","meaningEn":"To perform or put a planned action into effect.","usageEn":"Common objects include a test, plan, or repair. Put a pronoun in the middle, as in carry it out."},{"term":"consist of","meaning":"由……组成","usage":"主语是整体，of 后接组成部分；这个搭配通常不用被动。","example":"The frame consists of four pieces of wood and two bolts.","exampleZh":"框架由四块木材和两个螺栓构成。","meaningEn":"To be made up of the listed parts.","usageEn":"The subject is the whole, and of introduces the parts. Consists of already has an active form and does not need a passive."},{"term":"close a gap","meaning":"补足缺口、填补不足","usage":"可用于金钱、资源、能力等抽象差距，常用 close the gap between A and B 比较双方。","example":"A small grant helped close the gap in the school’s budget.","exampleZh":"一笔小额补助填补了学校的预算缺口。","meaningEn":"To make up a shortage or narrow a difference.","usageEn":"Close the gap between A and B identifies the two sides. Here, the gap involves what the project needs and what the builder can afford."}],"glossary":[["depend on","取决于，依靠"],["misleading","容易使人误解的"],["carry out","实施，做完"],["consist of","由……组成"],["investment","投资"],["close a gap","补上缺口"]]},{"en":"Build Something Small First","zh":"先做一个小的","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["A drawing can look complete while a machine is still full of unknowns.","图可能画得很完整，动手造机器时却还有一大堆未知的事。"],[" William tried out the idea on a small scale before relying on a full windmill.","在指望一台完整的风车之前，威廉先小规模地试了试自己的主意。"],[" This mattered because part of the question was very simple.","这一步很重要，因为其中有一个很简单的问题。"],[" Could movement from the air be made to turn a generator and produce a visible result?","他能不能用流动的空气带动发电机，做出看得见的结果？"],[" A small test could answer that question with much less material and work than a tower beside the house.","小试验就能回答这个问题，花的材料和力气都远少于在屋边立一座塔。"]],"translation":"图可能画得很完整，动手造机器时却还有一大堆未知的事。在指望一台完整的风车之前，威廉先小规模地试了试自己的主意。这一步很重要，因为其中有一个很简单的问题。他能不能用流动的空气带动发电机，做出看得见的结果？小试验就能回答这个问题，花的材料和力气都远少于在屋边立一座塔。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["A first model may deal with just one connection.","第一个模型也许只处理一个连接处。"],[" The builder can see a set of blades move and check what happens to the part they are meant to turn.","造模型的人可以看着叶片动，再查叶片本来要带动的零件有没有动。"],[" During a test the result may be brief.","试验中的结果可能只出现一瞬间。"],[" A flicker from a lamp is useful information.","灯短短闪一下，也是有用的信息。"],[" It means a current reached the lamp for a moment.","这意味着那一刻有电流到达了灯。"],[" It can also lead to questions about how fast the generator turned and why the light faded.","接下来还可以追问，当时发电机转得有多快，灯后来为什么又暗了。"],[" A short success gives the next round of work a direction.","短暂的成功给下一轮工作指了一个方向。"]],"translation":"第一个模型也许只处理一个连接处。造模型的人可以看着叶片动，再查叶片本来要带动的零件有没有动。试验中的结果可能只出现一瞬间。灯短短闪一下，也是有用的信息。这意味着那一刻有电流到达了灯。接下来还可以追问，当时发电机转得有多快，灯后来为什么又暗了。短暂的成功给下一轮工作指了一个方向。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Scale changes the questions.","规模变了，问题也就变了。"],[" A model close to the ground is easy to watch and easy to reach when the wind has stopped.","靠近地面的模型容易观察，风停后也容易够到。"],[" Taller supports have to hold more weight and face stronger forces.","更高的支架，既得承更多重量，也要面对更大的作用力。"],[" Larger blades catch more air and can also make the tower shake.","大一些的叶片能借到更多风，也可能把塔晃起来。"],[" Wires have to go farther.","电线得拉得更远。"],[" A machine that can run for a short demonstration may need steadier connections to serve a household over several weeks.","演示时能短暂运转的机器，要给一家人用上几个星期，连接处可能就得更牢靠。"]],"translation":"规模变了，问题也就变了。靠近地面的模型容易观察，风停后也容易够到。更高的支架，既得承更多重量，也要面对更大的作用力。大一些的叶片能借到更多风，也可能把塔晃起来。电线得拉得更远。演示时能短暂运转的机器，要给一家人用上几个星期，连接处可能就得更牢靠。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["The small model is therefore evidence for part of a plan.","所以小模型能为计划的一部分提供证据。"],[" It shows that a particular arrangement can make something happen.","它证明这样安排零件能让事情发生。"],[" It leaves the builder with new work when he moves up to a bigger machine.","等到要做更大的装置时，建造者还有新的活儿。"],[" For William it offered a point between an illustration in a book and a windmill that could be used at home.","对威廉来说，它是书上的图和家里真正用得上的风车之间的一站。"],[" Once a small version had worked, he had a more precise reason to invest time in the larger project.","小版本成功之后，他就有了更具体的理由，把时间花在大项目上。"],[" He could work on changing the scale without having to start again with the question of whether wind could make light.","他可以专心解决变大之后的麻烦，省得从头再问一次风能不能点亮灯。"]],"translation":"所以小模型能为计划的一部分提供证据。它证明这样安排零件能让事情发生。等到要做更大的装置时，建造者还有新的活儿。对威廉来说，它是书上的图和家里真正用得上的风车之间的一站。小版本成功之后，他就有了更具体的理由，把时间花在大项目上。他可以专心解决变大之后的麻烦，省得从头再问一次风能不能点亮灯。"}],"terms":[{"term":"on a small scale","meaning":"以小规模、做个小型版本","usage":"scale 指项目体量；常用 test something on a small scale 说明先小范围试验。","example":"They tried the design on a small scale before building the tower.","exampleZh":"他们先小规模试验设计，然后再建塔。","meaningEn":"Using fewer resources or a smaller scope than a full project.","usageEn":"Testing something on a small scale means trying a limited version first. Scale refers to the size or scope of the work."},{"term":"flicker","meaning":"忽明忽暗、一下下闪烁","usage":"通常表示光线不稳定；flash 往往指一次突然而明亮的闪现。","example":"The lamp flickered when the speed dropped.","exampleZh":"转速一降，灯就开始忽明忽暗。","meaningEn":"To shine with quick, irregular changes in brightness.","usageEn":"A light that flickers repeatedly gets brighter and dimmer. A flash often describes one brief burst of light."},{"term":"fade","forms":["faded"],"meaning":"逐渐变弱、淡去","usage":"可形容光、色彩或声音；fade out 常强调逐渐消失这一过程。","example":"The glow faded as the wheel slowed down.","exampleZh":"轮子慢下来时，那点亮光也渐渐变弱了。","meaningEn":"To become weaker, less vivid, or less noticeable over time.","usageEn":"Light, colour, and sound can all fade. Fade out emphasizes the gradual move toward disappearing."},{"term":"demonstration","meaning":"演示、用实物展示","usage":"give a demonstration of + 操作或装置；公开集会语境也可指示威活动。","example":"She gave a demonstration of how the switch worked.","exampleZh":"她演示了开关的工作原理。","meaningEn":"A practical display of how something works.","usageEn":"Give a demonstration of a device means show it in action. In public affairs, a demonstration can also mean a protest."}],"glossary":[["on a small scale","以较小的规模"],["flicker","闪烁，短暂闪光"],["fade","逐渐变弱"],["demonstration","演示"],["arrangement","组合，安排"],["invest time","投入时间"]]},{"en":"The Shape of a Blade","zh":"叶片的形状","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["A fan and a windmill both have blades, and their familiar shapes make an interesting pair.","风扇和风车都有叶片，把它们放在一起看很有意思。"],[" An electric fan uses power to push air. A windmill uses the moving air to draw power from it.","电风扇用电来推动空气，风车从流动的空气里取得能量。"],[" Because William could recognise useful shapes in objects around him, he could look at pieces from old machinery with a question in mind.","威廉能在身边的东西里辨认出有用的形状，于是可以带着一个问题来看旧机器的零件。"],[" Which pieces were light enough to move and shaped in a way that could work with the wind?","哪些东西既够轻，形状又适合借风转动？"]],"translation":"风扇和风车都有叶片，把它们放在一起看很有意思。电风扇用电来推动空气，风车从流动的空气里取得能量。威廉能在身边的东西里辨认出有用的形状，于是可以带着一个问题来看旧机器的零件。哪些东西既够轻，形状又适合借风转动？"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Plastic pipe is useful to think about because it already has a curve.","塑料管值得想一想，因为它本身有弧度。"],[" The curve means the material offers a different surface to the wind from a flat piece of wood.","弯曲的表面遇上风，和一块平木板产生的效果不同。"],[" A piece of curved plastic still needs to face the right way and to move without striking its neighbour.","弯曲的塑料还是得朝对方向，转动时也不能打到旁边的叶片。"],[" The set of blades has to turn together.","整组叶片得一起转。"],[" If one blade is much heavier than the others, its extra weight pulls the moving set out of balance.","如果有一片比别的重了许多，多出来的重量就会让转动的整组部件失去平衡。"]],"translation":"塑料管值得想一想，因为它本身有弧度。弯曲的表面遇上风，和一块平木板产生的效果不同。弯曲的塑料还是得朝对方向，转动时也不能打到旁边的叶片。整组叶片得一起转。如果有一片比别的重了许多，多出来的重量就会让转动的整组部件失去平衡。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Balance can be felt even in a familiar object.","在熟悉的东西上，也能感觉到平衡的作用。"],[" A washing machine can shake when heavy wet clothes collect on one side of the drum.","湿衣服全堆在洗衣机滚筒的一侧时，机器可能会晃动。"],[" A wheel can shake if its weight is uneven.","重量分布不均的轮子，也可能会晃。"],[" In a windmill, the same kind of motion can affect the support and loosen connections over repeated turns.","风车每转一圈，类似的晃动都可能影响支架，让连接处一点点变松。"],[" This helps explain why the position and size of each blade matter after the machine has begun to move.","这么一想就明白了，机器转起来以后，每个叶片的位置和大小为什么还有那么重要。"]],"translation":"在熟悉的东西上，也能感觉到平衡的作用。湿衣服全堆在洗衣机滚筒的一侧时，机器可能会晃动。重量分布不均的轮子，也可能会晃。风车每转一圈，类似的晃动都可能影响支架，让连接处一点点变松。这么一想就明白了，机器转起来以后，每个叶片的位置和大小为什么还有那么重要。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["The design has to work over a range of winds, too.","这个设计还得能应付不同大小的风。"],[" A gentler wind may have trouble starting a heavy set of blades.","风温和时，可能很难推动很重的叶片组。"],[" A strong gust might put more force on the blades and support than they were meant to handle.","突如其来的一阵大风，可能让叶片和支架承受超过设计范围的力。"],[" William's choice of available materials was only the beginning of this stage.","威廉从找得到的东西里挑出材料，只是这一步的开始。"],[" He also needed to find where those materials performed well enough together.","他还得找出能让这些材料配合着正常运转的方式。"],[" The blades would be one of the most visible parts of the windmill, yet much of the skill behind them lay in judging relationships that could only be seen in motion.","叶片是风车最显眼的部件之一，但藏在后面的许多功夫，要等机器动起来才能看见。"]],"translation":"这个设计还得能应付不同大小的风。风温和时，可能很难推动很重的叶片组。突如其来的一阵大风，可能让叶片和支架承受超过设计范围的力。威廉从找得到的东西里挑出材料，只是这一步的开始。他还得找出能让这些材料配合着正常运转的方式。叶片是风车最显眼的部件之一，但藏在后面的许多功夫，要等机器动起来才能看见。"}],"terms":[{"term":"out of balance","meaning":"失去平衡、不均衡","usage":"be 或 throw something out of balance 强调偏离平衡状态；out of balance 可形容机器或预算。","example":"A heavy blade threw the whole wheel out of balance.","exampleZh":"一片太重的叶片让整个轮子失去了平衡。","meaningEn":"Unevenly weighted or no longer stable.","usageEn":"An object can be out of balance, and a misplaced weight can throw it out of balance. A budget can also be out of balance."},{"term":"uneven","meaning":"不均匀的、不平整的","usage":"uneven weight distribution 指重量分配不均；uneven ground 指地面凹凸不平。","example":"The machine shook because the weight was uneven.","exampleZh":"由于重量分布不均，机器抖了起来。","meaningEn":"Unequal in distribution or irregular across a surface.","usageEn":"Uneven weight distribution puts more weight on some parts than others. Uneven ground has rises or dips."},{"term":"gust","meaning":"一阵骤起的强风","usage":"a gust of wind 可数，gales 持续性通常更强；常与 sudden 或 strong 搭配。","example":"A sudden gust set the loose sheet flapping.","exampleZh":"一阵突起的风吹得松动的薄板拍打起来。","meaningEn":"A sudden, short burst of strong wind.","usageEn":"A gust of wind is countable. A gale usually describes strong wind that is sustained for longer."},{"term":"handle","meaning":"能够承受或应对","usage":"机器能 handle a load 指承受负荷；人能 handle a problem 指处理问题。","example":"The frame was strong enough to handle a heavier motor.","exampleZh":"框架足够结实，可以承载更重的电机。","meaningEn":"To withstand a demand or deal with a problem.","usageEn":"A machine that can handle a load can cope with the strain. A person who handles a problem deals with it."}],"glossary":[["strike","碰撞，打到"],["out of balance","失去平衡"],["drum","滚筒"],["uneven","不均匀的"],["gust","一阵强风"],["handle","承受，处理"]]},{"en":"Making the Turn Count","zh":"让转动发挥作用","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["The wind was now part of the plan.","风已经派上了用场。"],[" William still needed a way of carrying the turn to the dynamo.","威廉还需要让叶片的转动传到小发电机。"],[" A turning blade and a spinning bicycle wheel suggest a connection because each goes round a centre.","转动的叶片和飞转的自行车轮，都绕着一个中心，这让人想到它们可以建立联系。"],[" Their most useful speeds can differ.","可它们最合适的速度或许并不相同。"],[" A blade may catch a steady breeze and turn gradually. A little generator may need to turn faster before the lamp receives enough electricity to be useful.","叶片借着平稳的微风慢慢地转，小发电机可能得转得更快，电灯才有足够的电发挥作用。"]],"translation":"风已经派上了用场。威廉还需要让叶片的转动传到小发电机。转动的叶片和飞转的自行车轮，都绕着一个中心，这让人想到它们可以建立联系。可它们最合适的速度或许并不相同。叶片借着平稳的微风慢慢地转，小发电机可能得转得更快，电灯才有足够的电发挥作用。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["The way a bicycle is built gives an everyday example of changing speed.","自行车提供了一个日常的变速例子。"],[" The rider's feet go round at one rate, and the back wheel can go round at another.","人的脚绕圈是一种速度，后轮绕圈可以是另一种速度。"],[" The sizes of the parts and the way they are joined determine the relationship.","零件的大小和连接方式决定了两种速度的关系。"],[" This makes it possible for a slow movement in one place to drive a faster movement nearby.","这样，一处较慢的动作就能带着旁边的零件更快地动。"],[" A bike that can't be ridden may still have parts that tell this useful mechanical story.","一辆已经骑不了的自行车，零件还可能讲得清这个有用的机械道理。"]],"translation":"自行车提供了一个日常的变速例子。人的脚绕圈是一种速度，后轮绕圈可以是另一种速度。零件的大小和连接方式决定了两种速度的关系。这样，一处较慢的动作就能带着旁边的零件更快地动。一辆已经骑不了的自行车，零件还可能讲得清这个有用的机械道理。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["A fast turn is only part of the result a builder needs.","转得快只是建造者所需结果的一部分。"],[" Consider a belt that drives a wheel well in still air.","想象一根在无风的地方能带动轮子的皮带。"],[" Outside, a frame may bend a little, a joint may shift, or dust may change the surfaces.","到了室外，车架可能有点弯，一处接头可能错位，灰尘也可能改变接触面的情况。"],[" A piece that is too loose can slip. A piece that is held under too much strain can make the machine harder to turn.","太松的零件可能打滑，拉得太紧的零件可能让机器更难转。"],[" The decision has to be tested where the machine actually sits and moves.","到底要怎样装，还要到机器实际运行的地方去试。"]],"translation":"转得快只是建造者所需结果的一部分。想象一根在无风的地方能带动轮子的皮带。到了室外，车架可能有点弯，一处接头可能错位，灰尘也可能改变接触面的情况。太松的零件可能打滑，拉得太紧的零件可能让机器更难转。到底要怎样装，还要到机器实际运行的地方去试。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["It is easy to imagine that the most important work was picking a generator and putting it high in the air.","人们很容易觉得，最重要的活儿就是挑一台发电机，再把它抬到高处。"],[" Much of the challenge was at the points where materials met.","很多难处其实都在材料彼此接触的地方。"],[" William had to make objects with different original jobs share their movement.","威廉必须让原本各有不同用途的东西一起动。"],[" A small tool designed for a bicycle had to turn because of the force of the wind, and connected parts had to keep delivering that motion over and over.","一件为自行车设计的小装置，得靠风的力量转动，相连的零件还得一次又一次地把转动传过去。"],[" The usefulness of the electricity inside the house depended on how well he made these moving pieces cooperate outdoors.","房子里的电有多好用，就取决于他能多好地让屋外这些活动的零件配合起来。"]],"translation":"人们很容易觉得，最重要的活儿就是挑一台发电机，再把它抬到高处。很多难处其实都在材料彼此接触的地方。威廉必须让原本各有不同用途的东西一起动。一件为自行车设计的小装置，得靠风的力量转动，相连的零件还得一次又一次地把转动传过去。房子里的电有多好用，就取决于他能多好地让屋外这些活动的零件配合起来。"}],"terms":[{"term":"at one rate","meaning":"以一种速率","usage":"at + 速率，说明变化或运动有多快；at the same rate 指两者速率相同。","example":"The shaft could turn at one rate while the wheel turned at another.","exampleZh":"转轴和轮子可以分别以不同的速率转动。","meaningEn":"At a particular speed or degree of change.","usageEn":"Use at before a rate. At the same rate means two things change or move equally quickly."},{"term":"mechanical","meaning":"机械的、由部件运动形成的","usage":"常搭配 mechanical energy、mechanical failure；mechanic 则常指修理工。","example":"The pump converted mechanical energy into the movement of water.","exampleZh":"水泵利用机械能推动水流动。","meaningEn":"Related to machines, moving parts, or the energy of motion.","usageEn":"Mechanical energy and mechanical failure are common combinations. A mechanic is a person who repairs machines."},{"term":"joint","meaning":"接头、连接处","usage":"指两个构件相接的地方；a welded joint 是焊接接头，a loose joint 是连接松动处。","example":"One wooden joint needed a stronger bolt.","exampleZh":"有一个木结构接头需要更结实的螺栓。","meaningEn":"The point where two parts of a structure are connected.","usageEn":"A welded joint names the method used to connect the parts. A loose joint is a connection that is no longer firm."},{"term":"under strain","meaning":"处于拉力或压力之下","usage":"技术语境中强调构件受力；人或系统 under strain 表示承受压力。","example":"The wires were under strain whenever the tower swayed.","exampleZh":"塔身一摇晃，电线就被拉紧。","forms":["under too much strain"],"meaningEn":"Subject to tension, force, or sustained pressure.","usageEn":"A component under strain may be stretched or pulled. A person or system under strain is coping with persistent pressure."}],"glossary":[["gradually","逐渐地，缓慢地"],["at one rate","以一种速率"],["mechanical","机械的"],["joint","连接处，接头"],["under strain","承受拉力或压力"],["cooperate","协作，配合"]]},{"en":"Putting the Windmill in the Air","zh":"把风车架到空中","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["A windmill tested near the ground has to be lifted into a better position before it can provide dependable power.","贴近地面试过的风车，需要升到更合适的位置，才可能稳定地提供电力。"],[" The moving air above nearby obstacles may be stronger and steadier.","高过附近障碍物的风，可能更强，也更平稳。"],[" Raising the machine changes the demands on its support.","把机器升高，支架要做到的事就变了。"],[" The tower has to carry the weight of the parts even on a still day.","无风的日子里，塔也要担着零件的重量。"],[" When the blades start turning, the tower also has to deal with changing forces.","叶片开始转动时，塔还必须应付不断变化的作用力。"]],"translation":"贴近地面试过的风车，需要升到更合适的位置，才可能稳定地提供电力。高过附近障碍物的风，可能更强，也更平稳。把机器升高，支架要做到的事就变了。无风的日子里，塔也要担着零件的重量。叶片开始转动时，塔还必须应付不断变化的作用力。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["William used wooden supports to raise his windmill.","威廉用木支架把风车架高了。"],[" In photographs of the early machine the tower can look like a simple shape, with long pieces holding a small collection of parts at the top.","早期机器的照片里，塔看起来是个很简单的形状，几根长木头托着顶端一小堆零件。"],[" From below, the appearance can hide many questions.","从下面看，许多问题都藏在这个外形里。"],[" How can weight be shared among the supports?","重量要怎样分给各根木料？"],[" What stops the structure from leaning?","靠什么让塔不歪？"],[" A point that barely moves in the workshop may work loose after the machine has spent a month outdoors.","在室内试装时几乎不动的一处连接，放在外面过一个月，就可能慢慢松脱。"]],"translation":"威廉用木支架把风车架高了。早期机器的照片里，塔看起来是个很简单的形状，几根长木头托着顶端一小堆零件。从下面看，许多问题都藏在这个外形里。重量要怎样分给各根木料？靠什么让塔不歪？在室内试装时几乎不动的一处连接，放在外面过一个月，就可能慢慢松脱。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["A strong support is useful when a person needs to inspect the machine later.","结实的支架，以后有人检查机器时也有用。"],[" Blades can wear out, wires can come loose, and a generator can eventually need changing.","叶片会磨损，电线会松脱，发电机也可能到了该换的时候。"],[" A good position for catching wind can be an awkward place for maintenance.","适合接风的位置，维修起来可能很不方便。"],[" The machine and its support have to be thought of as something a person will live with.","机器和支架是人以后要长期使用的东西，需要从这一点出发去考虑。"],[" Each adjustment made after a storm or an ordinary week of use teaches the builder something a first test could not show.","暴风雨过后或者平常用了一周之后，每调一次，建造者都能学到第一次测试时看不出来的东西。"]],"translation":"结实的支架，以后有人检查机器时也有用。叶片会磨损，电线会松脱，发电机也可能到了该换的时候。适合接风的位置，维修起来可能很不方便。机器和支架是人以后要长期使用的东西，需要从这一点出发去考虑。暴风雨过后或者平常用了一周之后，每调一次，建造者都能学到第一次测试时看不出来的东西。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["The tower also changed the size of the public experiment.","塔也一下子让更多人看得见这场试验。"],[" Small parts and quiet attempts can stay close to a builder.","小零件和没有声响的尝试，可以只在建造者身边进行。"],[" A tower outside rises into view and gives other people a reason to look up.","屋外的塔立起来，进了大家的视野，让人抬起头去看。"],[" Even someone who had never seen the library book could look at the blades and wonder what they would do.","连从来没见过那本书的人，都能望着叶片，想想它们会做什么。"],[" William had put his answer where the wind could reach it.","威廉把自己的答案放到了风能够到的地方。"],[" If it worked, the result would be visible in another place, in a room below.","如果成功，成果会在另一个地方显现，就在下面的一间屋子里。"]],"translation":"塔也一下子让更多人看得见这场试验。小零件和没有声响的尝试，可以只在建造者身边进行。屋外的塔立起来，进了大家的视野，让人抬起头去看。连从来没见过那本书的人，都能望着叶片，想想它们会做什么。威廉把自己的答案放到了风能够到的地方。如果成功，成果会在另一个地方显现，就在下面的一间屋子里。"}],"terms":[{"term":"dependable","meaning":"可靠、经得起日常使用","usage":"可形容人或设备；dependable supply 强调持续可用，available 只说明当下可获得。","example":"They needed a dependable way to keep the radio running.","exampleZh":"他们需要一种可靠的办法让收音机持续工作。","meaningEn":"Reliable enough to be counted on repeatedly.","usageEn":"A dependable supply keeps working when it is needed. An available supply is one you can access now."},{"term":"work loose","meaning":"逐渐松动","usage":"work 此处表示动作或震动逐渐导致状态变化；come loose 不强调这个累积过程。","example":"The screws worked loose after days of vibration.","exampleZh":"经过连日震动，螺钉渐渐松了。","meaningEn":"To become less firmly attached through repeated movement.","usageEn":"Work suggests a gradual change caused by movement or vibration. Come loose does not specify how it happened."},{"term":"wear out","meaning":"用到磨损、磨坏","usage":"部件可自行 wear out，也可说 use wears it out；人 feel worn out 则是筋疲力尽。","example":"The rubber strip wore out after months of use.","exampleZh":"用了几个月后，橡胶条磨坏了。","meaningEn":"To deteriorate through use until something is no longer effective.","usageEn":"A part can wear out, and repeated use can wear it out. A person who feels worn out is exhausted."},{"term":"maintenance","meaning":"维护、日常保养","usage":"通常不可数；routine maintenance 重在预防故障，repair 是故障出现后的修理。","example":"Regular maintenance kept the old pump working for years.","exampleZh":"定期保养让旧水泵持续用了多年。","meaningEn":"Regular care that keeps equipment in working condition.","usageEn":"Maintenance is normally uncountable. Routine maintenance prevents problems, while repair addresses an existing fault."}],"glossary":[["dependable","可靠的"],["obstacle","障碍物"],["lean","倾斜"],["work loose","逐渐松动"],["wear out","磨损"],["maintenance","维护，保养"]]},{"en":"The Moment the Light Came On","zh":"灯亮起来的那一刻","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["When the windmill produced enough electricity to light a bulb, the result could be seen without anyone needing to understand the entire machine.","风车发出的电足够点亮一个灯泡时，即使不懂整台机器，也看得见结果。"],[" A person standing near the bulb could see it grow bright.","站在灯旁就能看见它亮起来。"],[" The source of that light was outdoors, where the blades were turning.","光的来源在屋外，那里有转动的叶片。"],[" William had shown that he could take energy from the wind and use it in a different form inside his family's home.","威廉证明了自己能从风中取得能量，换一种形式用在家里。"]],"translation":"风车发出的电足够点亮一个灯泡时，即使不懂整台机器，也看得见结果。站在灯旁就能看见它亮起来。光的来源在屋外，那里有转动的叶片。威廉证明了自己能从风中取得能量，换一种形式用在家里。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["It is worth thinking about what each person could verify.","可以想想，每个人能亲自确认什么。"],[" Someone watching the blades could see that the windmill moved.","看叶片的人能看见风车在动。"],[" Someone standing at the bottom of the tower could follow a wire with their eyes.","站在塔脚的人，能顺着电线的方向看过去。"],[" A person in the house could tell that the light was there.","在屋里的人，能确定灯确实亮了。"],[" William, who had joined the parts, could connect those observations.","威廉亲手接起各个部件，可以把这些各自看到的事联系到一起。"],[" The full demonstration was more convincing than any one of them on its own.","整套演示比任何一个单独的现象都更能说明问题。"]],"translation":"可以想想，每个人能亲自确认什么。看叶片的人能看见风车在动。站在塔脚的人，能顺着电线的方向看过去。在屋里的人，能确定灯确实亮了。威廉亲手接起各个部件，可以把这些各自看到的事联系到一起。整套演示比任何一个单独的现象都更能说明问题。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["The bulb was also a test of a useful kind.","这个灯泡做的也是一种很实际的测试。"],[" People understand the difference between a quick flash and a lamp that lets them see what is on the table.","人们能分清闪一下的光和照得见桌面上物件的灯。"],[" The amount of electricity a windmill can make changes with the weather.","风车发多少电会随天气变化。"],[" A little light at one particular moment is enough to show that the idea works.","某一个时刻出现一点光，足以证明主意可行。"],[" A family wanting to use its light in the evening will ask another question about how often it can rely on it.","一家人想在晚上用灯，会接着问，究竟有多少时候可以指望它。"]],"translation":"这个灯泡做的也是一种很实际的测试。人们能分清闪一下的光和照得见桌面上物件的灯。风车发多少电会随天气变化。某一个时刻出现一点光，足以证明主意可行。一家人想在晚上用灯，会接着问，究竟有多少时候可以指望它。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["William could now take that further question seriously.","威廉现在可以认真研究这个新问题了。"],[" He had a working machine that could be changed and measured.","他有一台可以继续调整、可以测量的机器。"],[" Its limits had become limits that he could observe.","机器的极限，也成了能够观察到的极限。"],[" A wire that grew damaged, a connection that failed, or a wind that dropped too low would now show itself in an ordinary room.","电线受损、接头失灵、风小得不够用，都会在一间普通的屋子里表现出来。"],[" After the work of collecting, fitting, and lifting the parts, the room itself could become a place to learn.","收集零件、把它们装好、抬到高处之后，这间屋本身也成了可以学习的地方。"],[" For anyone following the project from the ground, the light made the purpose of all that work clear in a way that a description never quite could.","对于站在地面上看过这个项目的人，那一点灯光把所有工作的目的照了出来，光凭一番解释很难达到同样的效果。"]],"translation":"威廉现在可以认真研究这个新问题了。他有一台可以继续调整、可以测量的机器。机器的极限，也成了能够观察到的极限。电线受损、接头失灵、风小得不够用，都会在一间普通的屋子里表现出来。收集零件、把它们装好、抬到高处之后，这间屋本身也成了可以学习的地方。对于站在地面上看过这个项目的人，那一点灯光把所有工作的目的照了出来，光凭一番解释很难达到同样的效果。"}],"terms":[{"term":"verify","meaning":"核实、证实","usage":"比 check 更明确强调通过证据确认；verify that + 从句可说明核实的事实。","example":"They verified that the second lamp lit at the same speed.","exampleZh":"他们核实了第二盏灯在同样的转速下也会亮。","meaningEn":"To confirm that something is true using evidence.","usageEn":"Verify that introduces the fact being confirmed. Check can refer to the inspection even when the result remains uncertain."},{"term":"convincing","meaning":"有说服力的、足以让人信服的","usage":"convincing evidence 建立在理由或验证上；convince someone of... 用于说服某人相信。","example":"A single flash was not convincing evidence that the machine worked.","exampleZh":"仅凭一次闪光，还不足以证明机器运转正常。","meaningEn":"Strong enough to make someone believe a claim or explanation.","usageEn":"Convincing evidence supports a conclusion. Convince someone of something uses the related verb."},{"term":"on its own","meaning":"单靠自身、没有外力帮助","usage":"常强调独立运作；与 of its own（它自己的）区别，如 a battery of its own。","example":"The motor could no longer start on its own.","exampleZh":"电机已经不能自行启动。","meaningEn":"By itself, without help or without other evidence.","usageEn":"A test can be weak on its own if it needs supporting evidence. Of its own expresses possession, as in a battery of its own."},{"term":"rely on","meaning":"依靠、指望","usage":"rely on + 名词或动名词；rely on somebody to do 强调可指望对方去做。","example":"The household could not rely on a single small bulb for all its light.","exampleZh":"那一家人的照明不能全指望一只小灯泡。","meaningEn":"To depend on a person or thing for what you need.","usageEn":"Rely on can take a noun or an -ing form. Rely on somebody to do something states what you trust them to do."}],"glossary":[["verify","核实，证实"],["observation","观察到的现象"],["convincing","有说服力的"],["on its own","单独地，靠自身"],["rely on","依靠，指望"],["drop too low","降到过低的程度"]]},{"en":"An Evening with Electric Light","zh":"有电灯的夜晚","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["What does electric light change in a house?","电灯会给一家人带来什么变化？"],[" The answer depends on what people were doing after dark before it arrived.","要看原来天黑以后，大家会做些什么。"],[" A lamp can make it easier to prepare food, find a tool, sew a piece of cloth, or see a page.","有一盏灯，准备食物、找工具、缝一块布或者看清一页书，都能容易些。"],[" Several people can share the same patch of light.","好几个人也可以围在同一片灯光下。"],[" The time between sunset and bedtime can be used with a little more freedom.","日落到睡觉中间那段时间，能用得自在一点。"]],"translation":"电灯会给一家人带来什么变化？要看原来天黑以后，大家会做些什么。有一盏灯，准备食物、找工具、缝一块布或者看清一页书，都能容易些。好几个人也可以围在同一片灯光下。日落到睡觉中间那段时间，能用得自在一点。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["A family that depends on another fuel for light may also have to think about carrying it home and paying for it.","原本靠别的燃料照明的人家，还可能要考虑怎么把燃料带回家、要花多少钱。"],[" The choices vary from home to home.","各家的选择不一样。"],[" A small electrical system has expenses and work of its own.","小型发电系统也有自己的开销和需要干的活儿。"],[" It also makes it possible to keep using the same bulb as long as the machine can run and the lamp stays in good condition.","同时，只要机器还能运转，灯泡也没坏，就可以继续用同一个灯泡。"],[" For William's household, having a home source of electricity changed what was possible on an ordinary evening.","对威廉一家来说，家里有了电源，普通一个晚上也会多出几种可能。"]],"translation":"原本靠别的燃料照明的人家，还可能要考虑怎么把燃料带回家、要花多少钱。各家的选择不一样。小型发电系统也有自己的开销和需要干的活儿。同时，只要机器还能运转，灯泡也没坏，就可以继续用同一个灯泡。对威廉一家来说，家里有了电源，普通一个晚上也会多出几种可能。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["A description of William's system several years later says that the power reached lights and radios in the home.","几年后，有关威廉的系统的介绍提到，电能送到家里的灯和收音机。"],[" The radio makes an interesting return to the story.","收音机又回到故事里，这一点挺有意思。"],[" As a boy, William had studied how to keep a radio working.","小时候，威廉研究的是怎么让收音机正常工作。"],[" A radio depends on power at the point where the listener uses it.","收音机需要在听众使用它的地方接到电。"],[" The windmill gave him a way of approaching the supply side of the same problem.","风车让他有了一个办法，从电力供应的这一头来处理同一个问题。"],[" The voice that came from the radio could now be connected, in part, to moving air over the house.","收音机里传来的声音，现在有一部分就连着屋外流动的空气。"]],"translation":"几年后，有关威廉的系统的介绍提到，电能送到家里的灯和收音机。收音机又回到故事里，这一点挺有意思。小时候，威廉研究的是怎么让收音机正常工作。收音机需要在听众使用它的地方接到电。风车让他有了一个办法，从电力供应的这一头来处理同一个问题。收音机里传来的声音，现在有一部分就连着屋外流动的空气。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["A useful invention is tested again each time people use it.","每一次拿来用，都是对发明的一次新检验。"],[" A demonstration may last a few minutes.","演示可以只持续几分钟。"],[" A light in the house belongs to an evening that can be repeated.","家里的灯，却属于一天又一天的夜晚。"],[" People can plan what to do under it, and they can tell when it is absent.","人们可以计划在灯下做什么，也会在灯不亮时感觉到它不在。"],[" The small movement of a blade outdoors has a consequence indoors, where nobody has to look at the tower to appreciate it.","屋外叶片的小小转动，会在屋里产生后果。在屋里的人不用望着塔，也能体会到它的用处。"],[" That daily experience explains why making light was a reasonable first purpose for the machine.","这种天天可以体会到的事情，说明照明为何是机器一个合适的开端。"]],"translation":"每一次拿来用，都是对发明的一次新检验。演示可以只持续几分钟。家里的灯，却属于一天又一天的夜晚。人们可以计划在灯下做什么，也会在灯不亮时感觉到它不在。屋外叶片的小小转动，会在屋里产生后果。在屋里的人不用望着塔，也能体会到它的用处。这种天天可以体会到的事情，说明照明为何是机器一个合适的开端。"}],"terms":[{"term":"patch of light","meaning":"一小片亮处","usage":"patch 指背景中有限的一块，形状未必规则；也可说 a patch of shade。","example":"She moved her sewing into the patch of light by the window.","exampleZh":"她把针线活挪到窗边那块亮处。","meaningEn":"A small area where light falls.","usageEn":"Patch suggests a limited area against a background without a fixed shape. A patch of shade follows the same pattern."},{"term":"fuel","meaning":"燃料","usage":"fuel 泛指用来提供能量的材料；用作动词时 fuel a debate 可比喻推动争议。","example":"The family bought less fuel after installing the lamp.","exampleZh":"装了灯之后，这家人买的燃料少了。","meaningEn":"A substance used to provide energy.","usageEn":"Fuel can mean material burned or otherwise used to power equipment. As a verb, fuel a debate means help make it more intense."},{"term":"expense","forms":["expenses"],"meaning":"费用、开销","usage":"at one's own expense 指自费；at the expense of... 另指以牺牲某事为代价。","example":"Replacing the battery was an unexpected expense.","exampleZh":"更换电池是一笔意料之外的开销。","meaningEn":"Money spent or a cost that must be paid.","usageEn":"At your own expense means you pay yourself. At the expense of something means sacrificing it to gain another benefit."},{"term":"point of use","meaning":"实际使用的地点","usage":"at the point of use 强调装置最终服务用户的位置；可与发电、净水等发生的位置区分。","example":"The water was filtered at the point of use.","exampleZh":"水是在实际使用的地方过滤的。","forms":["at the point where the listener uses it"],"meaningEn":"The location where a service or product is actually used.","usageEn":"At the point of use identifies where the benefit is delivered. This may differ from where the electricity is generated."}],"glossary":[["sew","缝，缝补"],["patch of light","一小片亮处"],["fuel","燃料"],["expense","开销"],["point of use","使用的地点"],["consequence","结果，影响"]]},{"en":"What Happens When the Wind Stops","zh":"风停下来之后","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["A machine powered by wind works with a source that changes.","靠风运行的机器，用的是随时会变的能源。"],[" People can decide when they would like to use a light. They have very little control over when a breeze arrives.","人可以决定自己什么时候想开灯，却很难决定微风什么时候吹来。"],[" That difference becomes important at the end of the day.","到了一天快结束时，这处差别就变得重要。"],[" A family might find the light most useful at the very hour when the blades are hardly moving.","一家人最想用灯的那个小时，叶片也许几乎没在动。"]],"translation":"靠风运行的机器，用的是随时会变的能源。人可以决定自己什么时候想开灯，却很难决定微风什么时候吹来。到了一天快结束时，这处差别就变得重要。一家人最想用灯的那个小时，叶片也许几乎没在动。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["One general way to deal with a gap like this is to store energy.","应付这类时间错配，一个常见办法是储存能量。"],[" A rechargeable battery can accept electrical energy when a suitable source supplies it.","有合适的电源供电时，可充电的电池可以把电能储起来。"],[" Later, the battery can provide some of that energy to a device.","之后，它可以拿出一部分储存的能量供给设备。"],[" The windmill and the battery then have different jobs.","风车和电池于是各负责一项工作。"],[" The first draws energy from the wind when it can. The second allows a person to shift some of the use to a different time.","风车在有条件的时候从风中取得能量，电池让人把一部分用电挪到别的时间。"],[" Useful storage depends on connecting the battery through equipment suitable for its safe operation.","要好好利用电池储能，还得用适合电池安全工作的设备来连接。"]],"translation":"应付这类时间错配，一个常见办法是储存能量。有合适的电源供电时，可充电的电池可以把电能储起来。之后，它可以拿出一部分储存的能量供给设备。风车和电池于是各负责一项工作。风车在有条件的时候从风中取得能量，电池让人把一部分用电挪到别的时间。要好好利用电池储能，还得用适合电池安全工作的设备来连接。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Storage has limits as well.","储存也有极限。"],[" A charged battery can run a load only for a certain time.","充了电的电池，只能带着用电设备运行一定时间。"],[" Some energy is lost in charging and use.","充电和用电时都会损失一部分能量。"],[" If a system has several days of little wind and no other power source, it may need more time to fill up again.","如果连着几天没什么风，系统又没有别的电源，也许得再过一段时间才充得满。"],[" Its owner might choose which lights to use or find a different way to meet the need for that evening.","用电的人可能得挑几盏灯来开，或者想想那天晚上有什么别的办法。"],[" These are ordinary decisions for a small independent supply.","这些都是小型独立供电系统会遇到的日常决定。"]],"translation":"储存也有极限。充了电的电池，只能带着用电设备运行一定时间。充电和用电时都会损失一部分能量。如果连着几天没什么风，系统又没有别的电源，也许得再过一段时间才充得满。用电的人可能得挑几盏灯来开，或者想想那天晚上有什么别的办法。这些都是小型独立供电系统会遇到的日常决定。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["William's work can be placed in that wider problem.","可以把威廉的发明放到这个更大的问题里去看。"],[" Producing some electricity was one major achievement.","发出电是一项重要成果。"],[" Giving the household a dependable service added a decision about when energy would be there, how much the family needed, and what happened in poor weather.","要稳定地供应一家人用电，还得考虑什么时候有电、这家需要多少电、天气不佳时怎么办。"],[" A larger system already available in some places spreads those decisions over many people and machines.","有些地方已经用上较大的供电系统，把这些决定分给许多人和许多机器承担。"],[" With a little windmill near the house, tasks that might normally be carried out far away became visible at home.","一户人家的小风车就在屋边，一些通常会在远处做完的工作，在这里看得见。"],[" The weather, the people, and the way they used the machine each helped determine the amount of light they would have.","天气、用电的人，以及他们用机器的方式，一起决定了家里能有多少光。"]],"translation":"可以把威廉的发明放到这个更大的问题里去看。发出电是一项重要成果。要稳定地供应一家人用电，还得考虑什么时候有电、这家需要多少电、天气不佳时怎么办。有些地方已经用上较大的供电系统，把这些决定分给许多人和许多机器承担。一户人家的小风车就在屋边，一些通常会在远处做完的工作，在这里看得见。天气、用电的人，以及他们用机器的方式，一起决定了家里能有多少光。"}],"terms":[{"term":"rechargeable","meaning":"可以反复充电的","usage":"re- 表示再次，-able 表示可以；rechargeable 构成属性，charged 只指当前充了电。","example":"A rechargeable battery kept the radio going after dark.","exampleZh":"天黑后，充电电池让收音机继续工作。","meaningEn":"Able to be charged again for repeated use.","usageEn":"The prefix re- means again. Rechargeable describes a continuing capability, while charged describes the current state."},{"term":"store energy","meaning":"储存能量","usage":"store 此处作动词；battery stores energy，随时能否供电还取决于剩余电量。","example":"The system stores energy for nights when the wind stops.","exampleZh":"这套系统储存能量，以备夜里停风时使用。","meaningEn":"To keep energy available for later use.","usageEn":"Store is the verb here. A battery stores energy, but what it can deliver depends in part on the charge remaining."},{"term":"equipment","meaning":"设备、器材","usage":"不可数，不说 an equipment；需要计件时用 a piece of equipment。","example":"The school shared its equipment with the village repair group.","exampleZh":"学校与村里的修理小组共用设备。","meaningEn":"The tools and devices needed for an activity.","usageEn":"Equipment is uncountable. Use a piece of equipment when you refer to one item."},{"term":"independent supply","meaning":"独立供给、独立电源","usage":"independent supply of + 所供物；强调有别于主供给的来源，未必表示能无限储备。","example":"The clinic needed an independent supply of electricity.","exampleZh":"诊所需要一个独立的电力来源。","meaningEn":"A supply that can operate separately from the main one.","usageEn":"Use of to name what the supply delivers. Independent describes the connection to the main system, with no guarantee about capacity."}],"glossary":[["rechargeable","可充电的"],["store energy","储存能量"],["equipment","设备"],["charged","已充电的"],["independent supply","独立供电"],["dependable service","可靠的供给"]]},{"en":"Keeping the Machine Working","zh":"让机器一直能用","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Finishing a windmill gives its builder a machine to look after.","完成一台风车，也就有了一台要照看的机器。"],[" The pieces experience rain, sunlight, dust, changes in temperature, and repeated movement.","零件要经历下雨、日晒、灰尘、温度变化，还要一次又一次地运动。"],[" A part that was strong enough on its first day may need attention later.","第一天够结实的部件，后来也许需要照料。"],[" A wire may have been pulled out of place. A surface that once turned smoothly can begin to rub.","电线可能被拉得离开了原位，原本顺畅转动的零件表面也可能开始蹭到别的东西。"],[" The challenge continues for as long as the machine is useful.","机器有用多久，维护它的挑战就持续多久。"]],"translation":"完成一台风车，也就有了一台要照看的机器。零件要经历下雨、日晒、灰尘、温度变化，还要一次又一次地运动。第一天够结实的部件，后来也许需要照料。电线可能被拉得离开了原位，原本顺畅转动的零件表面也可能开始蹭到别的东西。机器有用多久，维护它的挑战就持续多久。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["A sensible question to ask about a design is how a person can repair it.","衡量一个设计，可以问问，人能怎么修它。"],[" Suppose a part will eventually wear out.","假设一个零件用久了准会磨坏。"],[" If everyone nearby knows what the part is and where to look for another, replacing it may take a short time.","附近的人都认得它，也知道去哪里找一个一样的，换起来可能很快。"],[" If it takes a long journey or a special tool, a small fault can leave the machine stopped for months.","如果需要跑很远，或者得有特殊的工具，一个小毛病就可能让机器停上几个月。"],[" Keeping spare parts can help when they are affordable and there is somewhere to store them.","买得起备件、有地方放的时候，留几个备用的零件会有帮助。"]],"translation":"衡量一个设计，可以问问，人能怎么修它。假设一个零件用久了准会磨坏。附近的人都认得它，也知道去哪里找一个一样的，换起来可能很快。如果需要跑很远，或者得有特殊的工具，一个小毛病就可能让机器停上几个月。买得起备件、有地方放的时候，留几个备用的零件会有帮助。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["William's use of familiar objects made some problems easier to understand.","威廉用的有些物件大家熟悉，所以有些问题也容易理解。"],[" Someone who repairs bicycles can recognise the movement of a wheel.","懂得修自行车的人，认得轮子是怎么转的。"],[" Yet a part coming from a familiar machine can behave differently when exposed to strong wind and rain.","但是把熟悉机器上的部件放到大风和雨里，表现可能会变。"],[" Moving it into a new setting may reveal a weakness that mattered very little when the part lived in its original frame.","把零件挪到新环境中，有时会看见它一个原本无关紧要的弱点。"],[" Repair and design begin to overlap.","修理和设计开始有了重合的地方。"]],"translation":"威廉用的有些物件大家熟悉，所以有些问题也容易理解。懂得修自行车的人，认得轮子是怎么转的。但是把熟悉机器上的部件放到大风和雨里，表现可能会变。把零件挪到新环境中，有时会看见它一个原本无关紧要的弱点。修理和设计开始有了重合的地方。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Look again at the light in the house.","再想想屋里那盏灯。"],[" The effect of a repair at the tower shows up at the far end of a wire.","在塔上修了什么，效果会在电线远处的另一头显现。"],[" The family needs access to both ends of the system and to the knowledge that joins them.","家里得能接触系统的两头，也得掌握把两头联系起来的知识。"],[" A useful machine has to be looked after without asking a different person to explain it from the beginning every time.","一台实用机器的维护，得做得到不用每次都请别人从头讲解。"],[" Over years William could replace parts, try new arrangements, and learn from the ones that lasted.","经过许多年，威廉可以更换零件，也可以尝试新的组装方式，看看哪些经用。"],[" His blog describes a later change in the generator.","后来，他在自己的博客里记过一次换发电机的经过。"],[" That change gives a rare view of an invention with an ordinary history, including wear, tools, gifts, and a person coming home to work on it again.","从中可以少见地看清，一件发明也有平常的经历，有磨损，有工具，有别人送来的东西，也有人回到家再来动手修它。"]],"translation":"再想想屋里那盏灯。在塔上修了什么，效果会在电线远处的另一头显现。家里得能接触系统的两头，也得掌握把两头联系起来的知识。一台实用机器的维护，得做得到不用每次都请别人从头讲解。经过许多年，威廉可以更换零件，也可以尝试新的组装方式，看看哪些经用。后来，他在自己的博客里记过一次换发电机的经过。从中可以少见地看清，一件发明也有平常的经历，有磨损，有工具，有别人送来的东西，也有人回到家再来动手修它。"}],"terms":[{"term":"repeated movement","meaning":"反复的运动","usage":"repeated 描述多次发生；repetitive 还可含动作单调、令人厌倦的意味。","example":"Repeated movement slowly loosened the wire connection.","exampleZh":"反复的运动让电线接头渐渐松动。","meaningEn":"Motion that occurs again and again.","usageEn":"Repeated states that it happens more than once. Repetitive can also suggest monotony or strain."},{"term":"spare part","forms":["spare parts"],"meaning":"备用零件","usage":"spare part 在安装前是备件，装上去发挥更换作用时也可说 replacement part。","example":"Without a spare part, the pump stayed broken for a week.","exampleZh":"没有备件，水泵坏了整整一周。","meaningEn":"An extra component kept ready in case a machine needs it.","usageEn":"Spare part highlights its reserve role. Replacement part highlights that it takes the place of another component."},{"term":"affordable","meaning":"在负担得起的价位","usage":"affordable to households 或 affordable for families；强调与购买者的承受力相符。","example":"The store offered a more affordable replacement.","exampleZh":"店里有个更负担得起的替换件。","meaningEn":"Priced within what the intended buyer can reasonably pay.","usageEn":"Affordable for families and affordable to households identify the buyer. The word takes their resources as well as the price into account."},{"term":"exposed to","meaning":"暴露于……、直接受……影响","usage":"expose A to B；被动 be exposed to 常接雨、阳光、风险等外部条件。","example":"Wires exposed to rain may wear out faster.","exampleZh":"暴露在雨中的电线可能老化得更快。","meaningEn":"Open to the effects of a force, condition, or risk.","usageEn":"Expose A to B identifies the object and what it encounters. In the passive, be exposed to often takes rain, sunlight, or a hazard."}],"glossary":[["repeated movement","反复运动"],["pull out of place","拉离原位"],["spare part","备件"],["affordable","负担得起的"],["exposed to","暴露于……之下"],["overlap","重叠，交叠"]]},{"en":"A New Generator in 2007","zh":"2007 年的新发电机","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["In July 2007 William described going home to Wimbe from Madisi Secondary School to work on the windmill again.","2007 年 7 月，威廉写到，他从马迪西中学回了温贝村的家，再动手弄一弄那台风车。"],[" The trip mattered because the invention had become a continuing project.","这趟回家值得留意，因为这项发明已经变成一个会一直做下去的项目。"],[" He returned to a machine he already knew, and he brought a new idea for changing the way it made electricity.","他回到自己熟悉的机器边，带了一个可以改变发电方式的主意。"],[" A motor from a treadmill could give the old windmill a different electrical heart.","把从跑步机上来的电机用起来，老风车就可能换上一颗新的发电心脏。"]],"translation":"2007 年 7 月，威廉写到，他从马迪西中学回了温贝村的家，再动手弄一弄那台风车。这趟回家值得留意，因为这项发明已经变成一个会一直做下去的项目。他回到自己熟悉的机器边，带了一个可以改变发电方式的主意。把从跑步机上来的电机用起来，老风车就可能换上一颗新的发电心脏。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["The motor had come from people working with Baobab Health.","电机是供职于 Baobab Health 的人送的。"],[" They had been looking at a windmill kit in connection with a possible source of power for a remote computer system.","他们看过一套风车组件，想过用风来为位置偏远的计算机系统供电。"],[" When they met William, they gave him the motor along with a meter for measuring voltage.","见到威廉后，他们把电机和测量电压的一只表送给了他。"],[" A machine for indoor exercise and a piece of equipment associated with health work thus entered the history of a windmill in a farming village.","就这样，室内锻炼用的机器、和医疗工作有关的设备，一起走进了农家村庄的一台风车的历史。"],[" The connection was practical.","把大家连起来的是同一种实际需要。"],[" Each person was looking for small sources of electricity that might work away from the usual supply.","他们都在找能离开一般供电系统而工作的小型电源。"]],"translation":"电机是供职于 Baobab Health 的人送的。他们看过一套风车组件，想过用风来为位置偏远的计算机系统供电。见到威廉后，他们把电机和测量电压的一只表送给了他。就这样，室内锻炼用的机器、和医疗工作有关的设备，一起走进了农家村庄的一台风车的历史。把大家连起来的是同一种实际需要。他们都在找能离开一般供电系统而工作的小型电源。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["An electric motor generally uses electrical energy to create movement.","电动机通常用电来产生运动。"],[" Some kinds of motors can also generate electricity when another source turns them.","有些类型的电机，如果由其他动力转动它，也能发电。"],[" The suitability of a particular motor depends on how it is designed and on how it will be used.","某一台电机是否合适，要看它是怎样设计的，还要看将怎样使用。"],[" In William's account the treadmill motor represented a chance to get more power than he could get from the bicycle dynamo.","按威廉的说法，跑步机电机带来了一种可能，让他获得比自行车发电机更多的电力。"],[" Fitting it meant returning to older questions about mechanical movement and electrical connections.","把它装上去，也就要重新考虑怎样传递机械转动、怎样接电这些旧问题。"]],"translation":"电动机通常用电来产生运动。有些类型的电机，如果由其他动力转动它，也能发电。某一台电机是否合适，要看它是怎样设计的，还要看将怎样使用。按威廉的说法，跑步机电机带来了一种可能，让他获得比自行车发电机更多的电力。把它装上去，也就要重新考虑怎样传递机械转动、怎样接电这些旧问题。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["The measuring tool mattered alongside the new generator.","除了新的发电机，测量工具也很重要。"],[" A bulb gives immediate evidence that some power has arrived.","灯泡能当场说明，有电到了这里。"],[" A measurement can help a builder compare the result under different conditions.","测量则能让建造者比较不同条件下的结果。"],[" If the result changes after an adjustment, the meter gives the builder a way to describe how much it changed.","调整后结果如果有变化，有了表，就有办法说明它变了多少。"],[" William's account allows us to follow a windmill across time.","看威廉的记录，我们能一路跟着一台风车走过一段时间。"],[" A part that had once been sufficient gave way to a new possibility.","原先够用的零件，给新的可能让出了位置。"],[" A project that began with a library picture had grown into work that he could test, describe, and share.","在图书馆里从一张图片开始的项目，发展成了能试验、能说明、也能和别人分享的工作。"]],"translation":"除了新的发电机，测量工具也很重要。灯泡能当场说明，有电到了这里。测量则能让建造者比较不同条件下的结果。调整后结果如果有变化，有了表，就有办法说明它变了多少。看威廉的记录，我们能一路跟着一台风车走过一段时间。原先够用的零件，给新的可能让出了位置。在图书馆里从一张图片开始的项目，发展成了能试验、能说明、也能和别人分享的工作。"}],"terms":[{"term":"voltage","meaning":"电压","usage":"voltage measured in volts；measure voltage across two points 指测两点间的电势差。","example":"She checked the voltage across the battery terminals.","exampleZh":"她测量了电池两端的电压。","meaningEn":"The difference in electrical potential between two points.","usageEn":"Voltage is measured in volts. Measure voltage across two points identifies the locations being compared."},{"term":"treadmill","meaning":"跑步机","usage":"on a treadmill 指在跑步机上运动；treadmill motor 指从跑步机来的驱动电机。","example":"The group salvaged a motor from an old treadmill.","exampleZh":"小组从旧跑步机上拆下了一台还能用的电机。","meaningEn":"A walking or running exercise machine with a moving belt.","usageEn":"You run on a treadmill. A treadmill motor is the part that normally drives its belt."},{"term":"suitability","meaning":"适用性、是否适合特定用途","usage":"the suitability of A for B；常用于材料、地点或条件评估。","example":"They tested the suitability of the motor for charging batteries.","exampleZh":"他们检测这台电机是否适合给电池充电。","meaningEn":"How well something meets the requirements of a particular purpose.","usageEn":"The suitability of A for B names the item and its intended use. It is common when evaluating a material, location, or method."},{"term":"give way to","forms":["gave way to"],"meaning":"让位给、被某物取代","usage":"旧方法作主语时表示被新方法替代；道路标识 give way 表示让行。","example":"Guesswork gave way to a series of careful measurements.","exampleZh":"凭感觉估计的做法让位给了一连串仔细的测量。","meaningEn":"To be replaced by something else or yield to it.","usageEn":"An old method may give way to a newer one. On a road sign, give way tells drivers to let other traffic pass first."}],"glossary":[["treadmill","跑步机"],["voltage","电压"],["remote","偏远的"],["suitability","适用性"],["measurement","测量；测量结果"],["give way to","让位给，被……取代"]]},{"en":"Why Water Is a Larger Task","zh":"为什么抽水是个更大的任务","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Lighting a house and moving water can both be useful jobs for a windmill.","给屋里照明和抽水，都可以是风车有用的工作。"],[" The jobs involve very different demands.","两项工作有不同的要求。"],[" A small lamp can produce light for the people near it as soon as an appropriate electric current reaches it.","一旦有合适的电流，一盏小灯马上就可以照亮附近的人。"],[" A pump has to move a certain amount of water from one place to another.","水泵要把一定数量的水从一处送到另一处。"],[" It can be asked to lift the water uphill or send it through a long pipe.","它也许得把水抽到高处，或把水送过一根长管。"],[" Both the quantity of water and the height it must travel affect the work.","水量有多大、得升到多高，都会影响要做多少功。"]],"translation":"给屋里照明和抽水，都可以是风车有用的工作。两项工作有不同的要求。一旦有合适的电流，一盏小灯马上就可以照亮附近的人。水泵要把一定数量的水从一处送到另一处。它也许得把水抽到高处，或把水送过一根长管。水量有多大、得升到多高，都会影响要做多少功。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["A crop does not need water merely because the pump has power that day.","水泵今天有电，并不代表庄稼今天就正需要水。"],[" The crop has a schedule of its own.","作物有自己的时间表。"],[" Farmers have to think about when rain is likely, how wet the soil already is, and which plants are likely to suffer first.","农人要考虑什么时候最可能下雨，土壤已经有多湿，哪些植物可能最早受旱。"],[" A storage tank could help match the day when power is available with the day when the plants need water.","储水罐能帮人接上供电的日子和庄稼需水的日子。"],[" A tank also has a size, a cost, and a place in the system.","储水罐也有自己的尺寸、成本，还得找个地方安放。"]],"translation":"水泵今天有电，并不代表庄稼今天就正需要水。作物有自己的时间表。农人要考虑什么时候最可能下雨，土壤已经有多湿，哪些植物可能最早受旱。储水罐能帮人接上供电的日子和庄稼需水的日子。储水罐也有自己的尺寸、成本，还得找个地方安放。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["The water itself has to come from somewhere.","水本身也得从某个地方来。"],[" A good wind can power a machine, but it cannot refill an empty source.","一阵好风能给机器提供能量，却不能把空了的水源重新灌满。"],[" If several households share a supply, decisions about when to take water may be as important as the equipment that lifts it.","如果好几家共用一个水源，什么时候可以取水，可能和用什么设备抽水同样重要。"],[" A working system has to address the amount of water available and who can use it as well as the question of energy.","一个能运行的系统，既要考虑能源，也要弄清水有多少、谁可以用。"],[" A pump is one part of that larger system.","水泵是这个更大系统中的一个部件。"]],"translation":"水本身也得从某个地方来。一阵好风能给机器提供能量，却不能把空了的水源重新灌满。如果好几家共用一个水源，什么时候可以取水，可能和用什么设备抽水同样重要。一个能运行的系统，既要考虑能源，也要弄清水有多少、谁可以用。水泵是这个更大系统中的一个部件。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["William spoke publicly about his wish to use wind power for pumping and irrigation.","威廉曾公开说过，希望用风力抽水灌溉。"],[" That goal makes sense in the farming setting where the project began.","想想项目是在哪种农业环境里开始的，这个目标就很好理解。"],[" It also helps explain why success with a light was a beginning.","它也说明点亮一盏灯为什么只是开端。"],[" The lamp showed that a source of energy could be found and adapted close to home.","灯证明，人可以就近找到一种能源，再想办法利用它。"],[" Water brought a new set of measurements, materials, and decisions.","水带来的是一整套新的测量、新的材料和新的决定。"],[" The same inventor could take on the next question with experience he did not have when he first walked into the library.","同一位发明者可以带着经验去做下一道题，这些经验是他第一次走进图书馆时没有的。"]],"translation":"威廉曾公开说过，希望用风力抽水灌溉。想想项目是在哪种农业环境里开始的，这个目标就很好理解。它也说明点亮一盏灯为什么只是开端。灯证明，人可以就近找到一种能源，再想办法利用它。水带来的是一整套新的测量、新的材料和新的决定。同一位发明者可以带着经验去做下一道题，这些经验是他第一次走进图书馆时没有的。"}],"terms":[{"term":"lift uphill","meaning":"把水等提升或抽送到高处","usage":"uphill 描述逆坡向上的方向；pump water uphill 常用来描述水泵的实际动作。","example":"The pump lifted water uphill to the garden.","exampleZh":"水泵把水抽送到坡上的菜园。","forms":["lift the water uphill"],"meaningEn":"To raise or move something to a higher point on a slope.","usageEn":"Uphill describes the direction. Pump water uphill names the action of a powered pump more explicitly."},{"term":"storage tank","meaning":"储存罐，本文指储水罐","usage":"tank 用于储存液体或气体；water storage tank 明确储存物。","example":"Rainwater from the roof flowed into a storage tank.","exampleZh":"屋顶上的雨水流进了储水罐。","meaningEn":"A container that holds liquid or gas until it is needed.","usageEn":"Water storage tank identifies the contents. Storage describes the purpose of the tank."},{"term":"refill","meaning":"重新注满、补充","usage":"re- 表示再一次；refill a container 用及物，the tank refills 可指水箱自己补满。","example":"The workers refilled the tank before the dry spell.","exampleZh":"工人赶在少雨期前把水箱重新注满。","meaningEn":"To fill something again after some or all of its contents have been used.","usageEn":"Refill the tank makes the tank the object. The tank refills describes it filling up again."},{"term":"irrigation","meaning":"灌溉","usage":"通常不可数；irrigation system 是灌溉系统，irrigate a field 指对田地进行灌溉。","example":"The channel supplied water for irrigation during the dry season.","exampleZh":"旱季时，这条水渠为灌溉提供用水。","meaningEn":"The process of supplying water to land or crops to help them grow.","usageEn":"The noun is usually uncountable. An irrigation system supplies water, and farmers irrigate a field."}],"glossary":[["lift uphill","抽送到高处"],["quantity","数量"],["crop","庄稼，作物"],["storage tank","储水罐"],["refill","重新注满"],["irrigation","灌溉"]]},{"en":"News Travels Farther","zh":"消息传到更远的地方","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["A working windmill is easy to point at and harder to explain to someone who has never visited.","一台能用的风车，很容易用手指给人看，给从没来过的人讲却要费些力气。"],[" People near the machine could see it turn and follow the wire to the house.","站在机器旁的人，看得见它转，也能沿着电线找到房子。"],[" The story had to travel differently once it left the village.","故事一旦出了村子，就得用不一样的方式传播。"],[" A writer could describe the parts. A photograph could make the wooden tower seem real to people who had never heard of Wimbe.","写作者可以描述用了哪些零件，一张照片可以让从没听过温贝村的人相信，那座木塔真的在那里。"],[" The name of the person who built it could travel with those details.","造塔的人的名字，也能随着这些细节传出去。"]],"translation":"一台能用的风车，很容易用手指给人看，给从没来过的人讲却要费些力气。站在机器旁的人，看得见它转，也能沿着电线找到房子。故事一旦出了村子，就得用不一样的方式传播。写作者可以描述用了哪些零件，一张照片可以让从没听过温贝村的人相信，那座木塔真的在那里。造塔的人的名字，也能随着这些细节传出去。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Reports of William's work reached a wider audience in Malawi and beyond.","威廉的事传给了马拉维国内外更多的人。"],[" One of the people who learned about it was Emeka Okafor, who was involved in organising the TEDGlobal conference in Arusha, Tanzania, in 2007.","其中有一位叫埃梅卡·奥卡福，他参与筹办了 2007 年在坦桑尼亚阿鲁沙举行的 TEDGlobal 大会。"],[" An invitation to the conference gave William a reason to travel and a chance to speak about the invention.","会议邀请威廉前去，让他有了出门走一趟的理由，也给了他讲述这项发明的机会。"],[" The visit depended on people who thought the windmill was worth understanding before it was recognised in many other places.","有些人早在风车闻名各地之前，就觉得这是一台值得了解的机器。正是这些人，让那趟旅行成了可能。"]],"translation":"威廉的事传给了马拉维国内外更多的人。其中有一位叫埃梅卡·奥卡福，他参与筹办了 2007 年在坦桑尼亚阿鲁沙举行的 TEDGlobal 大会。会议邀请威廉前去，让他有了出门走一趟的理由，也给了他讲述这项发明的机会。有些人早在风车闻名各地之前，就觉得这是一台值得了解的机器。正是这些人，让那趟旅行成了可能。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Information that travels can become simpler with each retelling.","消息传播开来，每重讲一次，内容可能就会变得简单一些。"],[" As an illustration of invention, the contrast between a pile of used parts and a working source of light is easy to grasp.","把一堆旧零件和真正能用的光源放在一起，人们很容易看出这是个关于发明的好例子。"],[" A concise story may leave little room to explain the conditions that pushed William out of school, the help he received, and the questions he was still trying to answer.","故事讲得短了，就不容易展开威廉为什么离开学校、谁帮过他、还有什么问题他仍在试着解答。"],[" Each of those details matters if someone hopes to understand why similar talent does not always have the same opportunity.","想弄清为什么有相似才能的人并不总有同样的机会，其中每一项都值得了解。"]],"translation":"消息传播开来，每重讲一次，内容可能就会变得简单一些。把一堆旧零件和真正能用的光源放在一起，人们很容易看出这是个关于发明的好例子。故事讲得短了，就不容易展开威廉为什么离开学校、谁帮过他、还有什么问题他仍在试着解答。想弄清为什么有相似才能的人并不总有同样的机会，其中每一项都值得了解。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["The journey of the news created another practical problem.","消息传开，也带来了另一个实际问题。"],[" William was now being asked to explain a machine that he had already learned to build.","现在有人请威廉讲明白他已经学会怎样造的机器。"],[" He could use in-person gestures when standing next to a bicycle frame.","站在车架旁，他可以边指边比划。"],[" Far from home, he had to choose words deliberately and trust other people to help carry the story.","离开家乡，他得仔细选择怎样表达，也得相信别人能帮他把故事传下去。"],[" The audience would have to picture the village, the library, the blades, and the lamp.","听众要在脑子里想象出村子、图书馆、叶片和那盏灯。"],[" Explaining the creation was about to become a kind of work in itself.","解释这项发明，本身就要成为一项工作了。"]],"translation":"消息传开，也带来了另一个实际问题。现在有人请威廉讲明白他已经学会怎样造的机器。站在车架旁，他可以边指边比划。离开家乡，他得仔细选择怎样表达，也得相信别人能帮他把故事传下去。听众要在脑子里想象出村子、图书馆、叶片和那盏灯。解释这项发明，本身就要成为一项工作了。"}],"terms":[{"term":"be worth doing","forms":["worth understanding"],"meaning":"值得做某事","usage":"worth 后用动名词，不用不定式；主语是值得理解、阅读或考虑的对象。","example":"Her early attempts were worth studying even though they had failed.","exampleZh":"尽管她早期的尝试失败了，仍然值得研究。","meaningEn":"To deserve the time or effort involved in an action.","usageEn":"Worth takes an -ing form, as in worth reading or worth understanding. The subject is what you would read or understand."},{"term":"recognised","meaning":"受到认可、被承认","usage":"英式 recognised 对应美式 recognized；recognized for 表示因某成就获得认可。","example":"She was recognised for her work with local schools.","exampleZh":"她与本地学校合作的工作获得了认可。","meaningEn":"Known and acknowledged, often for an achievement.","usageEn":"Recognised is the British spelling of recognized. Recognised for introduces the achievement or quality that drew notice."},{"term":"retelling","meaning":"对同一故事的重述","usage":"a retelling of the story 可保留情节但改变写法；retell 是相应动词。","example":"Each retelling began at a different point in the story.","exampleZh":"每次重述都从故事里的不同节点讲起。","meaningEn":"A new account of a story that has already been told.","usageEn":"A retelling of a story can keep its central events while changing its perspective or style. Retell is the related verb."},{"term":"concise","meaning":"精炼、用简洁语言交代清楚","usage":"concise 强调删去冗余仍把重点说清；brief 主要说明篇幅或时间短。","example":"He prepared a concise explanation of how the machine worked.","exampleZh":"他准备了一段简明的机器原理说明。","meaningEn":"Brief but complete enough to make the main point clear.","usageEn":"Concise emphasizes leaving out unnecessary words. Brief mainly conveys that the length or duration is short."}],"glossary":[["beyond","在更远处，在……之外"],["organise","组织，筹办"],["recognised","受到认可的"],["retelling","重述"],["concise","简明的"],["deliberately","有意地，审慎地"]]},{"en":"Questions on a Stage in Arusha","zh":"阿鲁沙台上的问答","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["In 2007 William appeared onstage at TEDGlobal in Arusha.","2007 年，威廉走上了阿鲁沙 TEDGlobal 大会的舞台。"],[" The visit brought him into a room where other people were accustomed to hearing short presentations about inventions.","来到这里，他面对的是一群习惯听发明者做简短介绍的听众。"],[" He took questions about how he had made the windmill.","他回答了关于怎样造风车的问题。"],[" People wanted to know where the idea came from, what parts he could find, and what the electricity could do.","人们想知道这个主意是哪里来的，他找得到哪些零件，发的电又能够做什么。"]],"translation":"2007 年，威廉走上了阿鲁沙 TEDGlobal 大会的舞台。来到这里，他面对的是一群习惯听发明者做简短介绍的听众。他回答了关于怎样造风车的问题。人们想知道这个主意是哪里来的，他找得到哪些零件，发的电又能够做什么。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["The conversation took place in English, the same language he had met on the pages of his science books.","这场问答用英语进行，正是他从科学书上见过的语言。"],[" The work of using that language had changed.","不过，用这门语言要做的事变了。"],[" In the library, he could stop on a word, use an illustration, or spend another afternoon on the same page.","在图书馆，他可以在一个词上停住，借助插图猜一猜，也可以再用一个下午读同一页。"],[" Onstage, a question arrived aloud and needed an answer the audience can follow.","在台上，问题是别人当场说出来的，他得说出听众跟得上的答案。"],[" The skills required to understand a mechanism and to explain it quickly are only partly the same.","弄懂一个机械装置，和迅速对别人讲明白，所需要的本领有一部分是相通的。"]],"translation":"这场问答用英语进行，正是他从科学书上见过的语言。不过，用这门语言要做的事变了。在图书馆，他可以在一个词上停住，借助插图猜一猜，也可以再用一个下午读同一页。在台上，问题是别人当场说出来的，他得说出听众跟得上的答案。弄懂一个机械装置，和迅速对别人讲明白，所需要的本领有一部分是相通的。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["An audience can help an inventor explain things by asking about a concrete detail.","听众问到具体细节，也能帮发明者把事情说清楚。"],[" A question about what the windmill powered could be answered with the things inside his parents' home.","想知道风车给什么供电，可以从父母家里的物件说起。"],[" A question about the parts could be answered by referring to a bicycle.","要回答零件是什么，可以举自行车为例。"],[" Those objects gave the people in the room a way to follow along. They also let William begin with the details he had spent years learning in a place well outside the conference hall.","这些大家认识的东西，给了在场的人一条能听下去的线索，也让威廉能从自己在远离会场的地方花多年摸熟的细节谈起。"]],"translation":"听众问到具体细节，也能帮发明者把事情说清楚。想知道风车给什么供电，可以从父母家里的物件说起。要回答零件是什么，可以举自行车为例。这些大家认识的东西，给了在场的人一条能听下去的线索，也让威廉能从自己在远离会场的地方花多年摸熟的细节谈起。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["The appearance gave a small machine a large audience.","这次登台，让一台小机器有了很多听众。"],[" The audience could recognise the value of the work without knowing every step that had led to it.","即使还不知道风车是怎样一步一步造出来的，大家也看得见这项工作的价值。"],[" It would still take more time for William to speak at length about the famine, his decision to keep learning, and the work of building the machine.","威廉还需要再过一些时间，才能细讲饥荒、继续学习的决定，以及造机器的经过。"],[" From the audience's side, looking for a little device that can run a light may seem like a step in electronics.","在听众眼里，找一件能点亮灯的小装置，可能是一项电气工作。"],[" From William's side, it also belonged to the story of trying to stay a student when the usual way to do so was closed.","从威廉这边看，这也是一个人在通常的上学之路走不通时，仍然设法当一名学生的故事。"],[" His later talk would bring more of that side into view.","后来那次演讲，让人们看见了这个故事里更多的一面。"]],"translation":"这次登台，让一台小机器有了很多听众。即使还不知道风车是怎样一步一步造出来的，大家也看得见这项工作的价值。威廉还需要再过一些时间，才能细讲饥荒、继续学习的决定，以及造机器的经过。在听众眼里，找一件能点亮灯的小装置，可能是一项电气工作。从威廉这边看，这也是一个人在通常的上学之路走不通时，仍然设法当一名学生的故事。后来那次演讲，让人们看见了这个故事里更多的一面。"}],"terms":[{"term":"accustomed to","meaning":"习惯于……","usage":"to 是介词，后接名词或动名词；grow accustomed to 表示逐渐习惯。","example":"She was accustomed to speaking to small groups.","exampleZh":"她习惯了面对小组讲话。","meaningEn":"Familiar with something through repeated experience.","usageEn":"To is a preposition and can take a noun or an -ing form. Grow accustomed to means become used to something gradually."},{"term":"mechanism","meaning":"机械装置、内部的运作原理","usage":"a locking mechanism 是具体机构；the mechanism behind... 可指某事背后的作用方式。","example":"The diagram revealed the mechanism inside the pump.","exampleZh":"这张图显示了水泵内部的装置。","meaningEn":"A set of parts that performs an action, or the way a process works.","usageEn":"A locking mechanism names a physical assembly. The mechanism behind something describes how it produces an effect."},{"term":"follow along","meaning":"跟上讲解、边听边理解","usage":"follow along with the demonstration 可表示跟着演示做或看；follow someone 多指跟在某人后面。","example":"The audience followed along as she drew the circuit.","exampleZh":"她画电路图时，听众跟着她的讲解理解。","meaningEn":"To keep up with a demonstration, explanation, or sequence of steps.","usageEn":"Follow along with a demonstration can mean watch and understand or perform the steps as they are shown. Follow someone can simply mean go behind them."},{"term":"at length","meaning":"详细地、较长时间地","usage":"speak at length 常指详细讲述；at length 也可用于叙事转折，表示终于。","example":"They discussed the design at length after the demonstration.","exampleZh":"演示之后，他们详细讨论了设计。","meaningEn":"In detail or for a considerable time.","usageEn":"Speak at length usually means explain something fully. In older narrative usage, at length can also mean finally."}],"glossary":[["accustomed to","习惯于"],["presentation","介绍，报告"],["mechanism","机械装置；运作原理"],["partly","部分地"],["follow along","跟上所讲的内容"],["at length","详细地，长时间地"]]},{"en":"Telling the Story Again","zh":"再讲一次自己的故事","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["In 2009 William returned to a TED stage with more room to tell his own story.","2009 年，威廉再次登上 TED 舞台，这一回，他有了更多时间亲口讲自己的故事。"],[" This time he could describe the interruption to his schooling and the books he had used.","他可以说到学业是怎样中断的，后来又用到了哪些书。"],[" He could guide the audience from the food emergency to the idea of building something that would help his family.","他可以带听众从粮食危机一路听到，自己怎么想到做件东西帮家里。"],[" Those connections give a different shape to a talk from one built entirely around the finished machine.","这些事连在一起，和一开始就只围着成品说的演讲，听起来有了不一样的脉络。"]],"translation":"2009 年，威廉再次登上 TED 舞台，这一回，他有了更多时间亲口讲自己的故事。他可以说到学业是怎样中断的，后来又用到了哪些书。他可以带听众从粮食危机一路听到，自己怎么想到做件东西帮家里。这些事连在一起，和一开始就只围着成品说的演讲，听起来有了不一样的脉络。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["The beginning of a story affects how people hear its ending.","故事从哪里开头，会影响人们怎样听结尾。"],[" Start with a picture of the windmill, and the audience may listen for the names of the pieces.","先放一张风车的照片，听众可能就想知道各个零件叫什么。"],[" Start with the time when William could no longer pay for school, and another question comes into view.","先讲威廉家交不起学费的时候，就看得见另一个问题了。"],[" What did he have to do in order to continue making progress?","为了还能继续学下去，他得做些什么？"],[" The same pieces of bicycle and plastic now appear after a search for a way to learn.","还是那些自行车和塑料零件，但它们现在出现在一个人寻找学习办法的过程之后。"],[" Viewers understand more of the route to the lamp.","人们也就多理解了一些走到那盏灯的路。"]],"translation":"故事从哪里开头，会影响人们怎样听结尾。先放一张风车的照片，听众可能就想知道各个零件叫什么。先讲威廉家交不起学费的时候，就看得见另一个问题了。为了还能继续学下去，他得做些什么？还是那些自行车和塑料零件，但它们现在出现在一个人寻找学习办法的过程之后。人们也就多理解了一些走到那盏灯的路。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["A talk also requires decisions about detail.","演讲还要求人决定细节的取舍。"],[" In a few minutes there is room to describe a library and a small generator, and perhaps to show a photograph of the machine.","几分钟里，可以讲到图书馆和一台小发电机，也许还能放一张机器的照片。"],[" A whole period of hunger or a long round of repairs cannot be shown at its full length.","挨饿的整个时期或者一轮轮修理的经过，很难完整展示。"],[" A speaker has to decide which details allow the audience to make sense of other things that are briefly mentioned.","演讲人得想想，要拿哪些细节出来，才能让听众也明白其他几件只能简略带过的事。"],[" William's own account is especially valuable because he chose which experiences he would put together in front of listeners.","威廉亲口讲的版本格外有价值，因为是他自己决定，把哪些经历放在一起说给听众。"]],"translation":"演讲还要求人决定细节的取舍。几分钟里，可以讲到图书馆和一台小发电机，也许还能放一张机器的照片。挨饿的整个时期或者一轮轮修理的经过，很难完整展示。演讲人得想想，要拿哪些细节出来，才能让听众也明白其他几件只能简略带过的事。威廉亲口讲的版本格外有价值，因为是他自己决定，把哪些经历放在一起说给听众。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["His talks allow readers to hear that account directly.","看两个演讲，可以直接听到他的讲述。"],[" There is a difference between hearing a story about what a person did and hearing the person explain what he was trying to do.","听别人说一个人做了什么，和听那个人解释他当时想做什么，感受不同。"],[" The audience can consider the size of the practical problem at each stage.","听众可以逐步想象那一刻的任务有多大。"],[" A boy looks for a book. A reader studies a drawing. A builder looks for a part.","一个男孩找一本书，一个读者研究一张图，一个造东西的人去找一个零件。"],[" The public story reaches people far away because those small acts give it a sequence they can follow.","这个故事能传到很远的地方，是因为这些小小的行动连起来，大家就能一路听下去。"]],"translation":"看两个演讲，可以直接听到他的讲述。听别人说一个人做了什么，和听那个人解释他当时想做什么，感受不同。听众可以逐步想象那一刻的任务有多大。一个男孩找一本书，一个读者研究一张图，一个造东西的人去找一个零件。这个故事能传到很远的地方，是因为这些小小的行动连起来，大家就能一路听下去。"}],"terms":[{"term":"interruption","meaning":"中断、使过程暂停的事","usage":"an interruption to one's education 指教育进程受干扰；without interruption 表示持续进行。","example":"Her return to class ended a long interruption to her studies.","exampleZh":"她重返课堂，结束了长期中断的学业。","meaningEn":"A pause or break in an activity that was already under way.","usageEn":"An interruption to one's education disrupts a period of study. Without interruption means the activity continues without a break."},{"term":"come into view","meaning":"进入视野、逐渐显现","usage":"可用于实景，也可比喻一段经历在叙述中变得清晰。","example":"As we climbed the hill, the tower came into view.","exampleZh":"我们爬上山时，看见塔出现在视野中。","forms":["comes into view"],"meaningEn":"To become visible or clear enough to notice.","usageEn":"A building can come into view on a journey. A question can come into view as a situation becomes clearer."},{"term":"at its full length","meaning":"以完整篇幅、充分展开地","usage":"at full length 侧重毫无缩减地展示；at length 可只表示讲得久或细。","example":"The book gave him room to tell the story at its full length.","exampleZh":"这本书给了他足够的篇幅来讲完整个故事。","meaningEn":"In its complete form, without being shortened.","usageEn":"At full length emphasizes the whole account. At length can suggest detail or duration even when some material is left out."},{"term":"sequence","meaning":"先后顺序、连续步骤","usage":"in sequence 指按顺序；a sequence of events 指相继发生的一系列事件。","example":"The diagram shows the sequence in which the parts were assembled.","exampleZh":"这张图展示了零件的组装顺序。","meaningEn":"A particular order in which events or steps follow one another.","usageEn":"Put the steps in sequence means arrange them in order. A sequence of events is a series linked by its order."}],"glossary":[["interruption","中断"],["come into view","进入视野，变得明显"],["at its full length","以完整的篇幅"],["briefly","简短地"],["directly","直接地"],["sequence","顺序，连续的过程"]]},{"en":"Back to Lessons","zh":"重新回到课堂","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["William's windmill brought attention to the person who had made it.","威廉的风车，让人们注意到了造机器的人。"],[" The opportunity to study again had a particular importance for him.","能重新上学，对他尤其重要。"],[" The ability to build a useful machine had shown what he could learn with limited resources.","能造出实用的机器，已经表明他能用有限的资源学到多少。"],[" A return to formal education gave him teachers, other students, and a wider range of subjects.","他重新接受学校教育，就有了老师、同学，也有了更广的学科可以学。"],[" He had already learned how difficult it could be to do without those things.","他先前已经知道，少了这些东西，学起来会有多难。"]],"translation":"威廉的风车，让人们注意到了造机器的人。能重新上学，对他尤其重要。能造出实用的机器，已经表明他能用有限的资源学到多少。他重新接受学校教育，就有了老师、同学，也有了更广的学科可以学。他先前已经知道，少了这些东西，学起来会有多难。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["William resumed school in Malawi and later studied at the African Leadership Academy in South Africa.","威廉在马拉维恢复了学业，后来到南非的非洲领导力学院学习。"],[" He eventually went to Dartmouth College in the United States and graduated in 2014.","再后来，他到美国达特茅斯学院上学，2014 年毕业。"],[" Those moves brought new places, different classmates, and unfamiliar expectations.","这些变化把他带到新的地方，见到不同的同学，也遇到不熟悉的要求。"],[" Each change required work at a new level.","每变一次，他就得在一个新的层次上努力。"],[" A windmill could help open a door, and a person still had to go through it and learn enough to stay there.","风车可以帮人打开一扇门，走进去以后，还是得学到足够的本领才能留下来。"]],"translation":"威廉在马拉维恢复了学业，后来到南非的非洲领导力学院学习。再后来，他到美国达特茅斯学院上学，2014 年毕业。这些变化把他带到新的地方，见到不同的同学，也遇到不熟悉的要求。每变一次，他就得在一个新的层次上努力。风车可以帮人打开一扇门，走进去以后，还是得学到足够的本领才能留下来。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Experience from Wimbe could be valuable in a classroom full of equipment.","在设备齐全的课堂里，温贝村的经验也能派上用场。"],[" William already knew that a clear diagram can lead to many practical choices. He knew that an idea changes as it meets available materials and that a useful result should be checked in more than one way.","威廉知道，一张清楚的示意图可以引出许多实际的选项，也知道主意遇上手里有的材料，形态就会变。有用的结果，也该用不止一种办法核实。"],[" Those lessons explain part of what a formal class offers in return.","这些体会，也能让人看到正式课堂能给他补上些什么。"],[" Having a laboratory or a teacher nearby makes it possible to test an explanation, compare it with other cases, and see why a particular result is likely to happen more than once.","附近有实验室、有老师，就能检验一种解释，把它和其他情况放在一起比，再试着弄懂为什么一个结果可能反复出现。"]],"translation":"在设备齐全的课堂里，温贝村的经验也能派上用场。威廉知道，一张清楚的示意图可以引出许多实际的选项，也知道主意遇上手里有的材料，形态就会变。有用的结果，也该用不止一种办法核实。这些体会，也能让人看到正式课堂能给他补上些什么。附近有实验室、有老师，就能检验一种解释，把它和其他情况放在一起比，再试着弄懂为什么一个结果可能反复出现。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["His return to education gives another ending to the library story.","重新上学，给早先的图书馆故事添上了另一个结尾。"],[" When fees interrupted his schooling, a local shelf of science books made it possible for him to keep going for a time.","学费让威廉的学校生活中断时，当地书架上的科学书让他继续学了一段。"],[" Years later, he had the chance to learn with many more people and resources.","多年以后，他有了机会，跟更多的人一起学习，用上更多资源。"],[" These settings belonged to one education.","这些地方构成的是同一个人的教育。"],[" The student who looked closely at a picture in a book and the student who made his way through a college programme both needed time to work through ideas.","仔细看书上的图片和努力读完大学课程，都得花时间把东西想通。"],[" The size of the classroom changed greatly. The task of paying attention to what he still had to learn remained familiar.","课堂的大小变了许多，留心自己还有哪些地方要学，仍是他熟悉的一件事。"]],"translation":"重新上学，给早先的图书馆故事添上了另一个结尾。学费让威廉的学校生活中断时，当地书架上的科学书让他继续学了一段。多年以后，他有了机会，跟更多的人一起学习，用上更多资源。这些地方构成的是同一个人的教育。仔细看书上的图片和努力读完大学课程，都得花时间把东西想通。课堂的大小变了许多，留心自己还有哪些地方要学，仍是他熟悉的一件事。"}],"terms":[{"term":"resume","forms":["resumed"],"meaning":"中断后重新开始","usage":"resume + 名词或动名词强调延续旧进程；名词 résumé 指简历，重音不同。","example":"She resumed her studies after a year away from school.","exampleZh":"离校一年后，她重新开始了学业。","meaningEn":"To begin an activity again after an interruption.","usageEn":"Resume can take a noun or an -ing form. The noun résumé has a different pronunciation and means a record of work experience."},{"term":"formal education","meaning":"正规学校教育","usage":"formal 指有课程和制度的教育；self-education 则是独立自学。","example":"The library helped him continue learning while formal education was out of reach.","exampleZh":"上不起正规学校期间，图书馆帮助他继续学习。","meaningEn":"Organized study through schools, colleges, or other institutions.","usageEn":"Formal describes the structured courses and institutions. Self-education describes learning you organize yourself."},{"term":"unfamiliar","meaning":"不熟悉、初次接触的","usage":"be unfamiliar with 表示自己对某事不熟悉，be unfamiliar to 则描述某事对某人而言陌生。","example":"The new equipment was unfamiliar to most of the students.","exampleZh":"大多数学生都没有接触过这套新设备。","meaningEn":"Not known well or not previously encountered.","usageEn":"A learner is unfamiliar with a topic. The topic is unfamiliar to the learner."},{"term":"work through","meaning":"逐步解决、一步步弄明白","usage":"work through a problem 暗示逐步骤处理；work on 只说明正在投入精力。","example":"They worked through the calculation on a sheet of paper.","exampleZh":"他们在纸上一步步算出了结果。","meaningEn":"To deal with something step by step until it is clearer or resolved.","usageEn":"Work through a problem suggests moving through several steps. Work on a problem says you are making an effort without specifying a sequence."}],"glossary":[["resume","重新开始"],["formal education","正规学校教育"],["unfamiliar","不熟悉的"],["laboratory","实验室"],["in return","作为回报，相应地"],["work through","逐步弄清，解决"]]},{"en":"Writing a Book Together","zh":"一起写一本书","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["In 2009 William and the writer Bryan Mealer published a memoir about William's life and his windmill.","2009 年，威廉和作家布莱恩·米勒合著了一本回忆录，讲威廉的生活和风车。"],[" A book offers room for scenes and relationships that a short talk has to pass over.","短演讲需要带过的场景和人际关系，一本书有地方展开。"],[" It can give people names. It can stay with a long period of difficulty and allow the reader to notice changes slowly.","书可以写出人物的名字，也可以停留在一段很长的困境里，让读者慢慢看到变化。"],[" The project that reaches a visible result in a few seconds onstage can take several chapters to develop on the page.","在舞台上几秒就能让人看到结果的项目，在纸上可能要花几章才发展到那里。"]],"translation":"2009 年，威廉和作家布莱恩·米勒合著了一本回忆录，讲威廉的生活和风车。短演讲需要带过的场景和人际关系，一本书有地方展开。书可以写出人物的名字，也可以停留在一段很长的困境里，让读者慢慢看到变化。在舞台上几秒就能让人看到结果的项目，在纸上可能要花几章才发展到那里。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["A memoir begins with somebody's life and makes choices about what to include.","回忆录从一个人的生活里取材，写作者会选择把哪些经历纳入书中。"],[" A writer can start near a moment of success, then go back to the events that explain it.","他可以从一次成功前后讲起，再转回去讲能够解释它的旧事。"],[" Another account can begin with a village, a family, or a childhood habit.","另一种叙述可以从村子、家庭或小时候的习惯开始。"],[" These choices affect where the reader gives most attention.","这些选择会影响读者把注意力更多放在哪里。"],[" The story of William's windmill has appeared in a book for adults, in editions for younger readers, and on film.","威廉的风车故事，见于成人书、面向年轻读者的版本，也见于电影。"],[" Those formats give their audiences different amounts of time and different ways of imagining a scene.","这些形式给观众或读者的时间不同，让人想象一个场景的方式也不同。"]],"translation":"回忆录从一个人的生活里取材，写作者会选择把哪些经历纳入书中。他可以从一次成功前后讲起，再转回去讲能够解释它的旧事。另一种叙述可以从村子、家庭或小时候的习惯开始。这些选择会影响读者把注意力更多放在哪里。威廉的风车故事，见于成人书、面向年轻读者的版本，也见于电影。这些形式给观众或读者的时间不同，让人想象一个场景的方式也不同。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["The invention is a useful point of comparison when you encounter two versions of the story.","遇上两个版本时，发明本身是一个好用的比较点。"],[" One account can explain a machine through a quick view of a blade or a wire.","一种叙述可以让人瞥一眼叶片或电线，就理解机器是怎么回事。"],[" Another can use several paragraphs to show why certain parts mattered.","另一种可以用好几段讲清某些零件为什么重要。"],[" A film can show people's faces as they respond. A talk can include an answer in William's voice.","电影能让人看到人物作出反应时的表情，演讲能让人听见威廉亲口回答。"],[" The life that supplied the events remains a source against which to check details that appear elsewhere.","其他版本里出现的细节，还可以回到当事人的生活经历中去核对。"]],"translation":"遇上两个版本时，发明本身是一个好用的比较点。一种叙述可以让人瞥一眼叶片或电线，就理解机器是怎么回事。另一种可以用好几段讲清某些零件为什么重要。电影能让人看到人物作出反应时的表情，演讲能让人听见威廉亲口回答。其他版本里出现的细节，还可以回到当事人的生活经历中去核对。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Readers who would like to read the memoir can take a number of questions with them.","想读回忆录的人，可以带着几个问题读下去。"],[" Which parts of William's experience does he describe closely?","威廉把哪些经历写得很细？"],[" How does he place his family and friends in the story?","他怎样写自己的家人和朋友？"],[" When does the work on the machine move forward, and when does it have to wait?","造机器的工作什么时候往前走，什么时候又只能等？"],[" Those questions help a reader notice how a finished book presents a life. They also draw attention to the years before and after a single success, when someone has to make decisions without knowing what will come of them.","这些问题能让读者留意，一本成书怎样呈现一个人的生活，也能让人注意到一次成功的前前后后，在那些年里，做决定的人并不知道最后会怎么样。"]],"translation":"想读回忆录的人，可以带着几个问题读下去。威廉把哪些经历写得很细？他怎样写自己的家人和朋友？造机器的工作什么时候往前走，什么时候又只能等？这些问题能让读者留意，一本成书怎样呈现一个人的生活，也能让人注意到一次成功的前前后后，在那些年里，做决定的人并不知道最后会怎么样。"}],"terms":[{"term":"memoir","meaning":"回忆录","usage":"memoir 往往聚焦人生的一段经历或主题；autobiography 通常按更长时段叙述一生。","example":"Her memoir describes the years she spent teaching in a village.","exampleZh":"她的回忆录讲述了在一个村庄教书的那几年。","meaningEn":"An account focused on the author's own experiences.","usageEn":"A memoir often selects a period, relationship, or theme. An autobiography usually covers a broader part of the author's life."},{"term":"pass over","meaning":"略过、没有展开","usage":"pass over a detail 常表示有意不多谈；被动 be passed over for promotion 指没得到晋升。","example":"The short interview passed over most of the technical difficulties.","exampleZh":"简短的采访略过了大部分技术困难。","meaningEn":"To leave something out or give it little attention.","usageEn":"Pass over a detail means move past it without much discussion. Be passed over for promotion means someone else was chosen."},{"term":"point of comparison","meaning":"比较的着眼点、比较基准","usage":"先找到两者能共同衡量的角度；for comparison 可在给出参照例子时使用。","example":"Running costs give us a useful point of comparison between the two designs.","exampleZh":"运行成本为两种设计提供了一个有用的比较角度。","meaningEn":"A shared feature or viewpoint useful for comparing things.","usageEn":"Here the invention lets readers compare different versions of the story. For comparison introduces an example or measurement used as a reference."},{"term":"come of","meaning":"由……产生、成为……的结果","usage":"What came of...? 询问尝试后的结果；come from 更常询问来源。","example":"What came of their first attempt to make a working pump?","exampleZh":"他们第一次尝试造出能用的水泵，结果如何？","meaningEn":"To arise as a result of an action or situation.","usageEn":"What came of the attempt? asks about its result. What did it come from? typically asks about its source."}],"glossary":[["memoir","回忆录"],["pass over","略过"],["edition","版本"],["point of comparison","用来比较的着眼点"],["encounter","遇到，接触到"],["come of","由……产生，成为……结果"]]},{"en":"How to Design with a Community","zh":"怎样和社区一起做设计","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["One lasting result of William's work is connected to an organisation called the Moving Windmills Project.","威廉的发明持续产生的影响，有一部分和一个叫 Moving Windmills 的组织连在一起。"],[" William is a co-founder.","威廉是共同创办人。"],[" The organisation describes its work in terms of local people taking part in the design of solutions.","这个组织在介绍工作时，强调让当地人参与设计解决办法。"],[" This approach grows out of a simple observation.","这种做法源于一个简单的观察。"],[" A person who lives with a problem can often describe how it changes through the day, who is most affected, and which attempts to fix it have already been tried.","生活在问题里的人，往往知道那个问题一天里会怎样变，谁最受影响，已经有人试过哪些办法。"]],"translation":"威廉的发明持续产生的影响，有一部分和一个叫 Moving Windmills 的组织连在一起。威廉是共同创办人。这个组织在介绍工作时，强调让当地人参与设计解决办法。这种做法源于一个简单的观察。生活在问题里的人，往往知道那个问题一天里会怎样变，谁最受影响，已经有人试过哪些办法。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Suppose a community is deciding how to improve access to water.","假设一个社区在商量怎样让取水容易些。"],[" Someone might first suggest a new pump.","最先有人提议的可能是装一台新水泵。"],[" Before that choice makes sense, it helps to know how far residents walk now, which source they use in the dry season, and what happens when a part needs replacing.","要判断这个选择好不好，最好先知道居民现在要走多远，旱季用什么水源，零件要换时会怎么样。"],[" A person bringing in equipment from a distance might know how the machine works.","从远处带设备来的人，可能很懂机器的原理。"],[" People who use the water know which distances, costs, and times of day the machine has to fit.","天天用水的人，知道机器要适应的距离、花费和使用时间。"],[" The project is better when those kinds of knowledge meet.","两方面的知识凑到一起，项目才能做得更好。"]],"translation":"假设一个社区在商量怎样让取水容易些。最先有人提议的可能是装一台新水泵。要判断这个选择好不好，最好先知道居民现在要走多远，旱季用什么水源，零件要换时会怎么样。从远处带设备来的人，可能很懂机器的原理。天天用水的人，知道机器要适应的距离、花费和使用时间。两方面的知识凑到一起，项目才能做得更好。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["The same applies to education.","教育也是这样。"],[" A room full of tools becomes useful when someone has time to teach, observe, and let a learner try again.","一屋子的工具有人抽出时间教、在一旁观察、再让学习的人试一次，就用得起来了。"],[" People have to be able to get to the room. They have to know which tools they are allowed to use and where to seek help.","人得来得到这个地方，也得知道允许他们用什么工具，有问题该到哪里找人帮忙。"],[" A building can create a place for this activity, and the people who use it put the learning into practice.","一栋楼能提供做这些事的地点，在里面活动的人，才让学习落到实处。"],[" Moving Windmills' materials describe learning, mentorship, and local knowledge as part of its design work.","Moving Windmills 的项目资料也把学习、指导和地方知识列在设计工作里。"]],"translation":"教育也是这样。一屋子的工具有人抽出时间教、在一旁观察、再让学习的人试一次，就用得起来了。人得来得到这个地方，也得知道允许他们用什么工具，有问题该到哪里找人帮忙。一栋楼能提供做这些事的地点，在里面活动的人，才让学习落到实处。Moving Windmills 的项目资料也把学习、指导和地方知识列在设计工作里。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["William's early project offers an example on a small scale.","威廉早期的项目，提供了一个小规模的例子。"],[" Reading a book helped him identify a possibility. Familiar parts helped him make that possibility real.","读书让他发现了一个可能，熟悉的旧零件让这个可能变得具体。"],[" A friend made a purchase possible, and a household had a reason to try the finished system.","一位朋友让他买得到东西，一家人又确实有理由试试成品。"],[" Working with a community expands the number of voices and decisions, yet retains the need to pay close attention to how people actually use things.","跟社区一起做，参与表达意见和作决定的人多了，但依然得留意大家实际上怎样用东西。"],[" The questions that arise in those conversations are part of the work itself.","这些谈话中冒出来的问题，也是设计工作的一部分。"]],"translation":"威廉早期的项目，提供了一个小规模的例子。读书让他发现了一个可能，熟悉的旧零件让这个可能变得具体。一位朋友让他买得到东西，一家人又确实有理由试试成品。跟社区一起做，参与表达意见和作决定的人多了，但依然得留意大家实际上怎样用东西。这些谈话中冒出来的问题，也是设计工作的一部分。"}],"terms":[{"term":"co-founder","meaning":"共同创办人","usage":"co- 表示共同；创办机构用 co-found，起步后加入的人则未必是 co-founder。","example":"One co-founder ran the workshops while the other arranged funding.","exampleZh":"一位共同创办人负责工作坊，另一位负责筹措资金。","meaningEn":"One of the people who start an organization together.","usageEn":"Co- expresses shared action. A co-founder establishes the organization, while an early member may join after it was founded."},{"term":"take part in","meaning":"参加并参与其中","usage":"后接活动名称；take part 不仅在场，语义通常突出实际参与。","example":"Families took part in planning the new learning centre.","exampleZh":"各个家庭参与了新学习中心的规划。","forms":["taking part in"],"meaningEn":"To participate in an activity.","usageEn":"In introduces the activity. Take part suggests involvement, whereas attend can simply mean be present."},{"term":"mentorship","meaning":"由经验丰富的人提供的指导","usage":"mentor 是指导者；mentorship 可指这种长期关系或有组织的指导体系。","example":"The programme paired technical training with mentorship.","exampleZh":"该项目把技术培训与导师指导结合起来。","meaningEn":"Support and guidance from someone with more experience.","usageEn":"A mentor is the person providing guidance. Mentorship can describe an ongoing relationship or a structured programme."},{"term":"put into practice","forms":["into practice"],"meaning":"付诸实践","usage":"put + 计划或知识 + into practice，强调从计划或理解走向实际操作。","example":"The workshop gave them a chance to put what they had learned into practice.","exampleZh":"工作坊让他们有机会把学到的东西应用到实践中。","meaningEn":"To apply a plan, idea, or skill in a real situation.","usageEn":"The object can go between put and into practice, as in put the plan into practice. The phrase marks the shift from understanding or planning to doing."}],"glossary":[["lasting","长久的"],["co-founder","共同创办人"],["take part in","参加，参与"],["resident","居民"],["mentorship","由有经验的人提供指导"],["put into practice","付诸实践"]]},{"en":"Books and Computers Close to Home","zh":"找得到书，也用得上电脑","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["In the Kasungu area, Moving Windmills has described a plan to establish community learning spaces at five schools.","在卡松古一带，Moving Windmills 曾介绍过一项计划，要在五所学校设立面向社区的学习场所。"],[" Its project materials describe books, computers, solar electricity, and local access to educational resources.","项目资料写到了图书、电脑、太阳能供电，以及让当地人有地方使用教育资源。"],[" The spaces are intended to welcome young people who are out of school as well as current students.","这些场所既欢迎在校学生，也欢迎没在上学的年轻人。"],[" That last detail connects the work directly with a difficulty William knew at fourteen.","最后这一点，正接上了威廉十四岁时知道的难处。"],[" Having no place in a class can make it much harder to find the next thing to learn.","人一旦离开了教室，就可能很难找到下一样可以学的事。"]],"translation":"在卡松古一带，Moving Windmills 曾介绍过一项计划，要在五所学校设立面向社区的学习场所。项目资料写到了图书、电脑、太阳能供电，以及让当地人有地方使用教育资源。这些场所既欢迎在校学生，也欢迎没在上学的年轻人。最后这一点，正接上了威廉十四岁时知道的难处。人一旦离开了教室，就可能很难找到下一样可以学的事。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["A learning space with computers faces a problem that a shelf of printed books does not.","有电脑的学习场所，要面对一个纸质书架没有的问题。"],[" A computer needs power. Many digital resources also seem to need an internet connection.","电脑需要电，许多数字资源看起来还需要联网。"],[" One answer described by the organisation is to store material so that a visitor can open it locally.","这个组织介绍过一个办法，就是把资料存下来，让来访者能在本地打开。"],[" Once the files are there, a reader can look up a subject, open a stored explanation, and return to it without being online at the time.","文件一旦存好，读者可以查一个主题，打开已经保存的讲解，以后再来看时，也不用正好连着网。"],[" Keeping digital material nearby can offer some of the same freedom as keeping books on a shelf.","把数字资料留在身边，可以带来一些像书放在架上时那样的自由。"]],"translation":"有电脑的学习场所，要面对一个纸质书架没有的问题。电脑需要电，许多数字资源看起来还需要联网。这个组织介绍过一个办法，就是把资料存下来，让来访者能在本地打开。文件一旦存好，读者可以查一个主题，打开已经保存的讲解，以后再来看时，也不用正好连着网。把数字资料留在身边，可以带来一些像书放在架上时那样的自由。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["People also belong in the picture.","这里也少不了人。"],[" Someone has to know what is in the room, how to help visitors find things, and who can repair the equipment.","得有人知道屋里有哪些东西，怎样帮来访者找到它们，设备坏了谁能修。"],[" A beginner may need to spend time with a mentor before being ready to use a tool alone.","新手或许得先跟着指导者学一阵，之后才会独自使用工具。"],[" A younger student will need reading material that fits a different stage from the material an older student needs.","年龄小的学生需要的读物，和大一点的学生适合的也不一样。"],[" Giving both of them access involves more than buying a set of objects.","想让两个人都用得上资源，需要做的事，比买来一套物件更多。"]],"translation":"这里也少不了人。得有人知道屋里有哪些东西，怎样帮来访者找到它们，设备坏了谁能修。新手或许得先跟着指导者学一阵，之后才会独自使用工具。年龄小的学生需要的读物，和大一点的学生适合的也不一样。想让两个人都用得上资源，需要做的事，比买来一套物件更多。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["William once had to build a route from a page in a book to an experiment he could do.","威廉曾经得自己从书里的一页摸索到一个做得成的实验。"],[" A learning space that offers materials, time, and guidance shortens parts of that route.","一个能提供材料、时间和指导的学习场所，可以缩短其中的一些路。"],[" It leaves the reader with freedom to decide what question to pursue.","至于想追着哪一个问题往下学，仍留给读者自己决定。"],[" In a district where one student once had to wait for a windmill picture to open a new direction, the next useful drawing or example can now be made easier to find.","在这个区里，曾经有一名学生得等到一本书里的风车图，才发现一个新方向。现在，人们可以让下一幅有用的图或下一个好例子变得更容易找到。"]],"translation":"威廉曾经得自己从书里的一页摸索到一个做得成的实验。一个能提供材料、时间和指导的学习场所，可以缩短其中的一些路。至于想追着哪一个问题往下学，仍留给读者自己决定。在这个区里，曾经有一名学生得等到一本书里的风车图，才发现一个新方向。现在，人们可以让下一幅有用的图或下一个好例子变得更容易找到。"}],"terms":[{"term":"establish","meaning":"建立、设立","usage":"可接机构、流程或联系；establish that... 另有查明并证实事实之义。","example":"They established a learning centre near the market.","exampleZh":"他们在集市附近设立了一个学习中心。","meaningEn":"To set up an organization, arrangement, or process.","usageEn":"Establish can take an institution, practice, or connection as its object. Establish that introduces a fact confirmed through evidence."},{"term":"internet connection","meaning":"网络连接","usage":"have an internet connection 指有可用网络；connect to the internet 表示设备连接网络。","example":"Students could download books when the internet connection was working.","exampleZh":"网络连接正常时，学生们就能下载书籍。","meaningEn":"A usable link to the internet.","usageEn":"Have an internet connection describes access. Connect to the internet describes how a device or user obtains that access."},{"term":"locally","meaning":"在当地、就近地","usage":"locally sourced parts 指从当地取得的零件；local 作形容词时放在名词前。","example":"Most of the replacement materials could be bought locally.","exampleZh":"大部分替换材料可以在当地买到。","meaningEn":"On site or on the device itself, without retrieving something online.","usageEn":"A locally stored file can be opened without going online. Locally can also refer to the surrounding area, as in locally sourced parts."},{"term":"pursue","meaning":"继续探究、致力于追求","usage":"常接 question、interest、career 等；pursue an idea 指有意识地把想法继续探索下去。","example":"The library gave her a place to pursue her interest in electronics.","exampleZh":"图书馆让她有地方继续探索自己感兴趣的电子技术。","meaningEn":"To continue working on an idea, interest, or goal with deliberate effort.","usageEn":"Pursue a question means keep investigating it. Pursue a career uses the same sense of sustained action toward a goal."}],"glossary":[["establish","设立，建立"],["current student","在校学生"],["internet connection","网络连接"],["locally","在本地"],["mentor","指导者，导师"],["pursue","继续探究，追求"]]},{"en":"Sunlight Joins the Story","zh":"太阳光也走进了故事","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["The use of solar electricity in the learning spaces introduces a second way to gather energy near the place where it is needed.","学习场所用到太阳能供电，这让我们看到另一种在用电地点附近取能的办法。"],[" A solar panel receives light.","太阳能板接收光。"],[" Inside it, suitable materials turn some of that light energy into electrical energy.","板内合适的材料把一部分光能转化成电能。"],[" The panel can do this without spinning blades or a bicycle generator.","它不用靠飞转的叶片，也不用靠自行车发电机，就能做到这件事。"],[" It still has to be mounted, connected, and looked after by people who understand what it supplies.","它依然需要装好、接好，并由懂得它给什么供电的人维护。"]],"translation":"学习场所用到太阳能供电，这让我们看到另一种在用电地点附近取能的办法。太阳能板接收光。板内合适的材料把一部分光能转化成电能。它不用靠飞转的叶片，也不用靠自行车发电机，就能做到这件事。它依然需要装好、接好，并由懂得它给什么供电的人维护。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["A windmill and a solar panel have different relationships with weather and time.","风车和太阳能板与天气、时间的关系不一样。"],[" A windmill can run after sunset if there is enough wind.","太阳落山后，只要风够大，风车还能转。"],[" A solar panel produces its power while light reaches it.","太阳能板得有光照到，才能发电。"],[" Tall trees or buildings can block light from a panel.","高大的树和房子会挡住照到板上的光。"],[" Nearby obstacles can affect the wind reaching a small turbine.","附近的障碍物也会影响到达小型风机的气流。"],[" Choosing a place for either machine calls for a closer look at the actual site over time.","给任何一种设备选地方，都得花一段时间仔细看看现场。"]],"translation":"风车和太阳能板与天气、时间的关系不一样。太阳落山后，只要风够大，风车还能转。太阳能板得有光照到，才能发电。高大的树和房子会挡住照到板上的光。附近的障碍物也会影响到达小型风机的气流。给任何一种设备选地方，都得花一段时间仔细看看现场。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["The place also tells people what kind of supply is needed.","实际使用的地方，也会告诉人们需要什么样的供电。"],[" A classroom may use a computer during daylight for much of the year.","一间教室在一年里大部分时候，可能都在白天用电脑。"],[" A family may want light in the hours after sundown.","一家人想用灯的时间，或许就在日落后的几个钟头。"],[" A clinic might need a supply for equipment at times nobody can predict.","一间诊所可能随时要启用某台设备，事前没人能确定具体时间。"],[" The right ways to collect, store, and share energy depend in part on those patterns.","应该怎样发电、怎样储能、怎样分配，一部分就要看这些使用规律。"],[" A machine that is excellent for one task will need more support when it is asked to do another.","做一件事很好用的机器，换个任务时可能需要更多配套设备。"]],"translation":"实际使用的地方，也会告诉人们需要什么样的供电。一间教室在一年里大部分时候，可能都在白天用电脑。一家人想用灯的时间，或许就在日落后的几个钟头。一间诊所可能随时要启用某台设备，事前没人能确定具体时间。应该怎样发电、怎样储能、怎样分配，一部分就要看这些使用规律。做一件事很好用的机器，换个任务时可能需要更多配套设备。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Those decisions give a new meaning to the first little lamp in William's house.","这些选择，也让威廉家第一盏小灯有了新的含义。"],[" A lamp was a task close enough for him to see when it was solved.","灯就在身边，问题解决了，他能看得见。"],[" A learning space with several devices has to do more work and needs people able to care for it.","摆了好几种设备的学习场所，有更多的工作要做，也需要有人会照看设备。"],[" A village can use several kinds of technology across different places.","一个村子可以在不同地方用上几种技术。"],[" The connection with William's early work lies in the habit of beginning with a job people need done and looking carefully at what the place can supply.","它和威廉早期工作的联系，在于先看人们有哪些事需要做完，再仔细看看当地能提供些什么。"],[" The first step is to learn what people are trying to do on an ordinary day.","第一步是了解，一个平常日子里，大家正想做些什么。"]],"translation":"这些选择，也让威廉家第一盏小灯有了新的含义。灯就在身边，问题解决了，他能看得见。摆了好几种设备的学习场所，有更多的工作要做，也需要有人会照看设备。一个村子可以在不同地方用上几种技术。它和威廉早期工作的联系，在于先看人们有哪些事需要做完，再仔细看看当地能提供些什么。第一步是了解，一个平常日子里，大家正想做些什么。"}],"terms":[{"term":"solar panel","meaning":"太阳能板","usage":"本文指把阳光转成电能的光伏板；mount solar panels 强调固定安装。","example":"Two solar panels supplied power for the classroom lights.","exampleZh":"两块太阳能板为教室照明供电。","meaningEn":"A panel that converts sunlight into electricity in this context.","usageEn":"The chapter refers to a photovoltaic panel. To mount solar panels is to fix them in position."},{"term":"mount","forms":["mounted"],"meaning":"安装并固定","usage":"mount A on B 表示把 A 固定在 B 上；install 涵盖布线、调试等更完整的安装过程。","example":"Workers mounted the panels on a roof that received sunlight all day.","exampleZh":"工人把面板固定在一处整天能晒到太阳的屋顶上。","meaningEn":"To attach something securely in a particular position.","usageEn":"Mount A on B identifies the support or surface. Install can include additional steps such as wiring and testing."},{"term":"sundown","meaning":"日落","usage":"after sundown 指日落以后；sunset 还可用来描述日落的景色。","example":"The batteries kept the lights on after sundown.","exampleZh":"日落后，电池让灯继续亮着。","meaningEn":"The time when the sun goes below the horizon.","usageEn":"After sundown means after the sun has set. Sunset can also describe the appearance of the sky at that time."},{"term":"in part","meaning":"部分地、在某种程度上","usage":"partly 的常用同义表达；due in part to 常用于说明某个结果的一部分原因。","example":"The centre succeeded in part because local residents helped run it.","exampleZh":"学习中心办得成功，部分是因为当地居民参与管理。","meaningEn":"Partly or to some extent.","usageEn":"In part often qualifies a cause, as in due in part to the weather. It signals that other things also contributed."}],"glossary":[["solar panel","太阳能板"],["mount","安装，固定"],["sundown","日落"],["block","挡住，阻挡"],["clinic","诊所"],["in part","部分地"]]},{"en":"The Town Where a Part Can Be Fixed","zh":"零件坏了以后去哪里修","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Think about a project a year after the first photograph is taken.","想想一个项目拍下第一张照片一年后的情形。"],[" A machine has served people for a long time.","机器已经为人工作了很久。"],[" Now one part is wearing out, and the person who originally installed it is working somewhere else.","现在一个零件快磨坏了，当初安装的人却在别处干活。"],[" On paper, the machine still belongs to the community.","按记载，这台机器还属于当地社区。"],[" In practice, its future depends on who can recognise the fault, where a suitable replacement can be found, and who can arrange the work.","实际能不能继续用，要看谁认得出故障，哪里找得到合适的替换件，谁能张罗修理。"]],"translation":"想想一个项目拍下第一张照片一年后的情形。机器已经为人工作了很久。现在一个零件快磨坏了，当初安装的人却在别处干活。按记载，这台机器还属于当地社区。实际能不能继续用，要看谁认得出故障，哪里找得到合适的替换件，谁能张罗修理。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["There is a useful reason to pay attention to a nearby repair shop or a person who understands tools.","留意附近的修理铺和会用工具的人，是有道理的。"],[" The repairer knows which parts are sold in town, what can be recovered from older machines, and what will take time to order.","修理的人知道镇上卖哪些零件，哪些能从旧机器上拆到，哪些订购了还得等。"],[" A design that makes room for that knowledge can be easier to keep working.","设计的时候容得下这些知识，机器就可能更容易一直用下去。"],[" Wherever training is available, another person can learn enough to take over a repair later.","有地方可以培训时，也就能再教会一个人，以后让他接手维修。"],[" The benefit of the training might only show up months after the machine first works.","这份培训的好处，也许要等机器能用了好几个月，才会显现。"]],"translation":"留意附近的修理铺和会用工具的人，是有道理的。修理的人知道镇上卖哪些零件，哪些能从旧机器上拆到，哪些订购了还得等。设计的时候容得下这些知识，机器就可能更容易一直用下去。有地方可以培训时，也就能再教会一个人，以后让他接手维修。这份培训的好处，也许要等机器能用了好几个月，才会显现。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Parts made for a different purpose can be valuable when a builder has no ready solution.","没有现成办法时，原本另有用途的零件可能很有价值。"],[" In some cases a commonly sold part offers advantages of its own.","有时候，市面上常卖的配件也有自己的好处。"],[" People can recognise it and expect to find another one.","人们认得它，也大概找得到另一个。"],[" In still other cases it makes sense to choose a special part because the job places greater demands on it.","有时候工作要求更高，挑一件专门的配件更合理。"],[" William's switch from a dynamo to a treadmill motor gives us a point to think from.","威廉把小发电机换成跑步机电机，给了我们一个思考的起点。"],[" Materials and equipment can change as the purpose and the resources of the project change.","项目的目的和手头的资源变了，选择的材料和设备也可以跟着变。"]],"translation":"没有现成办法时，原本另有用途的零件可能很有价值。有时候，市面上常卖的配件也有自己的好处。人们认得它，也大概找得到另一个。有时候工作要求更高，挑一件专门的配件更合理。威廉把小发电机换成跑步机电机，给了我们一个思考的起点。项目的目的和手头的资源变了，选择的材料和设备也可以跟着变。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["A useful machine can therefore create a challenge for the town as well as for the inventor.","所以，一台有用的机器既给发明者提出了挑战，也给镇上的人出了题。"],[" People have to agree who will use it, who can repair it, and where the money for that work will come from.","大家得商量谁能用、谁能修、修理的钱从哪里来。"],[" Every time someone can fix a problem with local knowledge and available materials, more of the system's value stays close to the people using it.","每次有人能用本地的知识和找得到的材料解决故障，这套系统就多留了一点价值给身边用它的人。"],[" The first lamp is still a good moment in the story.","第一盏灯亮起，依然是故事里一个好时刻。"],[" A light that people can bring back after it fails has a story of its own.","灯灭了之后，还能有人把它修亮，那又是一个值得讲的故事。"]],"translation":"所以，一台有用的机器既给发明者提出了挑战，也给镇上的人出了题。大家得商量谁能用、谁能修、修理的钱从哪里来。每次有人能用本地的知识和找得到的材料解决故障，这套系统就多留了一点价值给身边用它的人。第一盏灯亮起，依然是故事里一个好时刻。灯灭了之后，还能有人把它修亮，那又是一个值得讲的故事。"}],"terms":[{"term":"replacement","meaning":"替换件、替代品","usage":"a replacement for + 被替换物；replacement 作定语可见 replacement parts。","example":"They needed a replacement for the damaged switch.","exampleZh":"他们需要一个替换件换掉损坏的开关。","meaningEn":"A part or object that takes the place of another.","usageEn":"Use a replacement for to identify the thing replaced. Replacement parts uses the noun as a modifier."},{"term":"in practice","meaning":"实际应用中、操作起来","usage":"常与 in theory 配合，讨论设想与结果；put into practice 强调把设想实际执行。","example":"The process looked easy on paper, but in practice it took a day.","exampleZh":"流程写在纸上似乎简单，实际做起来花了一整天。","meaningEn":"In actual use or real conditions.","usageEn":"In theory and in practice can contrast what should happen with what does happen. Put into practice shows the act of applying an idea."},{"term":"take over","meaning":"接手、继任负责","usage":"take over from somebody 强调交接者；take over responsibility for... 强调接手的职责。","example":"A local team took over maintenance when the workshop closed.","exampleZh":"工作坊关闭后，本地团队接手了维护。","meaningEn":"To assume a task or responsibility that someone else handled before.","usageEn":"Take over from names the previous person. Take over responsibility for names what you now manage."},{"term":"place demands on","meaning":"给……带来要求或负担","usage":"demands 常用复数，可接系统、人或资源；place heavy demands on 强调负担重。","example":"Daily use placed extra demands on the battery.","exampleZh":"日常使用给电池带来了额外负担。","forms":["places greater demands on"],"meaningEn":"To require effort, capacity, or resources from someone or something.","usageEn":"Demands is often plural. Place heavy demands on emphasizes the burden on the person or system supplying what is needed."}],"glossary":[["install","安装"],["replacement","替换件，替代物"],["in practice","在实际中"],["take over","接手"],["place demands on","对……提出要求"],["bring back","使恢复，重新带回来"]]},{"en":"What the Light Leaves Us With","zh":"那盏灯留下的问题","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Return to the house in Wimbe.","回到温贝村的那间屋子。"],[" In daylight a visitor can see a tower and the parts it carries.","白天去看，可以见到一座塔，还有上面托着的零件。"],[" At night the visitor can see the result from inside the house.","夜里在屋内，就能看见结果。"],[" The lamp is now a familiar object in an unfamiliar arrangement.","灯本来是件常见的东西，却被安放在一种少见的系统里。"],[" It invites a person to trace its power back through a wire, a generator, and some moving blades, all the way to the wind outside.","有人顺着它的电沿路往回找，就会经过电线、发电机、活动的叶片，一直找到外面的风。"]],"translation":"回到温贝村的那间屋子。白天去看，可以见到一座塔，还有上面托着的零件。夜里在屋内，就能看见结果。灯本来是件常见的东西，却被安放在一种少见的系统里。有人顺着它的电沿路往回找，就会经过电线、发电机、活动的叶片，一直找到外面的风。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["A different path leads through the people and places behind it.","还有一条路，通向机器背后的人和地方。"],[" There is a classroom William could no longer attend and a shelf he could return to.","有一间威廉后来去不了的教室，也有一个他还能回去看书的书架。"],[" There is a friend who made a purchase possible. There are people opening radios and storing parts they might one day need. There are later classrooms and larger audiences, where a person who once worked close to home could learn from and teach people he had never expected to meet.","有一位帮他买到东西的朋友，也有人拆开收音机，存下一些哪天也许用得着的零件。之后还有新的课堂、更大群的听众。一个过去只在家附近动手做东西的人，可以向他从未想到会遇见的人学习，也有东西能教给他们。"],[" Every point on that path changed what he could do next.","这条路上的每一站，都改变了他下一步能做什么。"]],"translation":"还有一条路，通向机器背后的人和地方。有一间威廉后来去不了的教室，也有一个他还能回去看书的书架。有一位帮他买到东西的朋友，也有人拆开收音机，存下一些哪天也许用得着的零件。之后还有新的课堂、更大群的听众。一个过去只在家附近动手做东西的人，可以向他从未想到会遇见的人学习，也有东西能教给他们。这条路上的每一站，都改变了他下一步能做什么。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["The early windmill tells us something precise about how a piece of knowledge begins to be useful.","早期的风车讲清了一件具体的事，一点知识怎样开始派上用场。"],[" William learned from a book that wind could do work. Then he asked whether the materials he actually had could do a small job that mattered at home. The answer took time to build, and it was still open to change after the first bulb lit.","威廉从书里知道了风能做功，然后问自己，手里真有的材料，能不能完成一个家里用得着的小任务。要把这个答案做出来，需要时间。第一只灯泡亮了之后，它也一直还有调整的余地。"],[" A later visit to the tower could bring a new generator, a different measure of success, or another question about water.","以后哪天再去塔边，会带去一台新发电机，也可能改用一种办法衡量做得好不好，还可能想起另一个关于水的问题。"]],"translation":"早期的风车讲清了一件具体的事，一点知识怎样开始派上用场。威廉从书里知道了风能做功，然后问自己，手里真有的材料，能不能完成一个家里用得着的小任务。要把这个答案做出来，需要时间。第一只灯泡亮了之后，它也一直还有调整的余地。以后哪天再去塔边，会带去一台新发电机，也可能改用一种办法衡量做得好不好，还可能想起另一个关于水的问题。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Think, finally, about the kind of question a person could carry away from this story.","最后，可以想想，从这个故事里能带走怎样的问题。"],[" You can start with a familiar object and ask what part of its job depends on motion, light, heat, or something else that changes.","可以从一个熟悉的物件开始，问它做的哪一部分事得靠运动、光、热，或者别的会变化的条件。"],[" You can ask who repairs it or who goes without it.","也可以问谁会修它，还有谁没有它可用。"],[" Such questions give ordinary objects a history as well as a purpose.","这些问题，让日常物件除了用途，还有了来历。"],[" For William, the questions happened to lead from a village library to a windmill.","对威廉来说，它们恰好从村里的图书馆通到了风车那里。"],[" They made it possible for the people in one house to look up from an ordinary evening and see their room in a different light.","这些问题，让一户人家在平常的夜晚抬起头，第一次在风送来的灯光下看清自己的房间。"]],"translation":"最后，可以想想，从这个故事里能带走怎样的问题。可以从一个熟悉的物件开始，问它做的哪一部分事得靠运动、光、热，或者别的会变化的条件。也可以问谁会修它，还有谁没有它可用。这些问题，让日常物件除了用途，还有了来历。对威廉来说，它们恰好从村里的图书馆通到了风车那里。这些问题，让一户人家在平常的夜晚抬起头，第一次在风送来的灯光下看清自己的房间。"}],"terms":[{"term":"carry","forms":["carries"],"meaning":"承载、托住","usage":"指支架、塔所承载的部件；carry a message 可指传递，carry 的宾语会改变具体含义。","example":"The wooden tower was tall enough to carry the blades above the roof.","exampleZh":"木塔够高，能把叶片架在屋顶之上。","meaningEn":"To support the weight of something, here the parts attached to a tower.","usageEn":"A frame can carry a load. Carry a message uses the same verb to mean convey information."},{"term":"trace back","meaning":"沿着线索追溯到来源","usage":"trace A back to B，B 是起点或原因；字面上也可顺着电流路径往回查。","example":"They traced the power failure back to a loose connection.","exampleZh":"他们沿着线索查出断电是接头松动造成的。","forms":["trace its power back"],"meaningEn":"To follow a path or chain of events toward its source.","usageEn":"Trace A back to B identifies B as the origin. Here the physical route leads from the lamp through the system to the wind."},{"term":"go without","meaning":"在缺少某物的情况下生活或做事","usage":"go without + 物，常用于缺少应有的资源；can do without 也可表示某物可有可无。","example":"The village sometimes had to go without electricity for several days.","exampleZh":"村子有时只得好几天没电可用。","forms":["goes without"],"meaningEn":"To continue when something normally needed is absent.","usageEn":"Go without often takes a necessity such as food. Can do without can also express that something is optional."},{"term":"carry away","meaning":"从经历中带走某种认识","usage":"carry away a lesson 意为从一段经历有所收获；be carried away 另指兴奋过头或冲昏头脑。","example":"What did you carry away from your time at the repair shop?","exampleZh":"你在修理店的这段经历给了你什么收获？","meaningEn":"To leave an experience with a lesson or idea you keep.","usageEn":"Carry away a lesson describes what you learned and retained. Be carried away describes being so excited that you lose restraint."}],"glossary":[["carry","承载，托住"],["trace back","追溯，沿路往回找"],["go without","在缺少……的情况下生活"],["precise","准确而具体的"],["be open to","仍有……的可能"],["carry away","带走，此处指从故事中获得"]]},{"zh":"资料来源","intro":"本读本按公开资料撰写。威廉的经历主要参考他的演讲、博客及相关机构的记录。关于农业、发电和维修的例子用于帮助理解。全书英文正文共 10,221 词。","sources":[{"label":"威廉在 TEDGlobal 2007 的访谈","url":"https://www.ted.com/talks/william_kamkwamba_how_i_built_a_windmill","detail":"　登台经过、风车材料与家用照明。"},{"label":"威廉在 TEDGlobal 2009 的演讲","url":"https://www.ted.com/talks/william_kamkwamba_how_i_harnessed_the_wind","detail":"　学业中断、图书馆自学及早期风车。"},{"label":"威廉 2007 年的风车记录","url":"https://movingwindmills.org/2007/07/hacking-my-wind.html","detail":"　回温贝村改装风车，以及跑步机电机和电压表的来历。"},{"label":"Moving Windmills 项目资料","url":"https://movingwindmills.org/wp-content/uploads/2024/02/The-Dynamo-Effect-Create-Your-Own-Dynamo-Moments-with-Moving-Windmills.pdf","detail":"　吉尔伯特对早期项目的帮助。"},{"label":"Moving Windmills 社区学习点","url":"https://movingwindmills.org/project/community-hubs","detail":"　卡松古的图书、电脑与太阳能供电计划。"},{"label":"联合国粮农组织与世界粮食计划署 2002 年报告","url":"https://www.fao.org/4/y6811e/y6811e00.htm","detail":"　马拉维的粮食短缺、天气与粮价。"},{"label":"达特茅斯学院对威廉的访谈","url":"https://home.dartmouth.edu/news/2012/01/video-conversation-william-kamkwamba-14","detail":"　复学经历、非洲领导力学院和回忆录。"}],"en":"Sources","terms":[],"glossary":[],"blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["This reader draws on publicly available materials. William’s story is based mainly on his talks, his blog, and records from relevant organizations. The examples about farming, electricity generation, and repair help explain how things work. The English text contains 10,221 words.","本读本按公开资料撰写。威廉的经历主要参考他的演讲、博客及相关机构的记录。关于农业、发电和维修的例子用于帮助理解。全书英文正文共 10,221 词。"]],"translation":"本读本按公开资料撰写。威廉的经历主要参考他的演讲、博客及相关机构的记录。关于农业、发电和维修的例子用于帮助理解。全书英文正文共 10,221 词。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["TEDGlobal 2007 interview with William Kamkwamba — How he came to speak at TEDGlobal, what the windmill was made of, and how it lit his home.","威廉在 TEDGlobal 2007 的访谈　登台经过、风车材料与家用照明。"]],"translation":"威廉在 TEDGlobal 2007 的访谈　登台经过、风车材料与家用照明。","url":"https://www.ted.com/talks/william_kamkwamba_how_i_built_a_windmill"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["William Kamkwamba’s TEDGlobal 2009 talk — Leaving school, teaching himself at the library, and building an early windmill.","威廉在 TEDGlobal 2009 的演讲　学业中断、图书馆自学及早期风车。"]],"translation":"威廉在 TEDGlobal 2009 的演讲　学业中断、图书馆自学及早期风车。","url":"https://www.ted.com/talks/william_kamkwamba_how_i_harnessed_the_wind"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["William’s 2007 account of rebuilding his windmill — Returning to Wimbe to upgrade the windmill and finding a treadmill motor and a voltmeter.","威廉 2007 年的风车记录　回温贝村改装风车，以及跑步机电机和电压表的来历。"]],"translation":"威廉 2007 年的风车记录　回温贝村改装风车，以及跑步机电机和电压表的来历。","url":"https://movingwindmills.org/2007/07/hacking-my-wind.html"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Moving Windmills project materials — Gilbert’s contribution to the early project.","Moving Windmills 项目资料　吉尔伯特对早期项目的帮助。"]],"translation":"Moving Windmills 项目资料　吉尔伯特对早期项目的帮助。","url":"https://movingwindmills.org/wp-content/uploads/2024/02/The-Dynamo-Effect-Create-Your-Own-Dynamo-Moments-with-Moving-Windmills.pdf"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Moving Windmills community learning hubs — Plans for books, computers, and solar power in Kasungu.","Moving Windmills 社区学习点　卡松古的图书、电脑与太阳能供电计划。"]],"translation":"Moving Windmills 社区学习点　卡松古的图书、电脑与太阳能供电计划。","url":"https://movingwindmills.org/project/community-hubs"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["FAO and World Food Programme report, 2002 — Food shortages, weather, and grain prices in Malawi.","联合国粮农组织与世界粮食计划署 2002 年报告　马拉维的粮食短缺、天气与粮价。"]],"translation":"联合国粮农组织与世界粮食计划署 2002 年报告　马拉维的粮食短缺、天气与粮价。","url":"https://www.fao.org/4/y6811e/y6811e00.htm"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Dartmouth College interview with William Kamkwamba — Returning to school, the African Leadership Academy, and writing his memoir.","达特茅斯学院对威廉的访谈　复学经历、非洲领导力学院和回忆录。"]],"translation":"达特茅斯学院对威廉的访谈　复学经历、非洲领导力学院和回忆录。","url":"https://home.dartmouth.edu/news/2012/01/video-conversation-william-kamkwamba-14"}]}]},{"id":"valorant","zh":"VALORANT 1","en":"VALORANT 1","chapters":[{"en":"Welcome to VALORANT","zh":"欢迎来到无畏契约","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["VALORANT is a tactical 5v5 first-person shooter in which two teams compete to complete objectives, control territory, and eliminate each other.","《VALORANT》（无畏契约）是一款 5 对 5 的第一人称战术射击游戏。两支队伍通过完成目标、控制地图区域以及消灭对手来争夺胜利。"]],"translation":"《VALORANT》（无畏契约）是一款 5 对 5 的第一人称战术射击游戏。两支队伍通过完成目标、控制地图区域以及消灭对手来争夺胜利。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["But there is something that makes VALORANT different from ordinary shooting games.","但它与普通射击游戏有一个很大的不同。"]],"translation":"但它与普通射击游戏有一个很大的不同。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["You are not simply running around looking for enemies. Every movement has a purpose. Every ability can change the situation. Every second matters.","你并不是单纯地在地图上四处跑动、寻找敌人。每一次移动都有目的，每一个技能都可能改变战局，每一秒都很重要。"]],"translation":"你并不是单纯地在地图上四处跑动、寻找敌人。每一次移动都有目的，每一个技能都可能改变战局，每一秒都很重要。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["One team attacks, while the other defends.","一支队伍负责进攻，另一支队伍负责防守。"]],"translation":"一支队伍负责进攻，另一支队伍负责防守。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["The attacking team carries a device called the Spike.","进攻方携带一种叫作 Spike（爆能器）的装置。"],[" Their objective is to enter one of two designated bomb sites, plant the Spike, and protect it until it explodes.","他们的任务是进入 A 或 B 两个指定的爆能器安放区域之一，成功下包，然后保护爆能器，直到它爆炸。"]],"translation":"进攻方携带一种叫作 Spike（爆能器）的装置。他们的任务是进入 A 或 B 两个指定的爆能器安放区域之一，成功下包，然后保护爆能器，直到它爆炸。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["The defending team must prevent the attackers from planting the Spike.","防守方需要阻止进攻方下包。"],[" If the attackers successfully plant it, the defenders must eliminate the remaining attackers and defuse the Spike before it explodes.","如果进攻方已经成功下包，防守方就必须消灭剩余的进攻人员，并在爆能器爆炸之前完成拆包。"]],"translation":"防守方需要阻止进攻方下包。如果进攻方已经成功下包，防守方就必须消灭剩余的进攻人员，并在爆能器爆炸之前完成拆包。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["There are several ways to win a round:","一局比赛有几种获胜方式："]],"translation":"一局比赛有几种获胜方式："},{"kind":"bullet","sentences":[["The attackers eliminate all defenders before the Spike is planted.","进攻方在下包之前消灭所有防守方。"]],"translation":"进攻方在下包之前消灭所有防守方。"},{"kind":"bullet","sentences":[["The attackers successfully plant the Spike and allow it to explode.","进攻方成功下包，并保护爆能器直到爆炸。"]],"translation":"进攻方成功下包，并保护爆能器直到爆炸。"},{"kind":"bullet","sentences":[["The defenders eliminate all attackers before the Spike is planted.","防守方在进攻方下包之前消灭所有进攻方。"]],"translation":"防守方在进攻方下包之前消灭所有进攻方。"},{"kind":"bullet","sentences":[["The defenders successfully defuse the planted Spike.","防守方成功拆除已经安放的爆能器。"]],"translation":"防守方成功拆除已经安放的爆能器。"},{"kind":"bullet","sentences":[["If the attackers fail to plant before time runs out, the defenders win.","如果进攻方在时间结束之前没有成功下包，则防守方获胜。"]],"translation":"如果进攻方在时间结束之前没有成功下包，则防守方获胜。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["A standard Competitive match is played to 13 rounds.","标准竞技模式以 13 局胜利为目标。"],[" After 12 rounds, the teams switch sides.","进行完前 12 局后，双方交换攻防。"],[" If the score reaches 12–12, overtime begins.","如果比分达到 12:12，则进入加时赛。"]],"translation":"标准竞技模式以 13 局胜利为目标。进行完前 12 局后，双方交换攻防。如果比分达到 12:12，则进入加时赛。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["The most important thing to understand is that VALORANT is a game of information, space, timing, and teamwork.","最重要的是理解：无畏契约是一款围绕信息、空间、时机和团队协作展开的游戏。"]],"translation":"最重要的是理解：无畏契约是一款围绕信息、空间、时机和团队协作展开的游戏。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["A player who gets five kills but ignores the objective may be less useful than a player who gets one kill and successfully plants the Spike.","一个拿到五个人头却忽略比赛目标的玩家，可能还不如一个只拿到一个人头、但成功完成下包的玩家有价值。"]],"translation":"一个拿到五个人头却忽略比赛目标的玩家，可能还不如一个只拿到一个人头、但成功完成下包的玩家有价值。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Your goal is not necessarily to kill everyone.","你的目标不一定是杀光所有人。"]],"translation":"你的目标不一定是杀光所有人。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Your goal is to win the round.","你的目标是赢得这一局。"]],"translation":"你的目标是赢得这一局。"}],"terms":[{"term":"plant the Spike","forms":["plants the Spike","planting the Spike"],"meaning":"安放爆能器，也就是下包","usage":"plant 在这里是「安放」。plant the Spike 是持续动作，Spike planted 是告知队友动作已经完成。","example":"Tell me when the Spike is planted.","exampleZh":"下完包告诉我。","meaningEn":"Place and arm the Spike at a bomb site.","usageEn":"Plant takes the device as its object. Players say “I’m planting” while the action is in progress and “Spike planted” once it is complete."},{"term":"defuse","forms":["defused"],"meaning":"拆除已经安放的爆能器","usage":"defuse 接 Spike 或 bomb。命令 Start defusing 强调开始拆除，It’s defused 表示拆除完成。也可比喻缓和冲突。","example":"Can you defuse the Spike before it explodes?","exampleZh":"你能在爆能器爆炸前把它拆掉吗？","meaningEn":"Disarm the Spike after it has been planted.","usageEn":"Defuse is a transitive verb. “Start defusing” signals the beginning of the action, and “the Spike is defused” reports the result. In everyday English, people also defuse tensions."},{"term":"run out","forms":["runs out","ran out","run out of time"],"meaning":"（时间）耗尽","usage":"time runs out 用时间作主语。we run out of time 用人作主语，of 后接所缺的资源。","example":"We’ll run out of time if we wait here.","exampleZh":"如果在这里等下去，我们就来不及了。","meaningEn":"Come to the end of the time or resources available.","usageEn":"The resource is the subject in “time runs out.” In “we run out of time,” the subject is the person or team using it."},{"term":"match is played to","forms":["played to"],"meaning":"比赛打到某个胜局数为止","usage":"比赛语境的 play to + 数字指达到胜利门槛。play for + 奖品或目标则表示为某物而争。","example":"This match is played to five points.","exampleZh":"这场比赛先拿到五分的一方获胜。","meaningEn":"A match ends when a team reaches the stated number of wins or points.","usageEn":"Use play to + a number to give a winning threshold. “Played to 13 rounds” in this passage means the first team to win 13 rounds wins the match."},{"term":"not necessarily","meaning":"未必，不一定","usage":"not 否定的是 necessarily 所表达的必然性。A is not necessarily better 说明 A 可能更好，也可能没有。","example":"Getting there first is not necessarily an advantage.","exampleZh":"先到那里未必占优势。","meaningEn":"Possibly, with no guarantee that it is so.","usageEn":"Put necessarily after the negative in forms such as “isn’t necessarily true.” The speaker is allowing more than one outcome."}],"glossary":[]},{"en":"Meet the Ten Agents","zh":"认识十名特工","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Before entering the battlefield, let's meet the ten players.","在进入战场之前，我们先认识这场比赛中的十名选手。"],[" Each player chooses an Agent.","每名玩家都需要选择一名特工。"],[" Agents have different abilities and responsibilities.","不同特工拥有不同的技能和职责。"]],"translation":"在进入战场之前，我们先认识这场比赛中的十名选手。 每名玩家都需要选择一名特工。不同特工拥有不同的技能和职责。"},{"kind":"heading","sentences":[["Team Blue — The Attackers","蓝队——进攻方"]],"translation":"蓝队——进攻方"},{"kind":"subheading","sentences":[["1. Jett — Duelist","1. Jett（捷风）——决斗者"]],"translation":"1. Jett（捷风）——决斗者"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Jett is extremely mobile.","捷风拥有极强的机动能力。"],[" Her dash allows her to enter dangerous areas quickly, while her Cloudburst creates temporary cover.","她的冲刺技能可以让她快速进入危险区域，烟雾则能暂时遮挡敌人的视线。"],[" Her main responsibility is to create space for the team.","她最主要的职责是为团队创造进攻空间。"]],"translation":"捷风拥有极强的机动能力。她的冲刺技能可以让她快速进入危险区域，烟雾则能暂时遮挡敌人的视线。 她最主要的职责是为团队创造进攻空间。"},{"kind":"subheading","sentences":[["2. Sova — Initiator","2. Sova（猎枭）——先锋"]],"translation":"2. Sova（猎枭）——先锋"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Sova uses his Recon Bolt to reveal enemies and his Owl Drone to gather information.","猎枭可以使用侦察箭揭示敌人位置，也可以使用无人机获取信息。"],[" He helps the team understand where the defenders are hiding before entering a site.","在队伍进入爆能器区域之前，他负责帮助队友了解防守方的藏身位置。"]],"translation":"猎枭可以使用侦察箭揭示敌人位置，也可以使用无人机获取信息。 在队伍进入爆能器区域之前，他负责帮助队友了解防守方的藏身位置。"},{"kind":"subheading","sentences":[["3. Omen — Controller","3. Omen（幽影）——控场者"]],"translation":"3. Omen（幽影）——控场者"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Omen controls the battlefield with Dark Cover smokes.","幽影通过烟雾控制战场。"],[" He can block enemy sightlines and use Shrouded Step to reposition.","他能够封锁敌人的视线，也可以使用传送技能改变自己的位置。"],[" His job is to make dangerous areas safer for his teammates.","他的工作是降低队友进入危险区域时面临的风险。"]],"translation":"幽影通过烟雾控制战场。他能够封锁敌人的视线，也可以使用传送技能改变自己的位置。 他的工作是降低队友进入危险区域时面临的风险。"},{"kind":"subheading","sentences":[["4. Killjoy — Sentinel","4. Killjoy（奇乐）——哨卫"]],"translation":"4. Killjoy（奇乐）——哨卫"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Killjoy uses her Turret, Alarmbot, Nanoswarm, and Lockdown ultimate.","奇乐拥有炮台、报警机器人、纳米蜂群以及大招禁区。"],[" She can protect a planted Spike, monitor a flank, and delay enemy attacks.","她可以保护已经下包的区域、监控敌人的绕后路线，并延缓敌人的进攻。"]],"translation":"奇乐拥有炮台、报警机器人、纳米蜂群以及大招禁区。 她可以保护已经下包的区域、监控敌人的绕后路线，并延缓敌人的进攻。"},{"kind":"subheading","sentences":[["5. Gekko — Initiator","5. Gekko（盖可）——先锋"]],"translation":"5. Gekko（盖可）——先锋"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Gekko uses Dizzy to blind enemies, Wingman to help plant or defuse the Spike, and Mosh Pit to clear dangerous positions.","盖可可以使用眩晕生物 Dizzy 致盲敌人，使用 Wingman 协助下包或拆包，还可以利用 Mosh Pit 清理危险位置。"],[" His abilities are especially useful during coordinated attacks.","他的技能尤其适合配合队友进行有组织的进攻。"]],"translation":"盖可可以使用眩晕生物 Dizzy 致盲敌人，使用 Wingman 协助下包或拆包，还可以利用 Mosh Pit 清理危险位置。 他的技能尤其适合配合队友进行有组织的进攻。"},{"kind":"heading","sentences":[["Team Red — The Defenders","红队——防守方"]],"translation":"红队——防守方"},{"kind":"subheading","sentences":[["1. Raze — Duelist","1. Raze（雷兹）——决斗者"]],"translation":"1. Raze（雷兹）——决斗者"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Raze uses explosives to clear corners and punish enemies who gather in narrow spaces.","雷兹使用爆炸物清理角落，并惩罚聚集在狭窄区域的敌人。"]],"translation":"雷兹使用爆炸物清理角落，并惩罚聚集在狭窄区域的敌人。"},{"kind":"subheading","sentences":[["2. Skye — Initiator","2. Skye（斯凯）——先锋"]],"translation":"2. Skye（斯凯）——先锋"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Skye uses Guiding Light to flash enemies and Trailblazer to gather information.","斯凯使用闪光技能致盲敌人，并利用寻路猎犬获取信息。"]],"translation":"斯凯使用闪光技能致盲敌人，并利用寻路猎犬获取信息。"},{"kind":"subheading","sentences":[["3. Brimstone — Controller","3. Brimstone（炼狱）——控场者"]],"translation":"3. Brimstone（炼狱）——控场者"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Brimstone can deploy multiple smokes at once and use Incendiary to delay attackers.","炼狱能够一次性部署多个烟雾，还可以使用燃烧弹拖延进攻方。"],[" His Orbital Strike ultimate can force enemies away from important positions.","他的大招天基光束可以迫使敌人离开重要位置。"]],"translation":"炼狱能够一次性部署多个烟雾，还可以使用燃烧弹拖延进攻方。 他的大招天基光束可以迫使敌人离开重要位置。"},{"kind":"subheading","sentences":[["4. Cypher — Sentinel","4. Cypher（零）——哨卫"]],"translation":"4. Cypher（零）——哨卫"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Cypher uses cameras, Trapwires, and Cyber Cages to monitor enemy movement.","零利用摄像头、绊线和网络牢笼监控敌人的移动。"],[" He is particularly dangerous when attackers attempt to flank or rotate without checking their surroundings.","当进攻方试图绕后或者在没有检查周围环境的情况下转点时，他尤其危险。"]],"translation":"零利用摄像头、绊线和网络牢笼监控敌人的移动。 当进攻方试图绕后或者在没有检查周围环境的情况下转点时，他尤其危险。"},{"kind":"subheading","sentences":[["5. Sage — Sentinel","5. Sage（贤者）——哨卫"]],"translation":"5. Sage（贤者）——哨卫"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Sage uses Slow Orbs to delay enemy movement, Healing Orb to restore health, and Barrier Orb to block important entrances.","贤者可以使用减速法球延缓敌人移动，使用治疗法球恢复生命，还可以利用屏障法球封锁重要入口。"],[" She can also revive a teammate with her ultimate.","她还可以使用大招复活队友。"]],"translation":"贤者可以使用减速法球延缓敌人移动，使用治疗法球恢复生命，还可以利用屏障法球封锁重要入口。 她还可以使用大招复活队友。"}],"terms":[{"term":"create space","meaning":"为队友腾出进场和站位的空间","usage":"create space 的主语常是率先入场的队员。space 在这里不可数，可接 for + 受益对象。","example":"Her dash created space for the rest of the team.","exampleZh":"她的冲刺为其他队员腾出了进场空间。","meaningEn":"Give teammates room to move into useful positions.","usageEn":"Space is uncountable in this sense. Use “create space for the team” when a player's movement or abilities open a route others can use."},{"term":"sightline","forms":["sightlines"],"meaning":"从一个位置看出去的视线通道","usage":"常说 block a sightline（挡住视线）、maintain a clear sightline（保持视野畅通）。line of sight 是常见的同义表达。","example":"The smoke blocked our sightline across the map.","exampleZh":"烟幕挡住了我们横看地图的视线。","meaningEn":"The path along which a player can see a location.","usageEn":"People block, clear, and watch sightlines. “Line of sight” is another common way to describe whether something is visible from a particular position."},{"term":"reposition","meaning":"调整站位","usage":"re-表示再次，reposition 可单独作不及物动词，也可接 oneself。它突出换位置，rotate 在本篇里强调跨区域转点。","example":"After being spotted, the player repositioned behind cover.","exampleZh":"被发现后，这名队员换到了掩体后面。","meaningEn":"Move to a more useful or safer spot.","usageEn":"Use reposition on its own or with a reflexive object, as in “reposition yourself.” A player can reposition within the same area. Rotate usually refers to moving to another area."},{"term":"flank","meaning":"侧翼、后路，或从侧翼绕过去","usage":"作名词时有 watch the flank。作动词时有 flank the defenders。定位语境中 behind the team 更直白，flank 则带有侧面位置的含义。","example":"One player stayed back to watch the flank.","exampleZh":"一名队员留在后面留意侧翼。","meaningEn":"A side or rear approach, or the act of moving around to attack from that direction.","usageEn":"As a noun, it appears in calls like “watch the flank.” As a verb, it takes an opponent or position directly: “flank the defenders.”"},{"term":"ultimate","meaning":"特工的大招","usage":"形容词 ultimate 可表示最终或最高级。在游戏中也作可数名词，常说 use her ultimate、the ultimate is ready。","example":"Her ultimate won’t be ready until the next round.","exampleZh":"她的大招要到下一回合才会就绪。","meaningEn":"An agent’s most powerful ability.","usageEn":"Game chat uses ultimate as a countable noun. Players say “use your ultimate” or “her ultimate is ready.” The shorter form “ult” is common in chat."}],"glossary":[]},{"en":"Understanding the Map — ASCENT","zh":"认识地图——亚海悬城","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Our match takes place on Ascent, one of VALORANT's classic maps.","本场比赛发生在 Ascent（亚海悬城），这是无畏契约中非常经典的一张地图。"],[" Ascent has two bomb sites: A Site and B Site.","亚海悬城有两个爆能器安放区域：A 点和 B 点。"],[" Between them lies Mid, a central area that connects several important routes.","两个区域之间是 Mid（中路），它连接着地图上多个重要路线。"]],"translation":"本场比赛发生在 Ascent（亚海悬城），这是无畏契约中非常经典的一张地图。 亚海悬城有两个爆能器安放区域：A 点和 B 点。 两个区域之间是 Mid（中路），它连接着地图上多个重要路线。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Understanding the map is essential because a team that controls Mid can threaten both bomb sites.","理解地图非常重要，因为一支队伍只要控制了中路，就可以同时威胁 A 点和 B 点。"]],"translation":"理解地图非常重要，因为一支队伍只要控制了中路，就可以同时威胁 A 点和 B 点。"},{"kind":"heading","sentences":[["The Attackers' Starting Position","进攻方出生位置"]],"translation":"进攻方出生位置"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["At the beginning of each round, the attacking team starts at Attacker Spawn.","每一局开始时，进攻方都会出现在 Attacker Spawn（进攻方出生点）。"],[" From there, players can move toward three main routes.","从这里出发，玩家可以选择三条主要路线。"]],"translation":"每一局开始时，进攻方都会出现在 Attacker Spawn（进攻方出生点）。 从这里出发，玩家可以选择三条主要路线。"},{"kind":"keyline","sentences":[["Route A: Attacker Spawn → A Lobby → A Main → A Site.","A 路线： 进攻方出生点 → A Lobby（A 大厅）→ A Main（A 大道）→ A Site（A 点）。"]],"translation":"A 路线： 进攻方出生点 → A Lobby（A 大厅）→ A Main（A 大道）→ A Site（A 点）。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["A Main is the primary entrance to A Site.","A Main 是进入 A 点的主要入口。"],[" It is a relatively narrow approach, making it dangerous to enter without clearing enemy positions.","这里的通道相对狭窄，如果不先排查敌人的防守位置，直接进入会非常危险。"]],"translation":"A Main 是进入 A 点的主要入口。这里的通道相对狭窄，如果不先排查敌人的防守位置，直接进入会非常危险。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Inside A Site, players need to watch for enemies holding Heaven, Generator, Dice, and other defensive angles.","进入 A 点后，玩家需要注意 Heaven（高台）、Generator（发电机）、Dice（骰子箱）以及其他防守角度。"],[" Heaven is an elevated position overlooking the site.","Heaven 是俯瞰 A 点的高处位置。"],[" Generator and Dice provide cover around the bomb site.","Generator 和 Dice 则是爆能器区域内的重要掩体。"]],"translation":"进入 A 点后，玩家需要注意 Heaven（高台）、Generator（发电机）、Dice（骰子箱）以及其他防守角度。 Heaven 是俯瞰 A 点的高处位置。Generator 和 Dice 则是爆能器区域内的重要掩体。"},{"kind":"keyline","sentences":[["Route B: Attacker Spawn → B Lobby → B Main → B Site.","B 路线： 进攻方出生点 → B Lobby（B 大厅）→ B Main（B 大道）→ B Site（B 点）。"]],"translation":"B 路线： 进攻方出生点 → B Lobby（B 大厅）→ B Main（B 大道）→ B Site（B 点）。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["B Main is another important entrance.","B Main 是进入 B 点的另一个重要入口。"],[" Once attackers enter B Site, they must watch for defenders holding from CT and Market.","进攻方进入 B 点后，必须注意来自 CT 和 Market 的防守。"]],"translation":"B Main 是进入 B 点的另一个重要入口。 进攻方进入 B 点后，必须注意来自 CT 和 Market 的防守。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Market is a room connecting the central part of the map to B Site. It is one of the most important defensive positions on B.","Market（市场）是一间连接地图中路与 B 点的房间，也是 B 点最重要的防守位置之一。"]],"translation":"Market（市场）是一间连接地图中路与 B 点的房间，也是 B 点最重要的防守位置之一。"},{"kind":"keyline","sentences":[["Route Mid: Attacker Spawn → Mid Top → Mid Courtyard.","中路路线： 进攻方出生点 → Mid Top（中路上方）→ Mid Courtyard（中路广场）。"]],"translation":"中路路线： 进攻方出生点 → Mid Top（中路上方）→ Mid Courtyard（中路广场）。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["From Mid, attackers can move in two important directions:","从中路出发，进攻方可以选择两个重要方向："]],"translation":"从中路出发，进攻方可以选择两个重要方向："},{"kind":"bullet","sentences":[["Mid Catwalk → A Tree → A Site.","Mid Catwalk（中路猫道）→ A Tree（A 树房）→ A 点。"]],"translation":"Mid Catwalk（中路猫道）→ A Tree（A 树房）→ A 点。"},{"kind":"bullet","sentences":[["Mid Market → Market → B Site.","Mid Market（中路市场方向）→ Market → B 点。"]],"translation":"Mid Market（中路市场方向）→ Market → B 点。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Mid Catwalk provides access toward A Tree, which connects to A Site.","Mid Catwalk 可以通往 A Tree，而 A Tree 则连接着 A 点。"],[" Mid Market connects the central area to the B-side Market.","Mid Market 则连接中路区域和 B 点一侧的 Market。"]],"translation":"Mid Catwalk 可以通往 A Tree，而 A Tree 则连接着 A 点。 Mid Market 则连接中路区域和 B 点一侧的 Market。"},{"kind":"heading","sentences":[["The Defenders' Starting Position","防守方出生位置"]],"translation":"防守方出生位置"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Defenders start on the opposite side of the map.","防守方出生在地图的另一侧。"],[" They normally spread out to protect A, Mid, and B.","通常情况下，他们会分散站位，分别保护 A 点、中路和 B 点。"],[" A defender near A can rotate through CT Spawn or Tree.","A 点附近的防守人员可以通过 CT Spawn 或 Tree 进行转点。"]],"translation":"防守方出生在地图的另一侧。 通常情况下，他们会分散站位，分别保护 A 点、中路和 B 点。 A 点附近的防守人员可以通过 CT Spawn 或 Tree 进行转点。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["A defender near B can rotate through CT or Market.","B 点附近的防守人员可以通过 CT 或 Market 进行转点。"],[" The exact route depends on which areas are safe and which doors are open.","具体路线取决于哪些区域安全，以及相关的门是否处于开启状态。"]],"translation":"B 点附近的防守人员可以通过 CT 或 Market 进行转点。 具体路线取决于哪些区域安全，以及相关的门是否处于开启状态。"},{"kind":"heading","sentences":[["Important Map Features","地图特殊机制"]],"translation":"地图特殊机制"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Ascent has two special doors, one near A Tree and another near B Market. These doors can be opened or closed using switches. They can also be destroyed.","亚海悬城有两扇特殊的门，一扇位于 A Tree 附近，另一扇位于 B Market 附近。 玩家可以通过开关打开或关闭这些门，也可以将它们破坏。"]],"translation":"亚海悬城有两扇特殊的门，一扇位于 A Tree 附近，另一扇位于 B Market 附近。 玩家可以通过开关打开或关闭这些门，也可以将它们破坏。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["This means that controlling a doorway can influence how quickly attackers and defenders move between areas.","因此，控制门的位置会影响进攻方和防守方在不同区域之间移动的速度。"],[" Remember these basic connections:","记住以下基本路线："]],"translation":"因此，控制门的位置会影响进攻方和防守方在不同区域之间移动的速度。 记住以下基本路线："},{"kind":"bullet","sentences":[["A Main leads toward A Site.","A Main 通向 A 点。"]],"translation":"A Main 通向 A 点。"},{"kind":"bullet","sentences":[["A Tree connects Mid Catwalk to A.","A Tree 连接 Mid Catwalk 和 A 点。"]],"translation":"A Tree 连接 Mid Catwalk 和 A 点。"},{"kind":"bullet","sentences":[["Mid Market connects Mid to B Market.","Mid Market 连接中路和 B Market。"]],"translation":"Mid Market 连接中路和 B Market。"},{"kind":"bullet","sentences":[["B Main leads toward B Site.","B Main 通向 B 点。"]],"translation":"B Main 通向 B 点。"},{"kind":"bullet","sentences":[["CT Spawn provides important defensive rotations.","CT Spawn 是防守方进行转点的重要路线。"]],"translation":"CT Spawn 是防守方进行转点的重要路线。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["When someone says \"They're coming through Tree,\" they are talking about the route connecting Mid to A.","当队友说 \"They're coming through Tree\"，意思是敌人正从连接中路与 A 点的 Tree 路线过来。"],[" When someone says \"Watch Market,\" they are referring to the important connection between Mid and B.","当队友说 \"Watch Market\"，意思是注意中路与 B 点之间的 Market 通道。"]],"translation":"当队友说 \"They're coming through Tree\"，意思是敌人正从连接中路与 A 点的 Tree 路线过来。 当队友说 \"Watch Market\"，意思是注意中路与 B 点之间的 Market 通道。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["These callouts will become much easier to understand once you imagine the map from above.","当你从俯视角想象整张地图时，这些报点就会容易理解得多。"]],"translation":"当你从俯视角想象整张地图时，这些报点就会容易理解得多。"}],"terms":[{"term":"watch for","meaning":"留意可能出现的敌人或情况","usage":"watch for + 人或信号，意味着对方可能尚未出现。watch + 地点是盯着该处，watch out 可单独作提醒。","example":"Watch for anyone coming through Tree.","exampleZh":"留意从树房过来的人。","meaningEn":"Look out for something that may appear or happen.","usageEn":"Use watch for with an expected person, event, or signal. “Watch the entrance” describes where to look. “Watch for a defender” describes what to look for."},{"term":"overlook","forms":["overlooking"],"meaning":"从高处俯瞰","usage":"overlook + 场地时可描述空间关系，如 a balcony overlooking the site。overlook a mistake 则是没注意到或未追究错误。","example":"The balcony overlooks both entrances.","exampleZh":"这个阳台能俯瞰两个入口。","meaningEn":"Have a view of a place from above.","usageEn":"Use overlook with the place that can be seen: “a balcony overlooking the site.” In a different sense, overlooking a detail means failing to notice it."},{"term":"spread out","meaning":"分散站位，拉开彼此距离","usage":"可作命令 Spread out!，也可说 spread out across the map。强调扩大覆盖面。split up 侧重把人分成不同组。","example":"The defenders spread out across the map.","exampleZh":"防守方分散到地图各处。","meaningEn":"Move apart to cover more ground.","usageEn":"“Spread out across the map” emphasizes distance and coverage. Used as an instruction by itself, “Spread out” tells the group to increase the space between players."},{"term":"provide access","forms":["provides access"],"meaning":"提供一条通往某处的通道","usage":"provide access to + 地点是最常见结构，access 通常不可数。provide access toward 在原段落里强调可由此朝某方向移动。","example":"The passage provides access to the market.","exampleZh":"这条通道连着市场。","meaningEn":"Make a place or route reachable.","usageEn":"The usual pattern is provide access to + destination. Access is normally uncountable, as in “the doorway provides access to the site.”"},{"term":"callout","forms":["callouts"],"meaning":"用于快速通报点位或信息的简短说法","usage":"make a callout 是报点。位置名本身也可称为 callout。日常写作里的 callout 还可以是醒目标注。","example":"Use the same callout for this corner every round.","exampleZh":"每一轮给这个角落报点时都用同一个叫法。","meaningEn":"A short spoken message about a location or situation.","usageEn":"Make a callout is the action. A fixed map name can also be called a callout because the team uses it to identify the same spot quickly."}],"glossary":[]},{"en":"Match Begins — First Half, Attackers","zh":"比赛开始——上半场，进攻方","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["The map loads.","地图加载完成。"],[" The scoreboard appears.","比分板出现在屏幕上。"]],"translation":"地图加载完成。 比分板出现在屏幕上。"},{"kind":"keyline","sentences":[["BLUE 0 — 0 RED","蓝队 0 : 0 红队"]],"translation":"蓝队 0 : 0 红队"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Blue attacks first.","蓝队先攻。"],[" Red defends.","红队负责防守。"],[" The players enter the buy phase.","玩家进入购买阶段。"]],"translation":"蓝队先攻。 红队负责防守。 玩家进入购买阶段。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Jett purchases a Ghost.","捷风购买 Ghost 手枪。"],[" Sova buys his basic reconnaissance ability.","猎枭购买基础侦察技能。"],[" Omen prepares his smokes.","幽影准备好烟雾。"],[" Killjoy purchases her defensive utility, while Gekko prepares Dizzy.","奇乐购买防守装备，盖可则准备好 Dizzy。"],[" The round timer begins.","比赛计时器开始。"]],"translation":"捷风购买 Ghost 手枪。猎枭购买基础侦察技能。幽影准备好烟雾。奇乐购买防守装备，盖可则准备好 Dizzy。 比赛计时器开始。"},{"kind":"dialogue","sentences":[["Jett: \"What are we doing first round?\"","Jett： \"What are we doing first round?\"　第一局我们怎么打？"]],"translation":"Jett： \"What are we doing first round?\"　第一局我们怎么打？"},{"kind":"dialogue","sentences":[["Omen: \"Let's play A. Sova, scan the site. I'll smoke Heaven and Tree.\"","Omen： \"Let's play A. Sova, scan the site. I'll smoke Heaven and Tree.\"　我们打 A 点吧。猎枭，你先侦察点内。我来封高台和树房烟。"]],"translation":"Omen： \"Let's play A. Sova, scan the site. I'll smoke Heaven and Tree.\"　我们打 A 点吧。猎枭，你先侦察点内。我来封高台和树房烟。"},{"kind":"dialogue","sentences":[["Sova: \"Copy. I'll reveal first.\"","Sova： \"Copy. I'll reveal first.\"　收到，我先探测敌人。"]],"translation":"Sova： \"Copy. I'll reveal first.\"　收到，我先探测敌人。"},{"kind":"dialogue","sentences":[["Gekko: \"I'll follow Jett. Let's trade each other.\"","Gekko： \"I'll follow Jett. Let's trade each other.\"　我跟着捷风进去，咱们互相补枪。"]],"translation":"Gekko： \"I'll follow Jett. Let's trade each other.\"　我跟着捷风进去，咱们互相补枪。"},{"kind":"dialogue","sentences":[["Killjoy: \"I'll carry the Spike.\"","Killjoy： \"I'll carry the Spike.\"　我来拿包。"]],"translation":"Killjoy： \"I'll carry the Spike.\"　我来拿包。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["The team moves toward A Lobby.","队伍向 A Lobby 移动。"],[" Jett takes the front position.","捷风走在最前面。"],[" Sova follows a few steps behind.","猎枭跟在她后面几步的位置。"]],"translation":"队伍向 A Lobby 移动。 捷风走在最前面。 猎枭跟在她后面几步的位置。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Omen stays near the back, ready to place smokes.","幽影留在后方，准备随时释放烟雾。"],[" Killjoy carries the Spike, while Gekko watches the team's right side.","奇乐携带爆能器，盖可则负责观察队伍右侧。"],[" They arrive at A Main.","他们抵达 A Main。"]],"translation":"幽影留在后方，准备随时释放烟雾。 奇乐携带爆能器，盖可则负责观察队伍右侧。 他们抵达 A Main。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["The entrance is quiet.","入口非常安静。"]],"translation":"入口非常安静。"},{"kind":"dialogue","sentences":[["Jett: \"No contact so far.\"","Jett： \"No contact so far.\"　目前还没发现敌人。"]],"translation":"Jett： \"No contact so far.\"　目前还没发现敌人。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Sova fires his Recon Bolt.","猎枭发射侦察箭。"],[" The arrow flies over the site and attaches to a wall.","箭矢飞过 A 点，附着在墙壁上。"],[" It begins scanning.","随后开始扫描。"]],"translation":"猎枭发射侦察箭。 箭矢飞过 A 点，附着在墙壁上。 随后开始扫描。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["A defender is revealed near Generator.","一名防守方出现在 Generator 附近。"]],"translation":"一名防守方出现在 Generator 附近。"},{"kind":"dialogue","sentences":[["Sova: \"One Generator! I see one!\"","Sova： \"One Generator! I see one!\"　发电机位置有一个人！我看到他了！"]],"translation":"Sova： \"One Generator! I see one!\"　发电机位置有一个人！我看到他了！"},{"kind":"dialogue","sentences":[["Omen: \"Smoking Heaven. Smoking Tree. Go now!\"","Omen： \"Smoking Heaven. Smoking Tree. Go now!\"　高台烟和树房烟已经封好，现在冲！"]],"translation":"Omen： \"Smoking Heaven. Smoking Tree. Go now!\"　高台烟和树房烟已经封好，现在冲！"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Two large smoke clouds appear, blocking the defenders' vision.","两团巨大的烟雾出现，遮挡了防守方的视线。"],[" Jett activates her dash and enters the site.","捷风使用冲刺技能进入 A 点。"]],"translation":"两团巨大的烟雾出现，遮挡了防守方的视线。 捷风使用冲刺技能进入 A 点。"},{"kind":"dialogue","sentences":[["Jett: \"I'm in! Generator, one!\"","Jett： \"I'm in! Generator, one!\"　我进来了！发电机一个！"]],"translation":"Jett： \"I'm in! Generator, one!\"　我进来了！发电机一个！"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["She shoots the defender but fails to eliminate him.","她向敌人射击，但没能成功击杀。"],[" Gekko follows immediately and trades the kill.","盖可立刻跟进，补枪击杀了敌人。"]],"translation":"她向敌人射击，但没能成功击杀。 盖可立刻跟进，补枪击杀了敌人。"},{"kind":"dialogue","sentences":[["Gekko: \"Got him! Site is clear!\"","Gekko： \"Got him! Site is clear!\"　击杀了！点内暂时安全！"]],"translation":"Gekko： \"Got him! Site is clear!\"　击杀了！点内暂时安全！"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Killjoy moves behind cover.","奇乐移动到掩体后方。"]],"translation":"奇乐移动到掩体后方。"},{"kind":"dialogue","sentences":[["Killjoy: \"Planting for default!\"","Killjoy： \"Planting for default!\"　我准备下包，放在常规下包位置！"]],"translation":"Killjoy： \"Planting for default!\"　我准备下包，放在常规下包位置！"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["The Spike is planted near a common defensive position, where the attackers can watch it from multiple angles.","爆能器被放在一个常见的防守位置附近，进攻方可以从多个角度观察它。"],[" The team immediately changes formation.","队伍立即改变阵型。"],[" Jett watches Heaven.","捷风看守高台。"]],"translation":"爆能器被放在一个常见的防守位置附近，进攻方可以从多个角度观察它。 队伍立即改变阵型。 捷风看守高台。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Gekko holds Tree.","盖可架住树房。"],[" Sova watches the main entrance.","猎枭观察 A 大道入口。"],[" Omen takes a position where he can support either side.","幽影则选择一个能够支援两侧的位置。"]],"translation":"盖可架住树房。 猎枭观察 A 大道入口。 幽影则选择一个能够支援两侧的位置。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["The defenders begin their retake.","防守方开始回防。"],[" Skye throws a flash through the entrance.","斯凯向入口投掷闪光。"]],"translation":"防守方开始回防。 斯凯向入口投掷闪光。"},{"kind":"dialogue","sentences":[["Omen: \"Flash! Don't look!\"","Omen： \"Flash! Don't look!\"　有闪！别看！"]],"translation":"Omen： \"Flash! Don't look!\"　有闪！别看！"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["A bright flash fills the screen.","一道强烈的闪光充满屏幕。"],[" Jett turns away just in time.","捷风及时转身，避免了被闪白。"],[" Raze pushes into the site.","雷兹冲入 A 点。"]],"translation":"一道强烈的闪光充满屏幕。 捷风及时转身，避免了被闪白。 雷兹冲入 A 点。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Sova eliminates her with a precise shot.","猎枭用精准的射击将她击杀。"],[" The defenders lose another player.","防守方又损失一人。"],[" The remaining defenders hesitate.","剩余的防守方开始犹豫。"]],"translation":"猎枭用精准的射击将她击杀。 防守方又损失一人。 剩余的防守方开始犹豫。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["The Spike continues beeping.","爆能器仍然在持续发出滴滴声。"],[" A few seconds later, it explodes.","几秒钟后，它发生爆炸。"]],"translation":"爆能器仍然在持续发出滴滴声。 几秒钟后，它发生爆炸。"},{"kind":"keyline","sentences":[["ROUND WON — BLUE　BLUE 1 — 0 RED","本局获胜——蓝队　蓝队 1 : 0 红队"]],"translation":"本局获胜——蓝队　蓝队 1 : 0 红队"},{"kind":"dialogue","sentences":[["Jett: \"Nice! Good entry!\"","Jett： \"Nice! Good entry!\"　漂亮！进点很好！"]],"translation":"Jett： \"Nice! Good entry!\"　漂亮！进点很好！"},{"kind":"dialogue","sentences":[["Gekko: \"Good trade. Let's keep doing that.\"","Gekko： \"Good trade. Let's keep doing that.\"　补枪打得不错，继续保持！"]],"translation":"Gekko： \"Good trade. Let's keep doing that.\"　补枪打得不错，继续保持！"}],"terms":[{"term":"buy phase","meaning":"回合开打前购买装备的阶段","usage":"phase 表示过程中的阶段，常用 during the buy phase。buy 作名词时可指全队采用的一种购买方案。","example":"We can discuss the plan during the buy phase.","exampleZh":"我们可以在购买阶段讨论计划。","meaningEn":"The part of a round when players can purchase equipment.","usageEn":"Use “during the buy phase” to describe when a purchase or planning discussion happens. A buy can also mean the team’s purchasing decision for the round."},{"term":"no contact so far","meaning":"目前还没碰到敌人","usage":"语音报点常省略 We’ve had。so far 指截至说话时，可与现在完成时连用。contact 在这里是不可数名词。","example":"No contact so far, but keep watching Mid.","exampleZh":"到目前还没遇敌，不过继续盯着中路。","meaningEn":"The team has yet to encounter an opponent.","usageEn":"This call omits the subject and verb from “we’ve had no contact so far.” So far covers the time up to the moment of speaking."},{"term":"trade the kill","forms":["trades the kill","trade each other","good trade"],"meaning":"补枪，击倒刚击倒队友的对手","usage":"trade 在此强调交战中的人员交换。trade each other 是约定互相补枪，Good trade 是对成功补枪的简短评价。","example":"Stay close enough to trade the kill.","exampleZh":"保持足够近的距离，好及时补枪。","meaningEn":"Eliminate the opponent who has just eliminated your teammate.","usageEn":"Trade describes the exchange of eliminations. “Let’s trade each other” is an instruction to stay close enough to follow up, and “good trade” praises the exchange afterward."},{"term":"default","forms":["planting for default"],"meaning":"默认下包点","usage":"此处 default 指约定俗成的常规下包位置。同一读本的 play a slow default 则指先分散站位收集信息，等局势明朗。","example":"Is she planting at default or behind the box?","exampleZh":"她是在常规点下包，还是在箱子后面？","meaningEn":"The usual place to plant the Spike at a site.","usageEn":"“Planting for default” announces a conventional plant location. In the separate phrase “play a slow default,” default describes a standard opening formation for gathering information."},{"term":"just in time","meaning":"及时赶上，差一点就来不及","usage":"just 强调余量很小。on time 表示按预定时间，in time 表示赶在某个结果或期限前。","example":"I looked away just in time.","exampleZh":"我及时转过头，差一点就晚了。","meaningEn":"Early enough to prevent a problem, with very little time left.","usageEn":"Just stresses the narrow margin. “In time” refers to beating a deadline. “On time” refers to following a schedule."}],"glossary":[]},{"en":"Round 2 — The Enemy Changes the Setup","zh":"第二局——敌人改变了防守阵型","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["The next round begins.","下一局开始。"],[" Red has lost the pistol round.","红队上一局输掉了手枪局。"],[" The defenders now have to decide whether to save their credits or buy weaker weapons.","现在，防守方需要决定是保留经济，还是购买一些较弱的武器。"]],"translation":"下一局开始。 红队上一局输掉了手枪局。 现在，防守方需要决定是保留经济，还是购买一些较弱的武器。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["They choose a partial force buy.","他们选择了部分强起。"]],"translation":"他们选择了部分强起。"},{"kind":"dialogue","sentences":[["Brimstone: \"We can't give them another free round. Buy what you can.\"","Brimstone： \"We can't give them another free round. Buy what you can.\"　不能再白送他们一局了，能买什么就买什么。"]],"translation":"Brimstone： \"We can't give them another free round. Buy what you can.\"　不能再白送他们一局了，能买什么就买什么。"},{"kind":"dialogue","sentences":[["Cypher: \"I'll hold B. Don't let them walk into Market.\"","Cypher： \"I'll hold B. Don't let them walk into Market.\"　我负责架 B 点，别让他们轻松走进市场。"]],"translation":"Cypher： \"I'll hold B. Don't let them walk into Market.\"　我负责架 B 点，别让他们轻松走进市场。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Blue expects the defenders to have weaker weapons.","蓝队认为防守方的武器比较弱。"],[" Instead of rushing, Omen suggests a slow default.","但幽影没有建议直接冲锋，而是提出先慢打。"]],"translation":"蓝队认为防守方的武器比较弱。 但幽影没有建议直接冲锋，而是提出先慢打。"},{"kind":"dialogue","sentences":[["Omen: \"Let's spread out. Two A, two Mid, one watching the flank.\"","Omen： \"Let's spread out. Two A, two Mid, one watching the flank.\"　我们先散开，两个人 A，一人看中路，两个人负责其他区域和绕后防范。"]],"translation":"Omen： \"Let's spread out. Two A, two Mid, one watching the flank.\"　我们先散开，两个人 A，一人看中路，两个人负责其他区域和绕后防范。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["The team divides.","队伍开始分散。"],[" Jett moves toward A Main.","捷风前往 A Main。"],[" Sova takes Mid Top.","猎枭前往 Mid Top。"]],"translation":"队伍开始分散。 捷风前往 A Main。 猎枭前往 Mid Top。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Omen stays near Mid Courtyard.","幽影留在 Mid Courtyard 附近。"],[" Gekko watches B Main.","盖可观察 B Main。"],[" Killjoy stays slightly behind the team.","奇乐则稍微落后于队伍。"]],"translation":"幽影留在 Mid Courtyard 附近。 盖可观察 B Main。 奇乐则稍微落后于队伍。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Suddenly, Sova hears footsteps.","突然，猎枭听到了脚步声。"]],"translation":"突然，猎枭听到了脚步声。"},{"kind":"dialogue","sentences":[["Sova: \"I hear at least two Mid.\"","Sova： \"I hear at least two Mid.\"　我听到中路至少有两个人。"]],"translation":"Sova： \"I hear at least two Mid.\"　我听到中路至少有两个人。"},{"kind":"dialogue","sentences":[["Omen: \"Don't peek. Let's wait for them.\"","Omen： \"Don't peek. Let's wait for them.\"　别探头，我们等他们过来。"]],"translation":"Omen： \"Don't peek. Let's wait for them.\"　别探头，我们等他们过来。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Red is attempting to take Mid control.","红队正在尝试争夺中路控制权。"],[" Cypher moves forward while Skye prepares a flash.","零向前移动，斯凯准备释放闪光。"]],"translation":"红队正在尝试争夺中路控制权。 零向前移动，斯凯准备释放闪光。"},{"kind":"dialogue","sentences":[["Skye: \"Flash out!\"","Skye： \"Flash out!\"　闪光出去了！"]],"translation":"Skye： \"Flash out!\"　闪光出去了！"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["The flash travels through Mid.","闪光穿过中路。"],[" Jett turns away.","捷风及时转身。"],[" But Raze throws a Paint Shells grenade toward the position where Sova is hiding.","但雷兹向猎枭藏身的位置投掷了集束手雷。"]],"translation":"闪光穿过中路。 捷风及时转身。 但雷兹向猎枭藏身的位置投掷了集束手雷。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["The explosion forces Sova out of cover.","爆炸迫使猎枭离开掩体。"]],"translation":"爆炸迫使猎枭离开掩体。"},{"kind":"dialogue","sentences":[["Raze: \"He's tagged! Push!\"","Raze： \"He's tagged! Push!\"　他被炸到了！冲！"]],"translation":"Raze： \"He's tagged! Push!\"　他被炸到了！冲！"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Cypher swings and eliminates Sova.","零探出身位，击杀了猎枭。"],[" Blue is now down one player.","蓝队现在少了一名队员。"],[" However, Jett immediately trades Cypher.","然而，捷风立即补枪，击杀了零。"]],"translation":"零探出身位，击杀了猎枭。 蓝队现在少了一名队员。 然而，捷风立即补枪，击杀了零。"},{"kind":"dialogue","sentences":[["Jett: \"I got him! One Mid down.\"","Jett： \"I got him! One Mid down.\"　我击杀他了！中路倒一个。"]],"translation":"Jett： \"I got him! One Mid down.\"　我击杀他了！中路倒一个。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["The fight becomes a 4v4.","战斗变成了 4 打 4。"],[" Blue decides to rotate toward B.","蓝队决定转向 B 点。"],[" They move from Mid Courtyard through Mid Market toward B Market.","他们从 Mid Courtyard 经过 Mid Market，向 B Market 移动。"]],"translation":"战斗变成了 4 打 4。 蓝队决定转向 B 点。 他们从 Mid Courtyard 经过 Mid Market，向 B Market 移动。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Gekko checks the entrance with Dizzy.","盖可使用 Dizzy 检查入口。"],[" The creature flies forward and detects a defender.","这个生物向前飞行，并发现了一名防守方。"]],"translation":"盖可使用 Dizzy 检查入口。 这个生物向前飞行，并发现了一名防守方。"},{"kind":"dialogue","sentences":[["Gekko: \"One Market! Blind him!\"","Gekko： \"One Market! Blind him!\"　市场一个人！闪他！"]],"translation":"Gekko： \"One Market! Blind him!\"　市场一个人！闪他！"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Jett dashes toward B Site.","捷风冲向 B 点。"],[" Omen smokes CT.","幽影封锁 CT 烟雾。"],[" Killjoy plants the Spike.","奇乐成功下包。"]],"translation":"捷风冲向 B 点。 幽影封锁 CT 烟雾。 奇乐成功下包。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["The attackers establish a post-plant crossfire.","进攻方建立起下包后的交叉火力阵型。"],[" Red attempts to enter through Market.","红队尝试从 Market 进入。"],[" But Jett and Gekko are watching different angles.","但捷风和盖可分别架住了不同角度。"]],"translation":"进攻方建立起下包后的交叉火力阵型。 红队尝试从 Market 进入。 但捷风和盖可分别架住了不同角度。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["The defenders are eliminated.","防守方被全部消灭。"]],"translation":"防守方被全部消灭。"},{"kind":"keyline","sentences":[["ROUND WON — BLUE　BLUE 2 — 0 RED","本局获胜——蓝队　蓝队 2 : 0 红队"]],"translation":"本局获胜——蓝队　蓝队 2 : 0 红队"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["This round demonstrates three important ideas.","这一局展示了三个重要概念。"],[" First, spreading out allows a team to gather information from different parts of the map.","第一，分散站位可以让队伍从地图不同位置收集信息。"],[" Second, trading kills prevents a single enemy from creating a large numerical advantage.","第二，及时补枪可以防止单个敌人建立巨大的人数优势。"]],"translation":"这一局展示了三个重要概念。 第一，分散站位可以让队伍从地图不同位置收集信息。 第二，及时补枪可以防止单个敌人建立巨大的人数优势。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Third, rotating through Mid allows attackers to change sites without returning to their original starting positions.","第三，通过中路转点，进攻方可以改变攻击目标，而不必返回最初的出生位置。"]],"translation":"第三，通过中路转点，进攻方可以改变攻击目标，而不必返回最初的出生位置。"}],"terms":[{"term":"pistol round","meaning":"主要持手枪打的回合","usage":"常见搭配 win/lose the pistol round。pistol 作名词修饰 round，表达该回合的装备类别。","example":"They won the pistol round and saved some credits.","exampleZh":"他们赢了手枪局，还省下了一些点数。","meaningEn":"A round in which players mainly use pistols.","usageEn":"Pistol modifies round. Common patterns are “win the pistol round” and “lose the pistol round.” The surrounding passage uses it for the opening round."},{"term":"force buy","forms":["partial force buy"],"meaning":"经济紧张时强起购买装备","usage":"常说 go for a force buy。原文 partial 指部分成员强起或全队只作部分投入，与全员全装备的 full buy 对应。","example":"They went for a partial force buy after losing the first round.","exampleZh":"首回合失利后，他们选择部分强起。","meaningEn":"Buy equipment despite a limited budget.","usageEn":"“Go for a force buy” describes a decision to spend under economic pressure. A partial force buy involves a more limited commitment than a full buy."},{"term":"tagged","forms":["he's tagged"],"meaning":"对方被击中或受到标记","usage":"在这句发生爆炸之后的报点里表示对手已经吃到伤害。tag 仍可意为标记，例如被侦察道具标出位置，要看前文触发条件。","example":"He’s tagged and moving back toward Mid.","exampleZh":"他中了伤害，正往中路撤。","meaningEn":"Hit or damaged by a shot or ability.","usageEn":"“He’s tagged” means the opponent has already taken a hit here. Tag can also mean mark or identify a target in a passage about reconnaissance."},{"term":"crossfire","forms":["post-plant crossfire","crossfires"],"meaning":"从不同角度形成的交叉火力","usage":"set up/establish a crossfire 都表示建立交叉枪线。post-plant 作前置修饰语，说明发生在下包后。","example":"The two players set up a crossfire near the entrance.","exampleZh":"两名队员在入口附近架出了交叉枪线。","meaningEn":"Fire covering the same area from two or more angles.","usageEn":"Players set up or establish a crossfire. “Post-plant crossfire” specifies that they establish it after planting the Spike."},{"term":"numerical advantage","meaning":"人数优势","usage":"常说 create、gain、maintain a numerical advantage。数字需要具体报出时也可说 a four-versus-three advantage。","example":"That trade stopped them from gaining a numerical advantage.","exampleZh":"那次补枪让对方没能取得人数优势。","meaningEn":"A greater number of active players than the opposing team.","usageEn":"Teams gain, keep, or lose a numerical advantage. A call can name the exact situation, such as “we have a four-against-three advantage.”"}],"glossary":[]},{"en":"Round 3 — The First Tactical Disaster","zh":"第三局——第一次战术灾难","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Red has lost two rounds.","红队已经连续输掉两局。"],[" The team is frustrated.","队伍开始感到焦躁。"],[" Brimstone calls for a fast B attack.","炼狱决定快速进攻 B 点。"]],"translation":"红队已经连续输掉两局。 队伍开始感到焦躁。 炼狱决定快速进攻 B 点。"},{"kind":"dialogue","sentences":[["Brimstone: \"We need to take control. Five B. No hesitation.\"","Brimstone： \"We need to take control. Five B. No hesitation.\"　我们必须拿回主动权，五个人全部打 B，不要犹豫。"]],"translation":"Brimstone： \"We need to take control. Five B. No hesitation.\"　我们必须拿回主动权，五个人全部打 B，不要犹豫。"},{"kind":"dialogue","sentences":[["Raze: \"Let's explode onto the site!\"","Raze： \"Let's explode onto the site!\"　我们直接爆弹冲点！"]],"translation":"Raze： \"Let's explode onto the site!\"　我们直接爆弹冲点！"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["The attackers run toward B Main.","进攻方朝 B Main 冲去。"],[" They do not check Mid.","他们没有检查中路。"],[" They do not wait for their utility.","没有等待技能准备完成。"]],"translation":"进攻方朝 B Main 冲去。 他们没有检查中路。 没有等待技能准备完成。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["They simply rush.","而是直接开始冲锋。"],[" Blue's Killjoy has prepared a defensive setup.","蓝队的奇乐早已布置好了防守阵型。"],[" Her Turret detects the approaching enemies.","她的炮台发现了正在靠近的敌人。"]],"translation":"而是直接开始冲锋。 蓝队的奇乐早已布置好了防守阵型。 她的炮台发现了正在靠近的敌人。"},{"kind":"dialogue","sentences":[["Killjoy: \"They're rushing B! Five, all B!\"","Killjoy： \"They're rushing B! Five, all B!\"　他们在快速冲 B！五个人，全在 B！"]],"translation":"Killjoy： \"They're rushing B! Five, all B!\"　他们在快速冲 B！五个人，全在 B！"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Omen immediately smokes B Main.","幽影立即封锁 B Main 烟雾。"],[" The entrance becomes difficult to see through.","入口变得很难观察。"],[" Jett holds an angle near CT.","捷风在 CT 附近架枪。"]],"translation":"幽影立即封锁 B Main 烟雾。 入口变得很难观察。 捷风在 CT 附近架枪。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Sova prepares a Shock Bolt.","猎枭准备震击箭。"],[" Gekko sends Dizzy toward the entrance.","盖可将 Dizzy 朝入口释放。"],[" The attackers enter the smoke one by one.","进攻方开始一个接一个地进入烟雾。"]],"translation":"猎枭准备震击箭。 盖可将 Dizzy 朝入口释放。 进攻方开始一个接一个地进入烟雾。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Raze is the first to push.","雷兹第一个冲进去。"]],"translation":"雷兹第一个冲进去。"},{"kind":"dialogue","sentences":[["Raze: \"I'm in!\"","Raze： \"I'm in!\"　我进去了！"]],"translation":"Raze： \"I'm in!\"　我进去了！"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Jett fires.","捷风开火。"],[" Raze falls.","雷兹倒地。"],[" Skye follows, but Omen trades her.","斯凯跟进，但幽影立即补枪，将她击杀。"]],"translation":"捷风开火。 雷兹倒地。 斯凯跟进，但幽影立即补枪，将她击杀。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Cypher attempts to enter from the side.","零尝试从侧面进入。"],[" Killjoy's Nanoswarm activates.","奇乐的纳米蜂群启动。"],[" The attackers are forced away from the site.","进攻方被迫离开爆能器区域。"]],"translation":"零尝试从侧面进入。 奇乐的纳米蜂群启动。 进攻方被迫离开爆能器区域。"},{"kind":"dialogue","sentences":[["Killjoy: \"They're stuck! Don't let them through!\"","Killjoy： \"They're stuck! Don't let them through!\"　他们被卡住了！别让他们进来！"]],"translation":"Killjoy： \"They're stuck! Don't let them through!\"　他们被卡住了！别让他们进来！"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Red has lost three players within seconds.","短短几秒钟内，红队已经损失三人。"],[" Brimstone realizes the attack has failed.","炼狱意识到这次进攻失败了。"]],"translation":"短短几秒钟内，红队已经损失三人。 炼狱意识到这次进攻失败了。"},{"kind":"dialogue","sentences":[["Brimstone: \"Fall back! Save if you can!\"","Brimstone： \"Fall back! Save if you can!\"　撤退！能保枪就保枪！"]],"translation":"Brimstone： \"Fall back! Save if you can!\"　撤退！能保枪就保枪！"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["But it is too late.","但已经太晚了。"],[" Sova eliminates the final attacker.","猎枭击杀了最后一名进攻方。"]],"translation":"但已经太晚了。 猎枭击杀了最后一名进攻方。"},{"kind":"keyline","sentences":[["ROUND WON — BLUE　BLUE 3 — 0 RED","本局获胜——蓝队　蓝队 3 : 0 红队"]],"translation":"本局获胜——蓝队　蓝队 3 : 0 红队"},{"kind":"heading","sentences":[["Why did Red lose?","红队为什么会输？"]],"translation":"红队为什么会输？"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["The team made several mistakes.","这支队伍犯了几个错误。"],[" They attacked without gathering information.","他们没有收集信息就开始进攻。"],[" They entered through a narrow choke point.","他们从狭窄的入口进入。"]],"translation":"这支队伍犯了几个错误。 他们没有收集信息就开始进攻。 他们从狭窄的入口进入。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["They failed to clear defensive utility.","他们没有清理防守方布置的技能。"],[" They moved too close together, making them vulnerable to area damage.","他们的站位过于集中，很容易受到范围伤害。"],[" Most importantly, they did not coordinate their abilities.","最重要的是，他们没有协调技能的使用。"]],"translation":"他们没有清理防守方布置的技能。 他们的站位过于集中，很容易受到范围伤害。 最重要的是，他们没有协调技能的使用。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["A fast rush can be effective, but speed without preparation is simply running into a defensive setup.","快速冲锋本身并没有问题，但没有准备的速度，只不过是在直接撞进敌人的防守阵型。"]],"translation":"快速冲锋本身并没有问题，但没有准备的速度，只不过是在直接撞进敌人的防守阵型。"}],"terms":[{"term":"call for","forms":["calls for"],"meaning":"提出或要求采用某种打法","usage":"人作主语时可接行动或计划，比如 call for a pause。事物作主语时也可表示需要某种条件，如 The plan calls for patience。","example":"The team leader called for a slower start.","exampleZh":"队长要求开局打慢一点。","meaningEn":"Ask for a particular plan or action.","usageEn":"A person can call for a pause or a faster approach. With a plan as the subject, “calls for patience” means the plan requires patience."},{"term":"hold an angle","forms":["holds an angle"],"meaning":"架住一条枪线，等待对手出现","usage":"hold 强调已经占据视角并持续盯守。peek an angle 侧重短暂探出去看或对枪。","example":"I’ll hold this angle while you move.","exampleZh":"你移动时我来架这条枪线。","meaningEn":"Keep your aim trained on one line of approach.","usageEn":"Hold emphasizes staying in position and watching the line over time. “Hold this angle” tells a teammate to cover a known direction."},{"term":"fall back","meaning":"后撤，退到更安全的位置","usage":"短促指令 Fall back! 常指战术后撤。可接 to + 退回的位置或 from + 放弃的位置。","example":"Fall back to the entrance and regroup.","exampleZh":"退回入口重新集合。","meaningEn":"Retreat to a safer position.","usageEn":"“Fall back!” works as a complete command. Add “to” plus the safe destination or “from” plus the position you are leaving."},{"term":"choke point","meaning":"行进路线受限的瓶颈处","usage":"既可指地图上的狭窄入口，也可用于交通或流程。choke 在游戏评价里单独出现时还可能指关键时刻发挥失常。","example":"The team got stuck at a narrow choke point.","exampleZh":"队伍被卡在一个狭窄的隘口。","meaningEn":"A narrow point that funnels movement through a larger area.","usageEn":"The phrase can describe an in-game doorway or a real-world bottleneck in traffic or logistics. Players often say “get stuck at a choke point.”"},{"term":"vulnerable to","meaning":"容易受到某种伤害或影响","usage":"to 在此是介词，后接名词或动名词。become vulnerable to 强调从较安全转为暴露。","example":"Standing too close makes players vulnerable to area damage.","exampleZh":"站得过近会使队员更容易受到范围伤害。","meaningEn":"Likely to be harmed or disrupted by something.","usageEn":"To is a preposition here. Follow it with a noun or an -ing form, as in “vulnerable to area damage” or “vulnerable to being detected.”"}],"glossary":[]},{"en":"Round 4 — The Fake Strategy","zh":"第四局——假打战术","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Red finally changes its approach.","红队终于改变了战术。"],[" Cypher suggests using a fake attack.","零提出使用假打。"]],"translation":"红队终于改变了战术。 零提出使用假打。"},{"kind":"dialogue","sentences":[["Cypher: \"They keep stacking their utility on B. Let's make them rotate.\"","Cypher： \"They keep stacking their utility on B. Let's make them rotate.\"　他们一直把技能集中布置在 B 点，我们想办法让他们转点。"]],"translation":"Cypher： \"They keep stacking their utility on B. Let's make them rotate.\"　他们一直把技能集中布置在 B 点，我们想办法让他们转点。"},{"kind":"dialogue","sentences":[["Brimstone: \"Two players show A. The rest of us take Mid.\"","Brimstone： \"Two players show A. The rest of us take Mid.\"　两个人在 A 点露面，剩下的人走中路。"]],"translation":"Brimstone： \"Two players show A. The rest of us take Mid.\"　两个人在 A 点露面，剩下的人走中路。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["The attackers divide into two groups.","进攻方分成两组。"],[" Skye and Raze move toward A Main.","斯凯和雷兹前往 A Main。"],[" They deliberately make noise.","他们故意制造声音。"]],"translation":"进攻方分成两组。 斯凯和雷兹前往 A Main。 他们故意制造声音。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Skye uses her flash.","斯凯使用闪光技能。"],[" Raze fires a few shots.","雷兹开了几枪。"],[" They want Blue to believe that a full A execute is coming.","他们希望蓝队认为一场完整的 A 点进攻即将开始。"]],"translation":"斯凯使用闪光技能。 雷兹开了几枪。 他们希望蓝队认为一场完整的 A 点进攻即将开始。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Meanwhile, Brimstone, Cypher, and Sage move toward Mid.","与此同时，炼狱、零和贤者向中路移动。"]],"translation":"与此同时，炼狱、零和贤者向中路移动。"},{"kind":"dialogue","sentences":[["Skye: \"They're reacting! Two defenders leaving B!\"","Skye： \"They're reacting! Two defenders leaving B!\"　他们有反应了！两个防守方正在离开 B！"]],"translation":"Skye： \"They're reacting! Two defenders leaving B!\"　他们有反应了！两个防守方正在离开 B！"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Blue has heard the noise.","蓝队听到了声音。"]],"translation":"蓝队听到了声音。"},{"kind":"dialogue","sentences":[["Omen: \"A contact! They might be executing A.\"","幽影：A 点有动静！他们可能准备进攻 A！"]],"translation":"幽影：A 点有动静！他们可能准备进攻 A！"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Killjoy begins rotating toward A.","奇乐开始向 A 点转移。"],[" Jett also moves toward the A-side defensive position.","捷风也移动到了 A 侧的防守位置。"],[" However, Sova notices that Mid is unusually quiet.","然而，猎枭发现中路异常安静。"]],"translation":"奇乐开始向 A 点转移。 捷风也移动到了 A 侧的防守位置。 然而，猎枭发现中路异常安静。"},{"kind":"dialogue","sentences":[["Sova: \"Wait. I haven't seen anyone Mid.\"","Sova： \"Wait. I haven't seen anyone Mid.\"　等等，我在中路没有看到任何人。"]],"translation":"Sova： \"Wait. I haven't seen anyone Mid.\"　等等，我在中路没有看到任何人。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Omen realizes something is wrong.","幽影意识到情况不对。"]],"translation":"幽影意识到情况不对。"},{"kind":"dialogue","sentences":[["Omen: \"Don't overrotate. Check Market!\"","Omen： \"Don't overrotate. Check Market!\"　不要过度转点，检查一下市场！"]],"translation":"Omen： \"Don't overrotate. Check Market!\"　不要过度转点，检查一下市场！"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["But Red has already reached B Market.","但红队已经抵达 B Market。"],[" Cypher uses his Trapwire to secure the route behind the attackers.","零使用绊线保护进攻方身后的路线。"],[" Brimstone places smokes at CT and the B entrance.","炼狱在 CT 和 B 点入口部署烟雾。"]],"translation":"但红队已经抵达 B Market。 零使用绊线保护进攻方身后的路线。 炼狱在 CT 和 B 点入口部署烟雾。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Sage uses her Slow Orb to delay the remaining defender.","贤者使用减速法球拖延剩余的防守人员。"],[" The attackers enter B Site.","进攻方进入 B 点。"]],"translation":"贤者使用减速法球拖延剩余的防守人员。 进攻方进入 B 点。"},{"kind":"dialogue","sentences":[["Brimstone: \"Go! Go! Go!\"","Brimstone： \"Go! Go! Go!\"　冲！冲！冲！"]],"translation":"Brimstone： \"Go! Go! Go!\"　冲！冲！冲！"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Raze and Skye immediately rotate from A Main toward Mid to join their teammates.","雷兹和斯凯立即从 A Main 转向中路，与队友会合。"],[" The Spike is planted.","爆能器成功安放。"],[" Blue attempts to recover, but the defenders are out of position.","蓝队尝试回防，但防守人员已经离开了合适的位置。"]],"translation":"雷兹和斯凯立即从 A Main 转向中路，与队友会合。 爆能器成功安放。 蓝队尝试回防，但防守人员已经离开了合适的位置。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Red wins its first round.","红队赢得了第一局。"]],"translation":"红队赢得了第一局。"},{"kind":"keyline","sentences":[["ROUND WON — RED　BLUE 3 — 1 RED","本局获胜——红队　蓝队 3 : 1 红队"]],"translation":"本局获胜——红队　蓝队 3 : 1 红队"},{"kind":"dialogue","sentences":[["Cypher: \"That's how you manipulate rotations.\"","Cypher： \"That's how you manipulate rotations.\"　这就是如何影响敌人的转点决策。"]],"translation":"Cypher： \"That's how you manipulate rotations.\"　这就是如何影响敌人的转点决策。"},{"kind":"dialogue","sentences":[["Brimstone: \"Good. Now they have to respect both sites.\"","Brimstone： \"Good. Now they have to respect both sites.\"　很好，现在他们必须同时防备两个点。"]],"translation":"Brimstone： \"Good. Now they have to respect both sites.\"　很好，现在他们必须同时防备两个点。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["A fake attack is not simply making noise somewhere.","假打并不只是简单地在某个地方制造声音。"],[" It is a deliberate attempt to manipulate the enemy's decisions.","它是一种有目的地影响敌人决策的战术。"],[" The attackers want defenders to leave the actual target before the real attack begins.","进攻方希望防守人员在真正的攻击开始之前，就已经离开了实际目标区域。"]],"translation":"假打并不只是简单地在某个地方制造声音。 它是一种有目的地影响敌人决策的战术。 进攻方希望防守人员在真正的攻击开始之前，就已经离开了实际目标区域。"}],"terms":[{"term":"stack","forms":["stacking their utility"],"meaning":"把多项技能集中叠在同一个区域","usage":"stack + 事物表示集中或叠加，on B 是区域。游戏里 stack B 也可指集中多人守 B，宾语能帮助确定具体含义。","example":"They keep stacking their defensive utility near the entrance.","exampleZh":"他们总把防守技能集中在入口附近。","meaningEn":"Concentrate several resources or players in one place.","usageEn":"“Stack utility on B” specifies what is being concentrated. In calls such as “stack B,” the omitted object can be the players themselves."},{"term":"execute","forms":["full A execute","executing A"],"meaning":"按计划协同发起一波进攻","usage":"a full A execute 中 execute 是游戏术语名词。execute A 作动词时表示把进攻计划付诸执行，常有技能和进场的配合。","example":"Wait for my signal before we execute A.","exampleZh":"等我发信号再对 A 发起协同进攻。","meaningEn":"Carry out a coordinated attack on a site.","usageEn":"The verb takes a target in “execute A.” The countable game noun in “a full A execute” refers to the planned push as a whole."},{"term":"overrotate","meaning":"过度转点，过早把过多人调离原位","usage":"over-表示过量。Don’t overrotate 常在信息不完整时提醒队友别因动静就放空另一侧。","example":"Don’t overrotate until we see the Spike.","exampleZh":"看到爆能器之前，先别把太多人调过去。","meaningEn":"Move too many defenders, or move them too soon, to another site.","usageEn":"Over- indicates an excessive response. “Don’t overrotate” asks the team to leave enough coverage elsewhere while a call is still being confirmed."},{"term":"out of position","meaning":"离开应守的位置，站位不利","usage":"多用 be、get、catch + 人 + out of position。强调当下位置难以履行任务，未必说明队员走错地图方向。","example":"They caught our defender out of position.","exampleZh":"他们趁我们防守队员站位不利时抓住了机会。","meaningEn":"Away from the place where you can carry out your role effectively.","usageEn":"Use it after be, or after a person in “catch someone out of position.” It often describes a temporary disadvantage that opponents notice and exploit."},{"term":"respect both sites","meaning":"认真对待两个点的进攻威胁","usage":"respect 在体育和电竞语境中可表示不低估风险。respect the threat 是认真看待威胁。","example":"After that fake, they had to respect both sites.","exampleZh":"那次假打之后，他们不得不兼顾两边的威胁。","meaningEn":"Treat an attack on either site as a serious possibility.","usageEn":"In tactical commentary, respect a threat means account for it when planning. Here, a successful fake forces the defenders to keep covering both targets."}],"glossary":[]},{"en":"Round 5 — Mid Control and a Split Attack","zh":"第五局——控制中路与分推战术","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["The score is now 3–1.","比分现在是 3:1。"],[" Blue decides to take Mid control.","蓝队决定先控制中路。"],[" This time, the attackers do not immediately choose A or B.","这次，进攻方不会立刻选择 A 或 B 点。"]],"translation":"比分现在是 3:1。 蓝队决定先控制中路。 这次，进攻方不会立刻选择 A 或 B 点。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["They want to control the central area first.","他们希望先控制地图中央区域。"]],"translation":"他们希望先控制地图中央区域。"},{"kind":"dialogue","sentences":[["Omen: \"We take Mid. Once we control it, we can split either site.\"","Omen： \"We take Mid. Once we control it, we can split either site.\"　我们先拿下中路。控制住之后，A 和 B 都可以分推。"]],"translation":"Omen： \"We take Mid. Once we control it, we can split either site.\"　我们先拿下中路。控制住之后，A 和 B 都可以分推。"},{"kind":"dialogue","sentences":[["Sova: \"I'll scan Mid Top.\"","Sova： \"I'll scan Mid Top.\"　我先扫描中路上方。"]],"translation":"Sova： \"I'll scan Mid Top.\"　我先扫描中路上方。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Jett moves toward Mid Catwalk.","捷风移动到 Mid Catwalk。"],[" Sova fires a Recon Bolt toward Mid Courtyard.","猎枭向 Mid Courtyard 发射侦察箭。"],[" Omen places a smoke near the dangerous defensive angle.","幽影在危险的防守角度附近部署烟雾。"]],"translation":"捷风移动到 Mid Catwalk。 猎枭向 Mid Courtyard 发射侦察箭。 幽影在危险的防守角度附近部署烟雾。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Gekko checks Mid Market with Dizzy.","盖可使用 Dizzy 检查 Mid Market。"]],"translation":"盖可使用 Dizzy 检查 Mid Market。"},{"kind":"dialogue","sentences":[["Gekko: \"Market is clear. No one spotted.\"","Gekko： \"Market is clear. No one spotted.\"　市场安全，没有发现敌人。"]],"translation":"Gekko： \"Market is clear. No one spotted.\"　市场安全，没有发现敌人。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Blue now controls most of Mid.","现在蓝队控制了大部分中路区域。"],[" The team has two choices.","队伍有两个选择。"],[" They can move through Mid Catwalk toward A Tree and enter A Site from the side.","他们可以经过 Mid Catwalk，前往 A Tree，从侧面进入 A 点。"]],"translation":"现在蓝队控制了大部分中路区域。 队伍有两个选择。 他们可以经过 Mid Catwalk，前往 A Tree，从侧面进入 A 点。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Or they can move through Mid Market toward B.","也可以经过 Mid Market，前往 B 点。"],[" Omen chooses A.","幽影选择了 A 点。"]],"translation":"也可以经过 Mid Market，前往 B 点。 幽影选择了 A 点。"},{"kind":"dialogue","sentences":[["Omen: \"Split A. Jett, take Catwalk. Gekko, follow me through Tree.\"","Omen： \"Split A. Jett, take Catwalk. Gekko, follow me through Tree.\"　分推 A 点。捷风走猫道，盖可跟我从树房进入。"]],"translation":"Omen： \"Split A. Jett, take Catwalk. Gekko, follow me through Tree.\"　分推 A 点。捷风走猫道，盖可跟我从树房进入。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["The team separates into two groups.","队伍分成两组。"],[" Jett moves along Mid Catwalk.","捷风沿着 Mid Catwalk 移动。"],[" Omen and Gekko approach A Tree.","幽影和盖可靠近 A Tree。"]],"translation":"队伍分成两组。 捷风沿着 Mid Catwalk 移动。 幽影和盖可靠近 A Tree。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Sova stays in Mid and watches for a defender attempting to flank.","猎枭留在中路，观察是否有防守方试图绕后。"]],"translation":"猎枭留在中路，观察是否有防守方试图绕后。"},{"kind":"dialogue","sentences":[["Jett: \"I'm at Catwalk. One Heaven!\"","Jett： \"I'm at Catwalk. One Heaven!\"　我到猫道了！高台有一个！"]],"translation":"Jett： \"I'm at Catwalk. One Heaven!\"　我到猫道了！高台有一个！"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Jett spots a defender.","捷风发现了一名防守方。"],[" She uses her dash to create space and enters A Site from the elevated side.","她使用冲刺技能创造进攻空间，从高台一侧进入 A 点。"],[" At the same time, Omen and Gekko open the Tree-side pressure.","与此同时，幽影和盖可开始从 Tree 一侧施压。"]],"translation":"捷风发现了一名防守方。 她使用冲刺技能创造进攻空间，从高台一侧进入 A 点。 与此同时，幽影和盖可开始从 Tree 一侧施压。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["The defenders are attacked from two directions.","防守方同时遭到两个方向的攻击。"]],"translation":"防守方同时遭到两个方向的攻击。"},{"kind":"dialogue","sentences":[["Red Brimstone: \"They're splitting A! One Tree, one Heaven!\"","Red Brimstone： \"They're splitting A! One Tree, one Heaven!\"　他们在分推 A！树房一个，高台一个！"]],"translation":"Red Brimstone： \"They're splitting A! One Tree, one Heaven!\"　他们在分推 A！树房一个，高台一个！"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Red cannot watch both entrances comfortably.","红队无法同时舒服地观察两个入口。"],[" Jett eliminates one defender.","捷风击杀一名防守方。"],[" Gekko trades another.","盖可补枪击杀另一名敌人。"]],"translation":"红队无法同时舒服地观察两个入口。 捷风击杀一名防守方。 盖可补枪击杀另一名敌人。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Killjoy plants the Spike.","奇乐成功下包。"],[" Blue establishes a strong post-plant setup.","蓝队建立了非常有利的下包后防守阵型。"]],"translation":"奇乐成功下包。 蓝队建立了非常有利的下包后防守阵型。"},{"kind":"keyline","sentences":[["ROUND WON — BLUE　BLUE 4 — 1 RED","本局获胜——蓝队　蓝队 4 : 1 红队"]],"translation":"本局获胜——蓝队　蓝队 4 : 1 红队"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["This is called a split attack.","这就是分推战术（Split）。"],[" Instead of entering through one doorway, the team attacks the same site from multiple connected routes.","队伍不再只从一个入口进入，而是利用地图中相互连接的多条路线，同时攻击同一个爆能器区域。"],[" This makes the defenders divide their attention and creates opportunities for crossfires and trades.","这会迫使防守方分散注意力，也为交叉火力和补枪创造机会。"]],"translation":"这就是分推战术（Split）。 队伍不再只从一个入口进入，而是利用地图中相互连接的多条路线，同时攻击同一个爆能器区域。 这会迫使防守方分散注意力，也为交叉火力和补枪创造机会。"}],"terms":[{"term":"split attack","forms":["split either site","split A","splitting A"],"meaning":"从两条路线分进合击","usage":"split + 点位 是简短战术口语，指分路攻击同一目标。split up 仅表示把人分开，未必有共同进攻点。","example":"Let’s split A through Main and Tree.","exampleZh":"我们从大道和树房分两路打 A。","meaningEn":"A coordinated attack on the same objective from multiple routes.","usageEn":"In a call such as “split A,” split is a verb and A names the common target. “Split up” simply tells people to separate and can describe other situations."},{"term":"scan","meaning":"用侦察技能探查某处","usage":"scan + 地区、scan for + 搜索对象。scan Mid Top 说的是侦察范围。","example":"I’ll scan the entrance for defenders.","exampleZh":"我会侦察入口有没有防守方。","meaningEn":"Search an area with a reconnaissance ability.","usageEn":"Scan + place identifies the area. Add for + person or object to state what you hope to detect, as in “scan the entrance for defenders.”"},{"term":"no one spotted","meaning":"暂未发现敌人","usage":"省略式报点，可展开成 No one has been spotted。它说的是眼下没有观察到敌人。","example":"No one spotted near Market yet.","exampleZh":"市场附近目前没看到人。","meaningEn":"Nobody has been seen in the area so far.","usageEn":"The full form is “no one has been spotted.” The short call reports what players could observe at that moment."},{"term":"at the same time","meaning":"与此同时，同一时刻","usage":"能连接两件同步发生的事。in time 是及时赶上，on time 是准时，语义不同。","example":"We reached both entrances at the same time.","exampleZh":"我们同时抵达了两个入口。","meaningEn":"During the same period or at the same moment.","usageEn":"Place it at the start to link parallel actions, or at the end to stress that two movements happened simultaneously."},{"term":"divide their attention","meaning":"使他们分散注意力","usage":"divide attention between A and B 指一组人要分心兼顾两件事。distract 则强调使人从本来在做的事上分心。","example":"The noise made them divide their attention between the two doors.","exampleZh":"动静让他们不得不同时留意两道门。","meaningEn":"Make a group pay attention to several things at once.","usageEn":"The pattern divide attention between A and B names the competing demands. Here, those demands are two different lines of attack."}],"glossary":[]},{"en":"Round 6 — The Operator Changes the Game","zh":"第六局——冥驹改变了战局","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Red has saved enough credits.","红队已经攒够了经济。"],[" Brimstone decides to purchase an Operator for the team's strongest sniper.","炼狱决定为队伍中最擅长狙击的选手购买 Operator（冥驹）。"],[" The Operator is one of the most powerful weapons in the game.","冥驹是游戏中最强大的武器之一。"]],"translation":"红队已经攒够了经济。 炼狱决定为队伍中最擅长狙击的选手购买 Operator（冥驹）。 冥驹是游戏中最强大的武器之一。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["It can eliminate most enemies with a single body shot.","它能够通过一次身体命中击杀大多数敌人。"],[" The weapon is particularly dangerous when holding long, open angles.","这把枪在架设远距离、开阔角度时尤其危险。"]],"translation":"它能够通过一次身体命中击杀大多数敌人。 这把枪在架设远距离、开阔角度时尤其危险。"},{"kind":"dialogue","sentences":[["Red Brimstone: \"Operator is online. Hold A Main.\"","Red Brimstone： \"Operator is online. Hold A Main.\"　冥驹已经买好了，架住 A 大道。"]],"translation":"Red Brimstone： \"Operator is online. Hold A Main.\"　冥驹已经买好了，架住 A 大道。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Red's sniper positions himself near A Heaven.","红队的狙击手在 A Heaven 附近寻找位置。"],[" Blue approaches A Main.","蓝队靠近 A Main。"],[" Jett wants to peek.","捷风想要探头对枪。"]],"translation":"红队的狙击手在 A Heaven 附近寻找位置。 蓝队靠近 A Main。 捷风想要探头对枪。"},{"kind":"dialogue","sentences":[["Jett: \"Can I take this fight?\"","Jett： \"Can I take this fight?\"　我能和他对枪吗？"]],"translation":"Jett： \"Can I take this fight?\"　我能和他对枪吗？"},{"kind":"dialogue","sentences":[["Omen: \"No. Don't challenge the Operator. We need another route.\"","Omen： \"No. Don't challenge the Operator. We need another route.\"　不行，不要主动挑战冥驹，我们换一条路线。"]],"translation":"Omen： \"No. Don't challenge the Operator. We need another route.\"　不行，不要主动挑战冥驹，我们换一条路线。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Sova sends his drone toward A Main.","猎枭向 A Main 派出无人机。"],[" The drone moves through the entrance and checks several corners.","无人机穿过入口，检查了几个角落。"],[" The sniper fires and destroys the drone.","狙击手开枪，将无人机击毁。"]],"translation":"猎枭向 A Main 派出无人机。 无人机穿过入口，检查了几个角落。 狙击手开枪，将无人机击毁。"},{"kind":"dialogue","sentences":[["Sova: \"Operator A. He's holding the long angle.\"","Sova： \"Operator A. He's holding the long angle.\""]],"translation":"Sova： \"Operator A. He's holding the long angle.\""},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Omen immediately changes the plan.","A 点有冥驹，他正在架远距离角度。 幽影立即改变计划。"]],"translation":"A 点有冥驹，他正在架远距离角度。 幽影立即改变计划。"},{"kind":"dialogue","sentences":[["Omen: \"Rotate Mid. We can pressure B.\"","Omen： \"Rotate Mid. We can pressure B.\"　转中路，我们可以给 B 点施加压力。"]],"translation":"Omen： \"Rotate Mid. We can pressure B.\"　转中路，我们可以给 B 点施加压力。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["The attackers retreat from A Main.","进攻方从 A Main 撤退。"],[" They move toward Mid Top.","他们向 Mid Top 移动。"],[" But Red has anticipated this possibility.","但红队已经预料到这种可能。"]],"translation":"进攻方从 A Main 撤退。 他们向 Mid Top 移动。 但红队已经预料到这种可能。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Cypher watches the rotation.","零正在观察转点路线。"],[" His camera detects movement.","他的摄像头发现了移动。"]],"translation":"零正在观察转点路线。 他的摄像头发现了移动。"},{"kind":"dialogue","sentences":[["Cypher: \"They're leaving A. Two Mid!\"","Cypher： \"They're leaving A. Two Mid!\"　他们离开 A 了！中路两个！"]],"translation":"Cypher： \"They're leaving A. Two Mid!\"　他们离开 A 了！中路两个！"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Skye begins moving toward B.","斯凯开始向 B 点移动。"],[" Blue realizes that the defenders are rotating.","蓝队意识到防守方也在转移。"],[" The team decides to slow down.","队伍决定放慢速度。"]],"translation":"斯凯开始向 B 点移动。 蓝队意识到防守方也在转移。 队伍决定放慢速度。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Instead of rushing B, they wait near Mid Market.","他们没有直接冲向 B，而是在 Mid Market 附近等待。"],[" Omen places a smoke.","幽影部署烟雾。"],[" Gekko uses Dizzy.","盖可使用 Dizzy。"]],"translation":"他们没有直接冲向 B，而是在 Mid Market 附近等待。 幽影部署烟雾。 盖可使用 Dizzy。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["The attackers enter B.","进攻方进入 B 点。"],[" However, Brimstone has already reached CT.","然而，炼狱已经抵达 CT。"],[" He places a defensive smoke and delays the plant.","他部署防守烟雾，拖延下包。"]],"translation":"进攻方进入 B 点。 然而，炼狱已经抵达 CT。 他部署防守烟雾，拖延下包。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["The round becomes a 3v3.","战斗变成了 3 打 3。"],[" The attackers finally plant, but there is very little time left to establish their positions.","进攻方最终成功下包，但已经没有多少时间建立合适的防守阵型。"],[" Red retakes the site.","红队开始回防。"]],"translation":"战斗变成了 3 打 3。 进攻方最终成功下包，但已经没有多少时间建立合适的防守阵型。 红队开始回防。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["The Spike is defused.","爆能器被成功拆除。"]],"translation":"爆能器被成功拆除。"},{"kind":"keyline","sentences":[["ROUND WON — RED　BLUE 4 — 2 RED","本局获胜——红队　蓝队 4 : 2 红队"]],"translation":"本局获胜——红队　蓝队 4 : 2 红队"},{"kind":"heading","sentences":[["The Operator lesson","关于冥驹的战术知识"]],"translation":"关于冥驹的战术知识"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Never challenge a powerful sniper rifle on its strongest angle without a good reason.","如果敌人正在利用冥驹架设最有利的角度，不要没有理由地主动对枪。"],[" You can use smokes, flashes, drones, or alternative routes to force the sniper to move.","你可以使用烟雾、闪光、无人机或其他路线迫使狙击手移动。"]],"translation":"如果敌人正在利用冥驹架设最有利的角度，不要没有理由地主动对枪。 你可以使用烟雾、闪光、无人机或其他路线迫使狙击手移动。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Sometimes the best way to defeat a weapon is to avoid fighting it directly.","有时候，击败一把强力武器最好的方法，就是避免与它正面对抗。"]],"translation":"有时候，击败一把强力武器最好的方法，就是避免与它正面对抗。"}],"terms":[{"term":"body shot","meaning":"击中身体的一枪","usage":"a single body shot 强调只需一次命中身体。和 headshot 相对，用于表述命中部位。","example":"One body shot was enough to stop the push.","exampleZh":"一次击中身体就阻止了这次推进。","meaningEn":"A shot that hits the opponent’s body.","usageEn":"Body shot and headshot name different hit locations. “A single body shot” emphasizes that one hit to the body can be enough in this situation."},{"term":"online","forms":["operator is online"],"meaning":"武器已到位，威胁已经出现","usage":"游戏中 X is online 可指某武器、技能或队员已经就绪并形成威胁。普通语境也可能只是已联网。","example":"Their sniper is online, so watch the long lane.","exampleZh":"对面狙击手已经就位，留意那条长通道。","meaningEn":"Available, in position, and ready to be used.","usageEn":"In “the Operator is online,” online signals that the weapon is in play and threatening a route. Elsewhere, it can mean a device is connected to a network."},{"term":"challenge the Operator","forms":["challenge a powerful sniper rifle"],"meaning":"主动和持冥驹、占有利视角的对手交手","usage":"challenge + 对手、武器或点位在语境里可指主动对抗某个威胁。日常里 challenge a claim 表示质疑一项说法。","example":"Don’t challenge the Operator from the open lane.","exampleZh":"别从开阔的通道主动去跟冥驹对枪。","meaningEn":"Directly take a fight against someone using the Operator.","usageEn":"In game chat, challenge can take the weapon as its object even though the opponent is the person holding it. In “challenge an assumption,” it means question the assumption."},{"term":"anticipate","forms":["anticipated"],"meaning":"预先料到对方可能采取的行动","usage":"接名词或动名词，如 anticipate a rotation、anticipate losing control。anticipate this possibility 强调对潜在情况已有准备。","example":"They anticipated a rotation through Mid.","exampleZh":"他们预料到有人会经过中路转点。","meaningEn":"Expect something in advance and take it into account.","usageEn":"Use anticipate with a noun or an -ing form, as in “anticipate a rotation” or “anticipate losing control of Mid.”"},{"term":"establish their positions","meaning":"站好预定位置并稳住阵型","usage":"establish 强调建立并稳定下来，常搭配 positions、control、a crossfire。take a position 偏重走到或占住该位置。","example":"We didn’t have time to establish our positions after planting.","exampleZh":"下包后我们来不及站好预定位置。","meaningEn":"Take up stable positions from which they can carry out the plan.","usageEn":"Establish suggests creating and maintaining a useful arrangement. Teams can also establish control or establish a crossfire."}],"glossary":[]},{"en":"Round 7 — Post-Plant: The Real Battle Begins","zh":"第七局——下包后的战斗才是真正的开始","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Blue now understands that planting the Spike is only half the job.","蓝队现在明白，下包只是任务的一半。"],[" The team needs to survive after planting.","队伍还必须在下包之后存活下来。"],[" Omen proposes a new strategy.","幽影提出了一个新战术。"]],"translation":"蓝队现在明白，下包只是任务的一半。 队伍还必须在下包之后存活下来。 幽影提出了一个新战术。"},{"kind":"dialogue","sentences":[["Omen: \"Let's play for post-plant. Don't stay on site.\"","Omen： \"Let's play for post-plant. Don't stay on site.\"　我们围绕下包后的局势来打，不要一直待在点内。"]],"translation":"Omen： \"Let's play for post-plant. Don't stay on site.\"　我们围绕下包后的局势来打，不要一直待在点内。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["The attackers execute B.","进攻方开始执行 B 点进攻。"],[" Sova scans the entrance.","猎枭扫描入口。"],[" Gekko uses Dizzy.","盖可使用 Dizzy。"]],"translation":"进攻方开始执行 B 点进攻。 猎枭扫描入口。 盖可使用 Dizzy。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Omen smokes Market and CT.","幽影封锁 Market 和 CT 烟雾。"],[" Jett dashes into the site.","捷风冲进爆能器区域。"],[" Killjoy plants the Spike.","奇乐成功下包。"]],"translation":"幽影封锁 Market 和 CT 烟雾。 捷风冲进爆能器区域。 奇乐成功下包。"},{"kind":"dialogue","sentences":[["Killjoy: \"Spike planted!\"","Killjoy： \"Spike planted!\"　包已经下好了！"]],"translation":"Killjoy： \"Spike planted!\"　包已经下好了！"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Immediately, Blue retreats to predetermined positions.","蓝队立即撤退到事先安排好的位置。"],[" Jett moves toward B Main.","捷风移动到 B Main。"],[" Sova holds a long angle.","猎枭架住远距离角度。"]],"translation":"蓝队立即撤退到事先安排好的位置。 捷风移动到 B Main。 猎枭架住远距离角度。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Omen watches Market.","幽影观察 Market。"],[" Gekko positions himself near CT.","盖可位于 CT 附近。"],[" Killjoy places Nanoswarm near the Spike.","奇乐在爆能器附近放置纳米蜂群。"]],"translation":"幽影观察 Market。 盖可位于 CT 附近。 奇乐在爆能器附近放置纳米蜂群。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Red begins the retake.","红队开始回防。"]],"translation":"红队开始回防。"},{"kind":"dialogue","sentences":[["Red Skye: \"Flash going out!\"","Red Skye： \"Flash going out!\"　闪光出去了！"]],"translation":"Red Skye： \"Flash going out!\"　闪光出去了！"},{"kind":"dialogue","sentences":[["Red Raze: \"I'm entering Market!\"","Red Raze： \"I'm entering Market!\"　我要从市场进点！"]],"translation":"Red Raze： \"I'm entering Market!\"　我要从市场进点！"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Skye flashes through Market.","斯凯通过 Market 释放闪光。"],[" Raze enters.","雷兹进入。"],[" But Jett is waiting near B Main.","但捷风已经在 B Main 附近等待。"]],"translation":"斯凯通过 Market 释放闪光。 雷兹进入。 但捷风已经在 B Main 附近等待。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["She eliminates Raze.","她击杀了雷兹。"],[" Omen trades Skye.","幽影补枪击杀斯凯。"],[" The defenders are down two players.","防守方已经损失两人。"]],"translation":"她击杀了雷兹。 幽影补枪击杀斯凯。 防守方已经损失两人。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Cypher attempts to enter through CT.","零尝试从 CT 进入。"],[" Gekko spots him.","盖可发现了他。"]],"translation":"零尝试从 CT 进入。 盖可发现了他。"},{"kind":"dialogue","sentences":[["Gekko: \"One CT! He's low!\"","Gekko： \"One CT! He's low!\""]],"translation":"Gekko： \"One CT! He's low!\""},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Sova fires and eliminates him. The last defender is Brimstone. He approaches the Spike and begins defusing.","CT 一个！他残血了！ 猎枭开枪将其击杀。 最后一名防守方是炼狱。"]],"translation":"CT 一个！他残血了！ 猎枭开枪将其击杀。 最后一名防守方是炼狱。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["The sound starts. The defenders are desperate.","他靠近爆能器并开始拆包。 拆包声音响起。 防守方已经非常着急。"]],"translation":"他靠近爆能器并开始拆包。 拆包声音响起。 防守方已经非常着急。"},{"kind":"dialogue","sentences":[["Brimstone: \"I'm sticking it!\"","Brimstone： \"I'm sticking it!\"　我正在拆！我不松手！"]],"translation":"Brimstone： \"I'm sticking it!\"　我正在拆！我不松手！"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Omen hears the defuse.","幽影听到了拆包的声音。"],[" He swings from cover.","他从掩体后探出。"],[" Brimstone is eliminated.","炼狱被击杀。"]],"translation":"幽影听到了拆包的声音。 他从掩体后探出。 炼狱被击杀。"},{"kind":"dialogue","sentences":[["Omen: \"He's off the bomb!\"","Omen： \"He's off the bomb!\"　他已经离开爆能器了！"]],"translation":"Omen： \"He's off the bomb!\"　他已经离开爆能器了！"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["The Spike continues ticking.","爆能器仍然在持续倒计时。"],[" Red cannot recover.","红队已经无法挽回局势。"]],"translation":"爆能器仍然在持续倒计时。 红队已经无法挽回局势。"},{"kind":"keyline","sentences":[["ROUND WON — BLUE　BLUE 5 — 2 RED","本局获胜——蓝队　蓝队 5 : 2 红队"]],"translation":"本局获胜——蓝队　蓝队 5 : 2 红队"},{"kind":"heading","sentences":[["Why is post-plant positioning important?","为什么下包后的站位非常重要？"]],"translation":"为什么下包后的站位非常重要？"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["After the Spike is planted, attackers do not need to eliminate every defender. They only need to prevent the defenders from completing the defuse.","下包之后，进攻方并不需要消灭所有防守方。 他们只需要阻止防守方完成拆包。 这意味着他们可以围绕时间进行防守，使用技能拖延回防，并迫使敌人进入危险的射击角度。"]],"translation":"下包之后，进攻方并不需要消灭所有防守方。 他们只需要阻止防守方完成拆包。 这意味着他们可以围绕时间进行防守，使用技能拖延回防，并迫使敌人进入危险的射击角度。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["This means they can play around time, use utility to delay the retake, and force enemies to enter dangerous angles. Sometimes a team wins by refusing to fight.","有时候，一支队伍不主动交战，反而能够赢得比赛。"]],"translation":"有时候，一支队伍不主动交战，反而能够赢得比赛。"}],"terms":[{"term":"play for post-plant","meaning":"下包后按守包方案执行","usage":"play for + 目标在这里表达战术优先级。post-plant 既可单独指下包后的阶段，也可作前置修饰。","example":"Let’s play for post-plant and stay within reach of each other.","exampleZh":"下包后按守包方案打，队友之间保持能接应的距离。","meaningEn":"Set up for the part of the round after the Spike is planted.","usageEn":"Play for + objective tells teammates what to prioritize. Post-plant also modifies nouns, as in “post-plant positions.”"},{"term":"predetermined","meaning":"预先定好的","usage":"pre-表示事先。predetermined positions 已在行动之前决定。a predetermined outcome 含义则是结果事先已被决定。","example":"We fell back to our predetermined positions.","exampleZh":"我们撤回事先约定的位置。","meaningEn":"Decided in advance.","usageEn":"The prefix pre- means before. “Predetermined positions” means teammates decided where to go before the current action began."},{"term":"be down","forms":["are down two players"],"meaning":"少了若干名队员","usage":"be down + 数量或人员表示人手或比分减少。be down to two players 则明确表示还剩两人。","example":"We’re down one player, but we still have time.","exampleZh":"我们少了一人，但还有时间。","meaningEn":"Have lost the specified number of players.","usageEn":"“We’re down two players” reports two losses. “We’re down to two players” reports that two players are still active."},{"term":"stick it","forms":["i'm sticking it","stick the Spike"],"meaning":"坚持拆包，不中途松手","usage":"拆包语境里 stick it 表示准备继续拆完。动词 stick 作坚持解时常搭配 stick with the plan，意思是继续执行计划。","example":"I’m sticking it. Cover me.","exampleZh":"我会继续拆到底，掩护我。","meaningEn":"Keep defusing until the action is complete.","usageEn":"“I’m sticking it” tells teammates the speaker intends to keep holding the defuse. In everyday speech, “stick with the plan” similarly conveys continuing an action or commitment."},{"term":"play around time","meaning":"利用剩余时间安排动作","usage":"play around + 限制或信息，表示据此调整打法。play for time 更具体，重在拖延消耗时间。","example":"We can play around time once the Spike is down.","exampleZh":"爆能器安好后，我们可以围绕剩余时间来打。","meaningEn":"Choose when to act based on the time remaining.","usageEn":"Play around + constraint means adapt your decisions to it. A post-plant team can use the running clock to decide when to delay or engage."}],"glossary":[]},{"en":"Round 8 — A 1v3 Clutch","zh":"第八局——1 对 3 的残局","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["The next round becomes chaotic.","下一局比赛变得混乱。"],[" Blue executes A, but the attack fails.","蓝队执行 A 点进攻，但进攻失败。"],[" Three attackers are eliminated.","三名进攻方被击杀。"]],"translation":"下一局比赛变得混乱。 蓝队执行 A 点进攻，但进攻失败。 三名进攻方被击杀。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Only Omen and Jett remain.","只剩下幽影和捷风。"],[" Jett attempts to recover the situation, but a defender catches her near Tree.","捷风试图挽回局势，但在 Tree 附近被一名防守方发现。"],[" She falls.","她倒下了。"]],"translation":"只剩下幽影和捷风。 捷风试图挽回局势，但在 Tree 附近被一名防守方发现。 她倒下了。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Omen is now alone.","现在只剩幽影一个人。"],[" The scoreboard shows:","比分板显示："]],"translation":"现在只剩幽影一个人。 比分板显示："},{"kind":"keyline","sentences":[["1 vs 3","1 对 3"]],"translation":"1 对 3"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["The Spike is planted.","爆能器已经安放。"],[" Three defenders remain.","还剩三名防守方。"],[" Omen has very little health.","幽影的生命值也已经非常低。"]],"translation":"爆能器已经安放。 还剩三名防守方。 幽影的生命值也已经非常低。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["He hears footsteps.","他听到了脚步声。"],[" One enemy is near Heaven.","一名敌人在 Heaven 附近。"],[" Another is approaching Tree.","另一名敌人正在接近 Tree。"]],"translation":"他听到了脚步声。 一名敌人在 Heaven 附近。 另一名敌人正在接近 Tree。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["The last one is holding A Main.","最后一名敌人架住了 A Main。"]],"translation":"最后一名敌人架住了 A Main。"},{"kind":"dialogue","sentences":[["Omen: \"I need to isolate them.\"","Omen： \"I need to isolate them.\"　我必须把他们分开处理。"]],"translation":"Omen： \"I need to isolate them.\"　我必须把他们分开处理。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["He moves toward cover.","他移动到掩体后方。"],[" He knows that fighting all three enemies simultaneously would be almost impossible.","他知道，如果同时与三个人交战，几乎没有获胜的可能。"],[" He throws a smoke near Heaven.","他向 Heaven 附近释放烟雾。"]],"translation":"他移动到掩体后方。 他知道，如果同时与三个人交战，几乎没有获胜的可能。 他向 Heaven 附近释放烟雾。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["The smoke blocks one defender's vision.","烟雾遮挡了一名防守方的视线。"],[" Omen uses Shrouded Step to reposition.","幽影使用传送技能改变位置。"],[" The defender near Tree does not expect him to appear from another angle.","Tree 附近的防守方没有想到他会从另一个角度出现。"]],"translation":"烟雾遮挡了一名防守方的视线。 幽影使用传送技能改变位置。 Tree 附近的防守方没有想到他会从另一个角度出现。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Omen swings.","幽影探出身位。"],[" One shot.","一枪。"],[" First kill.","第一个击杀。"]],"translation":"幽影探出身位。 一枪。 第一个击杀。"},{"kind":"dialogue","sentences":[["Omen: \"One down.\"","Omen： \"One down.\"　倒一个。"]],"translation":"Omen： \"One down.\"　倒一个。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["He immediately retreats.","他立即撤退。"],[" The remaining two defenders start searching for him.","剩下两名防守方开始寻找他。"],[" Omen hears the defuse sound.","幽影听到了拆包的声音。"]],"translation":"他立即撤退。 剩下两名防守方开始寻找他。 幽影听到了拆包的声音。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["One defender is attempting to stick the Spike.","一名防守方正在尝试拆除爆能器。"],[" He has to make a decision.","他必须作出决定。"],[" He swings toward the Spike.","他朝爆能器方向探出。"]],"translation":"一名防守方正在尝试拆除爆能器。 他必须作出决定。 他朝爆能器方向探出。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["The defender is eliminated.","防守方被击杀。"],[" Second kill.","第二个人头。"],[" But the final defender is waiting near A Main.","但最后一名防守方正在 A Main 附近等待。"]],"translation":"防守方被击杀。 第二个人头。 但最后一名防守方正在 A Main 附近等待。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Omen is low on health.","幽影的生命值已经很低。"],[" He throws a Paranoia through the entrance.","他向入口释放致盲技能 Paranoia。"],[" The final defender is blinded.","最后一名防守方被致盲。"]],"translation":"幽影的生命值已经很低。 他向入口释放致盲技能 Paranoia。 最后一名防守方被致盲。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Omen pushes through the smoke.","幽影穿过烟雾冲出。"],[" A short burst.","短暂扫射。"],[" The enemy falls.","敌人倒下。"]],"translation":"幽影穿过烟雾冲出。 短暂扫射。 敌人倒下。"},{"kind":"keyline","sentences":[["THREE KILLS!","三杀！"]],"translation":"三杀！"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["The Spike detonates.","爆能器发生爆炸。"],[" Omen wins the round alone.","幽影独自赢下了这一局。"]],"translation":"爆能器发生爆炸。 幽影独自赢下了这一局。"},{"kind":"keyline","sentences":[["ROUND WON — BLUE　BLUE 6 — 2 RED","本局获胜——蓝队　蓝队 6 : 2 红队"]],"translation":"本局获胜——蓝队　蓝队 6 : 2 红队"},{"kind":"dialogue","sentences":[["Jett: \"No way! That was insane!\"","Jett： \"No way! That was insane!\"　不是吧！太离谱了！"]],"translation":"Jett： \"No way! That was insane!\"　不是吧！太离谱了！"},{"kind":"dialogue","sentences":[["Omen: \"One at a time. Never fight all three.\"","Omen： \"One at a time. Never fight all three.\"　一个一个处理，绝对不要同时和三个敌人交战。"]],"translation":"Omen： \"One at a time. Never fight all three.\"　一个一个处理，绝对不要同时和三个敌人交战。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["This is a clutch.","这就是残局（Clutch）。"],[" The most important skill in a clutch situation is not always aim.","残局中最重要的能力不一定是枪法。"],[" It is isolating enemies, managing time, and avoiding multiple simultaneous fights.","更重要的是分割敌人、管理时间，以及避免同时面对多个敌人。"]],"translation":"这就是残局（Clutch）。 残局中最重要的能力不一定是枪法。 更重要的是分割敌人、管理时间，以及避免同时面对多个敌人。"}],"terms":[{"term":"clutch","forms":["clutch situation"],"meaning":"人数劣势下逆转拿下残局","usage":"a clutch 指一次残局逆转，clutch a round 作动词。achieve a clutch 不如 win a clutch 或 clutch the round 常见。","example":"She won a one-versus-two clutch.","exampleZh":"她赢下了一打二的残局。","meaningEn":"A round won from a difficult situation, often by the last player alive.","usageEn":"“Win a clutch” uses clutch as a noun. Players also use it as a verb, as in “she clutched the round.”"},{"term":"isolate","forms":["isolating enemies"],"meaning":"把对手分隔开，逐个处理","usage":"isolate + 敌人强调限制同其他人互相支援的机会。练习语境也能说 isolate a problem（把问题单独抽出来分析）。","example":"The smoke helped him isolate one opponent.","exampleZh":"烟幕帮他隔开了其中一名对手。","meaningEn":"Separate an opponent so they can be dealt with individually.","usageEn":"Use isolate with the person or problem you want to separate. An isolated opponent has less opportunity to receive immediate help from teammates."},{"term":"low on health","meaning":"生命值很低","usage":"low on + 资源，也常说 low on time/ammo。He’s low 是语音里的简略形式，游戏语境默认说血量低。","example":"I’m low on health, so I’ll hold back.","exampleZh":"我血量很低，先站后面一点。","meaningEn":"With very little health remaining.","usageEn":"Low on also takes other limited resources, such as time and ammunition. In quick game calls, “he’s low” commonly leaves out “on health.”"},{"term":"burst","forms":["a short burst"],"meaning":"一小串连续射击","usage":"burst 作名词时指突然而短暂的一阵，可用 a burst of fire。a short burst 强调射击集中且时间短。","example":"She fired a short burst and stepped back.","exampleZh":"她短促连射几发，然后向后退了一步。","meaningEn":"A short, sudden series of shots.","usageEn":"Burst is countable here. “A burst of fire” describes the shots, and “a short burst” emphasizes the brief duration."},{"term":"one at a time","meaning":"一个接一个，一次只处理一个","usage":"at a time 强调每一轮动作涉及的数量。at the same time 表示同时，顺序正好相反。","example":"Deal with the opponents one at a time.","exampleZh":"一次对付一个对手。","meaningEn":"Individually, in sequence.","usageEn":"At a time describes how many are involved in each action or step. Players can say “take them one at a time” to describe separate engagements."}],"glossary":[]},{"en":"Half-Time — The Score Changes Everything","zh":"中场休息——比分改变一切","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["The first half ends.","上半场结束。"]],"translation":"上半场结束。"},{"kind":"keyline","sentences":[["BLUE 8 — 4 RED","蓝队 8 : 4 红队"]],"translation":"蓝队 8 : 4 红队"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["The teams switch sides.","双方交换攻防。"],[" Blue becomes the defending team.","蓝队成为防守方。"],[" Red becomes the attacking team.","红队成为进攻方。"]],"translation":"双方交换攻防。 蓝队成为防守方。 红队成为进攻方。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["The economy resets according to the side-switch rules.","经济按照双方交换阵营后的规则结算。"],[" The players now have to think differently.","现在，玩家必须用完全不同的思路思考。"],[" Blue no longer needs to plant the Spike.","蓝队不再需要下包。"]],"translation":"经济按照双方交换阵营后的规则结算。 现在，玩家必须用完全不同的思路思考。 蓝队不再需要下包。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Its job is to control the map, gather information, delay the attackers, and prevent the plant.","他们的任务是控制地图、收集信息、拖延进攻方，并阻止对方完成下包。"],[" Red now needs to create space and enter a bomb site.","红队则需要创造进攻空间，并进入爆能器区域。"],[" During the buy phase, Brimstone speaks.","购买阶段，炼狱开始讲话。"]],"translation":"他们的任务是控制地图、收集信息、拖延进攻方，并阻止对方完成下包。 红队则需要创造进攻空间，并进入爆能器区域。 购买阶段，炼狱开始讲话。"},{"kind":"dialogue","sentences":[["Brimstone: \"We've been too predictable. We keep entering through the same routes.\"","Brimstone： \"We've been too predictable. We keep entering through the same routes.\"　我们太容易被预测了。一直从相同路线进攻。"]],"translation":"Brimstone： \"We've been too predictable. We keep entering through the same routes.\"　我们太容易被预测了。一直从相同路线进攻。"},{"kind":"dialogue","sentences":[["Cypher: \"We need to control Mid. Their defense is too comfortable.\"","Cypher： \"We need to control Mid. Their defense is too comfortable.\"　我们必须控制中路，他们现在的防守太舒服了。"]],"translation":"Cypher： \"We need to control Mid. Their defense is too comfortable.\"　我们必须控制中路，他们现在的防守太舒服了。"},{"kind":"dialogue","sentences":[["Skye: \"I'll flash for the entry. Raze, wait for my call.\"","Skye： \"I'll flash for the entry. Raze, wait for my call.\"　我负责进点闪光。雷兹，等我指挥再冲。"]],"translation":"Skye： \"I'll flash for the entry. Raze, wait for my call.\"　我负责进点闪光。雷兹，等我指挥再冲。"},{"kind":"dialogue","sentences":[["Raze: \"Got it.\"","Raze： \"Got it.\"　明白。"]],"translation":"Raze： \"Got it.\"　明白。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["On Blue's side, Omen gives instructions.","蓝队这边，幽影开始安排防守。"]],"translation":"蓝队这边，幽影开始安排防守。"},{"kind":"dialogue","sentences":[["Omen: \"Don't fight too early. We have utility. Make them spend time.\"","Omen： \"Don't fight too early. We have utility. Make them spend time.\"　不要过早交战。我们有技能，尽量拖延他们的时间。"]],"translation":"Omen： \"Don't fight too early. We have utility. Make them spend time.\"　不要过早交战。我们有技能，尽量拖延他们的时间。"},{"kind":"dialogue","sentences":[["Killjoy: \"I'll anchor B. If they rush, I'll delay them.\"","Killjoy： \"I'll anchor B. If they rush, I'll delay them.\"　我负责守 B，如果他们强冲，我会拖住他们。"]],"translation":"Killjoy： \"I'll anchor B. If they rush, I'll delay them.\"　我负责守 B，如果他们强冲，我会拖住他们。"},{"kind":"dialogue","sentences":[["Sova: \"I'll watch Mid and call rotations.\"","Sova： \"I'll watch Mid and call rotations.\"　我负责观察中路并报告敌人的转点。"]],"translation":"Sova： \"I'll watch Mid and call rotations.\"　我负责观察中路并报告敌人的转点。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["The second half begins.","下半场开始。"],[" The map feels different now.","地图似乎变得不一样了。"],[" The same positions have completely different purposes.","相同的位置，现在拥有完全不同的意义。"]],"translation":"下半场开始。 地图似乎变得不一样了。 相同的位置，现在拥有完全不同的意义。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["A Main is no longer a route to attack.","A Main 不再是进攻路线，而是防守方阻止敌人进攻的区域。"],[" It is a place where defenders can stop an incoming push.","中路也不再只是通往爆能器区域的路线，而是进攻方可能被发现、防守方可以转点的关键区域。"],[" Mid is no longer just a path toward the bomb sites.","地图没有变化。"]],"translation":"A Main 不再是进攻路线，而是防守方阻止敌人进攻的区域。 中路也不再只是通往爆能器区域的路线，而是进攻方可能被发现、防守方可以转点的关键区域。 地图没有变化。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["It is a place where attackers can be detected and defenders can rotate. The map has not changed. But the objective has.","但比赛目标已经改变。"]],"translation":"但比赛目标已经改变。"}],"terms":[{"term":"switch sides","meaning":"交换攻防角色","usage":"switch sides 也可表示改换阵营，在上下半场过渡时通常指规则要求的攻守互换。","example":"The teams switch sides at half-time.","exampleZh":"双方在中场休息时交换攻防。","meaningEn":"Exchange attacking and defending roles.","usageEn":"At half-time in this passage, the switch is required by the match rules. In other settings, switching sides can mean choosing to support another group."},{"term":"reset","forms":["resets"],"meaning":"（经济）重置，恢复到规则规定的起点","usage":"可不及物作 The economy resets，也可及物说 The rules reset the economy。Let’s reset 在队内语音里也可以是打起精神、重新来。","example":"Everyone’s credits reset when the sides switch.","exampleZh":"队伍交换攻防时，所有人的点数都会重置。","meaningEn":"Return to the starting value or state.","usageEn":"“The economy resets” has the changing system as its subject. “The rules reset the economy” states what causes the change. “Let’s reset” can also suggest regaining focus."},{"term":"predictable","meaning":"易被预判，容易猜到","usage":"too predictable 常用于描述某个反复出现的行为模式。predictable、expected 都能说「可预期」，前者更强调行为缺少变化。","example":"Our routes have become too predictable.","exampleZh":"我们的路线变得太容易被猜到了。","meaningEn":"Easy to anticipate from a repeated pattern.","usageEn":"“Too predictable” suggests the pattern is now easy for opponents to exploit. Common subjects include positions, routes, and reactions."},{"term":"wait for my call","meaning":"等我发口令","usage":"call 在团队沟通里可指给出决定或信号。wait for + 事物，可以说 wait for my signal。","example":"Don’t move until you hear my call.","exampleZh":"听到我的口令再动。","meaningEn":"Wait until I give the signal to act.","usageEn":"Call means a decision, instruction, or signal in this context. “Wait for my signal” expresses the same request in more general language."},{"term":"anchor B","forms":["anchor"],"meaning":"留守 B 点，撑住首次接触","usage":"anchor + 点位在游戏里表示固定守点，通常晚于轮转队员离开。作名词 a site anchor 指负责留守的队员。","example":"I’ll anchor B while the others check Mid.","exampleZh":"其他人查中路，我来留守 B。","meaningEn":"Remain the primary defender on B and hold the position.","usageEn":"Anchor + site names a player’s responsibility. “A site anchor” is the person assigned that role while others may rotate earlier."}],"glossary":[]},{"en":"Round 13 — Defending Without Giving Away Kills","zh":"第十三局——不送人头的防守","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Red attacks first.","红队首先进攻。"],[" They decide to play slowly.","他们决定采取慢打。"],[" Two players move toward A Main.","两个人前往 A Main。"]],"translation":"红队首先进攻。 他们决定采取慢打。 两个人前往 A Main。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["One takes Mid Top.","一人前往 Mid Top。"],[" Two stay near B Lobby.","剩下两个人留在 B Lobby 附近。"],[" Blue has a balanced defensive setup.","蓝队采用了比较均衡的防守阵型。"]],"translation":"一人前往 Mid Top。 剩下两个人留在 B Lobby 附近。 蓝队采用了比较均衡的防守阵型。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Sova watches Mid.","猎枭观察中路。"],[" Jett holds A Main.","捷风架住 A Main。"],[" Killjoy protects B.","奇乐负责保护 B 点。"]],"translation":"猎枭观察中路。 捷风架住 A Main。 奇乐负责保护 B 点。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Omen stays near CT, ready to rotate.","幽影留在 CT 附近，随时准备转点。"],[" The attackers begin probing the defenses.","进攻方开始试探防守阵型。"],[" Skye sends her Trailblazer toward A.","斯凯向 A 点派出寻路猎犬。"]],"translation":"幽影留在 CT 附近，随时准备转点。 进攻方开始试探防守阵型。 斯凯向 A 点派出寻路猎犬。"},{"kind":"dialogue","sentences":[["Skye: \"Checking A. No contact yet.\"","Skye： \"Checking A. No contact yet.\"　正在检查 A，目前还没发现敌人。"]],"translation":"Skye： \"Checking A. No contact yet.\"　正在检查 A，目前还没发现敌人。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["The Trailblazer moves forward.","寻路猎犬向前移动。"],[" Jett hears it and retreats.","捷风听到了声音，并选择后撤。"],[" She does not shoot immediately.","她没有立即开枪。"]],"translation":"寻路猎犬向前移动。 捷风听到了声音，并选择后撤。 她没有立即开枪。"},{"kind":"dialogue","sentences":[["Jett: \"They have information utility. I'm backing off.\"","Jett： \"They have information utility. I'm backing off.\"　他们用了侦察技能，我先撤一下。"]],"translation":"Jett： \"They have information utility. I'm backing off.\"　他们用了侦察技能，我先撤一下。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Red attempts to use this information to push A.","红队尝试利用获得的信息进攻 A。"],[" But Omen places a smoke at the entrance.","但幽影在入口部署了烟雾。"],[" Killjoy's setup detects movement near B.","奇乐的防守装置检测到 B 点附近有移动。"]],"translation":"红队尝试利用获得的信息进攻 A。 但幽影在入口部署了烟雾。 奇乐的防守装置检测到 B 点附近有移动。"},{"kind":"dialogue","sentences":[["Killjoy: \"Two B. They're preparing a hit.\"","Killjoy： \"Two B. They're preparing a hit.\""]],"translation":"Killjoy： \"Two B. They're preparing a hit.\""},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Blue rotates carefully.","B 点两个，他们准备进攻了。"],[" They do not abandon A completely.","蓝队谨慎地开始转点。"],[" Instead, Sova moves toward CT while Jett holds her angle.","他们并没有完全放弃 A 点。"]],"translation":"B 点两个，他们准备进攻了。 蓝队谨慎地开始转点。 他们并没有完全放弃 A 点。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Red sees the defensive movement and decides to cancel the B attack. They return toward Mid.","而是让猎枭向 CT 移动，同时让捷风继续架住角度。 红队看到防守方的移动后，决定取消 B 点进攻。 他们重新回到中路附近。"]],"translation":"而是让猎枭向 CT 移动，同时让捷风继续架住角度。 红队看到防守方的移动后，决定取消 B 点进攻。 他们重新回到中路附近。"},{"kind":"dialogue","sentences":[["Sova: \"They're rotating Mid. I heard footsteps.\"","Sova： \"They're rotating Mid. I heard footsteps.\"　他们在往中路转移，我听到了脚步声。"]],"translation":"Sova： \"They're rotating Mid. I heard footsteps.\"　他们在往中路转移，我听到了脚步声。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Omen responds:","幽影回应："]],"translation":"幽影回应："},{"kind":"dialogue","sentences":[["Omen: \"Stay alive. Don't chase.\"","Omen： \"Stay alive. Don't chase.\"　活下来就行，不要追。"]],"translation":"Omen： \"Stay alive. Don't chase.\"　活下来就行，不要追。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["The attackers eventually run out of time.","进攻方最终时间不足。"],[" They fail to plant.","他们未能成功下包。"],[" Blue wins without needing to eliminate every attacker.","即使没有消灭所有进攻方，蓝队也赢下了这一局。"]],"translation":"进攻方最终时间不足。 他们未能成功下包。 即使没有消灭所有进攻方，蓝队也赢下了这一局。"},{"kind":"keyline","sentences":[["ROUND WON — BLUE　BLUE 9 — 4 RED","本局获胜——蓝队　蓝队 9 : 4 红队"]],"translation":"本局获胜——蓝队　蓝队 9 : 4 红队"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["This is called playing for time.","这叫作拖时间防守。"],[" Defenders do not always need to fight.","防守方并不总是需要与敌人交战。"],[" Sometimes the best strategy is to delay the attackers until they have no time left to complete their objective.","有时候，最好的战术就是不断拖延进攻方，直到他们没有时间完成目标。"]],"translation":"这叫作拖时间防守。 防守方并不总是需要与敌人交战。 有时候，最好的战术就是不断拖延进攻方，直到他们没有时间完成目标。"}],"terms":[{"term":"give away kills","forms":["giving away kills"],"meaning":"白送人头，让对手轻易拿到击杀","usage":"give away 表示无偿给出，也能表示无意暴露信息。此处是因冒进让对手不费力地获得击杀。","example":"Don’t give away kills when there’s no time left for them to plant.","exampleZh":"对手已经快没时间下包了，别白送人头。","meaningEn":"Allow opponents to earn easy eliminations through avoidable mistakes.","usageEn":"Give away often means hand something over for free. In “give away your position,” it instead refers to revealing information inadvertently."},{"term":"probe","forms":["probing the defenses"],"meaning":"试探防线，搜集对方布防信息","usage":"probe + 对象通常表示小规模地探索或试探，如 probe a weakness。它在这里指查信息阶段。","example":"They probed the defense before committing to a site.","exampleZh":"他们在确定打哪个点之前先试探了防线。","meaningEn":"Test a defense to learn how it is set up or how it responds.","usageEn":"Probe takes the thing being tested as its object. “Probe the defenses” suggests an initial effort to gather information before choosing a larger action."},{"term":"back off","forms":["backing off"],"meaning":"主动退出当前接触，往后拉开","usage":"back off 常指眼下别继续对抗，可接 from + 特定行动或位置。fall back 更强调撤向下一处防守点。","example":"Back off and wait for the others.","exampleZh":"先后撤，等其他队友到位。","meaningEn":"Move away from an engagement or reduce pressure immediately.","usageEn":"“Back off from the doorway” names the place or action to leave. A teammate can also say “back off” on its own as an immediate warning."},{"term":"hit","forms":["preparing a hit"],"meaning":"某点即将遭受一波进攻","usage":"a hit 是口语名词，a B hit 指针对 B 的一波进攻。hit B 作动词指发起这波进攻。","example":"They might be preparing a hit on B.","exampleZh":"他们可能正准备打一波 B。","meaningEn":"A coordinated attack on a particular site.","usageEn":"“A B hit” names the attack as an event. “Hit B” uses hit as a verb and names the site the team intends to attack."},{"term":"play for time","forms":["playing for time"],"meaning":"把拖时间当作当前打法","usage":"play for time 中 for 表示目的。run out of time 指时间已经不够，一般说 they’re playing for time 说明还能够利用时限。","example":"We can play for time and avoid a risky fight.","exampleZh":"我们可以拖时间，避免冒险交战。","meaningEn":"Deliberately delay so the remaining time works in your favor.","usageEn":"For identifies the objective of the action. A defender can play for time by postponing a fight as the attacking team approaches its deadline."}],"glossary":[]},{"en":"Round 14 — The Retake Fails","zh":"第十四局——回防失败","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Red has learned from the previous round.","红队已经从上一局吸取了教训。"],[" This time, they execute B with full coordination.","这一次，他们进行了一次完整的 B 点协同进攻。"],[" Skye flashes through B Main.","斯凯通过 B Main 释放闪光。"]],"translation":"红队已经从上一局吸取了教训。 这一次，他们进行了一次完整的 B 点协同进攻。 斯凯通过 B Main 释放闪光。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Raze uses her explosive abilities to clear close corners.","雷兹使用爆炸技能清理近点角落。"],[" Brimstone places smokes at Market and CT.","炼狱在 Market 和 CT 部署烟雾。"],[" Cypher watches the flank.","零负责观察绕后路线。"]],"translation":"雷兹使用爆炸技能清理近点角落。 炼狱在 Market 和 CT 部署烟雾。 零负责观察绕后路线。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Sage follows the entry players.","贤者跟在进攻人员后面。"]],"translation":"贤者跟在进攻人员后面。"},{"kind":"dialogue","sentences":[["Skye: \"Flash out! Go!\"","Skye： \"Flash out! Go!\"　闪光出去了！冲！"]],"translation":"Skye： \"Flash out! Go!\"　闪光出去了！冲！"},{"kind":"dialogue","sentences":[["Raze: \"I'm entering!\"","Raze： \"I'm entering!\"　我进点了！"]],"translation":"Raze： \"I'm entering!\"　我进点了！"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["The attackers take B Site.","进攻方成功拿下 B 点。"],[" Killjoy tries to delay them, but the attacking utility forces her away.","奇乐试图拖延他们，但进攻方的技能迫使她离开原来的位置。"],[" The Spike is planted.","爆能器成功安放。"]],"translation":"进攻方成功拿下 B 点。 奇乐试图拖延他们，但进攻方的技能迫使她离开原来的位置。 爆能器成功安放。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Blue now has to retake.","现在蓝队必须回防。"],[" Jett, Omen, Sova, and Killjoy gather near CT and Market.","捷风、幽影、猎枭和奇乐在 CT 和 Market 附近集合。"]],"translation":"现在蓝队必须回防。 捷风、幽影、猎枭和奇乐在 CT 和 Market 附近集合。"},{"kind":"dialogue","sentences":[["Omen: \"Wait. We go together.\"","Omen： \"Wait. We go together.\"　等一下，我们一起进去。"]],"translation":"Omen： \"Wait. We go together.\"　等一下，我们一起进去。"},{"kind":"dialogue","sentences":[["Jett: \"I'll dash in first.\"","Jett： \"I'll dash in first.\"　我先冲进去。"]],"translation":"Jett： \"I'll dash in first.\"　我先冲进去。"},{"kind":"dialogue","sentences":[["Sova: \"I'll reveal site.\"","Sova： \"I'll reveal site.\"　我先侦察点内。"]],"translation":"Sova： \"I'll reveal site.\"　我先侦察点内。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Sova fires his Recon Bolt.","猎枭发射侦察箭。"],[" It reveals Sage behind cover.","箭矢揭示了藏在掩体后的贤者。"],[" Jett dashes into the site.","捷风冲入爆能器区域。"]],"translation":"猎枭发射侦察箭。 箭矢揭示了藏在掩体后的贤者。 捷风冲入爆能器区域。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["But Red is ready.","但红队早已做好准备。"],[" Brimstone's Incendiary lands near the entrance.","炼狱的燃烧弹落在入口附近。"],[" Jett cannot safely move forward.","捷风无法安全地继续前进。"]],"translation":"但红队早已做好准备。 炼狱的燃烧弹落在入口附近。 捷风无法安全地继续前进。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Skye flashes the defenders.","斯凯向防守方释放闪光。"],[" Raze eliminates Jett.","雷兹击杀捷风。"],[" Sova tries to trade, but Cypher catches him.","猎枭试图补枪，却被零抓住机会击杀。"]],"translation":"斯凯向防守方释放闪光。 雷兹击杀捷风。 猎枭试图补枪，却被零抓住机会击杀。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["The retake fails.","回防失败。"],[" Blue loses the round.","蓝队输掉了这一局。"]],"translation":"回防失败。 蓝队输掉了这一局。"},{"kind":"keyline","sentences":[["ROUND WON — RED　BLUE 9 — 5 RED","本局获胜——红队　蓝队 9 : 5 红队"]],"translation":"本局获胜——红队　蓝队 9 : 5 红队"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["The defenders made one major mistake.","防守方犯了一个重大错误。"],[" They entered through the same route at almost the same time, allowing the attackers to use area-denial utility and crossfires effectively.","他们几乎同时从同一条路线进入，让进攻方能够有效利用范围控制技能和交叉火力。"],[" A retake needs coordination, but it also needs multiple angles.","回防需要团队协作，但也需要多个不同的进攻角度。"]],"translation":"防守方犯了一个重大错误。 他们几乎同时从同一条路线进入，让进攻方能够有效利用范围控制技能和交叉火力。 回防需要团队协作，但也需要多个不同的进攻角度。"}],"terms":[{"term":"retake","forms":["retakes","red retakes the site"],"meaning":"丢掉点位之后重新争夺控制权，也就是回防","usage":"作动词可说 retake B。作名词 a retake 不仅指移动回点，还含争取重新掌控点位的过程。","example":"Wait until everyone is ready for the retake.","exampleZh":"等大家都准备好了再一起回防。","meaningEn":"Return to a lost site and try to regain control.","usageEn":"“Retake B” uses a verb. “Set up a retake” uses a noun for the whole coordinated effort to recover the site."},{"term":"with full coordination","meaning":"全员动作配合到位","usage":"coordination 是不可数名词。with + 抽象名词可说明行动方式，如 with great care。","example":"The group moved in with full coordination.","exampleZh":"全组配合到位后一起进场。","meaningEn":"With the participants’ actions carefully timed to work together.","usageEn":"Coordination is uncountable here. With + abstract noun describes how the action happens, as in “with care” or “with precision.”"},{"term":"clear close corners","meaning":"逐一排查入口附近的拐角","usage":"clear + 地点在这里是排查并清理威胁。the corner is clear 表示检查后的状态。","example":"They cleared the close corners before moving on.","exampleZh":"他们先排查近处拐角，然后继续推进。","meaningEn":"Check nearby corners and deal with any threats there.","usageEn":"In this context, clear takes the place being searched as an object. “The corner is clear” describes the resulting state."},{"term":"force away","forms":["forces her away"],"meaning":"把对手逼离位置","usage":"常见结构 force + 人 + away from + 位置，也有 force + 人 + to do。away 强调离开原来的位置。","example":"The pressure forced her away from the entrance.","exampleZh":"压力迫使她离开了入口。","meaningEn":"Make someone leave the current position.","usageEn":"The pattern is force + person + away from + place. The cause can be pressure, movement, or an ability in the game."},{"term":"area-denial utility","meaning":"用于封锁区域或阻止进入的技能","usage":"area denial 作名词时指区域封锁，放在 utility 前常用连字符作复合修饰。utility 是技能资源的集合说法。","example":"Their area-denial utility kept us out of the site.","exampleZh":"他们封锁区域的技能使我们进不了点内。","meaningEn":"Abilities used to keep opponents out of a particular area.","usageEn":"Area denial names the effect. Hyphenate area-denial when the phrase modifies utility. Utility is used collectively for tactical abilities or equipment."}],"glossary":[]},{"en":"Round 15 — A Defensive Trap","zh":"第十五局——防守陷阱","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Blue decides to change its defensive setup.","蓝队决定改变防守阵型。"],[" Instead of spreading out evenly, Killjoy and Omen prepare a trap near B Site.","奇乐和幽影不再平均分散站位，而是在 B 点附近准备一个陷阱。"],[" Killjoy places her Alarmbot near B Main.","奇乐将报警机器人放置在 B Main 附近。"]],"translation":"蓝队决定改变防守阵型。 奇乐和幽影不再平均分散站位，而是在 B 点附近准备一个陷阱。 奇乐将报警机器人放置在 B Main 附近。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["She hides Nanoswarm grenades close to the common plant position.","她把纳米蜂群隐藏在常见下包位置附近。"],[" Omen prepares a smoke.","幽影准备好烟雾。"],[" Jett watches Mid.","捷风观察中路。"]],"translation":"她把纳米蜂群隐藏在常见下包位置附近。 幽影准备好烟雾。 捷风观察中路。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Sova holds A.","猎枭负责 A 点。"],[" Red decides to attack B again.","红队决定再次进攻 B 点。"],[" Cypher detects that the defenders are using a different setup.","零发现防守方改变了阵型。"]],"translation":"猎枭负责 A 点。 红队决定再次进攻 B 点。 零发现防守方改变了阵型。"},{"kind":"dialogue","sentences":[["Cypher: \"Careful. Their positions have changed.\"","Cypher： \"Careful. Their positions have changed.\"　小心，他们的站位变了。"]],"translation":"Cypher： \"Careful. Their positions have changed.\"　小心，他们的站位变了。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Skye uses Trailblazer to check the entrance.","斯凯使用寻路猎犬检查入口。"],[" The Alarmbot activates.","报警机器人启动。"],[" Killjoy waits.","奇乐开始等待。"]],"translation":"斯凯使用寻路猎犬检查入口。 报警机器人启动。 奇乐开始等待。"},{"kind":"dialogue","sentences":[["Killjoy: \"They're in range. Hold.\"","Killjoy： \"They're in range. Hold.\"　他们进入范围了，先等一下。"]],"translation":"Killjoy： \"They're in range. Hold.\"　他们进入范围了，先等一下。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Raze enters B Main.","雷兹进入 B Main。"],[" Killjoy activates Nanoswarm.","奇乐启动纳米蜂群。"],[" The attackers are caught in the damaging area.","进攻方被困在持续伤害区域内。"]],"translation":"雷兹进入 B Main。 奇乐启动纳米蜂群。 进攻方被困在持续伤害区域内。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Omen immediately swings from cover.","幽影立即从掩体后探出。"],[" Jett rotates through Market.","捷风从 Market 转移过来。"],[" The attackers are trapped between two angles.","进攻方被夹在两个射击角度之间。"]],"translation":"幽影立即从掩体后探出。 捷风从 Market 转移过来。 进攻方被夹在两个射击角度之间。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Red loses three players.","红队损失了三名队员。"],[" The remaining two attempt to escape.","剩下两个人尝试撤退。"],[" But Sova catches one near Mid.","但猎枭在中路附近抓住并击杀了一人。"]],"translation":"红队损失了三名队员。 剩下两个人尝试撤退。 但猎枭在中路附近抓住并击杀了一人。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Blue wins.","蓝队获胜。"]],"translation":"蓝队获胜。"},{"kind":"keyline","sentences":[["ROUND WON — BLUE　BLUE 10 — 5 RED","本局获胜——蓝队　蓝队 10 : 5 红队"]],"translation":"本局获胜——蓝队　蓝队 10 : 5 红队"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["This is an example of defensive utility synergy.","这是一个防守技能联动的例子。"],[" One ability detects the enemy.","一个技能负责发现敌人。"],[" Another delays movement.","另一个技能负责拖延移动。"]],"translation":"这是一个防守技能联动的例子。 一个技能负责发现敌人。 另一个技能负责拖延移动。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["A third ability creates pressure from a different angle.","第三个技能从另一个角度施加压力。"],[" The real power comes from combining abilities rather than using them separately.","真正的威力来自技能之间的配合，而不是孤立地使用技能。"]],"translation":"第三个技能从另一个角度施加压力。 真正的威力来自技能之间的配合，而不是孤立地使用技能。"}],"terms":[{"term":"spread out evenly","forms":["spreading out evenly"],"meaning":"均匀分散站位","usage":"evenly 是副词，说明人员分布较均衡。the players are spread out 指分开站位，加入 evenly 才强调覆盖大致均匀。","example":"They spread out evenly across the three entrances.","exampleZh":"他们均匀分散在三个入口。","meaningEn":"Separate so that coverage is roughly balanced across the area.","usageEn":"“Spread out across the map” names the extent of the movement. The adverb evenly emphasizes that the overall distribution is balanced."},{"term":"in range","meaning":"处于技能可作用的范围内","usage":"常见对比 in range / out of range。within range of + 某技能或装置 是更完整的表达。","example":"Wait until they’re in range before using it.","exampleZh":"等他们进入作用范围以后再放。","meaningEn":"Close enough to be affected or detected.","usageEn":"Common forms are “in range,” “out of range,” and “within range of the ability.” Range describes the reach of a particular effect or device."},{"term":"swing from cover","forms":["swings from cover"],"meaning":"从掩体里拉出来交战","usage":"swing 常指横向拉出身位。from cover 指出起点是掩体之后。peek 在语境里可只是短暂探看。","example":"He swung from cover after hearing the call.","exampleZh":"他听见报点后从掩体里拉了出来。","meaningEn":"Move sideways out of protection to take an engagement.","usageEn":"Swing describes moving out into view. From cover identifies the starting position, and the following words can name the direction or opponent."},{"term":"trapped between two angles","meaning":"被来自两个方向的枪线夹住","usage":"be trapped between 表示无处可退，也可抽象用于在两个坏选择之间进退两难。angles 描述对手架枪的方向。","example":"They were trapped between two angles near the entrance.","exampleZh":"他们在入口附近被两个方向的枪线夹住了。","meaningEn":"Caught where opponents can engage from two directions.","usageEn":"“Be trapped between” describes limited options. In this passage, the two angles are lines of fire that make it hard to move to safety."},{"term":"synergy","forms":["defensive utility synergy"],"meaning":"几项技能相互配合，放大整体效果","usage":"常用 synergy between A and B 或 create synergy。重点是不同功能互补，例如一个负责侦测，一个负责拖延。","example":"There’s good synergy between those two abilities.","exampleZh":"那两项技能配合起来效果很好。","meaningEn":"The extra effect created when abilities complement each other.","usageEn":"Use “synergy between A and B” for a working relationship. The passage uses it for abilities that contribute different effects to the same setup."}],"glossary":[]},{"en":"Round 16 — The Final Push","zh":"第十六局——最后的进攻","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["The score is now 10–5.","比分现在是 10:5。"],[" Blue is getting closer to victory.","蓝队距离胜利越来越近。"],[" Red needs to win several consecutive rounds.","红队必须连续赢下多局比赛。"]],"translation":"比分现在是 10:5。 蓝队距离胜利越来越近。 红队必须连续赢下多局比赛。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["The attackers decide to take a risk.","进攻方决定冒一次险。"],[" They use a fast split attack.","他们采用快速分推战术。"],[" Two players move toward A Main.","两个人前往 A Main。"]],"translation":"进攻方决定冒一次险。 他们采用快速分推战术。 两个人前往 A Main。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Three players take Mid.","三个人进入中路。"]],"translation":"三个人进入中路。"},{"kind":"dialogue","sentences":[["Brimstone: \"We're going A. But don't show everything too early.\"","Brimstone： \"We're going A. But don't show everything too early.\"　我们打 A，但不要过早暴露全部战术。"]],"translation":"Brimstone： \"We're going A. But don't show everything too early.\"　我们打 A，但不要过早暴露全部战术。"},{"kind":"dialogue","sentences":[["Skye: \"I'll flash Main.\"","Skye： \"I'll flash Main.\"　我负责给大道闪光。"]],"translation":"Skye： \"I'll flash Main.\"　我负责给大道闪光。"},{"kind":"dialogue","sentences":[["Cypher: \"I'll watch our flank.\"","Cypher： \"I'll watch our flank.\"　我负责看绕后。"]],"translation":"Cypher： \"I'll watch our flank.\"　我负责看绕后。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Blue detects the attack.","蓝队发现了进攻。"],[" Sova sees two players near A.","猎枭看到 A Main 附近有两个人。"]],"translation":"蓝队发现了进攻。 猎枭看到 A Main 附近有两个人。"},{"kind":"dialogue","sentences":[["Sova: \"Two A Main. Possible execute.\"","Sova： \"Two A Main. Possible execute.\""]],"translation":"Sova： \"Two A Main. Possible execute.\""},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Omen prepares his smoke.","A 大道两个，可能准备进攻。"],[" Jett moves toward Heaven.","幽影准备部署烟雾。"],[" But Red has another plan.","捷风向 Heaven 移动。"]],"translation":"A 大道两个，可能准备进攻。 幽影准备部署烟雾。 捷风向 Heaven 移动。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["The two players at A Main are only creating pressure. The real attack is coming through Mid Catwalk and Tree.","但红队还有另一个计划。 A Main 的两个人只是为了制造压力。 真正的进攻来自 Mid Catwalk 和 Tree。"]],"translation":"但红队还有另一个计划。 A Main 的两个人只是为了制造压力。 真正的进攻来自 Mid Catwalk 和 Tree。"},{"kind":"dialogue","sentences":[["Cypher: \"Go! Tree is open!\"","Cypher： \"Go! Tree is open!\"　冲！树房路线已经打开！"]],"translation":"Cypher： \"Go! Tree is open!\"　冲！树房路线已经打开！"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Raze enters A from Tree.","雷兹从 Tree 进入 A 点。"],[" Skye flashes Heaven.","斯凯向 Heaven 释放闪光。"],[" Brimstone smokes the defensive angles.","炼狱封锁防守方的射击角度。"]],"translation":"雷兹从 Tree 进入 A 点。 斯凯向 Heaven 释放闪光。 炼狱封锁防守方的射击角度。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["The defenders are forced to fight from different directions.","防守方被迫从不同方向交战。"],[" Killjoy activates her ultimate.","奇乐启动大招。"],[" The Lockdown begins.","禁区开始倒计时。"]],"translation":"防守方被迫从不同方向交战。 奇乐启动大招。 禁区开始倒计时。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Red must leave the affected area or destroy the device.","红队必须离开影响范围，或者摧毁装置。"],[" Brimstone uses his Incendiary to delay the defenders.","炼狱使用燃烧弹拖延防守方。"],[" The Lockdown expires.","禁区倒计时结束。"]],"translation":"红队必须离开影响范围，或者摧毁装置。 炼狱使用燃烧弹拖延防守方。 禁区倒计时结束。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Blue's defensive positions have been disrupted.","蓝队原来的防守位置被打乱。"],[" Red plants the Spike.","红队成功下包。"],[" The post-plant fight begins.","下包后的战斗开始。"]],"translation":"蓝队原来的防守位置被打乱。 红队成功下包。 下包后的战斗开始。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Omen eliminates Raze.","幽影击杀雷兹。"],[" Skye trades Omen.","斯凯补枪击杀幽影。"],[" Jett eliminates Cypher.","捷风击杀零。"]],"translation":"幽影击杀雷兹。 斯凯补枪击杀幽影。 捷风击杀零。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["The round becomes a 2v2.","战局变成了 2 对 2。"],[" Brimstone and Sage remain against Jett and Killjoy.","炼狱和贤者对阵捷风和奇乐。"],[" Sage uses her Slow Orb.","贤者使用减速法球。"]],"translation":"战局变成了 2 对 2。 炼狱和贤者对阵捷风和奇乐。 贤者使用减速法球。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Jett cannot move freely.","捷风无法自由移动。"],[" Brimstone swings.","炼狱探出身位。"],[" Killjoy eliminates him.","奇乐将其击杀。"]],"translation":"捷风无法自由移动。 炼狱探出身位。 奇乐将其击杀。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Sage tries to defuse.","贤者尝试拆包。"],[" Jett appears from Heaven.","捷风从 Heaven 出现。"],[" One final shot.","最后一枪。"]],"translation":"贤者尝试拆包。 捷风从 Heaven 出现。 最后一枪。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Sage falls.","贤者倒下。"],[" Blue wins the round.","蓝队赢得这一局。"]],"translation":"贤者倒下。 蓝队赢得这一局。"},{"kind":"keyline","sentences":[["FINAL SCORE: BLUE 13 — 5 RED　BLUE WINS THE MATCH!","最终比分：蓝队 13 : 5 红队　蓝队赢得比赛！"]],"translation":"最终比分：蓝队 13 : 5 红队　蓝队赢得比赛！"}],"terms":[{"term":"consecutive","meaning":"连续的，中间没有中断","usage":"常说 three consecutive rounds，口语可说 three rounds in a row。successive 也表相继，在赛事比分语境里 consecutive 更直接。","example":"They won three consecutive rounds after the break.","exampleZh":"中场之后他们连赢了三回合。","meaningEn":"Following one after another without interruption.","usageEn":"A number often comes before consecutive, as in “three consecutive rounds.” In conversation, “three rounds in a row” conveys the same sequence."},{"term":"show everything","meaning":"过早把全部布置或意图暴露出来","usage":"show 在队内口语里可以表示让对手获得信息。show A 可以只是露面制造 A 点动静，show everything 则把完整意图都暴露了。","example":"Only two players should show at Main for now.","exampleZh":"目前只需要两名队员在大道露面。","meaningEn":"Reveal the full setup or intention to the opponents.","usageEn":"Show is a team shorthand for giving the opponents visible information. “Show at A” can mean briefly appear there, and “show everything” means reveal the full plan."},{"term":"create pressure","forms":["creating pressure"],"meaning":"在某处施加压力，迫使对方分配注意力","usage":"create/put pressure on + 人或点位。force somebody to react 描述这种压力引发的结果。","example":"Two teammates created pressure at A Main.","exampleZh":"两名队友在 A 大道制造压力。","meaningEn":"Make opponents respond to a threat or commit attention to an area.","usageEn":"“Put pressure on B” names the target of the pressure. “Create pressure at A Main” names the location where the threat is presented."},{"term":"expire","forms":["expires"],"meaning":"技能的有效时间结束","usage":"不及物，适用于计时器、权限或技能状态。run out 常用时间或资源作主语，而 expire 表示某件东西过了有效期。","example":"The effect expires after a short time.","exampleZh":"这个效果过一小会儿就会消失。","meaningEn":"Reach the end of a period of validity or effect.","usageEn":"Expire is intransitive in this sense. Effects, timers, and permissions can expire. Time and resources can run out."},{"term":"disrupt","forms":["disrupted"],"meaning":"打乱原先的防守位置或节奏","usage":"常搭配 disrupt a plan、a formation、communications。disrupt 指对正在运行的安排造成干扰，destroy 指彻底破坏。","example":"The sudden rotation disrupted their defensive setup.","exampleZh":"突然的转点打乱了他们的防守布置。","meaningEn":"Interfere with an existing plan, position, or rhythm.","usageEn":"Use disrupt with something already organized or in progress, such as a defensive setup, a rotation, or communications."}],"glossary":[]},{"en":"The Language of Real Players","zh":"真实玩家的游戏英语","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["The following expressions are commonly used in fast-paced VALORANT communication.","下面这些表达经常出现在无畏契约的快速语音交流中。"]],"translation":"下面这些表达经常出现在无畏契约的快速语音交流中。"},{"kind":"heading","sentences":[["Giving Information","提供信息"]],"translation":"提供信息"},{"kind":"dialogue","sentences":[["\"One A Main.\" — A single enemy is at A Main.","\"One A Main.\" — A Main 有一个敌人。"]],"translation":"\"One A Main.\" — A Main 有一个敌人。"},{"kind":"dialogue","sentences":[["\"Two pushing Mid.\" — Two enemies are pushing through Mid.","\"Two pushing Mid.\" — 有两个敌人正在推进中路。"]],"translation":"\"Two pushing Mid.\" — 有两个敌人正在推进中路。"},{"kind":"dialogue","sentences":[["\"Spike is down.\" — The Spike has been dropped.","\"Spike is down.\" — 爆能器掉了。"]],"translation":"\"Spike is down.\" — 爆能器掉了。"},{"kind":"dialogue","sentences":[["\"He's playing close.\" — The enemy is holding a close angle.","\"He's playing close.\" — 敌人在近点架枪。"]],"translation":"\"He's playing close.\" — 敌人在近点架枪。"},{"kind":"dialogue","sentences":[["\"One is low.\" — One enemy has very little health.","\"One is low.\" — 有一个敌人残血了。"]],"translation":"\"One is low.\" — 有一个敌人残血了。"},{"kind":"dialogue","sentences":[["\"Last seen Market.\" — The enemy was last spotted near Market.","\"Last seen Market.\" — 最后一次在 Market 看到他。"]],"translation":"\"Last seen Market.\" — 最后一次在 Market 看到他。"},{"kind":"dialogue","sentences":[["\"Could be a fake.\" — The attack might be a distraction.","\"Could be a fake.\" — 可能是假打。"]],"translation":"\"Could be a fake.\" — 可能是假打。"},{"kind":"heading","sentences":[["Giving Instructions","发出指令"]],"translation":"发出指令"},{"kind":"dialogue","sentences":[["\"Hold your position.\" — Stay where you are.","\"Hold your position.\" — 守住你现在的位置。"]],"translation":"\"Hold your position.\" — 守住你现在的位置。"},{"kind":"dialogue","sentences":[["\"Play off me.\" — Follow my movement and support my fight.","\"Play off me.\" — 跟着我的行动，支援我的交战。"]],"translation":"\"Play off me.\" — 跟着我的行动，支援我的交战。"},{"kind":"dialogue","sentences":[["\"Swing together.\" — Peek at the same time.","\"Swing together.\" — 一起探头对枪。"]],"translation":"\"Swing together.\" — 一起探头对枪。"},{"kind":"dialogue","sentences":[["\"Don't give them a free kill.\" — Do not expose yourself unnecessarily.","\"Don't give them a free kill.\" — 不要随便把人头送给敌人。"]],"translation":"\"Don't give them a free kill.\" — 不要随便把人头送给敌人。"},{"kind":"dialogue","sentences":[["\"Wait for my flash.\" — Do not enter until I use my flash.","\"Wait for my flash.\" — 等我闪光之后再进去。"]],"translation":"\"Wait for my flash.\" — 等我闪光之后再进去。"},{"kind":"dialogue","sentences":[["\"Play for time.\" — Delay the enemy rather than taking unnecessary fights.","\"Play for time.\" — 拖延敌人，不要进行没有必要的交战。"]],"translation":"\"Play for time.\" — 拖延敌人，不要进行没有必要的交战。"},{"kind":"dialogue","sentences":[["\"Let's group up.\" — Gather together before attacking.","\"Let's group up.\" — 我们先集合再进攻。"]],"translation":"\"Let's group up.\" — 我们先集合再进攻。"},{"kind":"heading","sentences":[["Reacting to Situations","对局势作出反应"]],"translation":"对局势作出反应"},{"kind":"dialogue","sentences":[["\"Nice shot!\" — Great aim!","\"Nice shot!\" — 枪打得漂亮！"]],"translation":"\"Nice shot!\" — 枪打得漂亮！"},{"kind":"dialogue","sentences":[["\"Unlucky.\" — That was unfortunate.","\"Unlucky.\" — 有点可惜。"]],"translation":"\"Unlucky.\" — 有点可惜。"},{"kind":"dialogue","sentences":[["\"That's my bad.\" — That was my mistake.","\"That's my bad.\" — 那是我的失误。"]],"translation":"\"That's my bad.\" — 那是我的失误。"},{"kind":"dialogue","sentences":[["\"My fault.\" — I'm responsible for that mistake.","\"My fault.\" — 我的责任。"]],"translation":"\"My fault.\" — 我的责任。"},{"kind":"dialogue","sentences":[["\"Well played.\" — That was a good play.","\"Well played.\" — 打得好。"]],"translation":"\"Well played.\" — 打得好。"},{"kind":"dialogue","sentences":[["\"Good trade.\" — You successfully avenged your teammate.","\"Good trade.\" — 补枪补得不错。"]],"translation":"\"Good trade.\" — 补枪补得不错。"},{"kind":"dialogue","sentences":[["\"Clutch or kick!\" — A joking expression used to encourage the last surviving teammate.","\"Clutch or kick!\" — 一种开玩笑的表达，鼓励最后存活的队友完成残局。"]],"translation":"\"Clutch or kick!\" — 一种开玩笑的表达，鼓励最后存活的队友完成残局。"},{"kind":"dialogue","sentences":[["\"Let's reset.\" — Forget the previous round and focus on the next one.","\"Let's reset.\" — 忘掉上一局，专注下一局。"]],"translation":"\"Let's reset.\" — 忘掉上一局，专注下一局。"},{"kind":"heading","sentences":[["Natural Voice Communication","自然的语音交流"]],"translation":"自然的语音交流"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["In real matches, players rarely speak in complete textbook sentences.","在真实比赛中，玩家很少使用完整的课本句子交流。"],[" They use short phrases because time is limited.","他们更倾向于使用简短的表达，因为时间非常有限。"]],"translation":"在真实比赛中，玩家很少使用完整的课本句子交流。 他们更倾向于使用简短的表达，因为时间非常有限。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["For example:","例如："]],"translation":"例如："},{"kind":"dialogue","sentences":[["\"One close left, 80.\" — This means there is one enemy close to the left side, and the enemy has approximately 80 health remaining.","\"One close left, 80.\" — 意思是左边近点有一个敌人，他大约还剩 80 点生命值。"]],"translation":"\"One close left, 80.\" — 意思是左边近点有一个敌人，他大约还剩 80 点生命值。"},{"kind":"dialogue","sentences":[["\"He's probably rotating.\" — The enemy is likely moving to another site.","\"He's probably rotating.\" — 敌人可能正在转点。"]],"translation":"\"He's probably rotating.\" — 敌人可能正在转点。"},{"kind":"dialogue","sentences":[["\"Don't overpeek.\" — Do not expose yourself too far while checking an angle.","\"Don't overpeek.\" — 不要过度探头检查角度。"]],"translation":"\"Don't overpeek.\" — 不要过度探头检查角度。"},{"kind":"dialogue","sentences":[["\"Play off contact.\" — Wait until someone makes contact with an enemy, then use that information to attack.","\"Play off contact.\" — 等待队友与敌人接触，然后利用获得的信息进行进攻。"]],"translation":"\"Play off contact.\" — 等待队友与敌人接触，然后利用获得的信息进行进攻。"},{"kind":"dialogue","sentences":[["\"Trade me.\" — If I die, eliminate the enemy who killed me.","\"Trade me.\" — 如果我被击杀，立即消灭击杀我的敌人。"]],"translation":"\"Trade me.\" — 如果我被击杀，立即消灭击杀我的敌人。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["These expressions will make your English sound much more natural in a gaming environment.","掌握这些表达，你在游戏环境中的英语听起来就会自然得多。"]],"translation":"掌握这些表达，你在游戏环境中的英语听起来就会自然得多。"}],"terms":[{"term":"fast-paced","meaning":"节奏快的","usage":"复合形容词，常置于名词前，如 a fast-paced match 或 fast-paced communication。pace 在这里是行动发生的节奏。","example":"In a fast-paced match, one clear callout helps the whole team.","exampleZh":"比赛节奏很快时，一条清楚的报点对全队都有帮助。","meaningEn":"Moving or changing quickly.","usageEn":"This compound adjective often comes before a noun, as in “fast-paced communication.” Pace is the speed at which events unfold."},{"term":"play off me","meaning":"根据我的动作接应或跟进","usage":"play off + 人、动作或信号，意思是以对方的行动作触发条件。Play off me 表示队友可以根据我的走位行动。","example":"Play off me once I make contact.","exampleZh":"等我遇敌后，你就跟着我的动作接应。","meaningEn":"Use my action as the signal for your own move and support me.","usageEn":"Play off + person or action means respond to that cue. Teammates can agree whether the cue is movement, a sighting, or the start of an engagement."},{"term":"that's my bad","meaning":"是我的失误","usage":"my bad 是非正式口语，语气通常比正式道歉轻。适合对小失误负责，工作邮件可用 That was my mistake。","example":"My bad, I called the wrong entrance.","exampleZh":"我的错，我报错了入口。","meaningEn":"That mistake was my responsibility.","usageEn":"My bad is an informal acknowledgment of a minor mistake. “That was my mistake” is a fuller version suitable for more formal speech."},{"term":"overpeek","forms":["don't overpeek"],"meaning":"探得太远或探得太久，过度暴露身位","usage":"over-表示越过合适限度。peek 本身只是探头看或短暂交战，所以 Don't overpeek 仍可允许谨慎观察。","example":"Don’t overpeek when we already have the information.","exampleZh":"信息已经拿到了，别再探得太远。","meaningEn":"Expose yourself farther or longer than the situation calls for.","usageEn":"The prefix over- indicates excess. In a call, “don’t overpeek” warns that the player is taking on more exposure than is useful."},{"term":"group up","forms":["let's group up"],"meaning":"重新集合","usage":"不及物短语，常用命令 Group up at B Lobby。regroup 也可表示在队伍分散或受挫后集合并重新组织。","example":"Let’s group up before the next move.","exampleZh":"下一步行动前我们先集合。","meaningEn":"Gather in one place as a team.","usageEn":"Group up is intransitive. Add a location after at or near. The related verb regroup also suggests reorganizing after being split or set back."}],"glossary":[]},{"en":"The Most Important Tactical Concepts","zh":"最重要的十个战术概念","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Before you start playing, remember these ten principles.","在真正开始游戏之前，请记住下面十个原则。"]],"translation":"在真正开始游戏之前，请记住下面十个原则。"},{"kind":"heading","sentences":[["1. Crosshair Placement","1. 准星预瞄（Crosshair Placement）"]],"translation":"1. 准星预瞄（Crosshair Placement）"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Keep your crosshair at head level and aim where enemies are likely to appear.","将准星保持在敌人头部高度，并提前瞄准敌人最可能出现的位置。"],[" Good crosshair placement reduces the amount of movement needed to hit an enemy.","良好的预瞄可以减少击杀敌人时需要进行的准星移动。"]],"translation":"将准星保持在敌人头部高度，并提前瞄准敌人最可能出现的位置。 良好的预瞄可以减少击杀敌人时需要进行的准星移动。"},{"kind":"heading","sentences":[["2. Map Awareness","2. 地图意识（Map Awareness）"]],"translation":"2. 地图意识（Map Awareness）"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Always understand where your teammates are and which routes the enemy might use.","始终清楚队友的位置，以及敌人可能使用哪些路线。"]],"translation":"始终清楚队友的位置，以及敌人可能使用哪些路线。"},{"kind":"heading","sentences":[["3. Trading","3. 补枪（Trading）"]],"translation":"3. 补枪（Trading）"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Stay close enough to support your teammate.","保持足够近的距离以支援队友。"],[" If they die, you should have an opportunity to eliminate the enemy.","如果队友被击杀，你应该有机会立即消灭击杀他的敌人。"]],"translation":"保持足够近的距离以支援队友。如果队友被击杀，你应该有机会立即消灭击杀他的敌人。"},{"kind":"heading","sentences":[["4. Utility Management","4. 技能管理（Utility Management）"]],"translation":"4. 技能管理（Utility Management）"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Do not waste flashes, smokes, or reconnaissance abilities without a purpose.","不要毫无目的地浪费闪光、烟雾或侦察技能。"]],"translation":"不要毫无目的地浪费闪光、烟雾或侦察技能。"},{"kind":"heading","sentences":[["5. Economy","5. 经济管理（Economy）"]],"translation":"5. 经济管理（Economy）"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Coordinate purchases with your teammates.","与队友协调购买装备。"],[" A team that buys together is usually stronger than five players making separate economic decisions.","一支统一购买的队伍，通常比五名玩家各自做经济决策的队伍更强。"]],"translation":"与队友协调购买装备。一支统一购买的队伍，通常比五名玩家各自做经济决策的队伍更强。"},{"kind":"heading","sentences":[["6. Communication","6. 沟通（Communication）"]],"translation":"6. 沟通（Communication）"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Give short, accurate information.","提供简短、准确的信息。"],[" The location of an enemy is usually more useful than a long explanation of what happened.","敌人的位置通常比一大段事情经过更有价值。"]],"translation":"提供简短、准确的信息。 敌人的位置通常比一大段事情经过更有价值。"},{"kind":"heading","sentences":[["7. Positioning","7. 站位（Positioning）"]],"translation":"7. 站位（Positioning）"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Do not stand in predictable places every round.","不要每一局都站在完全相同的位置。"],[" Change your positions to prevent the enemy from learning your habits.","改变站位，防止敌人摸清你的习惯。"]],"translation":"不要每一局都站在完全相同的位置。改变站位，防止敌人摸清你的习惯。"},{"kind":"heading","sentences":[["8. Timing","8. 时机（Timing）"]],"translation":"8. 时机（Timing）"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["An excellent ability used too early or too late can become useless.","一个非常好的技能，如果使用得太早或太晚，也可能失去作用。"]],"translation":"一个非常好的技能，如果使用得太早或太晚，也可能失去作用。"},{"kind":"heading","sentences":[["9. Adaptability","9. 适应能力（Adaptability）"]],"translation":"9. 适应能力（Adaptability）"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["If a strategy fails repeatedly, change it. Do not keep making the same mistake.","如果一种战术连续失败，就应该改变它，而不是重复犯同样的错误。"]],"translation":"如果一种战术连续失败，就应该改变它，而不是重复犯同样的错误。"},{"kind":"heading","sentences":[["10. Mentality","10. 心态（Mentality）"]],"translation":"10. 心态（Mentality）"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Do not blame teammates after every lost round.","不要每输一局就责怪队友。"],[" Analyze the mistake, communicate clearly, and focus on the next round.","分析失误，清楚沟通，然后专注下一局。"]],"translation":"不要每输一局就责怪队友。 分析失误，清楚沟通，然后专注下一局。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["The best players are not necessarily the players who win every gunfight.","最优秀的玩家不一定是每次对枪都获胜的人。"],[" They are the players who make the right decisions more consistently.","他们是那些能够更加稳定地作出正确决策的人。"]],"translation":"最优秀的玩家不一定是每次对枪都获胜的人。 他们是那些能够更加稳定地作出正确决策的人。"}],"terms":[{"term":"crosshair placement","meaning":"准星预瞄的位置安排","usage":"crosshair 是屏幕中间的准星，placement 是摆放位置。at head level 和 pre-aim a corner 是相邻术语。","example":"Good crosshair placement reduces how far you have to move your aim.","exampleZh":"好的准星预瞄能减少你需要调整瞄准的幅度。","meaningEn":"The way a player positions the on-screen aiming marker before an encounter.","usageEn":"Placement is the positioning of an object. “Good crosshair placement” means anticipating where an opponent might appear and already aiming near that spot."},{"term":"head level","forms":["at head level"],"meaning":"与对手头部大致同高的高度","usage":"at + 高度或水平。keep X at head level 描述让某物持续位于该高度。","example":"Keep your crosshair at head level when you approach the corner.","exampleZh":"接近拐角时，让准星保持在头部高度。","meaningEn":"The approximate height of an opponent’s head.","usageEn":"“At head level” describes a height. The pattern “keep the crosshair at head level” emphasizes maintaining that height as you move."},{"term":"utility management","meaning":"技能资源的分配与使用时机管理","usage":"名词 management 把一组选择概括为管理任务。和 use utility 相比，强调何时用、该留多少以及怎样与队友配合。","example":"Better utility management gave us more options late in the round.","exampleZh":"技能管理得更好，让我们在回合后段有了更多选择。","meaningEn":"Planning how and when to spend the team’s abilities.","usageEn":"Management covers decisions about timing, coordination, and saving abilities for later. Players can discuss their utility as the resources still available to use."},{"term":"coordinate purchases","meaning":"让队友对齐本回合的购买方案","usage":"coordinate + 行动表示协调安排，coordinate with + 人说明和谁协调。buy together 指大家执行同一轮经济决定。","example":"Coordinate purchases with the team before you spend your credits.","exampleZh":"花点数之前先和队友对齐购买方案。","meaningEn":"Agree on what to buy so the team follows a shared plan.","usageEn":"Coordinate takes the thing being organized as an object. Add with + person or group to identify the people involved in the decision."},{"term":"consistently","meaning":"稳定地，一贯地","usage":"consistently 常修饰反复表现出的动作。后缀 -ly 把 consistent 变成副词。constantly 强调一直发生或频率非常高。","example":"She consistently gives clear callouts under pressure.","exampleZh":"她在压力下也总能清楚报点。","meaningEn":"In a reliable or repeated way over time.","usageEn":"Consistently describes a pattern across repeated attempts. In “play well consistently,” the emphasis is on reliability from one performance to the next."}],"glossary":[]},{"en":"A Final Thought","zh":"最后的感受","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Imagine that you are standing at A Main.","想象一下，你正站在 A Main。"]],"translation":"想象一下，你正站在 A Main。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Your teammates are behind you.","你的队友就在你身后。"]],"translation":"你的队友就在你身后。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Sova is preparing his Recon Bolt.","猎枭正在准备侦察箭。"]],"translation":"猎枭正在准备侦察箭。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Omen is placing his smokes.","幽影正在部署烟雾。"]],"translation":"幽影正在部署烟雾。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Gekko is ready to send Dizzy into the site.","盖可准备将 Dizzy 放进爆能器区域。"]],"translation":"盖可准备将 Dizzy 放进爆能器区域。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Your Spike carrier is waiting.","携带爆能器的队友正在等待。"]],"translation":"携带爆能器的队友正在等待。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["The round timer is running.","比赛计时器正在倒数。"]],"translation":"比赛计时器正在倒数。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["You hear footsteps.","你听到了脚步声。"]],"translation":"你听到了脚步声。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Your teammate speaks:","队友突然说道："]],"translation":"队友突然说道："},{"kind":"dialogue","sentences":[["\"Two Heaven. One Generator. Flash ready. Let's go!\"","\"Two Heaven. One Generator. Flash ready. Let's go!\"　高台两个，发电机一个，闪光准备好了，冲！"]],"translation":"\"Two Heaven. One Generator. Flash ready. Let's go!\"　高台两个，发电机一个，闪光准备好了，冲！"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["You take a deep breath.","你深吸一口气。"]],"translation":"你深吸一口气。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["You check your crosshair.","检查自己的准星。"]],"translation":"检查自己的准星。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["You wait for the flash.","等待队友的闪光。"]],"translation":"等待队友的闪光。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["Then you dash into the site.","然后冲进爆能器区域。"]],"translation":"然后冲进爆能器区域。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["The fight begins.","战斗开始。"]],"translation":"战斗开始。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["This is VALORANT.","这就是无畏契约。"]],"translation":"这就是无畏契约。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["It is not just about shooting.","它不仅仅是射击。"]],"translation":"它不仅仅是射击。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["It is about reading your opponents, understanding the map, trusting your teammates, and making decisions under pressure.","它更是阅读对手、理解地图、信任队友，以及在压力之下作出决策的过程。"]],"translation":"它更是阅读对手、理解地图、信任队友，以及在压力之下作出决策的过程。"},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["And the next time you hear someone say:","下一次，当你听到有人说："]],"translation":"下一次，当你听到有人说："},{"kind":"dialogue","sentences":[["\"Play together. Don't peek. We have time.\"","\"Play together. Don't peek. We have time.\""]],"translation":"\"Play together. Don't peek. We have time.\""},{"kind":"paragraph","sentences":[["You will understand exactly what they mean.","你就会准确理解他们的意思。"]],"translation":"你就会准确理解他们的意思。"},{"kind":"keyline","sentences":[["Welcome to the game.","欢迎来到战场。"]],"translation":"欢迎来到战场。"}],"terms":[{"term":"spike carrier","meaning":"携带爆能器的队员","usage":"carrier 来自 carry，可指携带东西的人或运输机构。the Spike carrier 在这里是队内分工。","example":"Stay close to the Spike carrier until the site is clear.","exampleZh":"点内安全之前，跟携带爆能器的队友保持近距离。","meaningEn":"The teammate carrying the Spike.","usageEn":"Carrier is a noun formed from carry. “The Spike carrier” refers to the player currently responsible for bringing the device to the site."},{"term":"take a deep breath","forms":["you take a deep breath"],"meaning":"深吸一口气","usage":"take a breath 常见于动作叙述。take a deep breath and + 动词 可用于让自己冷静后再行动。","example":"Take a deep breath before you make the call.","exampleZh":"报点之前深吸一口气。","meaningEn":"Inhale fully, often to steady yourself before acting.","usageEn":"Take a breath is a common verb–noun combination. “Take a deep breath and…” links a small preparatory pause to the action that follows."},{"term":"read your opponents","forms":["reading your opponents"],"meaning":"根据迹象判断对手的意图","usage":"read 在 read a person 或 read the room 里是观察并理解。这里结合对方路线与行动推断下一步。","example":"She reads her opponents by noticing what they repeat.","exampleZh":"她留意对手反复做什么，以判断他们的意图。","meaningEn":"Infer what opposing players intend from their behavior.","usageEn":"Read can mean interpret people and situations, as in “read the room.” Map movement, repeated routes, and timing are clues in this passage."},{"term":"under pressure","meaning":"处在压力之下","usage":"make decisions under pressure 是常见搭配。under 在这里表达一种处境，可同 under stress 类比。","example":"It’s harder to make clear decisions under pressure.","exampleZh":"人在压力下更难作出清晰的判断。","meaningEn":"In a demanding situation where stress can affect decisions.","usageEn":"Under expresses a condition, as in “under stress.” It is common in phrases such as “stay calm under pressure” and “make decisions under pressure.”"},{"term":"peek","forms":["don't peek"],"meaning":"从掩体探出去观察或对枪","usage":"peek 的日常含义是偷看或看一眼。peek from behind cover 描述探出的起点，Don’t peek 常用于要求稳住当前安全位置。","example":"Hold your position and don’t peek until the flash goes out.","exampleZh":"守住位置，等闪光弹出手再探头。","meaningEn":"Move briefly out from cover to look or engage.","usageEn":"In the game, peek can take a position as its object, as in “peek the corner.” “Don’t peek” tells a teammate to remain behind cover for the moment."}],"glossary":[]}],"subtitle":"The Art of Tactical Combat"}];
